t-docs/ai","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/ai#fitness-course","content":"A fitness course creator fielding the same questions"},"982":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-24","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/ai#compare","content":"How EasyWebinar compares for AI for webinars"},"983":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-25","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/ai#compare-stronger","content":"Why EasyWebinar is the stronger choice for AI for webinars"},"984":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-26","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/ai#limits","content":"Limits"},"985":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-27","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/ai#common-questions","content":"Common questions"},"986":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-28","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/ai#what-can-ai-do","content":"What can AI do for a webinar?"},"987":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-29","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/ai#do-i-need-to-edit","content":"Do I still need to edit what the AI writes?"},"988":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-30","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/ai#only-some-parts","content":"Can I generate only some parts?"},"989":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-31","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/ai#how-many-credits","content":"How many credits does an AI webinar use?"},"990":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-32","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/ai#evergreen-and-simulive","content":"Does it work for evergreen and simulive webinars?"},"991":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-33","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/ai#regenerate-script","content":"Can I regenerate just the script?"},"992":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-34","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/ai#answer-questions-live","content":"Can AI answer attendee questions during a live webinar?"},"993":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-35","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/ai#simulated-chat-live","content":"Is simulated chat available on live webinars?"},"994":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-36","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/ai#good-prompt","content":"What makes a good prompt for an AI webinar?"},"995":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-37","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/ai#edit-later","content":"Can I edit an AI-built webinar later?"},"996":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-38","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/ai#related","content":"Related"},"997":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-39","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai","content":"An AI webinar starts the same way a hand-built one does: you know the topic and the offer, but the script, pages, emails and polls are still blank. AI for webinars in EasyWebinar fills that gap in two places. Before the session it drafts the whole webinar from one prompt, and during the session it can answer attendee questions from Pro onward. This page shows what each part does and what you still need to check yourself."},"998":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-40","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#at-a-glance","content":"| What the AI does                                                   | When it runs       | What you still check                                                   | Availability                            |\n| ------------------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| Drafts the script, pages, emails, polls and offers from one prompt | Before the webinar | The script first, then pricing and what's included on pages and emails | Uses credits, about 23 for a full build |","table":"table-0"},"999":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-41","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#at-a-glance","content":"| What the AI does                              | When it runs                         | What you still check           | Availability                      |\n| --------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------ | ------------------------------ | --------------------------------- |\n| Writes a simulated chat for recorded webinars | Before the webinar, played during it | The mix of simulated attendees | Beta, simulive and evergreen only |","table":"table-0"},"1000":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-42","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#at-a-glance","content":"| What the AI does                                                    | When it runs       | What you still check                 | Availability    |\n| ------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------ | ------------------------------------ | --------------- |\n| Answers attendee questions from your uploaded files, including PDFs | During the webinar | The files you give it to answer from | From Pro onward |","table":"table-0"},"1001":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-43","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#at-a-glance","content":"The short answer to \"what can AI do for my webinar\" is this: it writes the first draft of everything, and you still own the facts, the schedule and the offer."},"1002":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-44","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#what-it-is","content":"Picture a course creator who sells a self-paced course on another platform and wants a free webinar in front of it. The topic is clear, but writing a script, three pages, six emails and a set of polls takes days. An AI webinar is one where the AI writes those drafts from a description, so the work shifts from writing to reviewing."},"1003":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-45","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#what-it-is","content":"EasyWebinar is the webinar platform in front of your course, not the place the course lives. Its AI covers the parts of the webinar that sell it: the script you present, the registration and thank-you pages, the emails, the polls and the offers. You can see the whole flow in the short video below, which walks through an AI-built webinar for live and evergreen sessions."},"1004":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-46","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#what-it-is","content":"Everything the AI produces stays editable. The finished webinar behaves exactly like one you built by hand, with the same tabs and settings, so nothing locks you into the draft."},"1005":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-47","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#what-its-for","content":"It gets you from an idea to a webinar you can actually run without starting from a blank page. The AI writes the drafts, and your time goes into checking that they say what you mean."},"1006":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-48","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#how-it-helps","content":"**One prompt, five parts.** The script, pages, emails, polls and offers come from the same description, so they tell the same story."},"1007":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-49","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#how-it-helps","content":"**Pages built from the script.** The AI uses the script as source material for your pages, so the headline matches what you teach."},"1008":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-50","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#how-it-helps","content":"**Polls with a purpose.** You choose what the polls are for, such as qualifying leads, and the AI writes questions to suit."},"1009":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-51","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#how-it-helps","content":"**Help in the room.** From Pro onward, the AI answers attendee questions using files you upload."},"1010":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-52","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#without-it","content":"Every webinar starts from nothing. The script, pages and emails get written one after another, often by the same tired person, and the offer copy drifts away from what the session teaches."},"1011":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-53","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#why-buyers-care","content":"Course creators and coaches who run webinars alone feel this most. It matters when a new course launches and the webinar has to be ready before the promotion starts."},"1012":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-54","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#approach","content":"Take a typical case. A pottery teacher sells a self-paced glazing course on her course platform and wants an evergreen webinar to bring in buyers. She has the course and a price, but no script, no registration page and no follow-up emails."},"1013":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-55","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#approach","content":"The usual route is to write each piece separately, perhaps with a general AI chatbot in another browser tab. That tends to mean copying text between tools, and the pages, emails and offer can end up describing slightly different things."},"1014":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-56","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#approach","content":"What changed is that the webinar itself can now hold the description. If the same prompt feeds the script, and the script feeds the pages, the pieces stay consistent without any copying."},"1015":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-57","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#approach","content":"EasyWebinar builds the whole webinar from one description through **Create with AI**. It writes the script slide by slide, builds the pages from that script, drafts the emails, and creates polls and offers. During the session, AI Moderator answers attendee questions from uploaded context from Pro onward."},"1016":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-58","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#approach","content":"You can check this on the setup screen: five output chips, **Script**, **Landing pages**, **Emails**, **Polls** and **Offers**, sit under one prompt box. How that compares with other webinar platforms is covered in How EasyWebinar compares for AI for webinars, below."},"1017":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-59","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#before-the-webinar","content":"The step-by-step Create with AI guide covers every screen. Here is what each part gives you and what to look at."},"1018":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-60","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#script","content":"You set the number of slides and the duration, and the AI writes the script in named sections, each with timing and speaker notes. **Download PDF** lets you present from it. This is the part to read most carefully, because the pages and emails are built from it."},"1019":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-61","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#pages","content":"The AI writes your registration page, thank-you page and waiting area, using the script as its source. The pages open in the normal editor, so you can change any line. The AI landing page guide explains the editor tabs."},"1020":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-62","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#emails","content":"You get a welcome email, three reminders and two follow-ups, with merge tags already in place for dates, times and join links. They sit alongside your webinar reminder emails settings, where you can add more."},"1021":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-63","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#polls-and-offers","content":"For polls, you pick goals such as gauging interest in your offer, and the AI writes five, each with a note on where it fits. For offers, you choose a soft, balanced or direct pitch, and the AI writes the title, headline and button text. You then manage them as polls and offers like any others."},"1022":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-64","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#during-the-session","content":"Drafting is only half of it. Two features work while attendees are watching."},"1023":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-65","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#answering-questions","content":"From Pro onward, AI Moderator answers attendee questions using context you upload, including PDFs and other files. It works during live, simulive, automated and other webinar types. Upload the files that hold the answers people actually ask for, such as what the course includes. Questions you take yourself still run through questions and answers."},"1024":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-66","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#simulated-chat","content":"On a recorded webinar there is no shared conversation, and an empty chat panel looks abandoned. Chat Simulation (Beta) fills it, either with a conversation the AI generates or with messages you script yourself. It works on simulive and evergreen webinars, and the Chat Simulation (Beta) guide covers the setup."},"1025":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-67","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#what-you-review","content":"Do I still need to edit what the AI writes? Yes. The output is a draft, not a finished product, so work through this list before you publish."},"1026":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-68","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#what-you-review","content":"**Read the script before you continue.** It is much easier to fix the script than the pages and emails built from it."},"1027":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-69","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#what-you-review","content":"**Check pricing and what's included.** Read the pages and emails for the price and the contents of your offer."},"1028":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-70","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#what-you-review","content":"**Set your schedule.** The AI doesn't choose your session times."},"1029":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-71","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#what-you-review","content":"**Choose a video for recorded webinars.** Simulive and evergreen webinars still need one, uploaded through video hosting."},"1030":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-72","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#what-you-review","content":"**Check where the offer button goes.** The button sends people to the link you gave the AI, so test it once."},"1031":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-73","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#what-you-review","content":"**Look at the simulated chat cast (Beta).** A room of uniformly enthusiastic experts reads as fake, so mix beginners, a sceptic and quiet observers."},"1032":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-74","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#set-up","content":"Click **Create with AI** in the sidebar."},"1033":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-75","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#set-up","content":"Describe the webinar: who it's for, what it covers, how long it runs, the tone, and what you're selling at the end."},"1034":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-76","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#set-up","content":"Set **Type** to Live, Simulive or Evergreen before generating."},"1035":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-77","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#set-up","content":"Pick the output chips. **Script**, **Landing pages** and **Emails** are on by default; click **Polls** and **Offers** to add them."},"1036":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-78","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#set-up","content":"Click **Generate**, then work through the script, pages, emails, polls and offers in turn."},"1037":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-79","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#set-up","content":"Everything the AI drafts comes from this one prompt, so a specific description here saves editing in every later step."},"1038":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-80","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#set-up","content":"Credits show at the top right of every step. The script and pages cost 10 credits each, and emails, polls and offers cost 1 each."},"1039":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-81","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#set-up","content":"When the flow ends, you land on the finished webinar's Overview. It carries an **AI** badge in My Webinars, and from here you edit it like any other webinar."},"1040":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-82","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#set-up","content":"The AI badge marks a generated webinar, but its settings and tabs match a webinar you built by hand."},"1041":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-83","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#works-with","content":"The AI drafts land in the same places as your own work. Pages open in the normal builder, emails on the Notifications tab, and polls and offers under CTAs. That means you can follow up on attendees with your usual follow-up emails and read results in webinar analytics."},"1042":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-84","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#works-with","content":"The AI works with all three webinar types. You can create a live webinar, a simulive webinar or an evergreen webinar this way. The webinars overview explains the differences."},"1043":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-85","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#language-course","content":"A creator who sells a self-paced Italian course adds an intermediate level. She describes the new level, its audience and the price, and gets a live webinar draft with pages and emails. Her review time goes into the script and the offer copy."},"1044":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-86","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#photography-course","content":"A creator who sells a beginner photography course wants a webinar that runs without him. He sets the type to Evergreen, generates the drafts, picks his recorded video and adds a simulated chat (Beta) so the room doesn't look empty."},"1045":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-87","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#fitness-course","content":"A creator who sells a home workout course gets asked what equipment is needed in every session. On Pro, she uploads a PDF of her course details so the AI can answer those questions while she presents."},"1046":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-88","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#fitness-course","content":"The full funnel is covered in selling online courses with webinars, and the AI webinar builder overview shows the AI on the main site."},"1047":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-89","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#compare","content":"EasyWebinar's AI covers the webinar before and during the session. It drafts the script, pages, emails and polls from one prompt, writes simulated chat (Beta) for recorded webinars, and answers attendee questions from Pro onward."},"1048":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-90","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#compare","content":"AI for webinars features, from each platform's public documentation:"},"1049":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-91","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#compare","content":"| Platform        | AI drafts script, pages, emails and polls from one prompt | AI answers attendee questions in the session | AI writes simulated chat for recorded webinars |\n| --------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| **EasyWebinar** | Yes                                                       | Yes (from Pro onward)                        | Yes (Beta)                                     |","table":"table-1"},"1050":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-92","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#compare","content":"| Platform     | AI drafts script, pages, emails and polls from one prompt | AI answers attendee questions in the session | AI writes simulated chat for recorded webinars |\n| ------------ | --------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| **eWebinar** | Partly (pages, notifications and polls, separately)       | Partly (eChat, an add-on)                    | No (not supported by design)                   |","table":"table-1"},"1051":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-93","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#compare","content":"| Platform       | AI drafts script, pages, emails and polls from one prompt | AI answers attendee questions in the session | AI writes simulated chat for recorded webinars |\n| -------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| **WebinarKit** | Partly (scripts and slide decks)                          | Yes (AI Chat Responses)                      | Partly (claimed on its home page)              |","table":"table-1"},"1052":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-94","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#compare","content":"| Platform                       | AI drafts script, pages, emails and polls from one prompt | AI answers attendee questions in the session | AI writes simulated chat for recorded webinars |\n| ------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| **WebinarJam and EverWebinar** | Partly (AI Agenda Planner)                                | Not in docs                                  | Not in docs                                    |","table":"table-1"},"1053":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-95","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#compare","content":"| Platform  | AI drafts script, pages, emails and polls from one prompt | AI answers attendee questions in the session | AI writes simulated chat for recorded webinars |\n| --------- | --------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| **Demio** | Not in docs                                               | Yes (on-demand sessions)                     | Not in docs                                    |","table":"table-1"},"1054":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-96","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#compare","content":"| Platform      | AI drafts script, pages, emails and polls from one prompt | AI answers attendee questions in the session | AI writes simulated chat for recorded webinars |\n| ------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| **Livestorm** | Partly (post-event email drafts)                          | Not in docs                                  | Not in docs                                    |","table":"table-1"},"1055":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-97","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#compare","content":"*Yes: documented and built in. Partly: documented with a limit, shown in brackets. Not in docs: not found in the vendor's public documentation.*"},"1056":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-98","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#compare-stronger","content":"**One prompt for the whole webinar.** EasyWebinar drafts the script, pages, emails, polls and offers together, while eWebinar's AI works on pages and notifications one area at a time. See EasyWebinar vs eWebinar."},"1057":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-99","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#compare-stronger","content":"**Questions answered on every webinar type.** EasyWebinar's AI Moderator works on live and recorded webinars, while Demio documents its AI moderator for on-demand sessions. See EasyWebinar vs Demio."},"1058":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-100","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#compare-stronger","content":"**Drafts that go past the agenda.** EasyWebinar writes the pages, emails and polls as well as the script, while WebinarJam documents an AI Agenda Planner for the outline. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam."},"1059":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-101","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#compare-stronger","content":"**Polls written by the AI.** EasyWebinar's AI writes polls from the goals you pick, while WebinarKit's AI Creator Suite covers scripts and slide decks. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarKit."},"1060":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-102","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#compare-stronger","content":"*Competitor details checked against each vendor's public documentation on 4 November 2026. Features and plans change, so confirm with the vendor before you decide.*"},"1061":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-103","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#limits","content":"**The output is a draft.** Everything is editable, and you still review the script, prices and inclusions before publishing."},"1062":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-104","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#limits","content":"**Building uses credits.** A full build costs about 23 credits, and the script and pages are the expensive parts, as listed in limits and defaults."},"1063":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-105","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#limits","content":"**The AI doesn't set your schedule or video.** You add session times, and for simulive or evergreen webinars, a video."},"1064":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-106","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#limits","content":"**Simulated chat is for recorded webinars.** Chat Simulation (Beta) runs on simulive and evergreen webinars, with AI or manual simulation, not both."},"1065":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-107","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#limits","content":"**Answering attendee questions starts at Pro.** AI Moderator is available from Pro onward, and the pricing page lists each plan."},"1066":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-108","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#what-can-ai-do","content":"In EasyWebinar, AI drafts the script, registration and thank-you pages, emails, polls and offers from one prompt. It can write a simulated chat (Beta) for recorded webinars and, from Pro onward, answer attendee questions from your uploaded files."},"1067":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-109","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#do-i-need-to-edit","content":"Yes. The output is a draft. Read the script first, then check that the pages and emails get your price and inclusions right before you publish."},"1068":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-110","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#only-some-parts","content":"Yes. Turn off any of the five output chips before you click **Generate**. Script, Landing pages and Emails are on by default."},"1069":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-111","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#how-many-credits","content":"About 23 for all five parts. The script and pages use 10 each, and emails, polls and offers use 1 each. Your balance shows at the top right of every step."},"1070":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-112","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#evergreen-and-simulive","content":"Yes. Set **Type** before generating. For simulive and evergreen webinars, you still choose a video afterwards."},"1071":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-113","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#regenerate-script","content":"Yes. Use **Regenerate** on the script step. If you change the slides or duration first, the new script follows those settings."},"1072":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-114","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#answer-questions-live","content":"Yes, from Pro onward. AI Moderator answers attendee questions from context you upload, including PDFs and other files, on live, simulive, automated and other webinar types."},"1073":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-115","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#simulated-chat-live","content":"No. Chat Simulation (Beta) is for simulive and evergreen webinars, where there is no shared conversation. On a live webinar, attendees use live chat."},"1074":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-116","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#good-prompt","content":"Be specific about the audience, the three or four things you cover, the length, the tone and what you sell at the end. Vague prompts produce generic webinars."},"1075":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-117","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#edit-later","content":"Yes. Pages open in the normal builder, emails on the Notifications tab, and polls and offers under CTAs. You can also clone the webinar to reuse it."},"1076":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-118","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#related","content":"Create with AI, step by step"},"1077":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-119","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#related","content":"Chat Simulation (Beta)"},"1078":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-120","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#related","content":"AI-generated landing pages"},"1079":{"id":"/product-docs/ai-121","page_id":"/product-docs/ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/ai#related","content":"EasyWebinar product documentation"},"1080":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","type":"page","content":"Webinar CRM: Keep Contacts, Deals and Follow-Up Beside Webinars, or Keep Your Own","breadcrumbs":["EasyWebinar documentation","EasyCRM"],"tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/easycrm"},"1081":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-0","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm","content":"A webinar CRM holds the people your webinars produce. This guide shows how EasyCRM imports registrants and attendees, keeps leads, clients and deals, and sends broadcasts and workflows, or how to keep the CRM you already use."},"1082":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-1","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/easycrm#at-a-glance","content":"At a glance"},"1083":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-2","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/easycrm#what-it-is","content":"What a webinar CRM does here"},"1084":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-3","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/easycrm#what-you-see","content":"What you see on the dashboard"},"1085":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-4","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/easycrm#your-crm-or-ours","content":"Keep your CRM or use ours"},"1086":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-5","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/easycrm#why-it-matters","content":"Why a webinar CRM matters"},"1087":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-6","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/easycrm#what-its-for","content":"What it's for"},"1088":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-7","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/easycrm#how-it-helps","content":"How it helps"},"1089":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-8","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/easycrm#without-it","content":"What happens without it"},"1090":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-9","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/easycrm#why-buyers-care","content":"Who this matters to, and when"},"1091":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-10","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/easycrm#approach","content":"The EasyWebinar approach to webinar CRM"},"1092":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-11","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/easycrm#set-up","content":"The sections of the CRM"},"1093":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-12","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/easycrm#leads","content":"Leads: bring webinar people in"},"1094":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-13","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/easycrm#lists","content":"Lists and filters: pick who to contact"},"1095":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-14","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/easycrm#clients","content":"Clients: keep customers apart"},"1096":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-15","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/easycrm#deals","content":"Deals and pipelines: track what's open"},"1097":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-16","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/easycrm#marketing","content":"Broadcasts and workflows: send the follow-up"},"1098":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-17","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/easycrm#configurations","content":"Configurations: set up sending first"},"1099":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-18","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/easycrm#wallet","content":"Wallet: watch what sending uses"},"1100":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-19","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/easycrm#works-with","content":"What works with a webinar CRM"},"1101":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-20","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/easycrm#who-uses-it","content":"Who uses a webinar CRM"},"1102":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-21","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/easycrm#who-b2b-marketing","content":"B2B marketing teams"},"1103":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-22","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/easycrm#who-small-business","content":"Small businesses and solo operators"},"1104":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-23","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/easycrm#who-coaches","content":"Coaches and consultants"},"1105":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-24","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/easycrm#who-own-crm","content":"Teams that already have a CRM"},"1106":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-25","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/easycrm#compare","content":"How EasyWebinar compares for webinar CRM"},"1107":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-26","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/easycrm#compare-stronger","content":"Why EasyWebinar is the stronger choice for webinar CRM"},"1108":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-27","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/easycrm#limits","content":"Limits of a built-in webinar CRM"},"1109":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-28","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/easycrm#common-questions","content":"Common questions"},"1110":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-29","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/easycrm#need-separate-crm","content":"Do I need a separate CRM for my webinars?"},"1111":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-30","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/easycrm#keep-my-crm","content":"Can I keep HubSpot or ActiveCampaign?"},"1112":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-31","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/easycrm#registrants-in","content":"How do webinar registrants get into the CRM?"},"1113":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-32","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/easycrm#duplicates","content":"Will importing the same webinar twice create duplicates?"},"1114":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-33","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/easycrm#file-types","content":"What file types can I upload?"},"1115":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-34","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/easycrm#lead-vs-client","content":"What's the difference between a lead and a client?"},"1116":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-35","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/easycrm#cant-add-deal","content":"Why can't I add a deal?"},"1117":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-36","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/easycrm#broadcast-vs-workflow","content":"What's the difference between a broadcast and a workflow?"},"1118":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-37","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/easycrm#not-sending","content":"Why isn't my broadcast sending?"},"1119":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-38","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/easycrm#wallet-wrong","content":"Why does my Wallet look wrong?"},"1120":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-39","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/easycrm#open-easycrm","content":"How do I open EasyCRM?"},"1121":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-40","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/easycrm#related","content":"Related"},"1122":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-41","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm","content":"A webinar CRM is where the people your webinars produce get worked: registrants and attendees become leads, the promising ones get a deal, and follow-up goes out on time. The question most small teams ask is whether they need a separate CRM for that. With EasyWebinar you don't have to decide in one direction. It's your CRM or ours: keep HubSpot, Salesforce Pardot (Account Engagement), ActiveCampaign, Mailchimp or Kit (formerly ConvertKit), or use EasyCRM, the CRM built into EasyWebinar, natively."},"1123":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-42","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#at-a-glance","content":"|                                 |                                                                         |\n| ------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Do you need a separate CRM?** | No. EasyCRM is built in, and you can still connect your own CRM instead |","table":"table-0"},"1124":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-43","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#at-a-glance","content":"|                   |                                                                      |\n| ----------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **What it holds** | Leads, clients, deals and pipelines, lists, broadcasts and workflows |","table":"table-0"},"1125":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-44","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#at-a-glance","content":"|                               |                                                                                   |\n| ----------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **How webinar people get in** | **Import from EasyWebinar** pulls registrants and attendees across from a webinar |","table":"table-0"},"1126":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-45","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#at-a-glance","content":"|                   |                                                                |\n| ----------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Other ways in** | Upload a CSV or XLSX file, or add one person with **Add Lead** |","table":"table-0"},"1127":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-46","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#at-a-glance","content":"|                       |                                                                                      |\n| --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **Where you open it** | **EasyCRM** under **Other Products** in the EasyWebinar sidebar, with the same login |","table":"table-0"},"1128":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-47","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#at-a-glance","content":"|                           |                                                               |\n| ------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Before anything sends** | Set up email, SMS (Beta) and calling under **Configurations** |","table":"table-0"},"1129":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-48","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#at-a-glance","content":"|                              |                                                                                |\n| ---------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **What sends count against** | A monthly **Wallet** allowance of emails, SMS (Beta) messages and call minutes |","table":"table-0"},"1130":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-49","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#at-a-glance","content":"|          |                                                           |\n| -------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Plan** | EasyCRM starts at the Growth plan; check the pricing page |","table":"table-0"},"1131":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-50","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#at-a-glance","content":"|                       |                                                                 |\n| --------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Keep your own CRM** | EasyWebinar connects to fourteen integrations, EasyCRM included |","table":"table-0"},"1132":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-51","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#what-it-is","content":"Picture the morning after a webinar. You have a registrant list in one tool, an attendee list in another and a spreadsheet of who clicked the offer. Someone has to merge them before anyone gets a follow-up."},"1133":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-52","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#what-it-is","content":"EasyCRM is the CRM built into EasyWebinar for that job. Webinars generate leads, and EasyCRM is where you work them. You organise contacts, track deals, send campaigns and keep follow-up from slipping. You don't need it to run webinars. You need it when the number of people coming out of your webinars is more than a spreadsheet can handle."},"1134":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-53","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#what-it-is","content":"Leads that arrive from a webinar come in tagged with that webinar. So you can always tell which event produced which contact, months later."},"1135":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-54","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#what-you-see","content":"The dashboard is the first screen when you open EasyCRM. Four headline numbers run across the top: total leads, active clients, open deals and revenue. Each carries a comparison, such as new leads this week or deals converted this month, so you see direction as well as totals. Charts below show the revenue trend, deal outcomes and your pipeline."},"1136":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-55","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#what-you-see","content":"The dashboard is where you check whether last month's webinars turned into deals. The figures shown are sample data."},"1137":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-56","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#your-crm-or-ours","content":"If your team already runs a CRM, keep it. EasyWebinar connects to fourteen integrations, including HubSpot, ActiveCampaign, Mailchimp, Kit (formerly ConvertKit), GoHighLevel and AWeber. You map your webinar data to that CRM's fields, which is covered in connecting a CRM and mapping your webinar data. The full list is on the integrations page."},"1138":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-57","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#your-crm-or-ours","content":"EasyCRM is the option if you'd rather not run a separate tool. It suits teams that don't have a CRM yet, and it adds lead scoring and an auto-dialer beside your webinars. The webinar CRM vs traditional CRM post walks through how the two approaches differ."},"1139":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-58","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#your-crm-or-ours","content":"This EasyWebinar video shows how to connect your CRM and email tools to a webinar."},"1140":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-59","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#what-its-for","content":"A webinar CRM keeps the people a webinar produces in one place, with a next step attached. It turns \"we had a good webinar\" into deals you can count."},"1141":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-60","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#how-it-helps","content":"**Fewer hand-offs.** Registrants and attendees come across from the webinar instead of through an export and a re-upload."},"1142":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-61","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#how-it-helps","content":"**Clean lists.** Re-importing a webinar doesn't create duplicates, because the import reports who was already there."},"1143":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-62","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#how-it-helps","content":"**A visible pipeline.** Deals sit in stage columns, so you see where follow-up has stalled."},"1144":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-63","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#how-it-helps","content":"**Follow-up that runs.** Broadcasts handle one-off sends and workflows keep sending after every webinar."},"1145":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-64","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#without-it","content":"Without a CRM, webinar leads sit in exports and inboxes. Nobody owns the follow-up, so attendees and no-shows get the same message or none at all. The interest a webinar created fades before anyone acts on it."},"1146":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-65","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#why-buyers-care","content":"It matters most to small teams that sell through webinars and don't have a CRM yet. It also matters at the point a team's monthly webinars produce more contacts than a spreadsheet can track."},"1147":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-66","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#approach","content":"Take a typical case. A two-person marketing team at an office furniture supplier runs a monthly webinar for facilities managers. Each session brings a few hundred registrants. Their sales lead wants to know who attended, who asked for a quote and who should get a call."},"1148":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-67","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#approach","content":"The usual workaround is an export after every session. Someone downloads the attendee list, cleans it in a spreadsheet and uploads it to a separate CRM. That step can take an afternoon, and it tends to slip in a busy month. When it slips, the warmest leads may wait days for a reply."},"1149":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-68","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#approach","content":"The logic of the situation is simple. The webinar platform already knows who registered and who attended. Moving that data by hand adds a step every time a session ends, and every step is a chance to lose someone."},"1150":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-69","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#approach","content":"EasyWebinar puts the CRM next to the webinars. EasyCRM imports registrants and attendees with **Import from EasyWebinar** and tags each lead with its webinar. It keeps leads, clients and deals in one place, and it sends broadcasts and workflows to saved lists. A team that already has a CRM can connect it instead and skip all of this."},"1151":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-70","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#approach","content":"One fact you can check on this page: EasyCRM sits in a grid beside other webinar platforms, with a deal pipeline and email broadcasts to lists alongside the webinar data. That is covered in How EasyWebinar compares for webinar CRM, below."},"1152":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-71","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#set-up","content":"EasyCRM's sidebar lists every section. Here is what each one is for and the order most teams use them in."},"1153":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-72","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#set-up","content":"| Section       | What it's for                                                     |\n| ------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Dashboard** | Headline numbers and charts for leads, clients, deals and revenue |","table":"table-1"},"1154":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-73","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#set-up","content":"| Section   | What it's for                              |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| **Leads** | Everyone who has come in but hasn't bought |","table":"table-1"},"1155":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-74","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#set-up","content":"| Section     | What it's for                                      |\n| ----------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Clients** | Leads that converted, with their deals and revenue |","table":"table-1"},"1156":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-75","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#set-up","content":"| Section   | What it's for                           |\n| --------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| **Deals** | Opportunities moving through a pipeline |","table":"table-1"},"1157":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-76","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#set-up","content":"| Section       | What it's for                                                          |\n| ------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Marketing** | **Broadcasts** for one-off sends and workflows for automated sequences |","table":"table-1"},"1158":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-77","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#set-up","content":"| Section            | What it's for                                               |\n| ------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Configurations** | Connecting email, SMS (Beta) and calling so things can send |","table":"table-1"},"1159":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-78","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#set-up","content":"| Section    | What it's for                                                   |\n| ---------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Wallet** | Your monthly allowances for emails, SMS (Beta) and call minutes |","table":"table-1"},"1160":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-79","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#set-up","content":"| Section      | What it's for                |\n| ------------ | ---------------------------- |\n| **Settings** | Account settings for the CRM |","table":"table-1"},"1161":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-80","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#set-up","content":"A typical sequence runs like this:"},"1162":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-81","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#set-up","content":"A webinar runs and generates registrants."},"1163":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-82","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#set-up","content":"Those registrants arrive in **Leads**."},"1164":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-83","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#set-up","content":"The interesting ones get a **Deal** and move through your pipeline."},"1165":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-84","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#set-up","content":"**Broadcasts** and workflows handle the communication."},"1166":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-85","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#set-up","content":"When someone buys, they become a **Client**."},"1167":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-86","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#leads","content":"A lead is anyone who has come into your orbit but hasn't bought. The **Leads** table shows each contact's company, email, phone, tags, status and the date they arrived. There are three ways to add leads:"},"1168":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-87","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#leads","content":"**Import from EasyWebinar** brings registrants and attendees across from a webinar. This is the main route."},"1169":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-88","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#leads","content":"**Import** uploads a CSV or XLSX file in four steps: **Start**, **Upload**, **Map** and **Verify**. **Map** matches your file's columns to EasyCRM's fields."},"1170":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-89","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#leads","content":"**Add Lead** adds one person by hand, for a contact from a conversation rather than a list."},"1171":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-90","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#leads","content":"Every import is kept as an **audience** with its source, member count and status. If an import fails, open the audience's **Details**. It's usually a column that didn't map to a field."},"1172":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-91","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#leads","content":"Leads is where webinar registrants land after an import, each tagged with the webinar that produced them."},"1173":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-92","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#lists","content":"With a few hundred leads you can scroll. With a few thousand you can't. **Add Filter** narrows the table once, by status, tags, company or date created. **Add List** saves a group as a tab you can come back to and send to."},"1174":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-93","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#lists","content":"Lists are what broadcasts and workflows send to, so build them deliberately. A few patterns hold up: one list per webinar, a list for attendees and another for no-shows, and a list for people who clicked an offer. The people view in your webinar's analytics shows who watched and clicked on each session."},"1175":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-94","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#clients","content":"A client is a lead who bought. The **Clients** table adds two columns that leads don't have, **Deals** and **Revenue**. Sorting by revenue tells you who to look after. **Add Client** creates one directly, for a customer who came from somewhere other than a webinar."},"1176":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-95","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#deals","content":"A deal is a potential sale, and a pipeline is the set of stages it passes through to won or lost. Deals won't work until a pipeline exists, so create one first from the **Pipelines** tab. A webinar-led business often runs stages like New, Contacted, Demo booked, Proposal, then Won or Lost."},"1177":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-96","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#deals","content":"Deals show as cards in one column per stage. Each column shows how many deals it holds and its share of the pipeline. A column that fills up and never empties is where your process is stuck. The **Offers** tab holds the things you sell, so a deal records its value the same way every time."},"1178":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-97","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#marketing","content":"A broadcast is a one-off send to a list, such as a replay link after a webinar. You open it from **Marketing → Broadcasts**, choose the channel, pick the list, write the message, then send or schedule it. The screen shows average open and click rates beside benchmarks of 21% for opens and 2.6% for clicks."},"1179":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-98","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#marketing","content":"A workflow is an automated sequence that keeps running after you build it. You open it from **Marketing → Campaign**. A workflow stays in **Draft** until you publish it, so nothing reaches a contact while you're building. A good first workflow sends attendees one message and no-shows the replay. Our guide to webinar follow-up emails covers what to write in each."},"1180":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-99","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#marketing","content":"This EasyWebinar video shows EasyCRM follow-up that changes with what each attendee did."},"1181":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-100","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#configurations","content":"Email, SMS (Beta) and calling need setting up in **Configurations** before anything sends. That includes verifying who you send as. Nothing goes out until it's done. The steps are in email domain authentication for EasyCRM."},"1182":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-101","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#wallet","content":"Everything EasyCRM sends draws on a monthly allowance, and **Wallet** shows what's left. The Wallet screen lists 1,000 emails, 100 SMS (Beta) messages and 100 call minutes a month. The cycle resets on your signup date, not the first of the month. Workflows use more than broadcasts over time, because they keep sending every day."},"1183":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-102","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#works-with","content":"**Registration forms.** The fields on your form come across with each lead, including any custom registration fields you add."},"1184":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-103","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#works-with","content":"**Offers in the room.** People who click an offer during the webinar make your warmest list."},"1185":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-104","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#works-with","content":"**Replays.** A broadcast is a natural way to send the link to your replay page."},"1186":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-105","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#works-with","content":"**Automated webinars.** An evergreen webinar keeps producing registrants every day, so a workflow follows up without you."},"1187":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-106","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#works-with","content":"**Your own CRM.** Any of the fourteen integrations can take the webinar data instead. The CRM integration tracking post explains how teams track leads that way."},"1188":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-107","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#works-with","content":"**Team members.** Colleagues sign in with their own team member logins."},"1189":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-108","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#who-b2b-marketing","content":"A B2B marketing team runs prospect webinars and hands the warm ones to sales. It imports each session's attendees, builds a list of offer clickers and opens a deal for each one. The pipeline board then shows sales where the follow-up is stuck. The guide to webinar lead generation covers the earlier steps."},"1190":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-109","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#who-small-business","content":"A small business without a CRM can start in EasyCRM instead of buying another tool. One webinar list, one broadcast with the replay and one follow-up workflow cover most of the work."},"1191":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-110","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#who-coaches","content":"A consultant who fills a calendar from a monthly session can keep each booked call as a deal. The **Clients** table then shows what each client has been worth."},"1192":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-111","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#who-own-crm","content":"A team on HubSpot or ActiveCampaign keeps it and maps its webinar data across. It doesn't need EasyCRM at all, and nothing on this page changes how its webinars run."},"1193":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-112","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#compare","content":"EasyWebinar keeps contacts, a deal pipeline and email broadcasts beside the webinars that produce the leads. It also sends webinar data to an outside CRM when a team prefers its own. You get to choose either route without changing platforms."},"1194":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-113","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#compare","content":"Webinar CRM features, from each platform's public documentation:"},"1195":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-114","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#compare","content":"| Platform        | Contacts kept beside webinars | Deal pipeline with stages | Webinar data sent to another CRM | Email broadcasts to lists |\n| --------------- | ----------------------------- | ------------------------- | -------------------------------- | ------------------------- |\n| **EasyWebinar** | Yes                           | Yes                       | Yes (fourteen integrations)      | Yes                       |","table":"table-2"},"1196":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-115","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#compare","content":"| Platform     | Contacts kept beside webinars | Deal pipeline with stages | Webinar data sent to another CRM         | Email broadcasts to lists |\n| ------------ | ----------------------------- | ------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- | ------------------------- |\n| **eWebinar** | Not in docs                   | Not in docs               | Yes (HubSpot and MailChimp integrations) | Not in docs               |","table":"table-2"},"1197":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-116","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#compare","content":"| Platform  | Contacts kept beside webinars | Deal pipeline with stages | Webinar data sent to another CRM       | Email broadcasts to lists |\n| --------- | ----------------------------- | ------------------------- | -------------------------------------- | ------------------------- |\n| **Demio** | Not in docs                   | Not in docs               | Yes (integration to a CRM tag or list) | Not in docs               |","table":"table-2"},"1198":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-117","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#compare","content":"| Platform      | Contacts kept beside webinars | Deal pipeline with stages | Webinar data sent to another CRM         | Email broadcasts to lists |\n| ------------- | ----------------------------- | ------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- | ------------------------- |\n| **Livestorm** | Not in docs                   | Not in docs               | Yes (registrants and attendees to Brevo) | Not in docs               |","table":"table-2"},"1199":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-118","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#compare","content":"| Platform                     | Contacts kept beside webinars | Deal pipeline with stages | Webinar data sent to another CRM      | Email broadcasts to lists |\n| ---------------------------- | ----------------------------- | ------------------------- | ------------------------------------- | ------------------------- |\n| **WebinarJam + EverWebinar** | Not in docs                   | Not in docs               | Yes (autoresponder or CRM connection) | Not in docs               |","table":"table-2"},"1200":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-119","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#compare","content":"| Platform | Contacts kept beside webinars | Deal pipeline with stages | Webinar data sent to another CRM | Email broadcasts to lists |\n| -------- | ----------------------------- | ------------------------- | -------------------------------- | ------------------------- |\n| **ON24** | Not in docs                   | Not in docs               | Yes (SugarCRM integration)       | Not in docs               |","table":"table-2"},"1201":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-120","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#compare","content":"| Platform   | Contacts kept beside webinars | Deal pipeline with stages | Webinar data sent to another CRM | Email broadcasts to lists |\n| ---------- | ----------------------------- | ------------------------- | -------------------------------- | ------------------------- |\n| **Kajabi** | Yes (CRM tools for contacts)  | Not in docs               | Not in docs                      | Yes (Email Broadcasts)    |","table":"table-2"},"1202":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-121","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#compare","content":"*Yes: documented and built in. Partly: documented with a limit, shown in brackets. Not in docs: not found in the vendor's public documentation.*"},"1203":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-122","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#compare-stronger","content":"**Your CRM or ours.** eWebinar documents direct integrations with HubSpot and MailChimp. EasyWebinar connects to fourteen integrations and adds EasyCRM for teams without one. EasyWebinar vs eWebinar"},"1204":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-123","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#compare-stronger","content":"**Imports that skip duplicates.** Livestorm sends registrants and attendees to Brevo. EasyWebinar imports them into its own Leads, and a re-import reports who was already there. EasyWebinar vs Livestorm"},"1205":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-124","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#compare-stronger","content":"**Deals beside the webinar.** Kajabi offers CRM tools to track contacts. EasyCRM adds deals that move through pipeline stages, next to the webinars that produced them. EasyWebinar vs Kajabi"},"1206":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-125","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#compare-stronger","content":"**Follow-up from the same login.** WebinarJam connects an autoresponder or CRM for follow-up. EasyCRM sends broadcasts and workflows to saved lists with your EasyWebinar login. EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam"},"1207":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-126","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#compare-stronger","content":"*Competitor details checked against each vendor's public documentation on 4 November 2026. Features and plans change, so confirm with the vendor before you decide.*"},"1208":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-127","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#limits","content":"**Plan.** EasyCRM starts at the Growth plan. Live webinars are on every plan."},"1209":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-128","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#limits","content":"**Sending setup comes first.** No broadcast or workflow goes out until email, SMS (Beta) or calling is set up under **Configurations**."},"1210":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-129","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#limits","content":"**Deals need a pipeline.** The **Deals** screen stays empty of deals until you create at least one pipeline."},"1211":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-130","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#limits","content":"**A monthly allowance.** Sends draw on the **Wallet**, which resets on your signup date rather than the calendar month."},"1212":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-131","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#limits","content":"**Pardot, not Sales Cloud.** The connection for Salesforce Pardot (Account Engagement) covers that product, not Sales Cloud."},"1213":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-132","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#need-separate-crm","content":"No. EasyCRM is built into EasyWebinar from the Growth plan and holds leads, clients, deals and follow-up. If you already use a CRM, you can keep it and connect it instead."},"1214":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-133","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#keep-my-crm","content":"Yes. It's your CRM or ours. Keep HubSpot, Salesforce Pardot (Account Engagement), ActiveCampaign, Mailchimp or Kit (formerly ConvertKit), or use EasyCRM natively."},"1215":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-134","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#registrants-in","content":"Use **Import from EasyWebinar** on the **Leads** screen. It brings registrants and attendees across from a webinar, tagged with that webinar."},"1216":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-135","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#duplicates","content":"No. The import tells you how many people were new and how many were already in your leads."},"1217":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-136","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#file-types","content":"CSV or XLSX. The **Map** step matches each column in your file to the right EasyCRM field."},"1218":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-137","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#lead-vs-client","content":"A lead hasn't bought yet. A client has, and carries deals and revenue in the **Clients** table."},"1219":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-138","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#cant-add-deal","content":"Deals won't work until a pipeline exists. Create one from the **Pipelines** tab, then add deals to its stages."},"1220":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-139","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#broadcast-vs-workflow","content":"A broadcast is a one-off send to a list. A workflow is an automated sequence that keeps sending when people do something, without you being there."},"1221":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-140","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#not-sending","content":"Sending has to be set up under **Configurations** first, including verifying who you send as. Nothing goes out until that's done."},"1222":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-141","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#wallet-wrong","content":"The allowance resets on your signup date, not the first of the month. The activity log marks rows outside the current cycle as **Not counted**."},"1223":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-142","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#open-easycrm","content":"Click **EasyCRM** under **Other Products** in the EasyWebinar sidebar. The two share one login, and you can switch back from the same place."},"1224":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-143","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#related","content":"Email domain authentication for EasyCRM"},"1225":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-144","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#related","content":"Connect a CRM and map your webinar data"},"1226":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-145","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#related","content":"People view in webinar analytics"},"1227":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-146","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#related","content":"Webinar invitation emails"},"1228":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-147","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#related","content":"Webinar analytics"},"1229":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm-148","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/easycrm#related","content":"EasyWebinar product documentation"},"1230":{"id":"/product-docs/easycrm/sending-setup","page_id":"/product-docs/easycrm/sending-setup","type":"page","content":"Email Domain Authentication: Verify a Domain or Address and Choose How You Send","breadcrumbs":["EasyWebinar documentation","EasyCRM"],"tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/easycrm/sending-setup"},"123