 the campaign on the registration form with UTM parameters, see it beside attendance in **People**, and send attendees and no-shows their own follow-ups."},"3369":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-56","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#at-a-glance","content":"| Topic       | In short                                                                                    |\n| ----------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **The job** | Capture each registrant, record the campaign that sent them, and follow up by what they did |","table":"table-0"},"3370":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-57","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#at-a-glance","content":"| Topic            | In short                                                                                      |\n| ---------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Who it's for** | B2B marketers and demand generation leads who run webinars and report on the leads they bring |","table":"table-0"},"3371":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-58","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#at-a-glance","content":"| Topic       | In short                                                                                                         |\n| ----------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Capture** | The form collects **Full name** and **Email**, plus a **Phone** field and your own custom fields if you add them |","table":"table-0"},"3372":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-59","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#at-a-glance","content":"| Topic      | In short                                                                                          |\n| ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Source** | Turn on **UTM Params** on the form, and each registration records the campaign that brought it in |","table":"table-0"},"3373":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-60","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#at-a-glance","content":"| Topic                | In short                                                                                                 |\n| -------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Where you see it** | **People**, filtered by **Source & UTM**, beside each person's status, watch percentage and offer clicks |","table":"table-0"},"3374":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-61","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#at-a-glance","content":"| Topic         | In short                                                                                                                             |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **Follow-up** | **Webinar Follow-ups** go to registrants, attendees or no-shows; **Attendee Action Follow-ups** react to engagement and offer clicks |","table":"table-0"},"3375":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-62","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#at-a-glance","content":"| Topic        | In short                                                                               |\n| ------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Your CRM** | Integrations are set per webinar and sync registrants and attendees as separate events |","table":"table-0"},"3376":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-63","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#at-a-glance","content":"| Topic             | In short                     |\n| ----------------- | ---------------------------- |\n| **Webinar types** | Live, simulive and evergreen |","table":"table-0"},"3377":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-64","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#at-a-glance","content":"You can keep the tools you already run. Keep HubSpot, Salesforce Pardot (Account Engagement), ActiveCampaign, Mailchimp or Kit (formerly ConvertKit), or use EasyCRM natively: your CRM or ours, both are supported. Connecting a CRM and mapping your webinar data covers the set-up field by field."},"3378":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-65","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#where-it-fits","content":"Picture the week after a webinar. Your report shows 450 registrations, and someone in sales asks which of them are worth a call and where they came from. Webinar lead generation answers that question: the form captures the person, a campaign tag records the source, and attendance decides the follow-up."},"3379":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-66","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#fits-what-its-for","content":"It turns a webinar from a one-off event into a lead source you can measure. Each registrant arrives with a name, an email and the campaign that sent them. After the session you know who attended, who missed it and who clicked your offer."},"3380":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-67","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#fits-how-it-helps","content":"**Budget goes to channels that fill the room.** You compare campaigns on attendance, not just on sign-ups."},"3381":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-68","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#fits-how-it-helps","content":"**Sales calls the right people first.** Watch percentage and offer clicks separate the interested from the curious."},"3382":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-69","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#fits-how-it-helps","content":"**No-shows still become leads.** They registered, so they get the replay and a second chance."},"3383":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-70","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#fits-how-it-helps","content":"**Your CRM stays the record.** Registrants and attendees sync as separate events, so each group gets its own tag."},"3384":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-71","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#fits-without-it","content":"Without source tracking you'll know how many people registered, but not which ad, email or post sent them. Budget then follows registration counts, and a channel whose sign-ups never attend can look like the winner. No-shows sit in a list that nobody writes to."},"3385":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-72","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#fits-why","content":"It matters most to whoever owns the pipeline number. A demand generation lead has to show which webinars produce leads, and that question comes up whenever next quarter's budget is set. It comes up again each time a new channel is tested."},"3386":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-73","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#approach","content":"Take a typical case. A three-person demand generation team at a freight software company runs a live webinar each quarter for warehouse operations managers. It promotes each session through a paid LinkedIn ad, a partner's newsletter and its own email list. Registrations look healthy, but nobody can say which channel sent the people who stayed to the end."},"3387":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-74","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#approach","content":"The usual workaround is a spreadsheet. Someone exports the registrant list, exports attendance after the session and matches the two by email address. That can take an afternoon, and without a campaign tag on each registration it may still not show the source. Budget then tends to follow whichever channel produced the most sign-ups."},"3388":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-75","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#approach","content":"That measure misses the point of a webinar. A registration that never turns up gives sales nothing to follow up. A smaller channel, meanwhile, can send people who watch most of the session and click the offer. The useful question is which campaign produced attendees and interest, not just form fills."},"3389":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-76","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#approach","content":"EasyWebinar records the campaign on the registration itself when **UTM Params** is on. It keeps that campaign next to each person's status, watch percentage and offer clicks, and it sends follow-ups to attendees and no-shows separately. Its integrations pass each group to your CRM or email tool as its own event, so tagging happens without an export."},"3390":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-77","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#approach","content":"The **People** view shows this in practice. It lists every registrant and attendee across all your webinars, and its **Source & UTM** filter shows the campaign behind each one. How other webinar platforms record registrant source is covered in How EasyWebinar compares for generating leads with webinars, below."},"3391":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-78","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#how-sources-are-traced","content":"There are three common ways to learn where a registrant came from. Each one catches something the others miss, so most teams combine two of them."},"3392":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-79","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#ask-on-the-form","content":"A question such as \"How did you hear about us?\" is simply a custom field on the form. It catches sources that no link can tag, like a colleague forwarding the invitation or a mention at an event. It misses precision, because the answer depends on memory and on the options you offer."},"3393":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-80","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#utm-links","content":"UTM parameters are short tags added to the end of a link. Google's guidance is to always use utm_source, utm_medium and utm_campaign: the referrer, the marketing medium and the campaign name. Every click on a tagged link carries its source along, so the record doesn't rely on anyone's memory. It misses people who reach the page through a plain link, such as one copied into a chat."},"3394":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-81","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#ad-pixels","content":"An ad platform's pixel records who saw your registration page and who reached the thank-you page. The thank-you page only loads after someone registers, which makes it a reliable conversion signal. This catches which ads converted, and it lets you retarget people who looked and didn't sign up. It misses everything after registration, because the data sits in the ad platform rather than beside attendance."},"3395":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-82","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#confirmed-in-easywebinar","content":"EasyWebinar supports all three. The form takes your own custom fields, **UTM Params** records the campaign on each registration, and the **Tracking Code** settings hold pixels and analytics tags for five webinar pages. Only UTM capture puts the source inside EasyWebinar, where you can read it against real attendance and watch time rather than clicks."},"3396":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-83","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#tag-links","content":"Decide your tags before the first link goes out, because the campaign is recorded at the moment someone registers. Write the values down in one place and reuse the pattern for every webinar."},"3397":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-84","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#tag-links","content":"| Channel          | utm_source | utm_medium  | utm_campaign         |\n| ---------------- | ---------- | ----------- | -------------------- |\n| Paid LinkedIn ad | linkedin   | paid-social | q1-warehouse-webinar |","table":"table-1"},"3398":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-85","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#tag-links","content":"| Channel            | utm_source         | utm_medium | utm_campaign         |\n| ------------------ | ------------------ | ---------- | -------------------- |\n| Partner newsletter | partner-newsletter | email      | q1-warehouse-webinar |","table":"table-1"},"3399":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-86","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#tag-links","content":"| Channel             | utm_source | utm_medium | utm_campaign         |\n| ------------------- | ---------- | ---------- | -------------------- |\n| Your own email list | newsletter | email      | q1-warehouse-webinar |","table":"table-1"},"3400":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-87","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#tag-links","content":"| Channel               | utm_source | utm_medium | utm_campaign         |\n| --------------------- | ---------- | ---------- | -------------------- |\n| Organic LinkedIn post | linkedin   | social     | q1-warehouse-webinar |","table":"table-1"},"3401":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-88","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#tag-links","content":"These are sample tags for one webinar. The campaign value stays the same on every link, and only source and medium change by channel."},"3402":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-89","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#tag-links","content":"Three rules keep the report clean:"},"3403":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-90","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#tag-links","content":"**Use lowercase every time.** Values are case sensitive, so \"LinkedIn\" and \"linkedin\" count as two different sources."},"3404":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-91","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#tag-links","content":"**Always set source, medium and campaign.** A link missing one of them leaves a gap in every report that groups by it."},"3405":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-92","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#tag-links","content":"**Keep one name per campaign.** Use the same campaign value on every link for the webinar, and change only source and medium."},"3406":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-93","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#tag-links","content":"Build each link from your webinar's registration link and add the tags to the end. If you promote a form embedded on your own site, make one test registration through a tagged link and check that its campaign shows in **People** before launch."},"3407":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-94","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#by-hand","content":"If your webinar tool doesn't record the source, the job is still possible with a spreadsheet. It usually runs like this:"},"3408":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-95","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#by-hand","content":"List every channel you'll promote on, with the tags you'll use for each one."},"3409":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-96","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#by-hand","content":"Tag each link, and keep a copy of the full address beside its channel."},"3410":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-97","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#by-hand","content":"Read the campaign for each registration from your web analytics or form tool, and copy it into the sheet against the email address."},"3411":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-98","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#by-hand","content":"After the session, export the attendance list and match it to the sheet by email."},"3412":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-99","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#by-hand","content":"Count registrants, attendees and offer clicks for each campaign, and work out each show-up rate."},"3413":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-100","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#by-hand","content":"Split the sheet into attendees and no-shows, and send each group its own follow-up from your email tool."},"3414":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-101","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#by-hand","content":"Upload both lists to your CRM with a tag for the webinar and the source."},"3415":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-102","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#by-hand","content":"The weak point is step 4. Matching by email can break when someone registers with one address and joins with another, and the sheet is out of date by the next morning. Speed matters too: research published in 2011 found most companies weren't responding to online leads nearly fast enough. A sheet that takes an afternoon to build slows that first reply further."},"3416":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-103","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#same-job","content":"In EasyWebinar the seven steps shrink to set-up you do once per webinar. **UTM Params** records the campaign at registration, so steps 3 and 4 disappear. **People** holds every registrant with their status, watch percentage and offer clicks, and its **Source & UTM** filter does the counting in step 5. Follow-ups to attendees and no-shows send on their own, and the integration tags each group in your CRM without an export."},"3417":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-104","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#build-it","content":"Do these in order for each webinar you promote. The first three happen before any link goes out."},"3418":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-105","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#turn-on-utm","content":"Open the registration page in the page builder and select the form block. The default form collects **Full name** and **Email**, both required. On the same block you can:"},"3419":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-106","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#turn-on-utm","content":"turn on **UTM Params**, so each registration records the campaign that brought it in;"},"3420":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-107","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#turn-on-utm","content":"add a **Phone** field if sales will call;"},"3421":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-108","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#turn-on-utm","content":"add your own custom fields, such as company or job title;"},"3422":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-109","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#turn-on-utm","content":"turn on **GDPR Compliance**, which adds a consent checkbox you can word yourself and make mandatory."},"3423":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-110","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#turn-on-utm","content":"**Save** keeps your work as a draft, and **Publish** makes it public. Custom registration fields covers each option. Ask only for what your follow-up will use: UK data protection law expects personal data to be used for specified, explicit purposes, so say on the page why you want a phone number."},"3424":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-111","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#add-pixels","content":"Open the webinar, click **Settings**, then the **Tracking Code** sub-tab. Choose the page, paste your script into **Header Code** and click **Save Changes**. Put your ad pixel on both the **Registration Page** and the **Thank You Page**, and your conversion event on the **Thank You Page** only."},"3425":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-112","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#add-pixels","content":"Paste the same pixel on the Registration Page and the Thank You Page, so your ad platform sees both interest and sign-ups."},"3426":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-113","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#add-pixels","content":"Tracking code is set per page, and nothing applies until you click **Save Changes**. A Google Analytics tag goes in **Header Code** in the same way, on each page you want in your reports."},"3427":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-114","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#connect-crm","content":"Open the webinar's **Integrations** tab, find your tool under **Available integrations** and click **Connect**. You sign in to that service and allow access when it asks. Then map webinar events to tags in your CRM. **Registered**, **Attended**, **Missed**, **Left early**, **Watched full** and **Clicked offer** are the events lead follow-up usually needs."},"3428":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-115","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#connect-crm","content":"Integrations are set per webinar, so connect your CRM or email tool on every webinar you promote."},"3429":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-116","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#connect-crm","content":"Create your tags in the CRM first, then select them here. Map **Webinar Title** to a custom field so each contact shows which webinar it came from; the field has to exist in your CRM before you can map to it. The mapping guide lists all eleven events and every field."},"3430":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-117","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#connect-crm","content":"This EasyWebinar video shows how to connect your CRM and email tools to a webinar."},"3431":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-118","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#set-follow-ups","content":"Open the **Notifications** tab. Under **Webinar Follow-ups**, add one email for attendees and one for no-shows, and set the audience on each. No-shows are usually the biggest group, and the replay link is what they want. Under **Attendee Action Follow-ups**, add an email for people who clicked your offer, so they hear something different from someone who left after five minutes."},"3432":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-119","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#set-follow-ups","content":"Write and time the messages with the attendee and no-show templates. Set up the replay page before you paste its link into a follow-up."},"3433":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-120","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#filter-by-source","content":"Click **People** in the sidebar, then **Add Filter**. Choose **Source & UTM** and the campaign you want, then click **Apply Filter**. Add a **Behavior** filter for no-shows, or for high watch time plus an offer click."},"3434":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-121","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#filter-by-source","content":"Source & UTM is the filter that answers which campaign brought each registrant, once UTM Params is on."},"3435":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-122","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#filter-by-source","content":"**Export** downloads the filtered list, so filter first and then export. Each row is one person on one webinar, and the result count below the table shows how far a filter narrowed things. The People view explains every column."},"3436":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-123","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#filter-by-source","content":"This EasyWebinar video shows how to filter and export registrants in People."},"3437":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-124","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#keep-producing","content":"A webinar can keep collecting registrants long after the live date. An evergreen webinar runs continuously instead of on a fixed date, which suits a demo or an offer you run all year. On Demand, also called instant replay, lets someone watch straight after registering. The same UTM capture and follow-ups apply, and the **Type** column in People shows whether a lead came through a live, simulive or evergreen webinar."},"3438":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-125","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#keep-producing","content":"For next quarter's live session, clone this webinar and choose to copy its integration settings, so the new webinar feeds the same CRM."},"3439":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-126","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#measure-it","content":"Two measures show whether webinar lead generation is working: registration rate and show-up rate. Read both for the whole webinar first, then for each campaign."},"3440":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-127","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#two-measures","content":"Registration rate is registrants divided by visitors to the registration page. A low figure here is a page problem: the headline, the form or the promise. Show-up rate is attendees divided by registrants. A low figure there points at your reminder emails, not at the content."},"3441":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-128","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#two-measures","content":"This new webinar still shows zeros; the cards fill in as registrations arrive, and the date range covers every card on the page."},"3442":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-129","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#two-measures","content":"Open the webinar's **Analytics** tab. **Visitors**, **Registered**, **Live Attended**, **Replay Watched**, **Total Attended** and **Missed** sit along the top, and **Total Attended** splits into **Live only**, **Replay only** and **Both**. Webinar analytics explains each card."},"3443":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-130","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#two-measures","content":"This EasyWebinar video walks through a webinar's Analytics tab, including revenue."},"3444":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-131","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#per-campaign","content":"Analytics covers one webinar as a whole. For a campaign view, filter People by **Source & UTM**, then read **Status**, **Watch percentage** and **Offer clicked** for that group. Repeat for each campaign and note the counts. **Offers Performance** in Analytics adds views, clicks and purchases for each offer, with a click rate."},"3445":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-132","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#measure-limits","content":"**Visitors counts unique IPs on the landing page.** Several colleagues on one office network may count as one visitor, so treat registration rate as a guide."},"3446":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-133","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#measure-limits","content":"**Campaign figures exist only for registrations made while UTM Params was on.** Anyone who registered earlier carries no campaign."},"3447":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-134","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#measure-limits","content":"**Untagged links show no campaign.** People who arrived by a plain link sit outside every campaign filter."},"3448":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-135","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#measure-limits","content":"**The date range applies to everything on the page.** Widen it if a webinar looks emptier than you expected."},"3449":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-136","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#measure-limits","content":"**Replay views are counted separately from live attendance**, and someone who did both shows under **Both**."},"3450":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-137","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#worked-example","content":"This is an illustrative calculation with sample figures, not an EasyWebinar output. It follows the freight software team from the approach section after one quarterly webinar. The counts come from filtering People by **Source & UTM** for each campaign."},"3451":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-138","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#worked-example","content":"| Campaign (utm_source) | Registrants | Attended, live or replay | Show-up rate   | Offer clicks | Clicks per attendee |\n| --------------------- | ----------- | ------------------------ | -------------- | ------------ | ------------------- |\n| linkedin (paid ad)    | 200         | 60                       | 60 ÷ 200 = 30% | 6            | 6 ÷ 60 = 10%        |","table":"table-2"},"3452":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-139","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#worked-example","content":"| Campaign (utm_source) | Registrants | Attended, live or replay | Show-up rate   | Offer clicks | Clicks per attendee |\n| --------------------- | ----------- | ------------------------ | -------------- | ------------ | ------------------- |\n| partner-newsletter    | 100         | 45                       | 45 ÷ 100 = 45% | 9            | 9 ÷ 45 = 20%        |","table":"table-2"},"3453":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-140","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#worked-example","content":"| Campaign (utm_source) | Registrants | Attended, live or replay | Show-up rate   | Offer clicks | Clicks per attendee |\n| --------------------- | ----------- | ------------------------ | -------------- | ------------ | ------------------- |\n| newsletter (own list) | 150         | 75                       | 75 ÷ 150 = 50% | 6            | 6 ÷ 75 = 8%         |","table":"table-2"},"3454":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-141","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#worked-example","content":"| Campaign (utm_source) | Registrants | Attended, live or replay | Show-up rate        | Offer clicks | Clicks per attendee |\n| --------------------- | ----------- | ------------------------ | ------------------- | ------------ | ------------------- |\n| **Total**             | **450**     | **180**                  | **180 ÷ 450 = 40%** | **21**       | **21 ÷ 180 ≈ 12%**  |","table":"table-2"},"3455":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-142","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#worked-example","content":"The paid ad brought the most registrants but the lowest show-up rate. The partner newsletter brought half as many, yet its attendees clicked the offer at twice the paid ad's rate. The team's own list showed up best but clicked least, which suggests the offer suits new prospects more than existing contacts."},"3456":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-143","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#worked-example","content":"The follow-up lists come from the same numbers. Taking 180 attendees from 450 registrants leaves 270 no-shows, the largest single group for the replay email. The 21 people who clicked the offer are the first calls for sales."},"3457":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-144","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#what-goes-wrong","content":"**UTM Params left off.** The **Source & UTM** filter has nothing to show. Make one tagged registration of your own before launch and find it in People."},"3458":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-145","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#what-goes-wrong","content":"**Mixed capitalisation.** \"LinkedIn\" and \"linkedin\" split one channel into two. Fix the links before launch, because the report can't merge them."},"3459":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-146","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#what-goes-wrong","content":"**An integration connected on one webinar only.** Integrations are per webinar, so a new webinar sends nobody to your CRM until you connect it or clone the settings."},"3460":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-147","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#what-goes-wrong","content":"**Tags missing in the CRM.** The event mapping can only select tags that already exist there, so create them first."},"3461":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-148","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#what-goes-wrong","content":"**One follow-up for everyone.** Attendees get \"sorry you missed it\" and no-shows get \"thanks for coming\". Set the audience on each email."},"3462":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-149","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#what-goes-wrong","content":"**Exporting everything.** Cutting a full export down in a spreadsheet wastes the work the filters already do, so filter in People first."},"3463":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-150","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#works-with","content":"**Registration confirmation emails** go out immediately after someone registers, which is the first touch in the follow-up."},"3464":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-151","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#works-with","content":"**Offers** put a button in the room, and the **Offer clicked** column in People marks who used it."},"3465":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-152","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#works-with","content":"**Polls** give you another engagement signal, and the **Polls** column counts how many each person answered."},"3466":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-153","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#works-with","content":"**Simulive webinars** and **just-in-time sessions** capture registrants and their campaigns the same way."},"3467":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-154","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#works-with","content":"**EasyCRM sending setup** applies if you run your follow-up sequences in EasyCRM rather than your own CRM."},"3468":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-155","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#works-with","content":"**Team members** let colleagues in sales or operations work in the same account and read the People view."},"3469":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-156","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#who-b2b-marketing","content":"A demand generation lead tags every promotion link, then reports registrants, attendees and offer clicks per campaign after each webinar. The integration sends attendees and no-shows to the CRM with separate tags, so sales starts with the people who clicked."},"3470":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-157","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#who-saas","content":"A product team turns its standard demo into an evergreen webinar, so prospects can register any day of the week. Tags on the email and in-app links show which route brings people who watch the whole demo."},"3471":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-158","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#who-agencies","content":"An agency runs webinars for several clients from one account. Because integrations are set per webinar, each client's webinar can feed that client's own list, and a **Webinar** filter in People keeps their results apart."},"3472":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-159","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#who-small-business","content":"An owner without a CRM runs a monthly webinar and follows up from the **Notifications** tab alone. Exporting the filtered no-show list from People gives them a call list for the following week."},"3473":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-160","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#compare","content":"EasyWebinar records the campaign on each registration and keeps it beside attendance, watch time and offer clicks for every person. It follows up attendees, no-shows and offer clickers with separate emails, and it gives each person a lead score from their engagement."},"3474":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-161","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#compare","content":"Webinar lead generation features, from each platform's public documentation:"},"3475":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-162","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#compare","content":"| Platform        | Campaign (UTM) per registrant | Separate no-show follow-up | Follow-up on an offer click | Lead score per person |\n| --------------- | ----------------------------- | -------------------------- | --------------------------- | --------------------- |\n| **EasyWebinar** | Yes                           | Yes                        | Yes                         | Yes                   |","table":"table-3"},"3476":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-163","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#compare","content":"| Platform  | Campaign (UTM) per registrant                  | Separate no-show follow-up         | Follow-up on an offer click | Lead score per person |\n| --------- | ---------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------- | --------------------------- | --------------------- |\n| **Demio** | Yes (source and UTMs captured at registration) | Yes (Replay Follow Up to No Shows) | Not in docs                 | Not in docs           |","table":"table-3"},"3477":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-164","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#compare","content":"| Platform      | Campaign (UTM) per registrant   | Separate no-show follow-up                | Follow-up on an offer click | Lead score per person |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- | --------------------------- | --------------------- |\n| **Livestorm** | Yes (UTMs read at registration) | Partly (replay link for those who missed) | Not in docs                 | Not in docs           |","table":"table-3"},"3478":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-165","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#compare","content":"| Platform                       | Campaign (UTM) per registrant | Separate no-show follow-up             | Follow-up on an offer click            | Lead score per person |\n| ------------------------------ | ----------------------------- | -------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------- | --------------------- |\n| **WebinarJam and EverWebinar** | Yes (recorded at sign-up)     | Yes (follow-ups by attendee behaviour) | Partly (filters on orders, not clicks) | Not in docs           |","table":"table-3"},"3479":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-166","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#compare","content":"| Platform     | Campaign (UTM) per registrant | Separate no-show follow-up       | Follow-up on an offer click               | Lead score per person                    |\n| ------------ | ----------------------------- | -------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| **eWebinar** | Yes (tracked per registrant)  | Yes (one audience per follow-up) | Partly (counted when tracking code fires) | Yes (engagement scores on the dashboard) |","table":"table-3"},"3480":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-167","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#compare","content":"| Platform       | Campaign (UTM) per registrant               | Separate no-show follow-up      | Follow-up on an offer click                      | Lead score per person |\n| -------------- | ------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ | --------------------- |\n| **WebinarKit** | Yes (traffic source through URL parameters) | Yes (did-not-attend follow-ups) | Partly (offer clicks tag contacts in other apps) | Not in docs           |","table":"table-3"},"3481":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-168","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#compare","content":"*Yes: documented and built in. Partly: documented with a limit, shown in brackets. Not in docs: not found in the vendor's public documentation.*"},"3482":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-169","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#compare-stronger","content":"**An email for people who clicked your offer.** EasyWebinar's **Attendee Action Follow-ups** send on an offer click, while WebinarJam's mail filters work on whether attendees ordered. EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam"},"3483":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-170","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#compare-stronger","content":"**A lead score on every person.** EasyWebinar's People view rates each registrant's engagement, such as Hot, while Demio's People section builds lists by webinar and attendance. EasyWebinar vs Demio"},"3484":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-171","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#compare-stronger","content":"**No-shows get their own email.** EasyWebinar sends a follow-up set to no-shows from the webinar's **Notifications** tab, while Livestorm's docs describe a replay link for registrants who missed the live event. EasyWebinar vs Livestorm"},"3485":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-172","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#compare-stronger","content":"**Source read against attendance.** EasyWebinar's **Source & UTM** filter sits beside status and watch percentage, while WebinarKit tracks traffic source through URL parameters you add. EasyWebinar vs WebinarKit"},"3486":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-173","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#compare-stronger","content":"*Competitor details checked against each vendor's public documentation on 4 November 2026. Features and plans change, so confirm with the vendor before you decide.*"},"3487":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-174","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#limits","content":"**Integrations are set per webinar.** Connecting one doesn't connect the rest."},"3488":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-175","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#limits","content":"**UTM filtering needs UTM capture turned on** on the registration form, and only registrations made while it was on carry a campaign."},"3489":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-176","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#limits","content":"**Analytics reports one webinar at a time.** People is the view that lists every webinar together."},"3490":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-177","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#limits","content":"**Each People row is one person on one webinar**, so someone who registers for two webinars appears twice."},"3491":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-178","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#limits","content":"**Tracking code is set per page**, and none of it applies until you click **Save Changes**."},"3492":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-179","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#limits","content":"**Visitors counts unique IPs** on the landing page, not individual people."},"3493":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-180","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#faq-generate-leads","content":"Capture each registrant on a form, record the campaign that sent them, and follow up by what they did. In EasyWebinar that means **UTM Params** on the registration form, separate follow-ups for attendees and no-shows, and an integration that tags each group in your CRM."},"3494":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-181","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#faq-which-campaign","content":"Turn on **UTM Params** on the registration form and tag every promotion link. Then open **People**, click **Add Filter** and choose **Source & UTM**. The **Webinar** column shows which webinar each person registered for."},"3495":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-182","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#faq-no-shows","content":"Send them the replay. Add a **Webinar Follow-up** with its audience set to no-shows, and include the replay link. No-shows are usually the biggest group, so this is often your largest follow-up list."},"3496":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-183","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#faq-what-are-utm","content":"They're tags added to the end of a link that say where a click came from. The core three are utm_source, utm_medium and utm_campaign. When **UTM Params** is on, EasyWebinar records the campaign with each registration."},"3497":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-184","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#faq-turn-on-late","content":"Registrations made before it was on carry no campaign, so they won't appear under any **Source & UTM** filter. Turn it on and test one tagged registration before the first link goes out."},"3498":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-185","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#faq-pixel","content":"Put it in **Header Code** on the **Registration Page** and the **Thank You Page**, under **Settings** and then **Tracking Code**. Add your conversion event on the **Thank You Page** only, because that page loads only after someone registers."},"3499":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-186","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#faq-crm","content":"Yes. HubSpot, ActiveCampaign, Mailchimp, Kit (formerly ConvertKit), Keap and GoHighLevel are among the tools on a webinar's **Integrations** tab, and EasyWebinar also integrates with Salesforce Pardot (Account Engagement). Registrants and attendees sync as separate events."},"3500":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-187","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#faq-every-webinar","content":"Yes. Integrations are set per webinar, so one webinar can feed a different list from another. When you clone a webinar, you can choose to copy its integration settings."},"3501":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-188","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#faq-interested","content":"In **People**, filter by **Behavior** for high watch time plus an offer click. Those people stayed and clicked but didn't buy, which makes them a strong list for a personal follow-up."},"3502":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-189","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#faq-lead-score","content":"It's a rating of how engaged someone was, based on attendance, watch time and interaction, for example Hot. Sorting by it is a quick way to work through a long list of registrants."},"3503":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-190","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#faq-evergreen","content":"Yes. An evergreen webinar runs continuously instead of on a fixed date, so people keep registering. On Demand lets them watch straight after registering, and the same UTM capture and follow-ups apply."},"3504":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-191","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#faq-export","content":"Yes. **Export** in People downloads the filtered list, so filter first. It's the way to hand a segment to a colleague or load it into a tool you haven't connected."},"3505":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-192","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#faq-easycrm","content":"No. EasyCRM is for managing the people your webinars produce if you don't have a CRM. If you already have one, keep it and connect it through **Integrations**."},"3506":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-193","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#faq-extra-fields","content":"Yes. Select the form block and add the **Phone** field, plus your own custom fields for anything else. Ask only for what your follow-up will actually use."},"3507":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-194","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#further-reading","content":"URL builders: Collect campaign data with custom URLs, Google Analytics Help: what each UTM parameter means, and why consistent lowercase values matter."},"3508":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-195","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#further-reading","content":"The Short Life of Online Sales Leads, Harvard Business Review, March 2011: the case for replying to online leads quickly."},"3509":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-196","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#further-reading","content":"The UK's data protection legislation, GOV.UK: the principles that apply to the personal details you collect at registration."},"3510":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-197","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#related","content":"Webinar lead generation on easywebinar.com: the overview of running webinars to bring in leads."},"3511":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-198","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#related","content":"Webinar follow-up emails: what to send attendees and no-shows, and when to send it."},"3512":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-199","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#related","content":"People: every registrant across your webinars, with filters by behaviour and source."},"3513":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation-200","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-demand-generation#related","content":"*Updated 4 November 2026: first published, with the source-tracking methods, a UTM naming table, the manual method, a measurement guide and a worked example.*"},"3514":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-follow-up-emails","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-follow-up-emails","type":"page","content":"Webinar Follow Up Email: What to Send Attendees and No-Shows, and When to Send It","breadcrumbs":["EasyWebinar documentation","Use cases"],"tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-follow-up-emails"},"3515":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-follow-up-emails-0","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-follow-up-emails","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-follow-up-emails","content":"Not sure what to send after a webinar ends? A webinar follow up email has to fit what each person did, so this guide gives real templates for attendees and no-shows, says when to send each one and how to schedule them per webinar, so every registrant gets the right next step."},"3516":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-follow-up-emails-1","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-follow-up-emails","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-follow-up-emails#at-a-glance","content":"At a glance"},"3517":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-follow-up-emails-2","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-follow-up-emails","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-follow-up-emails#where-it-fits","content":"Where webinar follow-up emails fit"},"3518":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-follow-up-emails-3","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-follow-up-emails","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-follow-up-emails#fits-what-its-for","content":"What they're for"},"3519":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-follow-up-emails-4","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-follow-up-emails","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-follow-up-emails#fits-how-it-helps","content":"How they help"},"3520":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-follow-up-emails-5","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-follow-up-emails","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-follow-up-emails#fits-without-it","content":"What happens without them"},"3521":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-follow-up-emails-6","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-follow-up-emails","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-follow-up-emails#fits-why","content":"Why course creators and marketers care"},"3522":{"id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-follow-up-emails-7","page_id":"/product-docs/use-cases/webinar-follow-up-emails","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-d