time-52","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#at-a-glance","content":"|                   |                                                              |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **Combines with** | **On Demand** and **Recurring Schedule** on the same webinar |","table":"table-0"},"4953":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-53","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#at-a-glance","content":"|                 |     |\n| --------------- | --- |\n| **Also called** | JIT |","table":"table-0"},"4954":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-54","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#what-it-is","content":"A conventional webinar session sits at a time you chose in advance. A just-in-time session is generated around the person registering: EasyWebinar offers them a session that begins shortly, on a cycle set by the **Interval**."},"4955":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-55","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#what-it-is","content":"Someone who arrives at your page at 2:07 can be watching by 2:15, instead of waiting until tomorrow. The recording is the same one your other evergreen sessions play; only the start time changes."},"4956":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-56","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#what-it-is","content":"Just-in-time is one of three ways an evergreen webinar can be watched:"},"4957":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-57","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#what-it-is","content":"| Option                        | When the registrant watches     | Timezone                  |\n| ----------------------------- | ------------------------------- | ------------------------- |\n| **Just-in-time Registration** | A few minutes after registering | The attendee's local time |","table":"table-1"},"4958":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-58","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#what-it-is","content":"| Option        | When the registrant watches  | Timezone                   |\n| ------------- | ---------------------------- | -------------------------- |\n| **On Demand** | Immediately, with no session | Not tied to a session time |","table":"table-1"},"4959":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-59","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#what-it-is","content":"| Option                 | When the registrant watches  | Timezone               |\n| ---------------------- | ---------------------------- | ---------------------- |\n| **Recurring Schedule** | At set daily or weekly times | The webinar's timezone |","table":"table-1"},"4960":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-60","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#what-it-is","content":"You can run all three together, and the registration page offers each as a choice."},"4961":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-61","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#what-its-for","content":"Just-in-time is for evergreen webinars that sit inside a funnel. A visitor reaches your registration page from an ad, an email or a demo button on your website. They are interested now, so the next session should be minutes away."},"4962":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-62","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#how-it-helps","content":"**No long wait.** A session is always a few minutes away, so nobody has to plan a return visit."},"4963":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-63","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#how-it-helps","content":"**Interest is still fresh.** The person has just chosen to watch, and a short **Interval** lets them do it while that holds."},"4964":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-64","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#how-it-helps","content":"**Each attendee's own clock.** Sessions follow the attendee's local time, so you don't have to pick slots region by region."},"4965":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-65","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#how-it-helps","content":"**A real start time.** Unlike **On Demand**, there is still a session to turn up for, which keeps an event feel."},"4966":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-66","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#without-it","content":"With only set daily or weekly times, someone who arrives just after a session starts must wait for the next slot. That slot can be hours or a day away. The gap between interest and watching is where people disappear. Many who close the tab meaning to return never do."},"4967":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-67","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#why-buyers-care","content":"Just-in-time matters most to teams whose visitors arrive all day, from paid ads or a busy website. It matters when you judge an evergreen webinar by how many registrants watch, not only by how many sign up."},"4968":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-68","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#approach","content":"Take a typical case. A small skincare brand sells online with a team of four, and most new visitors arrive from social ads. It has made a 20-minute recorded webinar that walks through a morning and evening routine. The goal is to turn ad clicks into first orders."},"4969":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-69","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#approach","content":"A common setup is one fixed showing each evening, so the team can promote a single time. That probably suits people who plan ahead. Shoppers who click an ad at lunchtime, though, may face a wait of several hours. Many are likely to forget, and the ad spend that brought them is partly wasted."},"4970":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-70","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#approach","content":"The routine itself is not the problem. What matters is the time between the click and the first minute of the video. Ad traffic arrives all day and from more than one country, so any single fixed time is wrong for most visitors."},"4971":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-71","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#approach","content":"EasyWebinar handles this on the schedule step of an evergreen webinar. The brand switches on **Just-in-time Registration** and picks a 15-minute **Interval**, so a session is never far away. **Exclude specific time** keeps chosen hours clear, and each session runs in the shopper's own local time. **On Demand** can sit alongside it for anyone who wants to start straight away."},"4972":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-72","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#approach","content":"The screenshot under Set it up shows the **Just-in-time Registration** switch at the top of the schedule step, above **On Demand** and **Recurring Schedule**. How other platforms schedule sessions that start soon after registration is covered in How just-in-time compares, below."},"4973":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-73","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#set-up-new","content":"On **My Webinars**, click **Create a Webinar**, then **Create Manually**."},"4974":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-74","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#set-up-new","content":"Name the webinar, choose **Evergreen Webinar** and click **Continue to Schedule**."},"4975":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-75","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#set-up-new","content":"Switch on **Just-in-time Registration**."},"4976":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-76","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#set-up-new","content":"Choose an **Interval**: 2, 15, 30, 45 or 60 minutes."},"4977":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-77","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#set-up-new","content":"Set **Exclude specific time** if there are hours when no session should start."},"4978":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-78","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#set-up-new","content":"Set up any other options you want alongside it: **On Demand**, **Recurring Schedule**, **Availability** and **Schedule Preferences**."},"4979":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-79","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#set-up-new","content":"Click **Continue to Pricing** and finish the remaining steps."},"4980":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-80","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#set-up-new","content":"*1 Just-in-time Registration · 2 On Demand · 3 Recurring Schedule · 4 Availability · 5 Schedule Preferences.*"},"4981":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-81","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#set-up-new","content":"The full walkthrough, including pricing, video selection and templates, is in Create an evergreen webinar."},"4982":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-82","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#set-up-existing","content":"Open the webinar's **Overview** tab and use the options menu on the **Scheduling Options** panel. That menu changes the schedule for the whole webinar rather than for a single session."},"4983":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-83","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#settings","content":"| Setting                       | Options   | What it controls                                                |\n| ----------------------------- | --------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Just-in-time Registration** | On or off | Whether the registration page offers a session starting shortly |","table":"table-2"},"4984":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-84","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#settings","content":"| Setting      | Options                     | What it controls                           |\n| ------------ | --------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| **Interval** | 2, 15, 30, 45 or 60 minutes | How often just-in-time sessions come round |","table":"table-2"},"4985":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-85","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#settings","content":"| Setting                   | Options                   | What it controls                         |\n| ------------------------- | ------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| **Exclude specific time** | Hours you want kept clear | Hours kept free of just-in-time sessions |","table":"table-2"},"4986":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-86","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#settings","content":"| Setting                  | Options                   | What it controls                                                                                             |\n| ------------------------ | ------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **Schedule Preferences** | Depends on what's enabled | How many choices registrants see; with On Demand also on, it reads **Display Just-in-time & Instant-replay** |","table":"table-2"},"4987":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-87","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#choosing-an-interval","content":"Shorter intervals mean less waiting. The interval sets how often a new just-in-time session comes round, so it also sets the longest a new registrant waits."},"4988":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-88","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#choosing-an-interval","content":"Two minutes is also the setting to use when you want to check the webinar yourself, because a session starts almost as soon as you register. The steps are in Test a just-in-time session, below."},"4989":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-89","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#timezones","content":"Just-in-time is the only kind of session in EasyWebinar that follows each attendee's own local time. Everything else runs in the webinar's timezone:"},"4990":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-90","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#timezones","content":"| Session                                     | Runs in                   |\n| ------------------------------------------- | ------------------------- |\n| Just-in-time sessions on evergreen webinars | The attendee's local time |","table":"table-3"},"4991":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-91","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#timezones","content":"| Session                                      | Runs in                |\n| -------------------------------------------- | ---------------------- |\n| Recurring daily or weekly evergreen sessions | The webinar's timezone |","table":"table-3"},"4992":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-92","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#timezones","content":"| Session           | Runs in                |\n| ----------------- | ---------------------- |\n| Simulive sessions | The webinar's timezone |","table":"table-3"},"4993":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-93","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#timezones","content":"| Session       | Runs in                |\n| ------------- | ---------------------- |\n| Live sessions | The webinar's timezone |","table":"table-3"},"4994":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-94","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#timezones","content":"When just-in-time is on, the **Scheduling Options** panel on the Overview tab shows the timezone as **Attendee's local timezone**."},"4995":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-95","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#timezones","content":"*1 Scheduling Options · 2 Sessions.*"},"4996":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-96","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#timezones","content":"On the schedule step, EasyWebinar shows a message saying attendees will see times in their local time based on the selected timezone. On an evergreen webinar, that's true of just-in-time sessions only. Recurring daily and weekly sessions run at the times you set in the webinar's timezone."},"4997":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-97","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#test-it","content":"A recorded webinar has no live room for you to enter, so you check it by joining a running session. The quickest way to get one is to register yourself."},"4998":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-98","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#test-it","content":"Set the **Interval** to 2 minutes, the shortest option."},"4999":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-99","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#test-it","content":"Open your registration page link and register as an attendee."},"5000":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-100","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#test-it","content":"On the webinar's **Overview**, open the **Live** tab in the **Sessions** panel. A session on air appears there marked *Live now*, with **Enter room**."},"5001":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-101","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#test-it","content":"Join as an attendee to see what your audience sees."},"5002":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-102","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#test-it","content":"Set the interval back to your chosen value once you're done."},"5003":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-103","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#with-on-demand","content":"**On Demand** lets registrants watch immediately, with no session at all. Pair it with just-in-time and registrants choose between \"now\" and \"in a few minutes\". The On Demand (instant replay) option has its own page."},"5004":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-104","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#with-recurring","content":"A daily or weekly **Recurring Schedule** can run alongside just-in-time, for registrants who prefer to book a set time. Those sessions use the webinar's timezone."},"5005":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-105","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#with-sessions","content":"Evergreen webinars have a **Live** tab in the Sessions panel, alongside **Upcoming**, **Past** and **Cancelled**, showing sessions currently on air. The webinar Overview tab explains the rest of that screen."},"5006":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-106","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#with-chat-simulation","content":"Just-in-time attendees arrive at different moments, so there's no shared conversation to join. **Chat Simulation** on the **Engagement** tab fills the chat with an AI-generated or CSV-scripted conversation timed against the video. Chat simulation covers both methods."},"5007":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-107","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#with-ai-moderator","content":"The **AI Moderator**, in Beta, answers attendee questions from documents you upload and keeps the chat civil. On an automated webinar running at 3am, it can answer a question that would otherwise wait for someone on your team."},"5008":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-108","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#with-notifications","content":"Reminders on the **Notifications** tab are timed relative to the webinar, not to a fixed clock time, so they work with evergreen schedules. Set them up in reminder emails and confirmation emails."},"5009":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-109","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#with-analytics","content":"Polls, offers and analytics behave as on any webinar. In **People**, filter by **Webinar → Evergreen** to compare your automated funnel with your live sessions. The People view lists every registrant."},"5010":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-110","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#with-plan-usage","content":"People watching evergreen sessions, including just-in-time ones, count towards the **Automated attendees** meter on the **Plan** tab."},"5011":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-111","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#who-uses-it","content":"These are typical patterns, shown to illustrate how the setting is used."},"5012":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-112","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#saas-teams","content":"A product team links its \"watch the demo\" button to an evergreen registration page with just-in-time on a short interval. A visitor registers and is watching the recorded demo within minutes, in their own local time."},"5013":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-113","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#course-creators","content":"A creator's teaching webinar runs on just-in-time alongside a daily recurring time. New visitors from ads take the next just-in-time session; people who'd rather plan ahead book the daily slot. This pattern is part of selling online courses with webinars."},"5014":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-114","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#small-business","content":"A solo consultant can't keep a calendar of live sessions. A just-in-time evergreen webinar means an enquiry from the website can be watching the consultant's explainer within minutes, with **Exclude specific time** keeping chosen hours clear."},"5015":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-115","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#customer-success","content":"A customer success team sends new customers to an onboarding webinar with just-in-time sessions, so each customer starts onboarding in their own timezone shortly after signing up."},"5016":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-116","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#compare","content":"EasyWebinar puts just-in-time sessions, instant viewing and set daily or weekly times on one evergreen webinar. It also keeps chosen hours free of just-in-time sessions with **Exclude specific time**, and runs live webinars in the same product. EasyWebinar is the only platform in this table that does all four."},"5017":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-117","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#compare","content":"Just-in-time scheduling, from each platform's public documentation:"},"5018":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-118","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#compare","content":"| Platform        | Just-in-time sessions | Just-in-time, instant viewing and set times together | Hours kept free of just-in-time sessions | Live webinars in the same product |\n| --------------- | --------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- | --------------------------------- |\n| **EasyWebinar** | Yes                   | Yes                                                  | Yes                                      | Yes                               |","table":"table-4"},"5019":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time-119","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/automated/just-in-time#compare","content":"| Platform     | Just-in-time sessions | Just-in-time, instant viewing and set times together | Hours kept free of just-in-time 