"9596":2794,"9597":2793,"9598":2796,"9599":8042,"9600":856,"9601":2213,"9602":2212,"9603":2214,"9604":2211,"9605":8185,"9606":6347,"9607":1256,"9608":7491,"9609":2844,"9610":2853,"9611":2841,"9612":2852,"9613":4876,"9614":8180,"9615":808,"9616":622,"9617":623,"9618":1250,"9619":4538,"9620":936,"9621":86,"9622":427,"9623":9613,"9624":3396,"9625":4347,"9626":806,"9627":6329,"9628":4308,"9629":4180,"9630":4269,"9631":5697,"9632":3323,"9633":1262,"9634":1021,"9635":1000,"9636":1038,"9637":809,"9638":7748,"9639":6539,"9640":7749,"9641":646,"9642":878,"9643":602,"9644":68,"9645":9254,"9646":7743,"9647":7391,"9648":3126,"9649":7528,"9650":4970,"9651":7866,"9652":7811,"9653":6335,"9654":7659,"9655":1096,"9656":7952,"9657":8070,"9658":3090,"9659":3588,"9660":3258,"9661":3155,"9662":5059,"9663":8445,"9664":2406,"9665":2346,"9666":2459,"9667":2583,"9668":2492,"9669":1403,"9670":505,"9671":838,"9672":50,"9673":1301,"9674":1055,"9675":855,"9676":170,"9677":235,"9678":745,"9679":665,"9680":40,"9681":4346,"9682":530,"9683":8337,"9684":8338,"9685":4075,"9686":7076,"9687":8039,"9688":8339,"9689":3266,"9690":234,"9691":3324,"9692":7183,"9693":6802,"9694":6562,"9695":8400,"9696":6953,"9697":7434},"orderedDocs":[[2663,"\"Do paid attendees get the replay?\" is the question buyers ask most, so answer it on the registration page. You have three choices."],[1793,"\"Registered\" is a weak signal; **Watched full** and **Clicked offer** are strong ones. Tag them separately so your sales team works the right people first:"],[2059,"\"You can only have one event live at a time.\""],[3870,"[Outcome] in [length]: live on [day]"],[3872,"[Problem in four words]? Join me [day]"],[3944,"**A benchmark beside your rates.** EasyWebinar shows average open and click rates against 21% and 2.6%, while WebinarKit documents broadcasts to your contacts without one. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarKit."],[4683,"**A brand-new webinar shows zeros** until registrations start."],[3948,"**A broadcast is a one-off send.** For anything triggered or repeating, use an EasyCRM workflow instead."],[6405,"**A button URL is required on every offer**, paid offers included."],[6303,"**A button**, with its own size, icon, text, colours and the URL it opens."],[4375,"**A camera and a microphone are required to enter the room**, even if you turn them off once you're in."],[7296,"**A camera and microphone are needed to get past the device check,** even if you switch them off in the green room."],[7468,"**A camera and microphone are required to enter,** even if you switch them off afterwards."],[7659,"**A camera and microphone are required to enter**, even if you turn them off afterwards."],[5901,"**A chat that can be open to the room.** With **Everyone**, attendees see and reply to each other. eWebinar's help centre describes its chat as private, not public. See EasyWebinar vs eWebinar."],[5594,"**A chat the AI writes for you.** EasyWebinar's **AI Simulation** (Beta) generates chat and questions from a cast with set engagement, knowledge, language and behaviour. StealthSeminar's Chat Replay is built from messages you add or import. More detail in EasyWebinar vs StealthSeminar."],[8166,"**A closing point you control.** EasyWebinar's **Availability** setting closes the replay when you choose. Livestorm's help centre doesn't document a replay expiry setting. See EasyWebinar vs Livestorm."],[7566,"**A composed start:** you and your co-hosts get ready in private, so the audience sees the session only once it's ready."],[3281,"**A copy can change format.** EasyWebinar's clone can turn a live webinar into a simulive or evergreen one. WebinarJam's guide uses a cloned webinar to test the full experience in live conditions. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam and EverWebinar."],[8459,"**A copy of every sign-up.** EasyWebinar's **Notify admin** sends a copy of each registration to an address you choose. Demio's help centre doesn't document an admin copy of registrations, as EasyWebinar vs Demio shows."],[6214,"**A count of the questions you missed.** EasyWebinar's **Analytics** shows questions asked and answered, with a **Not Answered Rate**. Livestorm's analytics dashboard lists the number of questions. See EasyWebinar vs Livestorm."],[2235,"**A CRM beside each client's funnel:** EasyWebinar's EasyCRM adds deals and pipelines for clients without a CRM, while WebinarKit's documentation centres on custom domains across subaccounts and integrations. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarKit."],[1843,"**A CRM in the same product.** EasyCRM is EasyWebinar's own CRM and connects to a webinar like any other integration. Demio's integration guide has you connect an outside account in your User settings, and no Demio CRM is documented. See EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[1649,"**A CRM under the same login.** EasyWebinar runs workflows in EasyCRM, while Zoom passes no-shows to HubSpot workflow triggers in a separate tool. EasyWebinar vs Zoom."],[8163,"**A deadline in days or on a date.** EasyWebinar offers **Expire after days** and **Specific date**. WebinarJam's help centre sets replay access as a number of hours after the live session. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam and EverWebinar."],[6400,"**A deadline on the card itself.** EasyWebinar's **Countdown timer** is one toggle on each offer. Demio's help centre documents no countdown setting for its Featured Action call to action. More detail in EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[3102,"**A deadline on the offer itself.** EasyWebinar's offer editor has a **Countdown timer** switch. Demio's help docs describe no countdown on a Featured Action. WebinarKit's offer countdown appears on its product page, not in its help docs. See EasyWebinar vs Demio and EasyWebinar vs WebinarKit."],[5743,"**A documented offer countdown.** EasyWebinar's offer editor has a **Countdown timer** switch. Demio documents its Featured Actions, and Livestorm its in-room link promotion, without a countdown setting. See EasyWebinar vs Demio and EasyWebinar vs Livestorm."],[489,"**A final reminder fifteen minutes out.** EasyWebinar's drafts include reminders a day, an hour and fifteen minutes before, while WebinarKit's defaults are one day and 30 minutes before. More in EasyWebinar vs WebinarKit."],[4154,"**A full script, not just an agenda.** EasyWebinar writes the script slide by slide in timed sections with speaker notes, while WebinarJam's help centre describes an AI Agenda Planner that generates an agenda. EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam"],[3483,"**A lead score on every person.** EasyWebinar's People view rates each registrant's engagement, such as Hot, while Demio's People section builds lists by webinar and attendance. EasyWebinar vs Demio"],[7972,"**A library video in use** shows in the **Webinar Video** panel on that webinar's **Content** tab."],[1587,"**A list for attendees and another for no-shows**, with a different message and different timing for each."],[1588,"**A list for people who clicked an offer**, which is your warmest group."],[2708,"**A live session runs at one fixed time.** Buyers in other regions need another session added with **Add Session**."],[7970,"**A live session you recorded** appears on the **Recordings** tab after the session, named after its webinar."],[6743,"**A live webinar runs at one fixed time** in the timezone you set."],[1211,"**A monthly allowance.** Sends draw on the **Wallet**, which resets on your signup date rather than the calendar month."],[7971,"**A new document** appears on the **Files** tab with its name, upload date and page count."],[7968,"**A new upload** appears on the **Videos** tab with the **EasyWebinar** badge, and your storage figure at the top of the Library goes up."],[9680,"**A new webinar shows zeros** across all four stats until registrations start."],[3945,"**A one-click link for known contacts.** EasyWebinar's Share dialog includes a **One-Click Registration Link**, while Livestorm's invitations ask people to register and opt in. See EasyWebinar vs Livestorm."],[9493,"**A priced replay option.** EasyWebinar's **Live + Replay bundle** sells the recording as a second option with its own price. Zoom's replay access is complimentary viewing included with the ticket. WebinarNinja's help centre says multiple pricing levels aren't supported. See EasyWebinar vs Zoom and EasyWebinar vs WebinarNinja."],[6213,"**A public chat with private questions.** EasyWebinar sets chat and Q&A separately, so **Everyone** chat can run beside **Private Q&A**. eWebinar's help centre describes its chat as private, with questions answered through that chat. See EasyWebinar vs eWebinar."],[5987,"**A published state**, which decides whether the poll is live."],[5985,"**A question**, the thing you are asking."],[5677,"**A real deadline becomes visible.** Attendees see how long an offer stays open without relying on what they heard."],[2911,"**A real deadline on the offer.** EasyWebinar's offer editor has a **Countdown timer** switch. Demio's help docs describe the Featured Action without a countdown. See EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[4865,"**A real instant option.** EasyWebinar's **On Demand** starts the recording the moment someone registers. StealthSeminar's instant choice plays yesterday's session as a replay. Compare EasyWebinar vs StealthSeminar."],[4965,"**A real start time.** Unlike **On Demand**, there is still a session to turn up for, which keeps an event feel."],[9672,"**A record of called-off sessions.** EasyWebinar keeps cancelled sittings on a **Cancelled** tab so the webinar's history stays intact. WebinarJam's help centre doesn't document a list of cancelled sessions. Compare EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam and EverWebinar."],[6564,"**A recorded copy needs a video.** Simulive and evergreen webinars play a recording, chosen on the **Content** tab."],[5222,"**A recording exists only if Auto Recording was on.** Without it, you need another video for the copy."],[7108,"**A recording is required.** Every session plays the video chosen at creation or later on the **Content** tab."],[6923,"**A recording is required.** Simulive and evergreen both play a video; live webinars don't."],[4873,"**A recurring schedule runs until you stop it.** Set an **End Date**, or use **Blackout Dates** to skip days."],[7292,"**A rehearsal room inside the webinar.** EasyWebinar's green room is the full webinar room in a **Not Live** state. Demio's help centre describes a waiting room for attendees, with no presenter green room documented. More detail in EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[3660,"**A replay link that isn't live.** The link only works once the replay page is on, and the page then says it's live. Open it yourself after the session."],[8165,"**A replay page with its own pitch.** **Custom Build** gives the replay its own layout, CTAs and branding. eWebinar's help centre doesn't describe designing a separate replay page. See EasyWebinar vs eWebinar."],[3662,"**A reply line nobody reads.** People do reply to webinar emails, so set the reply-to address to an inbox someone checks."],[294,"**A script, not just an outline.** EasyWebinar writes the script in named sections with timings and speaker notes. WebinarJam's AI Agenda Planner generates a webinar agenda. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam and EverWebinar."],[8461,"**A sender name you choose.** EasyWebinar's **Sender name** can be you, your company or a client. WebinarJam shows the webinar host's full name as the sender, as EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam and EverWebinar sets out."],[1445,"**A sending identity you verify.** EasyWebinar lets you verify your own domain for sending, while Demio's technical sender address stays fixed. More in EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[113,"**A separate account for each client.** EasyWebinar's client workspaces give each client their own account that you manage, on its own plan. Demio's team article describes inviting Team Members to your one Demio account. See EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[5026,"**A session minutes away.** EasyWebinar's **Just-in-time Registration** offers a session starting shortly after someone registers. Demio's help centre and product pages don't document a just-in-time option. Compare EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[5420,"**A shared chat beside the recording.** Every EasyWebinar simulive session has one chat room that you and your moderators can answer in. ON24's Simu-live answers audience questions as text in its Q&A tool. Compare EasyWebinar vs ON24."],[5900,"**A shared room or private conversations.** EasyWebinar's **Who can see messages** offers **Everyone** or **Hosts only**. Livestorm's help centre says an enabled chat is public, so everyone in the room sees the messages. See EasyWebinar vs Livestorm."],[6886,"**A shared room.** Everyone in a session is at the same moment of the video, so chat messages make sense to all."],[9644,"**A straight route into the room.** **Enter Room** is on the same screen as the stats, so going live doesn't mean hunting for a link."],[599,"**A template is chosen for you.** You can let the AI pick one or browse the templates yourself."],[7764,"**A visible check:** the header says **Auto Recording Enabled** before you start and **Recording** once you're live."],[1143,"**A visible pipeline.** Deals sit in stage columns, so you see where follow-up has stalled."],[3946,"**A webinar platform first.** EasyWebinar's invitation leads to a live or automated webinar it runs itself, while Kajabi's email broadcasts sit inside a wider creator suite. See EasyWebinar vs Kajabi."],[5219,"**A webinar's type can't be changed in place.** The evergreen version is always a new webinar made by cloning."],[3287,"**A webinar's type is fixed.** To change it, clone the webinar and pick the new type on the copy."],[6744,"**A weekly webinar runs until you stop it**, unless you set an end date."],[8462,"**A WhatsApp welcome, in Beta.** EasyWebinar's Beta **Welcome Message** on the **Whatsapp** tab sends the moment someone registers. WebinarKit's help centre covers confirmation and reminder texts only, detailed in EasyWebinar vs WebinarKit."],[6735,"**A whole term in one schedule.** EasyWebinar's **Weekly** option sets days, an end date and blackout days at once. In Livestorm, each **Add session** click adds one session a week later. See EasyWebinar vs Livestorm."],[923,"**A written draft, not a blank template.** eWebinar documents a standard script template to start from. EasyWebinar writes the script itself from your prompt, with timing and speaker notes in every section. EasyWebinar vs eWebinar"],[8327,"**A YouTube video stays discoverable** unless you've unlisted it on YouTube."],[85,"**Access fits the job.** **Admin** suits people who handle billing and settings. **User** suits people who build and run webinars."],[6309,"**Action is one click away.** Attendees click while their interest is high, without leaving the room to look for a link."],[3250,"**Add each colleague.** Click **Settings**, then **Team**, then **Add user**. Enter their name, email and a password, and choose **Admin** or **User**."],[3229,"**Add Filter** narrows the list by **Webinar**, **Dates**, **User**, **Behavior**, **Source & UTM** or **Device & Location**. Filter first, then **Export**, so whoever runs follow-up gets just the group they need. The full filter list is on the People view."],[1170,"**Add Lead** adds one person by hand, for a contact from a conversation rather than a list."],[7990,"**Add Media** is where you choose between hosting a video on EasyWebinar and importing it from YouTube, Vimeo, Wistia or a direct MP4 link. The choice decides whether the video uses your storage. See Video hosting."],[9621,"**Add presenter** adds someone who appears on camera and presents."],[3626,"**Add the behaviour emails** if you have time. The offer-click email comes first."],[9435,"**Add the Paid Webinars add-on.** It's listed under **Settings → Plan → Add-ons** as \"Selling access to webinars, with checkout\". Charging for a webinar needs it."],[3255,"**Add the session team.** On the new webinar's Overview tab, use **Team & Moderators** to add presenters, or send guests their join links."],[1930,"**Add the video for recorded types.** EasyWebinar can host the video itself, or play one that lives on YouTube, Vimeo or Wistia."],[6857,"**Add Video** opens two routes:"],[8123,"**After the replay ends**, under **Redirects**, sends viewers on as soon as the recording finishes playing. Point it at your offer, a booking page, or the next step you want people to take. Without it, viewers aren't sent anywhere when the recording ends."],[6370,"**After the replay ends**, under Redirects, sends viewers on to your offer or booking page once the recording finishes."],[1918,"**Agencies** run webinars for several clients, each in a separate client workspace."],[4371,"**AI answers are tested in the product.** EasyWebinar's **Test Chat Moderation** opens a private conversation with its own AI moderator. eWebinar's AI moderator is configured through Chatbase, a separate service. See EasyWebinar vs eWebinar."],[5602,"**AI chat varies between sessions; a manual script doesn't.**"],[9185,"**AI drafts the whole set of pages.** **Create with AI** writes the registration, thank-you and waiting-area pages from your script, while Demio's public docs describe no AI page writing. Compare EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[5909,"**AI Moderation and Chat Simulation need Easywebinar Chat.**"],[4378,"**AI moderation needs the built-in chat.** Choosing a third-party chat tool turns it off."],[5884,"**AI Moderation**, in Beta, can answer attendee questions from documents you upload and keep the chat civil. It works with the built-in chat only, and it doesn't replace a human moderator on a live session. It is switched on from the **Chat** screen once set up in the **AI Moderation** section."],[8020,"**AI Moderator documents** are PDF, DOCX or PPTX, up to 25MB each, and the AI Moderator is in Beta."],[6411,"**AI offers use credits**: 1 credit for the offers step."],[6074,"**AI polls use credits.** Generating polls costs 1 credit within a Create with AI build."],[3030,"**AI Simulation** builds a cast of simulated attendees, each with their own engagement level, knowledge level, language and behaviour."],[5510,"**AI Simulation**: you describe a cast of attendees, and the AI generates what they say."],[9193,"**AI-written copy needs a read.** Check pricing and what's included before publishing."],[7102,"**All three ways to watch in one webinar.** EasyWebinar offers just-in-time, On Demand and set times together on one page. Livestorm says recurring events can't be set up on-demand, and Demio's public docs show no just-in-time option. See EasyWebinar vs Livestorm and EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[2074,"**Allow camera and microphone access** for EasyWebinar when your browser asks. If you blocked it earlier, change the site's camera and microphone permission in your browser settings, then reload the page."],[1394,"**Allowance.** Your **Wallet** has room for the send. A channel that runs out stops sending until the cycle resets."],[3404,"**Always set source, medium and campaign.** A link missing one of them leaves a gap in every report that groups by it."],[4687,"**An abandoned checkout isn't a registration.**"],[9500,"**An abandoned checkout isn't a registration.** Only a successful payment registers someone."],[3482,"**An email for people who clicked your offer.** EasyWebinar's **Attendee Action Follow-ups** send on an offer click, while WebinarJam's mail filters work on whether attendees ordered. EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam"],[7969,"**An imported video** appears with its platform's badge, and your storage figure doesn't change."],[3459,"**An integration connected on one webinar only.** Integrations are per webinar, so a new webinar sends nobody to your CRM until you connect it or clone the settings."],[6306,"**An internal title**, which only your team sees."],[4098,"**An offer with no bridge.** The pitch reads as a change of subject instead of the next step."],[2709,"**An open replay page is public to anyone with the link.** Use an expiry if access should end."],[6305,"**An optional countdown**, shown on the card."],[6304,"**An optional price**, or a **Free** setting."],[9511,"**Analytics → Revenue → Paid Webinar** lists every transaction with its status. The Overview tab shows the total registrants and revenue."],[3290,"**Analytics are per webinar.** You compare webinars by opening each one's **Analytics** tab. Defaults are listed in limits and defaults."],[4681,"**Analytics is per webinar.** The **People** page in the sidebar is the one that spans every webinar."],[3489,"**Analytics reports one webinar at a time.** People is the view that lists every webinar together."],[687,"**Analytics.** Each published page feeds the visitor and registration counts in the People view and the funnel."],[5402,"**Analytics**, in the same place as your other webinars."],[1065,"**Answering attendee questions starts at Pro.** AI Moderator is available from Pro onward, and the pricing page lists each plan."],[3279,"**Any staff member can present.** EasyWebinar's User role suits presenters and moderators, and guests join by link. Demio says that on Starter plans only the account owner can be added as a Host. See EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[5196,"**Anything you untick.** Items you leave out of the copy have to be set up again on the new webinar."],[1659,"**Archiving is how you stop a workflow.** It keeps the record where deleting doesn't."],[8604,"**As many reminders as your schedule needs.** EasyWebinar adds another reminder with **Create New**. Livestorm documents two reminders by default, one hour and 24 hours before, covered in EasyWebinar vs Livestorm."],[2821,"**Ask a qualifying question at registration.** Add a custom field such as \"What are you hoping to change this year?\""],[3018,"**Ask for consent.** Turn on **GDPR Compliance** to add a consent checkbox you word yourself."],[6023,"**Ask what you will use.** If an answer won't change what you say next or who you follow up with, cut the question."],[7426,"**Attendance:** the webinar's **Analytics** tab shows **Live Attended** for people who joined the broadcast. See Webinar analytics."],[3062,"**Attendee Action Follow-ups** go further: they send based on what someone did, including how engaged they were and whether they clicked your offer. Someone who clicked **Enrol now** and didn't buy gets a different email from someone who left after five minutes."],[5724,"**Attendee Action Follow-ups** on the **Notifications** tab send emails based on what someone did, including whether they clicked an offer."],[2848,"**Attendee Action Follow-ups** send based on what someone did, including how engaged they were and whether they clicked an offer. Write to clickers who didn't book with the one question that may be holding them back."],[6381,"**Attendee Action Follow-ups** send based on what someone did, including whether they clicked an offer. They let you treat someone who clicked and didn't buy differently from someone who left after five minutes."],[1966,"**Attendee zoom has a narrow scope.** It works on desktop in live-room webinars and the green room. It is off on phones, in windows narrower than 768px and in automated webinars, and recordings never include it."],[7856,"**Attendee zoom stays out.** An attendee zooming in on a shared screen or file isn't captured, because the recorder doesn't turn zoom on."],[1942,"**Attendees can zoom in.** Attendees in live-room webinars can zoom in and move around a shared screen, video or slides, up to 400%. The zoom happens only in that attendee's browser, so nobody else's view changes."],[3594,"**Attendees get a reason to act.** The thank-you repeats the idea they came for and points at your offer."],[5830,"**Attendees help each other.** In a public chat, people often answer each other's questions before you get to them."],[4377,"**Attendees on phones can't zoom in** on a shared screen or file, and nor can anyone in a browser window narrower than 768 pixels."],[2003,"**Automated attendees** counts people watching simulive and evergreen sessions."],[1633,"**Automated webinars.** An evergreen webinar brings in registrants every day, which is when follow-up has to run on its own."],[1186,"**Automated webinars.** An evergreen webinar keeps producing registrants every day, so a workflow follows up without you."],[1920,"**B2B marketing teams** send registrants, attendance and offer clicks into the CRM they already use."],[7227,"**Backstage** is the part of the room for people who are present but not presenting yet. Anyone joining as a co-host or moderator arrives backstage rather than on stage. From there you move them onto the stage when it's their turn, and back off when they've finished. This works the same before and after you go live."],[7376,"**Be signed in as a team member.** Any team member signed in to EasyWebinar can open the room. To bring in a co-presenter or moderator, see The green room and backstage."],[6826,"**Be sure about the type.** The type is fixed once the webinar exists. If you later want an evergreen or live version, you clone it."],[2864,"**Blackout Dates** stop the webinar running on days you choose, such as the week your cohort starts. The evergreen set-up guide covers availability and preferences."],[3874,"**Body:**"],[3949,"**Broadcasts send to saved lists.** Build the list before you create the broadcast."],[1423,"**Broadcasts.** A broadcast is a one-off send to a list, such as a replay link after a webinar or an offer that's about to close. Each one depends on this setup being finished."],[1165,"**Broadcasts** and workflows handle the communication."],[3380,"**Budget goes to channels that fill the room.** You compare campaigns on attendance, not just on sign-ups."],[2822,"**Build the offer.** Add one offer card whose button opens your booking page or application."],[1931,"**Build the pages.** Use the registration page builder for the registration, thank-you and replay pages."],[7379,"**Build your polls and offers.** Create polls and offers on the **CTAs** tab. You can keep an offer switched off in the list until you want it."],[3084,"**Build** the webinar with **Create with AI**, choosing the course offer category and **Balanced Approach**."],[1062,"**Building uses credits.** A full build costs about 23 credits, and the script and pages are the expensive parts, as listed in limits and defaults."],[6348,"**Button URL** is where attendees land when they click: your checkout, booking page or sales page. Write the button **Text** to match what happens next. \"Download Free Toolkit\" tells people what they'll get; \"Click here\" tells them nothing."],[2700,"**Buyers are registered the moment they pay.** EasyWebinar registers the buyer once Stripe payment goes through. WebinarJam's PayPal guide warns that people aren't registered until they complete the post-payment form. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam."],[1463,"**Call Integration** and **SMS Integration** (Beta) each have their own tab on **Configurations**, and you set them up the same way as email. Your **Wallet** meters call minutes and SMS (Beta) messages separately from your email allowance."],[1387,"**Call Integration** and **SMS Integration** (Beta) have their own tabs, and you set them up the same way as email. Skip both if your first sends are email only, and come back when you need them. Calling is connected here, and your **Wallet** meters the minutes."],[8889,"**Campaign capture is a switch on the hosted form.** EasyWebinar's **UTM Params** records the campaign behind each registration, while eWebinar describes UTM capture as a job for its widgets. More in EasyWebinar vs eWebinar."],[3446,"**Campaign figures exist only for registrations made while UTM Params was on.** Anyone who registered earlier carries no campaign."],[9676,"**Cancelled sessions stay listed.** They're kept under their own tab so the history of the webinar stays intact."],[1810,"**Change integration** swaps the connected tool. **Disconnect** removes it from the webinar."],[3725,"**Change one thing at a time.** Between webinars, keep the schedule steady while you change one email, and keep the same date range. The range applies to everything on the page, so a different one will skew the comparison."],[5605,"**Changes apply when you click Save Changes.**"],[8173,"**Changes to the page design need publishing.** Each of the five pages has its own **Publish** button."],[6521,"**Changing the type.** The type can't be edited on an existing webinar, so a copy of the right type is how you move between live, simulive and evergreen."],[8329,"**Changing the video later** doesn't affect the schedule, pages or registrations."],[7013,"**Charging for access?** Paid registration needs a connected Stripe account. See Paid webinars."],[6825,"**Charging for it?** Paid registration runs through Stripe. Leave pricing on **Free** if you aren't charging. See Paid webinars."],[6734,"**Charging is part of the builder.** Choosing **Paid** in EasyWebinar sends registrants to a Stripe checkout. Demio's help centre says it has no native paid webinar feature and points to Zapier. See EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[4845,"**Chat and Q&A.** Live chat and Q&A work as on a live webinar; on simulive you can answer while the recording plays."],[1948,"**Chat and Q&A** let the audience talk to you. You can set live chat for everyone or hosts only, and run questions and answers in public, in private or not at all."],[4846,"**Chat Simulation (Beta).** Chat Simulation (Beta), turned on in the **Engagement** tab, makes the room feel populated."],[1949,"**Chat Simulation (Beta)** adds a scripted or AI-written chat to a recorded webinar. You run simulated chat (Beta) as AI Simulation or Manual Simulation, not both."],[5198,"**Chat Simulation (Beta)** can be turned on in the Engagement tab if you want the room to feel populated."],[7112,"**Chat Simulation runs one mode at a time:** AI or manual, not both."],[6898,"**Chat Simulation**, under **Engagement**, fills the chat on simulive and evergreen webinars, either with **AI Simulation** or with a scripted CSV in **Manual Simulation**. Only one can be active at a time. See Chat simulation."],[5419,"**Chat stays on a recorded session.** EasyWebinar keeps its chat on simulive webinars, and can embed a tool such as Chatroll instead. Kajabi's chat box doesn't display with a pre-recorded webinar. Compare EasyWebinar vs Kajabi."],[7474,"**Chat, Q&A and Show Attendees are setup controls.** Set them on the webinar's tabs before you go live."],[5401,"**Chat, Q&A and the contact box**, set up on the **Engagement** tab."],[3020,"**Check it on a phone.** Use the device toggle; most registrations come from phones."],[1027,"**Check pricing and what's included.** Read the pages and emails for the price and the contents of your offer."],[5567,"**Check the preview.** It shows timestamps, names and roles as attendees will see them."],[5343,"**Check the weeks around a clock change.** In the UK, the clocks go back on 25 October 2026 and forward on 28 March 2027, according to GOV.UK. If your audience is in a country that changes on a different date, or not at all, your session can move by an hour for them."],[1030,"**Check where the offer button goes.** The button sends people to the link you gave the AI, so test it once."],[6487,"**Check you have a recording if the copy will be simulive or evergreen.** Those types play a video. A live webinar's recording is in the Library if **Auto Recording** was on when it ran."],[7377,"**Check your camera and microphone.** The room won't let you past the device check without both."],[212,"**Check your credits.** AI generation uses credits, and your balance is shown at the top right of every step. A full build costs around 23."],[3252,"**Check your seats.** The Settings overview shows how many seats you've used, such as 2 of 10."],[9469,"**Checkout abandoned** counts people who reached checkout but didn't pay. They aren't registered. It is a useful number to watch: a high count points to the price, the checkout step, or a mismatch between the registration page and what checkout shows."],[7294,"**Checks before the broadcast starts.** EasyWebinar keeps you in **Not Live** until you click **Go Live** and confirm. WebinarJam's help centre doesn't document a green room or backstage for presenters. More detail in EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam and EverWebinar."],[1029,"**Choose a video for recorded webinars.** Simulive and evergreen webinars still need one, uploaded through video hosting."],[272,"**Choose a video** for simulive and evergreen webinars, which play a recording."],[2506,"**Choose how to build it.** In **Create a Webinar**, pick **Create with AI** or **Create Manually**."],[2818,"**Choose one problem to teach.** Pick the problem your best clients had before they found you, and teach one way through it."],[6740,"**Choose Paid when you create the webinar.** If you switch an existing free webinar to paid, its registration page keeps the free form."],[9437,"**Choose Paid when you create the webinar.** The price block is added to your registration page at creation. See Choose Paid at creation below."],[3254,"**Choose the type and parts.** Pick **Live**, **Simulive** or **Evergreen**, rename the copy, tick what it should include, and click **Clone Webinar**."],[1142,"**Clean lists.** Re-importing a webinar doesn't create duplicates, because the import reports who was already there."],[4492,"**Clear all** resets every filter. The result count below the table shows how far a filter narrowed the list."],[6401,"**Clicks and purchases in one report.** **Offers Performance** lists views, clicks and purchases for each offer. WebinarJam records sales through two tracking codes that you place on your own pages. More detail in EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam and EverWebinar."],[2236,"**Client accounts without an enterprise contract:** EasyWebinar's client workspaces run on Launch, Growth, Pro or Scale, while Livestorm lists multiple workspaces as an Enterprise paid add-on. See EasyWebinar vs Livestorm."],[114,"**Client work set up for agencies.** Each EasyWebinar workspace keeps a client's webinars, registrants and settings apart. Livestorm's help centre mentions multiple workspaces only in its HubSpot connection article. See EasyWebinar vs Livestorm."],[122,"**Client workspaces are separate** from team seats; adding a workspace doesn't use a seat."],[2826,"**Clone it as evergreen.** Once the pitch works, turn the live session into one that plays on a schedule."],[9168,"**Clone Webinar** can copy registration pages into a new webinar. To try a different registration page on a webinar that's already running, clone it and change the copy."],[3090,"**Clone** the webinar as **Evergreen**, select the live recording, turn on just-in-time and **Chat Simulation**, and let it sell every day."],[2075,"**Close other apps that are using the camera**, such as another video-call tool, then reload."],[7298,"**Co-hosts and moderators arrive backstage,** never straight onto the stage."],[7464,"**Co-hosts arrive out of sight.** In EasyWebinar, co-hosts and moderators land backstage and stay unseen until you move them on stage. Demio describes presenters choosing **Go On Stage** to appear immediately, and Livestorm's public docs describe no backstage. See EasyWebinar vs Demio and EasyWebinar vs Livestorm."],[4369,"**Co-hosts can get ready unseen.** EasyWebinar's co-hosts land backstage and sort out their audio before you bring them on. Livestorm documents a lobby where guest speakers test their devices. See EasyWebinar vs Livestorm."],[1916,"**Coaches and consultants** run a free talk live, answer questions in the room and follow up the people who clicked an offer."],[3017,"**Collect what you need.** The form starts with name and email. Add a **Phone** field, or your own custom fields such as the student's current level."],[5517,"**Common questions get answered in view.** A scripted question with an `Admin` reply puts an objection and its answer in front of everyone."],[1306,"**Configurations** opens on a row of channel tabs, one for each way the CRM can reach someone:"],[7268,"**Confirm recording.** **Auto Recording Enabled** in the header means the session will be recorded; **Settings → Recording Settings** changes it."],[7014,"**Confirm the type.** A webinar's type can't be changed after creation. If you have a live webinar you want to run this way, see Clone a webinar instead."],[9436,"**Connect a Stripe account.** Payments run through Stripe. You can connect it during the pricing step or from **Integrations → Payment**."],[7381,"**Connect any streaming destinations.** If you plan to stream to YouTube or LinkedIn as well, connect them once under **Integrations → EasyCast** in the sidebar."],[1634,"**Connected CRMs.** If you keep your own CRM, webinar data mapping sends it the tags its automation needs."],[1849,"**Connecting needs an account with that service**, and you sign in to it during setup."],[8888,"**Consent can differ from one webinar to the next.** StealthSeminar's GDPR option shows one consent checkbox on all its registration forms. Compare EasyWebinar vs StealthSeminar."],[8887,"**Consent is set on the form you're editing.** EasyWebinar's **GDPR Compliance** switch sits on the form block, with your own wording. Demio adds a default GDPR checkbox through an account setting. See EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[395,"**Consistent with the webinar.** The emails draw on the same script as your pages, so the promise matches."],[9690,"**Continue to Green Room** stays greyed out until the room can see a working camera and microphone. If you see \"You can only have one event live at a time.\", another webinar is already live. The camera not detected guide covers device problems."],[9677,"**Converting to paid doesn't add a price to the registration page.** Choose **Paid** at creation instead."],[6566,"**Copies are archived, not deleted.**"],[9024,"**Copy the code from the right webinar.** The Registration Widget sits on each webinar's own **Content** tab."],[1915,"**Course creators** run the sales webinar for a course they host elsewhere, then let a recorded version sell every day."],[2820,"**Create a live webinar.** Start with a live session, because your first run is where you find what lands."],[1929,"**Create the webinar and choose its type.** Name it, pick Live, Simulive or Evergreen, then set the schedule. The live webinar setup guide walks through each step."],[9579,"**Create the webinar first.** The Overview tab belongs to a webinar that already exists. Start from Create and schedule a live webinar, Create a simulive webinar or Create an evergreen webinar."],[7017,"**Create with AI** also supports evergreen: set **Type** before generating, then choose the video afterwards. See Create with AI."],[186,"**Create with AI** builds a complete EasyWebinar webinar from a written description. In five steps it writes a slide-by-slide presentation script, fills your registration, thank-you and waiting-area pages, drafts the email sequence, and creates polls and offers. A full build takes about ten minutes and uses around 23 credits, and everything it produces opens in the normal editors so you can change it."],[3008,"**Create with AI** builds a complete webinar from a description: the presentation script, the registration, thank-you and waiting pages, the email sequence, polls and offers. It takes about ten minutes, and everything stays editable."],[6355,"**Create with AI** builds a webinar from a description, and offers are one of its five outputs. Script, Landing pages and Emails are selected by default; click the **Offers** chip to include offers."],[6033,"**Create with AI** builds a webinar from a description, and polls are one of its five outputs. Script, Landing pages and Emails are selected by default; click the **Polls** chip to include polls in the build."],[9153,"**Create with AI** can build your pages as part of a full webinar. After it writes the script, the pages step asks you to choose **AI picks for you**, which auto-selects a template, or **Choose manually** to browse."],[5721,"**Create with AI** writes offers for you. Its **Direct Pitch** positioning is \"offer-focused, repeated CTAs, strong urgency\", while **Soft Pitch** is education-focused with the offer at the end. Whichever you choose, the offers it creates are normal offers on the **CTAs** tab, so you can add a countdown to any of them."],[1763,"**Create your tags in the CRM first**, then select them in EasyWebinar."],[496,"**Credits apply.** Each AI step uses credits from your balance, shown at the top right of every step. See pricing for what each plan includes."],[299,"**Credits are spent per step.** About 23 for a full build; the script and pages are 10 each."],[884,"**Credits.** The script step uses 10 credits, and your balance shows at the top right of every step."],[8894,"**CRM fields must exist first.** Create the field in your CRM, then click **Refresh** before mapping."],[5603,"**CSV files must be UTF-8**, with commas inside messages wrapped in double quotes."],[3258,"**Custom domain (C-Name)** points your own domain at your webinar pages, so links read like webinars.yourcompany.com. Add a CNAME record with your DNS provider first, then enter the domain on your profile. Every webinar the team builds then shares the same address."],[1764,"**Custom fields must exist in your CRM** before you can map to them."],[1921,"**Customer success teams** run release briefings and training live, then keep the recording available."],[9023,"**Customise first.** Use **View & Customize** to change how the widget looks before you copy the code."],[5223,"**Daily and weekly sessions use the webinar's timezone.** Only just-in-time sessions start in each attendee's local time."],[7072,"**Days off stay off.** **Blackout Dates** stop sessions on holidays and any other days you pick."],[3723,"**Deadlines bunch the activity.** A rush just before the replay closes could come from the last call, the deadline itself or both."],[1205,"**Deals beside the webinar.** Kajabi offers CRM tools to track contacts. EasyCRM adds deals that move through pipeline stages, next to the webinars that produced them. EasyWebinar vs Kajabi"],[1210,"**Deals need a pipeline.** The **Deals** screen stays empty of deals until you create at least one pipeline."],[7011,"**Decide how people should be able to watch.** Soon after registering, straight away, at set times, or a mix. The schedule step is built around that choice."],[7271,"**Decide on camera and mic.** You can switch **Camera** and **Mic** off in the green room and still go live, for a session built on slides or video."],[214,"**Decide the webinar type.** Choose **Live**, **Simulive** or **Evergreen** before generating. A webinar's type can't be changed after it's created."],[6488,"**Decide what to leave behind.** Everything is ticked if you choose **Select everything**, but you can untick, for example, the emails if the copy needs new ones."],[6823,"**Decide where the video will live.** Uploading it means EasyWebinar hosts it for you. Importing a link means it stays on YouTube, Vimeo or Wistia. See Which video source to use, below."],[5678,"**Deciding later stops being the easy choice.** A visible time limit gives people a reason to act during the webinar."],[7301,"**Design changes apply as you make them.** Anything you change after going live is visible."],[7471,"**Design changes apply immediately,** including mid-broadcast."],[7466,"**Destinations connected once.** An EasyCast destination is connected once for the account and switched on in the room. WebinarJam has you choose the streaming service for each webinar in its configuration wizard, from YouTube Live and Facebook Live. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam and EverWebinar."],[6219,"**Disable removes Q&A for the whole session.**"],[8018,"**Don't delete a video a webinar is using.** The webinar plays it."],[5574,"**Don't impersonate real customers.** A simulated message shouldn't pass itself off as something a real customer said."],[6928,"**Don't remove a video a webinar is using.** The webinar plays it."],[2819,"**Draft the session.** Write it yourself, or generate a webinar script and edit it into your own words."],[487,"**Drafted before the webinar runs.** EasyWebinar drafts reminders and follow-ups during the build, while WebinarNinja's AI writes follow-up emails once the webinar ends. More in EasyWebinar vs WebinarNinja."],[488,"**Drafting built into the product.** EasyWebinar's AI drafts the emails itself, while Kajabi describes giving an outside AI permission to draft your emails. More in EasyWebinar vs Kajabi."],[493,"**Drafts follow the script.** The emails are built from the script, so a vague prompt or an unchecked script carries into them."],[9107,"**Drafts stay private.** **Save** keeps your work, and visitors see nothing new until you **Publish**."],[1058,"**Drafts that go past the agenda.** EasyWebinar writes the pages, emails and polls as well as the script, while WebinarJam documents an AI Agenda Planner for the outline. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam."],[1941,"**Draw on your share.** Whoever is sharing their screen or slides can draw on them, and everyone in the session sees each line as it is drawn. Only the person sharing can draw."],[7664,"**Drawing belongs to the person sharing.** Drawings disappear when the share stops, aren't in the recording, and can't be made on video shares."],[7653,"**Drawing is built in.** Hosts and co-hosts draw on their own shared screen or slides, while Demio's help centre says to share a third-party whiteboard app instead. EasyWebinar vs Demio"],[7656,"**Drawing without a separate app.** Your drawings appear on your own share for everyone, while Livestorm documents a Visme whiteboard for whiteboarding. EasyWebinar vs Livestorm"],[5221,"**Drawings are not recorded.** Marks made on a shared screen or slides won't appear in the evergreen version."],[1967,"**Drawings are shared and short-lived.** Everyone in the session sees them, and they disappear when the share stops. They are not in the recording, and you can't draw on a video share."],[7855,"**Drawings stay out.** Drawings on a shared screen or slides are removed when you stop sharing and are not in the recording."],[5195,"**Drawings.** Drawings made on a shared screen or slides are not in the recording, so the evergreen version shows the share without them."],[4964,"**Each attendee's own clock.** Sessions follow the attendee's local time, so you don't have to pick slots region by region."],[3285,"**Each member needs their own email address.**"],[3490,"**Each People row is one person on one webinar**, so someone who registers for two webinars appears twice."],[3191,"**Each person has their own login.** You can tell who did what, and more than one host can be in the live room."],[4263,"**Each person knows their part.** Co-hosts join backstage at a time you set, with their own link."],[4529,"**Each row is one person on one webinar.** Someone who registered for two webinars appears twice."],[1817,"**Each webinar feeds its own list.** Integrations are set per webinar."],[8249,"**Easy to swap.** The **Webinar Video** panel changes the video without touching the schedule, pages or registrations."],[4779,"**Easy updates.** You can swap the recording later without touching the schedule or the registrations."],[7475,"**EasyCast is for live webinars.** Simulive and evergreen webinars play a recording rather than broadcasting."],[7637,"**EasyCast:** streaming to YouTube, LinkedIn or a custom RTMP destination, from the Growth plan."],[1943,"**EasyCast** streams your live webinar to YouTube, LinkedIn or a custom RTMP destination at the same time. Use it when part of your audience watches on those channels, and keep the registration page as the place where leads are collected."],[1852,"**EasyCRM is a plan add-on**, switched on from the **Add-ons** tab under **Settings → Manage Plan**."],[1353,"**EasyCRM Mail** appears above any provider you add. It carries the **Default** badge and has no **Configure** button of its own, and a connected provider shows a **Connected** badge with its server address. You pick between them with the selector at the left of each row."],[1461,"**EasyCRM Mail** is the service listed first under **Select Email service**, marked **Default**. Unlike a provider you add, its row has no **Configure** button. The verification notice sits above the whole list, so verify your domain or address whichever service you select."],[3467,"**EasyCRM sending setup** applies if you run your follow-up sequences in EasyCRM rather than your own CRM."],[1772,"**EasyCRM** is EasyWebinar's own CRM and connects the same way. The full list, with what each connection is for, is on the integrations overview."],[5348,"**Easywebinar Chat** is the built-in panel, described on the live chat page."],[3085,"**Edit** the script and pages, add UTM capture to the form, and **Publish** the registration page."],[1311,"**Email Integration** has four parts. **Email provider** lists your services, **Reply & forwarding settings** decides where replies go, and **Analytics** sits beside those two. **Domains** is a button on the provider list."],[8589,"**Email notifications** can come across when you clone a webinar, so a reminder schedule you have tuned carries into the copy."],[3952,"**Email sends draw on your Wallet allowance**, which resets on your signup date rather than the first of the month."],[1390,"**Email service.** The service you want is selected under **Email provider**, and a provider you added shows **Connected**."],[8612,"**Email stays the main channel.** Text and WhatsApp reminders work alongside email, not instead of it."],[8464,"**Emails are set per webinar.** Each webinar has its own confirmation and its own **Email Settings**; cloning is how you carry them to a new webinar."],[202,"**Emails arrive wired up.** Merge tags are already in place, so dates, times and join links fill themselves in."],[494,"**Emails only in the build.** The AI step drafts email. SMS (Beta) messages are built from templates on the **SMS** tab instead."],[297,"**Emails ready before the event.** EasyWebinar drafts the welcome email, three reminders and two follow-ups. Livestorm's AI drafts emails from an event recording, after the event. See EasyWebinar vs Livestorm."],[4100,"**Emails that promise a different session.** Write the registration page and follow-ups from the finished outline, not the first idea."],[4848,"**Emails.** Confirmation emails and reminder emails go out for each session."],[684,"**Emails.** The AI's welcome email goes out on registration; its settings are covered in registration confirmation emails."],[902,"**Emails.** The same build drafts the welcome email, reminder emails and follow-ups, with merge tags already in place."],[457,"**Emails** is one of the output chips, selected by default with **Script** and **Landing pages**. Leave it on, then click **Generate**."],[5398,"**Emails**, including reminder emails before each session."],[5426,"**Embedded chat shows only to attendees.** Entering as an admin shows your host tools, so you check an embedded widget by joining as an attendee."],[5908,"**Embedded widgets show to attendees.** Join as an attendee to see one; the admin view shows host tools."],[7679,"**End Session** asks you to confirm, because ending disconnects everyone and nobody can rejoin. The recording then appears in your Library."],[4376,"**Ending a session can't be undone.** **End Session** disconnects everyone, and nobody can rejoin."],[7858,"**Ending is final.** **End Session** disconnects everyone and nobody can rejoin, so end only when you're done."],[7473,"**Ending is final.** **End Session** disconnects everyone, and nobody can rejoin."],[7662,"**Ending is final.** **End Session** disconnects everyone, and nobody can rejoin."],[6221,"**Ending the session is final.** **End Session** disconnects everyone and nobody can rejoin."],[7636,"**Engagement:** chat, Q&A, polls and offers, set up before the session and run in the room."],[7835,"**Evergreen and simulive webinars:** both take their content from the Library. Create a simulive webinar and Create an evergreen webinar show where you choose it."],[5031,"**Evergreen only.** Just-in-time is part of the evergreen schedule step. Live and simulive webinars use dated sessions in the webinar's timezone."],[8745,"**Evergreen only.** On Demand is set on the evergreen schedule step. Live and simulive webinars don't have it."],[5029,"**Evergreen sessions that start soon.** EasyWebinar adds just-in-time to the evergreen schedule step. Livestorm's on-demand and automation pages don't document just-in-time sessions. Compare EasyWebinar vs Livestorm."],[1552,"**Every group gets its own message.** Attendees get one follow-up and no-shows get the replay, because each list gets its own sequence."],[6402,"**Every offer measured.** EasyWebinar reports each offer separately under **Revenue by Offer**. eWebinar's help centre says only one conversion event can be tracked per eWebinar. More detail in EasyWebinar vs eWebinar."],[9494,"**Every payment in one list.** EasyWebinar's **Paid Webinar** view lists each transaction with its status. Livestorm's help pages describe a Paid column per registrant, with no revenue total for the event. See EasyWebinar vs Livestorm."],[4525,"**Every UTM value you capture.** **Source & UTM** filters the table by the campaign that brought each person. Livestorm's registrant export says utm_term and utm_content are not exported. See EasyWebinar vs Livestorm."],[5217,"**Every way to watch at once.** EasyWebinar runs just-in-time, on-demand and set times together, while Livestorm stops adding sessions once someone registers on-demand. See EasyWebinar vs Livestorm."],[6178,"**Everyone** for chat plus **Private Q&A** is a common setup: the room stays sociable, and questions reach you in an orderly queue."],[5851,"**Everyone** is the recommended setting and suits most webinars. Pick **Hosts only** for:"],[304,"**Everything is a draft.** Check pages and emails before you publish, particularly prices and inclusions."],[8247,"**Existing videos work as they are.** If the video is already on YouTube, Vimeo or Wistia, you import the link and use no storage."],[9580,"**Expect zeros on a new webinar.** The four stats stay at zero until registrations start."],[6478,"**Expected result:** a new, independent webinar of the type you picked, carrying the settings and assets you selected, with no registrants, and the original webinar exactly as it was."],[6812,"**Expected result:** a simulive webinar with its schedule, pricing and recording in place, listed on the **Simulive** tab of **My Webinars**, with a **Webinar Video** panel on its **Content** tab."],[6636,"**Expected result:** a webinar with its schedule applied, open in the registration page builder, ready for you to publish."],[7000,"**Expected result:** an evergreen webinar with its schedule, pricing and recording set, a list of upcoming sessions generated on its **Overview** tab, and a registration page ready to publish."],[9310,"**Expired Session** on the webinar's **Settings → General** tab sets where people go if their link no longer works. It's empty by default, so fill it in with a page that tells people what to do next."],[4532,"**Export respects your filters.**"],[3435,"**Export** downloads the filtered list, so filter first and then export. Each row is one person on one webinar, and the result count below the table shows how far a filter narrowed things. The People view explains every column."],[8859,"**Export** downloads the filtered list."],[3462,"**Exporting everything.** Cutting a full export down in a spreadsheet wastes the work the filters already do, so filter in People first."],[2159,"**Faster launches:** a funnel built once can be cloned for the next client or the next month."],[1141,"**Fewer hand-offs.** Registrants and attendees come across from the webinar instead of through an export and a re-upload."],[7380,"**Fill in End of Session.** On the **Settings** tab, **End of Session** is where attendees go when the stream ends. It's empty by default, which leaves attendees on a finished webinar."],[4523,"**Filters on how people watched.** EasyWebinar's **Behavior** filter covers attendance, watch time and offer clicks. WebinarJam's registrant filter covers who attended, watched the replay or made a purchase. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam and EverWebinar."],[7938,"**Find it in the sidebar.** The Library sits in the main sidebar, alongside **My Webinars**, **Create with AI** and **Integrations**. It isn't inside a single webinar, so anything you add can be reused across your webinars."],[303,"**Five polls per poll step.** Each comes with its question, options and reasoning."],[4097,"**Five teaching points in 45 minutes.** Each point gets too little time to land, and the offer comes late."],[5032,"**Fixed interval choices.** 2, 15, 30, 45 or 60 minutes."],[2507,"**Follow the guide for your format.** Use the steps to create a live webinar, create a simulive webinar or create an evergreen webinar."],[2825,"**Follow up the same day.** Send attendees and no-shows different messages, and write to offer clickers on their own."],[3088,"**Follow up** with offer-clickers through **Attendee Action Follow-ups**, and tag them in your email tool with **Clicked offer**."],[1206,"**Follow-up from the same login.** WebinarJam connects an autoresponder or CRM for follow-up. EasyCRM sends broadcasts and workflows to saved lists with your EasyWebinar login. EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam"],[1553,"**Follow-up keeps going after day one.** A nurture sequence can run over the following fortnight without another send from you."],[1814,"**Follow-up matches behaviour.** A no-show can start a replay sequence, while an offer click goes to sales."],[3712,"**Follow-Up SMS** (Beta) and the WhatsApp **Follow-Up Message** (Beta) both send after the webinar ends. They work alongside email rather than replacing it: email carries the detail and the text carries the nudge. You'll need people's numbers, so the **Phone** field has to be on your registration form."],[1144,"**Follow-up that runs.** Broadcasts handle one-off sends and workflows keep sending after every webinar."],[3266,"**Follow-up.** Email notifications come across in a clone, and webinar follow-up emails covers what to send."],[3745,"**Follow-ups on recorded webinars too.** EasyWebinar drafts the same follow-ups for live, simulive and evergreen builds. Demio's best-practices guide says its Replay Follow-Up isn't available on Automated events. See EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[3880,"**Forgetting the time zone.** A time without a zone sends half a mixed list to the wrong hour."],[6684,"**Free** (selected by default): attendees register without paying."],[7104,"**From live to evergreen in one product.** EasyWebinar lists recordings of your past webinars under **Recordings** when you pick the video. EverWebinar can import a past WebinarJam session if the same account has an active WebinarJam subscription. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam and EverWebinar."],[7242,"**From the Overview tab.** The **Team & Moderators** panel lists the presenters and moderators who can run this webinar. A new webinar shows \"No presenters or moderators added yet.\" Use **Add presenter** for someone who appears on camera and presents, or **Invite** to send an invitation to join the webinar team."],[8892,"**Full name and Email come first, both required.** Phone, custom fields, consent and UTM capture are options you add."],[8897,"**Full name** and **Email**, both required."],[398,"**Fully editable.** Each draft opens like any other email, with its subject, content and timing."],[7823,"**Go Live** asks you to confirm and tells you anyone in the waiting area will be moved in. The header then shows **LIVE** with a timer, and **Go Live** becomes **End Session**. **End Session** disconnects everyone and nobody can rejoin, so it asks you to confirm."],[4347,"**Go Live** asks you to confirm, and reminds you that anyone in the waiting area will be moved in automatically and that offers and polls should be ready. Once live, the header shows **LIVE** with a timer, and **Go Live** becomes **End Session**. Ending disconnects everyone and nobody can rejoin, so end only when you're finished."],[7597,"**Go Live** asks you to confirm, because anyone in the waiting area is moved in automatically. Once live, the header shows **LIVE** with a timer, and **Go Live** becomes **End Session**. Ending disconnects everyone, and nobody can rejoin."],[6185,"**Group similar questions** and answer them together on air."],[9326,"**Guest speakers and moderators by link.** EasyWebinar's **Co-presenter Join Link** and **Moderator Join Link for Live room** let people join without an account. eWebinar's help centre doesn't document presenter or moderator join links, as EasyWebinar vs eWebinar sets out."],[7231,"**Guests arrive quietly.** A co-host can join early, sort out their audio and wait backstage without being shown."],[9278,"**Guests don't need accounts.** A co-presenter or moderator joins with a link, without an EasyWebinar login."],[7291,"**Guests held backstage during the session too.** In EasyWebinar, co-hosts and moderators land backstage and move to the stage and back as needed. ON24's guide describes presenters talking backstage before the webinar starts. More detail in EasyWebinar vs ON24."],[86,"**Guests stay guests.** A speaker on one session joins by link and needs no account."],[116,"**Guests without a login.** EasyWebinar's Co-presenter and Moderator join links bring a speaker into one webinar with no account. Kajabi's account users article covers people who help run the account, each with their own login. See EasyWebinar vs Kajabi."],[6822,"**Have a recording.** A simulive webinar plays a video, so you need one in your library or ready to add. You can add it during setup without leaving the builder."],[7010,"**Have the recording to hand.** Every session plays it. You can upload or import it during setup if it isn't in your library yet."],[1765,"**Have your login for that service ready.** You sign in to it during setup."],[6345,"**Headline**: what the attendee gets, in their terms."],[1009,"**Help in the room.** From Pro onward, the AI answers attendee questions using files you upload."],[6706,"**Holidays stay free.** **Blackout Dates** skip chosen days without ending a weekly run."],[5595,"**Host replies inside the script.** EasyWebinar's CSV has a **Role** column, so `Admin` lines appear as host replies. WebinarKit's chat simulator documents a username, message text and display time for each message. More detail in EasyWebinar vs WebinarKit."],[8325,"**Hosted files count towards storage; imported links don't.**"],[8317,"**Hosting comes with the webinar.** **Local import** uploads the file and EasyWebinar serves it. EverWebinar's help centre lists an external video as required for its primary video source. See EasyWebinar vs EverWebinar."],[225,"**How long it runs.**"],[636,"**How long it runs.**"],[881,"**How long it runs**, and roughly how many slides you want."],[6369,"**How long the replay stays up**: **Always Available**, **Expire after days** or **Specific date**. A replay that closes gives the offer a matching deadline."],[4092,"**How long the session runs**, so people can plan to stay for the offer and the questions."],[4091,"**How to ask a question**, and whether you will answer during the session or at the end."],[1168,"**Import from EasyWebinar** brings registrants and attendees across from a webinar. This is the main route."],[6859,"**Import from URL** plays a video already on **YouTube**, **Vimeo**, **Wistia** or a direct **MP4** link. You enter the link and the video's length."],[1169,"**Import** uploads a CSV or XLSX file in four steps: **Start**, **Upload**, **Map** and **Verify**. **Map** matches your file's columns to EasyCRM's fields."],[8326,"**Imported videos depend on the other platform.** Removing a YouTube video breaks the webinar that plays it."],[6926,"**Imported videos need an accurate duration.** EasyWebinar uses it to time sessions."],[7111,"**Imported videos need an accurate duration.** It's how EasyWebinar knows how long each session runs."],[8324,"**Imported videos need their duration entered.** EasyWebinar reads the length automatically only for uploaded files."],[8323,"**Imports come from four sources:** **YouTube**, **Vimeo**, **Wistia** or a direct **MP4 link**."],[1204,"**Imports that skip duplicates.** Livestorm sends registrants and attendees to Brevo. EasyWebinar imports them into its own Leads, and a re-import reports who was already there. EasyWebinar vs Livestorm"],[6515,"**In My Webinars**, the copy appears with the new name and its type badge, and the count on the matching type tab goes up."],[6870,"**In My Webinars**, the webinar sits under the **Simulive** tab and its card carries a type badge, the next session's date, time and timezone, and the registrant count."],[8169,"**Instant replay is set elsewhere.** **On Demand** belongs to an evergreen webinar's schedule, not to the Replay tab."],[8740,"**Instant viewing that keeps your schedule.** EasyWebinar runs **On Demand** beside a daily or weekly **Recurring Schedule** on one webinar. Livestorm's help centre says that once an on-demand registrant exists, you can't add more sessions. Compare EasyWebinar vs Livestorm."],[6539,"**Integration settings** carries the original's integration setup to the copy. Check the connections on the copy's **Integrations** tab before it goes live. See Connect a CRM and map your webinar data."],[1848,"**Integrations are per webinar.** Connecting one doesn't connect the rest, and different webinars can feed different lists."],[9333,"**Integrations are per webinar.** Mapping join and replay links into a CRM is set up on each webinar."],[3487,"**Integrations are set per webinar.** Connecting one doesn't connect the rest."],[6558,"**Integrations come along on request.** EasyWebinar has an **Integration settings** item in the clone dialog. Livestorm's public docs show no copying of integrations. See EasyWebinar vs Livestorm."],[4963,"**Interest is still fresh.** The person has just chosen to watch, and a short **Interval** lets them do it while that holds."],[7069,"**Interest meets a session quickly.** With **Just-in-time Registration** or **On Demand**, a visitor doesn't have to come back another day to watch."],[9622,"**Invite** sends an invitation to join the webinar team."],[3882,"**Inviting the whole list to a narrow topic.** A saved list for the segment the topic suits protects your open rate."],[8407,"**It arrives at the moment of highest interest.** It lands the moment someone registers, while the webinar is still on their mind."],[5990,"**It breaks up a long talk.** A question every so often turns a passive audience into a responsive one."],[1318,"**It brings replies back to you.** You choose the address, so a reply reaches someone who reads it."],[8546,"**It brings the session back into view.** A sign-up from days ago is easy to forget. A reminder an hour before puts it in front of the person again."],[8102,"**It can carry a deadline.** **Expire after days** or **Specific date** give the replay a closing point."],[9106,"**It can carry your tracking.** Pixels and analytics scripts go on the page from the builder's settings."],[8101,"**It can keep selling.** With **Webinar Replica**, the replay carries the same offers and polls as the live session."],[5992,"**It can point to buyers.** A question such as \"when are you planning to travel?\" separates people close to a decision from people who are browsing."],[2994,"**It catches late viewers.** **After the replay ends** can redirect replay viewers to your course checkout."],[1448,"**It covers the CRM only.** Broadcasts and workflows use it. A webinar's own emails, SMS (Beta) and WhatsApp (Beta) use that webinar's **Notifications** tab."],[929,"**It doesn't schedule the webinar.** After the build you still set the schedule and, for simulive or evergreen, choose a video."],[2992,"**It drafts the webinar for you.** **Create with AI** turns one description into a script, pages, emails, polls and offers."],[4459,"**It exports segments, not everything.** **Export** downloads the filtered list, so the work the filters did comes with it."],[8826,"**It feeds your CRM.** The phone number can be mapped into a CRM field of your choice."],[5993,"**It feeds your follow-up.** **People** records how many polls each person answered, next to watch time and offer clicks."],[5833,"**It fits an existing tool.** On recorded webinars, **Third party** keeps conversations in the chat tool your team already uses."],[2993,"**It follows up by behaviour.** Emails and email-tool tags can follow who attended and who clicked your offer."],[8408,"**It gives the join link a permanent home.** The registrant can search their inbox for it instead of hunting for your page."],[8103,"**It hands viewers a next step.** **After the replay ends** sends them to an offer or a booking page."],[1317,"**It improves your deliverability.** A verified domain gives you better deliverability than a verified single address."],[8549,"**It is measurable.** **Registered** to attended in Analytics shows whether the reminders are working."],[1964,"**It is not a course platform.** EasyWebinar does not host or deliver courses; it runs the webinar in front of your course platform."],[8746,"**It isn't the replay page.** Replay availability, deadlines, redirects and the replay page's look are set on the **Replay** tab for the replay page."],[2804,"**It keeps running.** A recorded version can play on a schedule while you coach your current clients."],[4607,"**It locates the leak.** **Visitors** to **Registered** measures your registration page. **Registered** to attended measures your reminder emails."],[8822,"**It makes text reminders possible.** SMS and WhatsApp reminders (both in Beta) go to the number someone gave you, so they depend on the **Phone** field."],[5423,"**It needs a recording.** A simulive webinar plays a video, so you must upload, import or pick one before sessions can run."],[5601,"**It needs the built-in chat.** Third-party chat replaces EasyWebinar's panel."],[8410,"**It opens a reply channel.** The **Reply-to email** is an address you choose, so a registrant with a question can simply reply."],[1315,"**It opens the gate.** Broadcasts and workflows can go out once a service and a verified sender are in place."],[5515,"**It plays in every session.** On an evergreen webinar that runs all day, the same setup plays each time without you."],[6526,"**It protects what's live.** The original isn't touched, so a working webinar keeps working while you experiment."],[8824,"**It puts consent on the form.** **GDPR Compliance** adds the checkbox with your own wording, so you don't need a separate consent step."],[1316,"**It puts your name on the mail.** Your contacts see a domain or address that belongs to your business."],[4457,"**It ranks engagement for you.** **Lead score** rates how engaged each person was, which makes a long list quick to sort."],[8100,"**It reaches the larger audience.** **Missed**, people who registered and never showed up, is the group most worth emailing."],[8548,"**It runs on every session by itself.** Timing is relative, so nothing needs rescheduling when new sessions appear."],[7071,"**It runs without staff.** Nobody needs to present, and Chat Simulation exists for rooms that run unattended."],[6888,"**It runs without you if needed.** The recording plays on schedule whether or not your team joins."],[6524,"**It saves the rebuild.** Everything you've already written and designed can come with the copy."],[4608,"**It separates offer problems from checkout problems.** **Views to Clicks** and **Clicks to Purchases** show where buyers drop out."],[8409,"**It sets the sender early.** The **Sender name** shown here is the one they'll see on every reminder."],[4456,"**It shows behaviour, not just registration.** **Watch percentage**, **Replay watch percentage** and **Offer clicked** separate interested people from casual sign-ups."],[2995,"**It shows what sold.** **Offers Performance** and **Revenue by Offer** report each offer's results for that webinar."],[8825,"**It shows which campaign worked.** With **UTM Params** on, you can filter registrants by **Source & UTM** in the People view."],[5991,"**It shows who is in the room.** Ask about their situation and you learn who you are talking to while you can still adjust."],[4609,"**It shows who to follow up.** **Missed** is everyone who registered and never attended."],[8695,"**It sits alongside scheduled options.** Registrants who'd rather turn up for a session can still pick a just-in-time or recurring one."],[9103,"**It starts filled in.** The schedule and countdown are applied when the webinar is created, so the page works before you touch it."],[6527,"**It starts the copy clean.** No registrants come across, so the new webinar's numbers are its own."],[8694,"**It suits people short on time.** Someone with twenty free minutes between meetings doesn't have to fit a session around them."],[8823,"**It tells you who registered, not just how many.** A custom question gives you context before the session starts."],[4458,"**It ties campaigns to attendance.** With UTM capture on, **Source & UTM** shows which campaign produced people who actually watched."],[4610,"**It ties money to the webinar.** Webinar revenue sits next to attendance, so you can see what each session earned."],[8968,"**It travels with clones.** When you clone a webinar, you can bring its embed widgets along."],[5606,"**It's labelled Beta in the app.**"],[6525,"**It's selective.** You choose which assets come across, item by item."],[8967,"**It's the same snippet everywhere.** Copy it once from the Content tab or the Share dialog and paste it into any page."],[7300,"**Joining by link needs no account,** but a person with a team login can also join as a presenter."],[4945,"**Just-in-time Registration** is an evergreen schedule option that offers each visitor a session starting a few minutes after they register, rather than at a fixed future time. You choose how often these sessions come round, from every 2 minutes to every hour. Each just-in-time session runs in the attendee's own local time, so someone who finds your registration page can be watching shortly afterwards."],[5187,"**Just-in-time Registration** offers a session starting shortly after someone registers. The just-in-time page explains the settings."],[2861,"**Just-in-time Registration** offers a session starting shortly. A just-in-time session starts soon after each person registers, in their own local time, which suits a global audience."],[6184,"**Keep an eye on Active during the session**, not only at the end, so a quick answer doesn't wait half an hour."],[5734,"**Keep deadlines consistent.** Match the offer countdown, the replay deadline and what your follow-up emails say."],[5575,"**Keep host answers accurate.** An `Admin` reply is read as your answer, so it should be one you'd give live."],[7940,"**Keep live recording on** if you want your sessions to land here. Recording is on by default in the live room, where the header reads **Auto Recording Enabled**."],[3405,"**Keep one name per campaign.** Use the same campaign value on every link for the webinar, and change only source and medium."],[6022,"**Keep options short and distinct**, so each one can be read at a glance."],[8579,"**Keep them short.** A reminder needs the time and the link."],[7939,"**Know what uses storage.** Only files uploaded to EasyWebinar count towards your storage. Videos imported from a URL use none."],[3019,"**Know which campaign worked.** Turn on **UTM Params** so each registration records the ad, email or post that brought it in."],[6486,"**Know which type you want the copy to be.** You choose it in the dialog, and it is fixed on the new webinar once created."],[213,"**Know your audience and offer.** The prompt drives everything. Have a specific audience, three or four teaching points, a length, a tone, and what you'll sell at the end ready before you start."],[7012,"**Know your audience's hours.** Recurring sessions run in the webinar's timezone, so pick times that work for the people you expect."],[7941,"**Know your upload limit.** Upload video as **MP4**, up to **4 GB** per file. See video and storage limits."],[5527,"**Know your video.** For a manual script, you'll time messages against the recording, so have it to hand."],[9670,"**Known contacts register in one click.** EasyWebinar's **One-Click Registration Link** carries a contact's name and email in the URL. Livestorm's help centre documents sharing the registration page, with no one-click registration link. Compare EasyWebinar vs Livestorm."],[9279,"**Known contacts skip the form.** The **One-Click Registration Link** registers someone whose details you already hold."],[8011,"**Larger uploads.** EasyWebinar takes video uploads up to **4 GB** per file. WebinarNinja's help centre lists a 2 GB limit for its video files. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarNinja."],[4533,"**Lead score is calculated from engagement.** It's a guide for sorting, not a replacement for the underlying columns."],[4505,"**Lead score** is calculated from engagement: attendance, watch time and interaction. It rates how engaged someone was, for example **Hot**, so you can sort a long list and start with the most engaged people. It's a quick way to prioritise. For the detail, read it alongside **Status**, **Watch percentage**, **Polls** and **Offer clicked** on the same row."],[2160,"**Leads where sales works:** registrants and attendees sync to the CRM the client already uses."],[1426,"**Leads.** **Import from EasyWebinar** pulls registrants and attendees across from a webinar, so the people in your webinar records can be sent to once sending works."],[6186,"**Leave time at the end** to clear what's left in Active before you close."],[6559,"**Less to redo after cloning.** EasyWebinar can copy pages, polls, offers and emails in one pass. WebinarNinja's guide has you clone, then update the title, date and time. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarNinja."],[4776,"**Less waiting.** A just-in-time session starts a few minutes after someone registers."],[5566,"**Let it breathe.** Real chat comes in bursts with quiet stretches, not one message every thirty seconds."],[5563,"**Line messages up with the video.** A question about a slide should land while that slide is on screen."],[7465,"**LinkedIn company pages built in.** EasyCast lists **LinkedIn** and **LinkedIn Organisation** next to **YouTube** and **Custom RTMP**. Zoom's livestreaming setting names Facebook, YouTube, Twitch and a custom service. See EasyWebinar vs Zoom."],[1395,"**List size.** Send to a targeted list rather than everyone, because it helps on both allowance and open rate."],[1652,"**Lists built from the webinar.** eWebinar passes properties to your CRM, while EasyWebinar imports registrants into lists a workflow sends to straight away. EasyWebinar vs eWebinar."],[6690,"**Live + Replay bundle**, to sell access to the webinar and its recording together"],[4864,"**Live and automated in one account.** EasyWebinar clones a live webinar into an evergreen one using the live session's recording. EverWebinar's live webinars run in the separate WebinarJam product. Compare EasyWebinar vs EverWebinar."],[2238,"**Live and automated in one place per client:** EasyWebinar runs live, simulive and evergreen webinars in the same workspace, while StealthSeminar's pricing lists a white label custom domain for its automated product. See EasyWebinar vs StealthSeminar."],[3100,"**Live and automated in one place.** EasyWebinar can run the same course webinar live, simulive or evergreen. eWebinar runs recorded sessions, so it covers the automated half of a launch. See EasyWebinar vs eWebinar."],[7654,"**Live and automated in one product.** A live session clones into an evergreen webinar, while WebinarJam runs automated sessions in EverWebinar, a separate product. EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam"],[6067,"**Live and automated polls in one product.** eWebinar runs automated webinars only, so there is no live poll to launch. Livestorm's help docs don't describe polls in automated events. See EasyWebinar vs Livestorm."],[6736,"**Live and recorded in one account.** EasyWebinar offers **Live Webinar**, **Simulive Webinar** and **Evergreen Webinar** in the same dialog. WebinarJam runs recorded webinars in its sister product, EverWebinar. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam and EverWebinar."],[5418,"**Live and recorded in one product.** EasyWebinar runs live, simulive and evergreen webinars side by side, with the same pages, emails and offers. EverWebinar sessions are recorded in advance, and live webinars run in its sister product, WebinarJam. Compare EasyWebinar vs EverWebinar."],[2421,"**Live and recorded in the same room.** EasyWebinar runs both from one account, while eWebinar is built for recorded sessions without a live presenter. See EasyWebinar vs eWebinar."],[4678,"**Live and replay in one count.** EasyWebinar's **Total Attended** shows unique people, split into **Live only**, **Replay only** and **Both**. WebinarJam shows live and replay data separately, and Zoom reports recording views on Webinars Plus. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam and EverWebinar and EasyWebinar vs Zoom."],[9682,"**Live Attended** counts people who joined the live session. **Total Attended** adds replay viewers, so it's the larger number."],[4627,"**Live Attended** covers the broadcast only. **Total Attended** counts each person once whether they watched live, on replay or both, which is why it's the number to use when you ask how many people the webinar reached."],[4688,"**Live Attended** is the live broadcast only. **Total Attended** counts unique people who watched live or on replay."],[2002,"**Live attendees** counts people joining live sessions in the current period."],[7980,"**Live sessions become reusable content.** You can pick a recording as the video for a simulive or evergreen webinar."],[8743,"**Live sessions in the same account.** EasyWebinar runs live, simulive and evergreen webinars, with **On Demand** on the evergreen ones. eWebinar describes its webinars as running without anyone having to be there live. Compare EasyWebinar vs eWebinar."],[7854,"**Live sessions you host in EasyWebinar.** Automatic recording applies to the live room. This page covers no other kind of session."],[6689,"**Live webinar price**, the amount each registrant pays"],[7105,"**Live webinars built in.** EasyWebinar runs live, simulive and evergreen webinars from one account. eWebinar's public docs show no live video broadcast, and StealthSeminar streams live video in from YouTube Live or Twitch. See EasyWebinar vs eWebinar and EasyWebinar vs Stealth Seminar."],[8328,"**Live webinars don't need a video.** Simulive and evergreen webinars are the types that play one."],[6070,"**Live webinars need manual launches.** On a live webinar, each poll is launched from the **Polls** panel."],[5751,"**Live-room timers are different.** Once you go live, the room header shows **LIVE** with a timer of how long you have been broadcasting. That timer counts up and is separate from offer countdowns."],[3263,"**Live, simulive and evergreen webinars.** Cloning works across all three, and can change the type on the way. Start with creating a live webinar."],[6858,"**Local import** uploads a file from your computer, and EasyWebinar stores and serves it. No YouTube or Vimeo account is involved."],[4840,"**Local import** uploads from your computer, and EasyWebinar hosts the video, so no YouTube 