n the attendee list as well.** **Attendees on Event Page** adds simulated names to the list attendees see. EverWebinar's help centre covers preloaded chat messages, with no simulated attendee list documented. More detail in EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam and EverWebinar."],[9495,"**Native, not a workaround.** Demio's help centre points to a Zapier workflow in place of a native paid webinar feature. EasyWebinar's paid registration is a step in creating the webinar. See EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[6503,"**New Webinar Name** starts as the original's name with \"(Copy)\" on the end. Replace it with something you'll recognise in your webinar list, especially if both versions will run side by side."],[686,"**Next month's webinar.** Clone the webinar to reuse its registration pages, and clone before you try a different page on a webinar that's already running."],[6708,"**No accidental launch.** The registration page stays private until you click **Publish**."],[6919,"**No add-on licence.** **Simulive Webinar** is one of the three type cards in EasyWebinar's create dialog. Zoom's simulive needs a Zoom Events or Zoom Webinars Plus licence on top of a webinar licence. See EasyWebinar vs Zoom."],[492,"**No behaviour-based drafts.** Attendee action and paid offer emails aren't part of the six, so you add them on the **Notifications** tab."],[5350,"**No Chat** hides chat, while the contact box still takes questions by email."],[9018,"**No CSS needed.** StealthSeminar styles its embedded widgets through CSS selectors you write. Compare EasyWebinar vs StealthSeminar."],[3075,"**No EasyWebinar branding:** the **White Label** add-on removes it."],[8245,"**No extra video host.** With **Local import**, a recorded webinar runs with nothing outside EasyWebinar."],[9277,"**No hunting for links.** Every link for the webinar sits in one dialog, a click from the Overview."],[5573,"**No invented testimonials.** Simulated attendees shouldn't claim results or endorse your product."],[120,"**No invitation email.** You set the password and pass the login on yourself."],[4962,"**No long wait.** A session is always a few minutes away, so nobody has to plan a return visit."],[394,"**No missing reminders.** The day, hour and fifteen-minute reminders exist from the start, so none gets forgotten."],[6737,"**No plan gate on the type.** Every EasyWebinar plan includes this builder. WebinarKit's help centre says live and automated creation depend on your plan. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarKit."],[6072,"**No practical cap on numbers.** Add as many polls as the session needs."],[8693,"**No waiting at all.** A registrant who is ready now can watch now."],[5745,"**No widget to install elsewhere.** eWebinar's countdown to the start comes from widgets you place on your own landing page. EasyWebinar's is a block in its own page builder. See EasyWebinar vs eWebinar."],[4872,"**No zooming in on shared content.** Attendees of a live room can zoom in on a shared screen or file, but automated webinars use a separate attendee page where that isn't available."],[3595,"**No-shows get a second chance.** The replay email lets them catch up before your deadline."],[3484,"**No-shows get their own email.** EasyWebinar sends a follow-up set to no-shows from the webinar's **Notifications** tab, while Livestorm's docs describe a replay link for registrants who missed the live event. EasyWebinar vs Livestorm"],[3382,"**No-shows still become leads.** They registered, so they get the replay and a second chance."],[3597,"**Nobody gets the wrong message.** Separate audiences mean no one is thanked for a session they missed."],[8896,"**Nothing changes for visitors until you publish.**"],[600,"**Nothing is locked.** Every word and every block stays editable in the page builder."],[1554,"**Nothing reaches a contact before you're ready.** A draft sends nothing, so you can build and revise in peace."],[7763,"**Nothing to remember:** recording is on by default, so a busy start can't cost you the session."],[7635,"**Notifications:** confirmation and reminder emails sent from the webinar's own settings."],[8466,"**Notify admin needs an address.** It sends a copy of registrations to the admin address you give it."],[8741,"**Now or in a few minutes.** EasyWebinar offers **On Demand** and **Just-in-time Registration** on the same registration page. Demio documents on-demand sessions for automated events, with no just-in-time option. Compare EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[9643,"**Numbers that update as you run.** The stats change as the webinar runs, so you can watch registrations and attendance move."],[1579,"**Nurture.** A new lead receives a short sequence over the following fortnight."],[5319,"**Odd hours stop being a problem.** A session can run in a timezone where you'd rather be asleep."],[6149,"**Off**, when the webinar shouldn't take questions at all."],[5149,"**Offer response.** For a session that sells, the number that matters is how many viewers see the offer and click it. Its weak spot is that a small evergreen audience gives jumpy percentages, so read it over several weeks."],[4676,"**Offer results.** EasyWebinar's **Offers Performance** shows views, clicks and purchases for each offer. Demio's Featured Action shows clicks and the share of attendees who clicked, and its docs describe no purchase tracking. See EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[6410,"**Offer revenue and registration revenue are reported separately**, under **Paid Offer** and **Paid Webinar**."],[2419,"**Offer views, clicks and purchases in one panel.** EasyWebinar reports all three per offer, while WebinarKit's dashboard lists clicks on offers. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarKit."],[8171,"**Offers and polls carry over only with Webinar Replica.** A **Custom Build** page has its own layout and CTAs."],[1184,"**Offers in the room.** People who click an offer during the webinar make your warmest list."],[204,"**Offers match your pitch.** You choose how hard to sell, and each offer comes back with a headline, button and link."],[4658,"**Offers Performance** reports on the offers you build on the **CTAs** tab. Comparing sessions is the clearest way to see whether a change, such as adding a countdown timer, helped."],[470,"**Offers:** offer clicks can trigger an attendee action follow-up."],[1632,"**Offers.** People who clicked an offer during the webinar make the warmest list to follow up."],[904,"**Offers.** Pick a soft, balanced or direct pitch and the build writes offers with a title, headline and button text."],[1946,"**Offers** appear in the room with a button that opens your checkout. Offers can carry a countdown timer to add urgency."],[4139,"**Offers** deliver section 7, with the button pointing to your own checkout."],[3464,"**Offers** put a button in the room, and the **Offer clicked** column in People marks who used it."],[5400,"**Offers**, whose buttons open your own checkout or sales page, covered under offers."],[1555,"**Old campaigns stay on record.** Archiving retires a workflow but keeps it, so you can reuse its structure."],[9616,"**On a free webinar** the panel reads **This webinar is free — attendees register without payment**, with a **Convert to paid** button."],[9617,"**On a paid webinar** the panel shows your pricing title and price, and the pencil edits them. A **Payment Gateway** panel shows the connected Stripe account, and **Manage** opens your payment settings."],[5674,"**On a registration page**, it tells visitors how soon the session begins, which turns \"sometime\" into \"in two days\"."],[5673,"**On an offer**, it tells attendees how long they have to act on what you are selling: a course enrolment, a coaching call, a bonus, a programme."],[8673,"**On Demand** is an evergreen schedule setting that lets a registrant start watching your webinar straight away, with no session to wait for. EasyWebinar also calls it **instant replay**: registrants click a button, labelled *Watch instant replay* unless you change it, and the recording starts. It is a different thing from the replay page on the **Replay** tab, which shows the recording of a session that has already happened."],[2862,"**On Demand** lets registrants start watching straight away, with no session to wait for."],[5188,"**On Demand** lets registrants start watching straight away. Its button reads *Watch instant replay* unless you change it. On-demand viewing covers when to use it."],[5003,"**On Demand** lets registrants watch immediately, with no session at all. Pair it with just-in-time and registrants choose between \"now\" and \"in a few minutes\". The On Demand (instant replay) option has its own page."],[6872,"**On the Content tab**, a **Webinar Video** panel shows the recording you chose. Live webinars don't have this panel."],[6516,"**On the copy's Overview tab**, **Registrants** starts at zero."],[6518,"**On the copy's tabs**, the items you ticked are present: pages on **Content**, polls and offers on **CTAs**, emails on **Notifications**, and connections on **Integrations**."],[6517,"**On the original**, registrants, sessions and settings are unchanged."],[6871,"**On the Overview tab**, the **Sessions** panel lists each sitting under **Upcoming**, **Past** and **Cancelled**. A daily or weekly schedule fills the list from its recurrence. See The Overview tab."],[6873,"**On the registration page**, check the session times and publish the page before you share the link."],[4679,"**One date range for the whole tab.** Set a date range, click **Apply**, and every number on EasyWebinar's tab follows it. WebinarJam filters by webinar, session and event, with no custom date range described."],[2335,"**One explanation for many buyers.** You present once instead of repeating the same call."],[7661,"**One fixed time.** A live session runs at one time for everyone, in the timezone you set."],[9492,"**One flow, no second form.** EasyWebinar registers the buyer as soon as payment succeeds. WebinarJam and EverWebinar send buyers back to a registration form, and their PayPal guide warns that people aren't registered until they complete it. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam and EverWebinar."],[3461,"**One follow-up for everyone.** Attendees get \"sorry you missed it\" and no-shows get \"thanks for coming\". Set the audience on each email."],[8965,"**One less step.** Visitors register where they are instead of clicking through to another page."],[8248,"**One library, many webinars.** You add a video once and reuse it on other webinars."],[1586,"**One list per webinar**, so you can follow up on a specific event."],[5600,"**One mode at a time.** Turning on AI Simulation disables Manual Simulation, and the reverse."],[7979,"**One place for every recording.** Live sessions with recording on land in **Recordings**, with no exporting or uploading."],[9641,"**One place to check before a session.** Schedule, pricing, team and links sit side by side, so a last check takes seconds."],[7765,"**One place to look:** every finished session lands in **Library** → **Recordings** with its webinar's name, duration and date."],[5746,"**One product for live and automated offers.** An EasyWebinar offer, countdown included, runs on every webinar type you create. WebinarJam handles live sessions and EverWebinar the automated ones, as two separate products. See EasyWebinar vs EverWebinar."],[5214,"**One product for live and evergreen.** EasyWebinar runs both types side by side, while EverWebinar's live webinars run in WebinarJam, a separate product. See EasyWebinar vs EverWebinar and WebinarJam."],[2418,"**One product for your live session and its automated copy.** EasyWebinar clones a live webinar into an evergreen one, while EverWebinar sessions run in a separate product from WebinarJam. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam."],[2910,"**One product from live to repeat.** EasyWebinar runs the live session and its evergreen clone side by side. EverWebinar sessions are recorded in advance, apart from live webinars in WebinarJam. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam and EverWebinar."],[1056,"**One prompt for the whole webinar.** EasyWebinar drafts the script, pages, emails, polls and offers together, while eWebinar's AI works on pages and notifications one area at a time. See EasyWebinar vs eWebinar."],[200,"**One prompt, five deliverables.** Script, pages, emails, polls and offers all start from the same description."],[1006,"**One prompt, five parts.** The script, pages, emails, polls and offers come from the same description, so they tell the same story."],[7852,"**One recording, two reuses.** EasyWebinar offers the recording as a replay and as an evergreen webinar's video, and WebinarNinja shows past recordings in a Replays picker when you add a video. EasyWebinar vs WebinarNinja."],[7438,"**One session can reach more places.** EasyCast sends the same broadcast to YouTube and LinkedIn."],[2801,"**One session replaces many first calls.** You explain your method once, to everyone who registered."],[6066,"**One set of polls for every webinar type.** EasyWebinar's live, simulive and evergreen webinars use the same polls. In EverWebinar, poll results are preconfigured, and no poll statistics come from attendee answers. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam and EverWebinar."],[1444,"**One setup for a CRM's sends.** EasyWebinar's setup serves CRM broadcasts and workflows, while WebinarJam's third-party SMTP service is described for webinar emails. More in EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam."],[4524,"**One table for every webinar.** **People** sits in the sidebar and spans all your webinars. Demio's People section sits under each event's activity. See EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[2606,"**One webinar shows its revenue.** The Overview tab and the Revenue view show what this workshop took."],[8014,"**Only EasyWebinar-hosted files count towards storage.** Imported URLs use none."],[7109,"**Only just-in-time sessions use local time.** Recurring daily and weekly sessions run in the webinar's timezone, despite the message on the schedule step."],[7469,"**Only one 