ccount. On simulive, pricing comes before video selection, so you set the price before you choose the recording."],[6685,"**Paid**: attendees pay to register. Requires a connected Stripe account."],[1212,"**Pardot, not Sales Cloud.** The connection for Salesforce Pardot (Account Engagement) covers that product, not Sales Cloud."],[5597,"**Part of the webinar itself.** Chat Simulation (Beta) sits on the same **Engagement** tab as chat and Q&A. Demio's help centre doesn't document simulated chat. More detail in EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[3251,"**Pass on the login yourself.** Nothing is emailed when you add someone, so send them their details and ask them to change the password."],[5403,"**Past recordings**, from webinars you've already run, through automatic recording."],[3879,"**Pasting a private link.** The **Co-presenter Join Link** and **Moderator Join Link for Live room** let anyone join your room in that role. Only the registration, attendee and replay links are meant for your audience."],[2603,"**Payment and the seat arrive together.** A buyer pays on the Stripe checkout and is registered once the payment goes through."],[6707,"**Payment at sign-up.** With **Paid** selected, people complete a Stripe checkout before they are registered."],[2702,"**Payment is built in.** EasyWebinar's checkout is part of the pricing step. Demio's help centre describes paid access through a payment app and a Zapier Zap. See EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[2707,"**Payment runs through Stripe only.** Connect a Stripe account on the pricing step or from **Integrations → Payment**."],[9425,"**Payouts are yours.** Payments land in your own Stripe account, and Stripe pays out to your bank on its usual schedule. EasyWebinar never holds your funds."],[9499,"**Payouts follow Stripe's schedule.** EasyWebinar doesn't hold or pay out funds."],[8029,"**PDF, DOCX or PPTX**, up to **25MB** per file. The AI Moderator is in Beta."],[1624,"**People can opt out.** Gmail asks bulk senders to support one-click unsubscribe with a visible unsubscribe link. Yahoo asks senders to honour unsubscribes within two days."],[4528,"**People spans every webinar,** unlike a webinar's own **Analytics** tab."],[4849,"**People.** The People list shows who registered and what they did."],[6384,"**People** has an **Offer clicked** column, and the **Behavior** filter can combine high watch time with offer clicks to find people who were interested and didn't buy. **Export** the filtered list to work with it elsewhere."],[6903,"**People** in the sidebar can filter registrants by webinar **Type**, so you can look at simulive audiences on their own. See People."],[6047,"**People** in the sidebar has a **Polls** column showing how many polls each person answered, next to **Watch percentage** and **Offer clicked**. Use it to see who took part, not only who turned up."],[9000,"**People** in the sidebar lists every registrant across your webinars. After your test registration, find yourself there to confirm the details came through."],[9474,"**People** in the sidebar lists every registrant across your webinars. Filter by webinar, behaviour or source, then **Export** to work with a list of paid attendees elsewhere."],[3228,"**People** in the sidebar lists every registrant and attendee across all your webinars in one table. Each row is one person on one webinar, with their status, lead score, watch percentage and whether they clicked your offer."],[8855,"**People** in the sidebar lists every registrant and attendee across all your webinars, one row per person per webinar. Columns include **Name** and email, **Phone** (if you collected it), the webinar and its type, the session, and when they registered. Use **Columns** to choose what appears."],[3083,"**People** in the sidebar shows the individuals behind the numbers across all your webinars, with each person's **watch percentage**, **replay watch percentage**, whether they **clicked your offer**, and a **lead score** for engagement. Filter by behaviour, for example high watch time plus an offer click, and **Export** the list."],[4444,"**People** is a single table of everyone who registered for or attended any of your EasyWebinar webinars. Each row shows one person on one webinar, with what they did: their attendance status, how much of the live session and the replay they watched, whether they clicked your offer, and a lead score for how engaged they were. You can filter the table by webinar, dates, behaviour, campaign source, device or location, and export exactly the segment you need."],[4531,"**Phone appears only if you collected it.**"],[2505,"**Pick the format.** Choose Live, Simulive or Evergreen from the table above. If the format needs a recording, have it ready first."],[3253,"**Pick the master.** On **My Webinars**, open the card menu on the webinar that worked and choose **Clone Webinar**."],[2076,"**Pick the right device** in the device check if you have more than one camera or microphone."],[5342,"**Pick the timezone your audience lives in.** The timezone is part of the schedule, so an attendee abroad sees your session at their own local equivalent."],[6824,"**Pick your session times and timezone.** Sessions play at the times you set, in one timezone, so choose times that suit the audience you are targeting."],[3661,"**Pitching people who already bought.** That's why the last-call templates above carry a line for buyers. It costs one sentence and saves an awkward reply."],[6024,"**Place buying-intent questions near the offer.** Asking when someone plans to act, just before you present an offer, tells you how ready the room is."],[2508,"**Plan the follow-up before the session.** Decide what attendees and no-shows each receive, using the follow-up email guide."],[1208,"**Plan.** EasyCRM starts at the Growth plan. Live webinars are on every plan."],[1846,"**Points in the session you choose.** EasyWebinar's **Joined webinar after** and **Left webinar before** let you set the point in the session. WebinarJam's trigger examples include leaving early, evaluated after the session concludes. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam and EverWebinar."],[4086,"**Poll A, in the opening.** Ask who is in the room: role, company size or how far along they are. It warms people up and tells you which examples to stress."],[4087,"**Poll B, after teaching point 2.** Ask about their experience with the problem. The answers give you a live example to use in point 3."],[4088,"**Poll C, in the bridge.** Ask how interested people are in going further. It gauges interest in your offer just before you make it."],[296,"**Polls and offers in the same build.** EasyWebinar generates polls from the goals you pick, then offers in the pitch style you choose. WebinarKit's AI Creator Suite covers scripts, slide decks and avatar videos. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarKit."],[4847,"**Polls and offers.** Polls and offers run on recorded webinars too."],[5197,"**Polls and timed offers** come across with the clone when ticked, and work as they do everywhere else."],[4374,"**Polls are launched by hand on a live webinar.** Plan who launches each one, because they don't appear on their own."],[7660,"**Polls are launched by hand** on a live webinar."],[7470,"**Polls are launched manually** on a live webinar."],[6068,"**Polls are part of the AI build.** EasyWebinar's **Create with AI** can include polls alongside the script, pages and emails. The help docs of Demio, Zoom and WebinarKit don't describe AI that writes polls. See EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[4156,"**Polls before the video exists.** EasyWebinar drafts polls when you plan the session, while eWebinar suggests interactions once your video is uploaded. EasyWebinar vs eWebinar"],[4051,"**Polls do a job.** Each poll is placed for a reason, such as learning who is attending or gauging interest before the pitch."],[203,"**Polls have a purpose.** You choose what the polls should achieve. Each one explains why it's there and where it fits."],[5749,"**Polls have no countdown setting.** The **Countdown timer** switch is in the offer editor only."],[6075,"**Polls have no countdown.** The poll editor has a question, response options and **Published**; countdowns belong to offers."],[4155,"**Polls planned from their purpose.** EasyWebinar writes polls from goals such as gauging interest in your offer, while WebinarKit's AI Creator Suite covers scripts and its help docs describe no AI-written polls. EasyWebinar vs WebinarKit"],[1008,"**Polls with a purpose.** You choose what the polls are for, such as qualifying leads, and the AI writes questions to suit."],[4099,"**Polls with no purpose.** A poll that tells you nothing you will act on wastes a minute of the session."],[1059,"**Polls written by the AI.** EasyWebinar's AI writes polls from the goals you pick, while WebinarKit's AI Creator Suite covers scripts and slide decks. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarKit."],[6065,"**Polls written from your goals.** EasyWebinar's polls step asks what the polls are for, then writes five polls with a note on where each fits. eWebinar's AI drafts interactions from the video transcript instead. See EasyWebinar vs eWebinar."],[471,"**Polls:** drafted in the same AI build, straight after the emails."],[903,"**Polls.** The build can write five polls, each with a note on where it fits in the run of show."],[6538,"**Polls** and **Offers** copy to the new webinar's **CTAs** tab, and **Email notifications** copy to its **Notifications** tab, if you leave them ticked. See Polls and Reminder emails."],[4138,"**Polls** carry out the poll plan from sections 1, 4 and 6."],[3465,"**Polls** give you another engagement signal, and the **Polls** column counts how many each person answered."],[3048,"**Polls** help too. A question about the audience, such as where they are now or what they want to achieve, keeps people engaged and tells you who is ready to buy. **Create with AI** can write five polls for you, each with a purpose, such as gauging interest in your offer or qualifying leads."],[1945,"**Polls** keep the audience taking part. Polls work best when they are easy to answer, such as a question about the audience."],[5399,"**Polls**, described on the polls page."],[4866,"**Present live when it counts.** EasyWebinar keeps live webinars beside simulive and evergreen. eWebinar describes its product as pre-recorded. Compare EasyWebinar vs eWebinar."],[2824,"**Present, then pitch.** Teach first, show the offer when you reach the next step, and stay for questions."],[9678,"**Presenter and moderator links are private.** Anyone holding one can join your room in that role."],[9330,"**Presenter and moderator links grant access.** Anyone holding one can join your room in that role."],[7299,"**Presenter and moderator links grant that role** to whoever holds them. Keep them private."],[3873,"**Preview text:** A free live session on [topic], [date] at [time] [time zone]."],[9497,"**Prices are set in US dollars.** Stripe may present a local-currency price to attendees outside the US."],[2706,"**Prices are set in US dollars.** Stripe may show buyers outside the US their local currency."],[6688,"**Pricing Title** and an optional **Description**, shown to attendees at checkout"],[6218,"**Private means hosts and moderators.** Attendees don't see private questions."],[6153,"**Private Q&A keeps the room on track.** One attendee's question doesn't set the agenda for everyone else, and you choose what to address on air."],[8246,"**Private videos stay private.** A recording you don't want public can live on EasyWebinar, not on a public site."],[6148,"**Private**, so only hosts and moderators see the questions."],[4262,"**Problems surface while they are private.** You find a muted microphone in the green room, not in the chat."],[3193,"**Proven setups get reused.** A clone carries the pages, schedule, polls, offers and emails into the next webinar."],[6152,"**Public Q&A cuts repeats.** When people can see a question has already been asked, you don't answer the same thing five times."],[6147,"**Public**, so attendees can see what has already been asked."],[3021,"**Publish it.** The link only works once the page is published."],[274,"**Publish the pages.** A registration link doesn't work until its page is published."],[9189,"**Publishing is per page.** Each of the five pages has its own **Publish** button, and the registration link only works once its page is published."],[4694,"**Questions & Answers** shows how many were asked and answered, and the **Not Answered Rate** shows how many you left behind."],[1057,"**Questions answered on every webinar type.** EasyWebinar's AI Moderator works on live and recorded webinars, while Demio documents its AI moderator for on-demand sessions. See EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[6151,"**Questions don't get lost in chat.** They sit in their own queue until they are answered."],[6212,"**Questions start in their own queue.** EasyWebinar collects them in the room's **Question** panel. In Demio and WebinarJam, a question is a chat message that the host or a moderator marks as one. See EasyWebinar vs Demio and EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam and EverWebinar."],[6215,"**Questions stay in the webinar room.** EasyWebinar's Q&A queue lives in the room on live, simulive and evergreen webinars. StealthSeminar's Q&A is a message box that sends each question to you by email. See EasyWebinar vs StealthSeminar."],[5028,"**Quiet hours you choose.** **Exclude specific time** keeps chosen hours free of just-in-time sessions. WebinarKit's help centre covers just-in-time labels and spacing, with no hour exclusion documented. Compare EasyWebinar vs WebinarKit."],[3951,"**Rates on the Broadcasts screen are averages** across all your broadcasts, not the figures for a single send."],[1580,"**Re-engagement.** Someone who hasn't opened anything in ninety days gets one last message."],[5903,"**Reachable with chat off.** EasyWebinar's **EW Contact Box** works with **No Chat** and sends questions to an email address you 