02,"**Registration and offer revenue are reported separately**, under **Paid Webinar** and **Paid Offer**."],[467,"**Registration confirmation emails:** the welcome draft lives in this group and carries each person's join link."],[3463,"**Registration confirmation emails** go out immediately after someone registers, which is the first touch in the follow-up."],[8999,"**Registration Confirmation** is sent immediately after someone registers, and it carries their join link."],[3052,"**Registration Confirmation**, sent the moment someone registers, carries their join link."],[1183,"**Registration forms.** The fields on your form come across with each lead, including any custom registration fields you add."],[4141,"**Registration page builder** turns the promise in section 2 into the page people sign up on."],[9626,"**Registration Page**, beside **Share**, opens the live registration page so you can see what visitors see."],[5397,"**Registration pages**, built from a template or designed later."],[9615,"**Registration Pricing** shows whether the webinar is **Free** or **Paid**."],[9637,"**Registrations are counting.** After a test registration, **Registrants** moves off zero and the session row's registration count goes up."],[8608,"**Reminders are set per webinar.** Use cloning to carry a schedule to a new webinar."],[8609,"**Reminders go to registrants.** They are written once per webinar and sent to the people who registered for it."],[6927,"**Removing a linked video at its source breaks the webinar.** If a YouTube video is deleted on YouTube, the webinar that plays it stops working. An uploaded video is contained in EasyWebinar."],[8019,"**Removing a video on YouTube, Vimeo or Wistia** breaks any webinar that plays the imported link."],[3663,"**Repeating your reminders.** The reminder emails you sent before the session were about turning up. Follow-ups should talk about what happens next."],[8172,"**Replay emails live on the Notifications tab**, as follow-ups that include the replay link."],[469,"**Replay pages:** the page your follow-ups and no-show emails point to."],[1631,"**Replay pages.** The no-show workflow is where your replay page link earns its keep."],[5199,"**Replay pages** and **embed widgets** can be copied from the live webinar."],[4140,"**Replay pages** keep the same offers and polls when the replay uses **Webinar Replica**."],[8149,"**Replay settings** are one of the webinar assets you can bring across when cloning a webinar. See Clone a webinar."],[6540,"**Replay settings** brings the replay configuration from the original's **Replay** tab. See Replay pages."],[3449,"**Replay views are counted separately from live attendance**, and someone who did both shows under **Both**."],[4685,"**Replay views are counted separately** from live attendance; someone who did both appears under **Both**."],[4660,"**Replay Watched** and the **Replay only** and **Both** splits only fill in if people can reach your recording. See Replay pages."],[8183,"**Replay Watched** in the webinar's Analytics, and **Replay watch percentage** per person in **People**."],[6409,"**Replays carry offers only with Webinar Replica.** A Custom Build replay page has its own CTAs."],[6073,"**Replays only carry polls with Webinar Replica.** A Custom Build replay page is a separate design."],[7834,"**Replays:** a recording becomes the replay for people who missed the session, through replay pages."],[1185,"**Replays.** A broadcast is a natural way to send the link to your replay page."],[4850,"**Replays.** Replay pages cover the viewer who wants to watch again."],[1393,"**Replies.** **Reply & forwarding settings** points at an address someone reads."],[1386,"**Reply & forwarding settings** decides where replies to your email go. Point it at an address someone reads, because people reply to marketing email more than you might expect. A monitored team inbox is a sensible choice for a small business, since replies still get seen when one person is away."],[8460,"**Reply-to set per webinar.** EasyWebinar keeps **Email Settings** with each webinar. Livestorm's reply-to address is the account owner's email, changed in team settings, covered in EasyWebinar vs Livestorm."],[5986,"**Response options**, the answers attendees choose from. You add or remove them freely."],[5148,"**Retention through the recording.** YouTube's help describes retention well. It reports what share of viewers still watched after the first 30 seconds, and it treats a dip as the point where viewers abandoning or skipping shows. The weak spot is that a dip tells you where people left, not why. A dated remark or a missing drawing can cause one, and so can a slow section."],[7766,"**Reuse without exporting:** pick the recording as an evergreen webinar's video straight from the Library."],[6522,"**Reusing a webinar that works.** Pages, emails, polls and offers come across, so a new event doesn't start from blank."],[9671,"**Revenue beside registrations.** EasyWebinar's Overview shows **Revenue** next to **Registrants** and attendance. Demio's help centre doesn't document a revenue figure for a webinar. Compare EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[4677,"**Revenue next to attendance.** EasyWebinar's **Revenue** view splits paid sign-ups from offers sold in the room. ON24's report docs show no revenue figure, and Livestorm's analytics docs show none either. See EasyWebinar vs ON24 and EasyWebinar vs Livestorm."],[3089,"**Review** **Offers Performance** and **Revenue by Offer**, and adjust the pitch."],[3192,"**Roles match the work.** Admins handle billing and settings, while Users build and run webinars."],[3086,"**Run it live** with recording on. Push your enrolment offer with a countdown at the close."],[1935,"**Run it, then read the results.** Go live, or let the recording play, then open **Analytics** to see where people dropped off."],[1917,"**SaaS and product teams** run product demos and onboarding sessions as evergreen webinars that new users watch when it suits them."],[7982,"**Safer deletions.** The badge tells you whether a video depends on another platform before you remove anything."],[3381,"**Sales calls the right people first.** Watch percentage and offer clicks separate the interested from the curious."],[5852,"**Sales sessions** where attendees shouldn't see each other."],[6885,"**Same delivery every time.** A recording doesn't lose its place, run over or forget a point."],[3423,"**Save** keeps your work as a draft, and **Publish** makes it public. Custom registration fields covers each option. Ask only for what your follow-up will use: UK data protection law expects personal data to be used for specified, explicit purposes, so say on the page why you want a phone number."],[5733,"**Say what ends.** Use the headline or sub headline to state what expires: the bonus, the price or the enrolment window."],[7036,"**Schedule Preferences** decides how many session choices a registrant sees. With just-in-time and On Demand both enabled, it reads **Display Just-in-time & Instant-replay**. Turn on **Blackout Dates** and pick the days the webinar shouldn't run, such as holidays."],[495,"**Schedule set separately.** The drafts are timed relative to the webinar, so they send only once you've set the schedule."],[1934,"**Schedule the emails.** A common pattern is reminder emails a day, an hour and fifteen minutes before."],[301,"**Scheduling isn't generated.** Set sessions yourself after the build."],[9675,"**Scheduling Options changes the whole webinar.** For one sitting, use the options menu on that session's row."],[9600,"**Scheduling Options** summarises when the webinar runs:"],[701,"**Script, pages and emails in one build.** WebinarKit documents scripts in its AI Creator Suite, and EasyWebinar carries the same script on into the pages and the email sequence. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarKit."],[3286,"**Seats are part of your plan.** Adding people beyond your allowance costs more."],[118,"**Seats depend on your plan.** Adding a member costs more only if you have used all the seats your plan includes. Seat and role rules are also listed under team and account limits."],[5526,"**Select Easywebinar Chat** on **Engagement** → **Chat**. Simulated chat works with EasyWebinar's own chat panel; **Third party** replaces it."],[7436,"**Selling happens in the room.** Offers and polls are pushed from the same rail you use for chat and questions."],[3087,"**Send the replay** to no-shows, with the replay set to expire after a few days and **Webinar Replica** keeping the offer on it."],[3878,"**Sending before sending is set up.** In EasyCRM nothing goes out until a provider is connected and your sender is verified, so do it days before, not on the morning."],[3950,"**Sending has to be configured first.** Nothing goes out until a provider is connected and your sender is verified."],[1391,"**Sending health.** Look at **Sending health**, beside **EasyCRM Mail**, before you send through that service."],[1392,"**Sending identity.** Your domain or single address has finished verification."],[1442,"**Sending is part of the product.** EasyWebinar connects your service directly under **Configurations**, while Livestorm's guide sends your own emails through a Zapier automation. More in EasyWebinar vs Livestorm."],[1622,"**Sending is set up.** The sender is verified, or nothing goes out."],[1655,"**Sending must be set up first.** Until a provider is connected and your sender verified, no workflow goes out."],[1209,"**Sending setup comes first.** No broadcast or workflow goes out until email, SMS (Beta) or calling is set up under **Configurations**."],[1657,"**Sends count against your Wallet.** Workflows and broadcasts share one monthly allowance, and an automated sequence uses more over time than a one-off send."],[1452,"**Sends draw on a monthly allowance.** Emails, SMS (Beta) and call minutes are counted separately, so running out of one leaves the others working. The cycle follows your signup date, not the calendar month."],[5853,"**Sensitive topics** where people won't speak openly in public."],[2157,"**Separate data:** each client's webinars, registrants and settings stay apart from yours and from other clients'."],[2237,"**Separation as well as a domain:** EasyWebinar keeps each client's registrants in their own workspace, while Demio documents a custom domain for event pages. See EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[1650,"**Sequences that outlast the first email.** Demio sends a replay follow-up by audience, and EasyWebinar adds a published workflow that keeps running for weeks. EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[7425,"**Session history:** on the webinar's **Overview**, the session moves to the **Past** tab of the **Sessions** panel."],[9642,"**Session-level control.** You can act on one sitting from its row without rewriting the whole schedule."],[4867,"**Sessions minutes away.** EasyWebinar's just-in-time sessions follow each attendee's local time. Demio's automated event docs describe scheduled and on-demand sessions, with no just-in-time option documented. Compare EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[6924,"**Sessions run in the webinar's timezone,** whatever the in-app message on the schedule step says."],[5424,"**Sessions run on your schedule.** Sessions play at the times you set in the webinar's timezone. A registrant who can't make any of them needs an evergreen webinar instead."],[5905,"**Set chat before the webinar.** Chat settings are part of the webinar's setup, not the live room."],[7378,"**Set chat, Q&A and the attendee list in advance.** Who can see chat messages and how Q&A works are chosen on the webinar's **Engagement** tab. Whether attendees can see each other is **Show Attendees** on the **Settings** tab. These belong to the webinar's setup, not the live room, so decide them before the session."],[6217,"**Set Q&A before the webinar.** It's part of the webinar's setup rather than the live room."],[2823,"**Set the end-of-session page.** Point **End of Session** at the same page, so nobody is left on a finished webinar."],[7269,"**Set the look.** Backgrounds, blur, frame overlays and layout are on **Design**. Changes apply immediately, so set them here rather than mid-broadcast."],[271,"**Set the schedule.** The build doesn't schedule sessions for you; set them on the Overview tab."],[4871,"**Set times use the webinar's timezone.** Daily and weekly sessions don't shift to each attendee's local time; only just-in-time sessions do."],[1933,"**Set up chat and Q&A.** These sit on the **Engagement** tab and are set before the webinar runs, not during it."],[1932,"**Set up polls and offers.** Do this on the **CTAs** tab, and add a countdown timer to an offer if it has a deadline."],[3621,"**Set your deadlines.** Decide when the offer closes and when the replay closes, and write both down."],[1028,"**Set your schedule.** The AI doesn't choose your session times."],[9140,"**Settings** in the builder's top bar applies to the whole page rather than one block."],[7293,"**Several streams from one room.** EasyCast broadcasts to YouTube, LinkedIn or a custom RTMP destination at the same time, switched on in the green room. Zoom's help centre covers livestreaming webinars to YouTube, with no multi-destination streaming documented. More detail in EasyWebinar vs Zoom."],[7589,"**Share** in the top bar shares your screen. Two newer features make a shared screen easier to follow."],[685,"**Sharing.** Send people a one-click registration link once the page is published."],[9325,"**Short links for any channel.** EasyWebinar's shorter links work in posts, emails and show notes alike. WebinarKit documents its short link as a keyword for its text messages, covered in EasyWebinar vs WebinarKit."],[9324,"**Shorter links from the Share dialog.** EasyWebinar's **Shorten URL's** toggle gives you shorter versions of the webinar's links. WebinarJam's help centre doesn't document a link shortener, as the EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam and EverWebinar comparison shows."],[9280,"**Shorter links when you need them.** **Shorten URL's** makes links easier to fit in a post or a text."],[1064,"**Simulated chat is for recorded webinars.** Chat Simulation (Beta) runs on simulive and evergreen webinars, with AI or manual simulation, not both."],[4870,"**Simulive and evergreen need a recording.** Only live webinars run without one."],[302,"**Simulive and evergreen still need a video** after generation."],[3466,"**Simulive webinars** and **just-in-time sessions** capture registrants and their campaigns the same way."],[5201,"**Simulive webinars** are the other option when you clone: they broadcast the recording at set times while you staff the chat live."],[491,"**Six emails, no invitation.** The AI drafts the confirmation, reminders and follow-ups, but not the email that invites your list to register."],[5854,"**Small audiences**, where a quiet public chat looks worse than private conversations."],[1919,"**Small businesses and solo operators** handle the pages, emails and follow-up without a separate marketing stack."],[397,"**Small credit cost.** The email step uses 1 credit, one of the smallest parts of a build."],[3724,"**Small lists swing.** On a list of 50, three extra purchases can look like a big change. Look across several webinars before you rewrite a template."],[8611,"**SMS and WhatsApp come from an EasyWebinar number**, so replies don't reach your phone."],[8610,"**SMS and WhatsApp reminders are in Beta** and only reach people who gave a phone number on your registration form."],[8469,"**SMS and WhatsApp welcome messages are in Beta** and need the **Phone** field on your registration form."],[2849,"**SMS reminders (Beta)** only reach people whose phone number you have, so add the **Phone** field to your registration form. Messages come from an EasyWebinar number, not your own."],[1965,"**SMS, WhatsApp and Chat Simulation are in Beta.**"],[3054,"**SMS** and **WhatsApp** reminders (both in Beta) suit the final reminder before a session, when an email may sit unread."],[9308,"**Social Sharing** on the webinar's **Settings** tab, and **Social Sharing (Open Graph)** in the page builder, control how your link looks when someone shares it."],[7665,"**Some features depend on plan.** EasyCast and offer checkout start at Growth."],[1963,"**Some features start on higher plans.** Automation, EasyCRM, checkout and EasyCast start at Growth, and the AI Moderator starts at Pro. The limits and defaults page lists the allowances."],[4499,"**Source & UTM** only has something to filter if your registration form records it. To set that up:"],[3485,"**Source read against attendance.** EasyWebinar's **Source & UTM** filter sits beside status and watch percentage, while WebinarKit tracks traffic source through URL parameters you add. EasyWebinar vs WebinarKit"],[7035,"**Start Date** is the day the schedule begins. Leave **End Date** on **No end date** if the webinar should keep running indefinitely, or set a date for a campaign with a finish."],[5190,"**Start Date** sets when the schedule begins, and **No end date** keeps it running. **Blackout Dates** stops it on particular days. Daily and weekly sessions run in the webinar's timezone, while just-in-time sessions start in each attendee's local time."],[7981,"**Storage is visible.** The figure at the top of each tab, and the badge on each video, show what uses your allowance."],[7836,"**Storage:** recordings are hosted in the Library and count towards your allowance. Extra space is an add-on, listed on pricing."],[7857,"**Storage.** Recordings are hosted in the Library and count towards your storage allowance."],[9498,"**Stripe is the payment processor** for paid registration."],[2892,"**Stripe.** Paid registration needs a connected Stripe account, and attendees pay through a secure Stripe checkout with the money going to you."],[1815,"**Strong signals stand out.** **Watched full** and **Clicked offer** sit apart from a plain registration."],[6346,"**Sub headline**: the detail that removes doubt, such as what's included, who it's for or when it closes."],[3869,"**Subject line options (pick one):**"],[7270,"**Switch on any EasyCast destinations.** Click **EasyCast** in the top bar and turn **Stream** on for each channel this session should reach."],[1850,"**Tags and custom fields must exist in your CRM first.** Use **Refresh** after adding a field."],[1844,"**Tags for how long people stayed.** EasyWebinar's **Stayed on webinar at least** and **Watched full** each apply their own tag. Livestorm's HubSpot article describes sending registrant and attendee data to HubSpot. See EasyWebinar vs Livestorm."],[3460,"**Tags missing in the CRM.** The event mapping can only select tags that already exist there, so create them first."],[1845,"**Tags without a separate tool.** EasyWebinar's **When**, **Then** and **Value** choices tag contacts directly from the webinar. eWebinar's CRM guide also covers connecting products it doesn't integrate with directly through Zapier. See EasyWebinar vs eWebinar."],[9620,"**Team & Moderators** shows everyone who can run this webinar. On a new webinar it reads \"No presenters or moderators added yet.\""],[1188,"**Team members.** Colleagues sign in with their own team member logins."],[3468,"**Team members** let colleagues in sales or operations work in the same account and read the People view."],[9190,"**Templates are per page, and switching replaces the layout.** Choose before detailed editing."],[9186,"**Templates come sorted by business type.** EasyWebinar sorts templates by business type, while Livestorm applies one set of design settings to its Detailed and Light pages. More in EasyWebinar vs Livestorm."],[9025,"**Test it after pasting.** Register once and check **Registrants** on the Overview before you send traffic to the page."],[7267,"**Test Share** with the window or screen you'll actually present."],[6523,"**Testing a change safely.** Try a different registration page or offer on a copy, leaving the webinar that's already running alone."],[8895,"**Text reminders depend on the Phone field.** SMS and WhatsApp are in Beta."],[8890,"**Text reminders need no SMS account of your own.** EasyWebinar's SMS reminders (Beta) come from an EasyWebinar number, while WebinarJam asks you to connect your own Twilio account. Read EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam."],[703,"**Thank-you and waiting pages written too.** Livestorm applies one set of design settings across its registration pages, and EasyWebinar writes the copy for the thank-you and waiting pages as well. See EasyWebinar vs Livestorm."],[3658,"**Thanking people who didn't come.** Check who each email goes to before you paste in the words. \"Thanks for joining me\" sent to a no-show undoes the rest of the message."],[1063,"**The AI doesn't set your schedule or video.** You add session times, and for simulive or evergreen webinars, a video."],[7113,"**The AI Moderator is in Beta.**"],[1658,"**The allowance resets on your signup date**, not the first of the month. When a channel runs out, it stops sending until the cycle resets."],[1623,"**The allowance will cover it.** Count the emails the sequence sends this cycle, as in the worked example."],[5911,"**The attendee list is a separate setting.** **Show Attendees** is on the **Settings** tab."],[8696,"**The button speaks your language.** **Instant replay text** lets you word the button to match your page."],[6302,"**The card attendees see**: a headline and sub headline, as a text offer or an image offer."],[5825,"**The chat mode** decides whether there is a chat panel, and whose chat it is: EasyWebinar's built-in panel, an external tool embedded in the room, or none."],[3746,"**The click is enough.** EasyWebinar's **Attendee Action Follow-ups** respond to the offer click. WebinarJam's purchase filters need tracking codes in your sales funnel. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam and EverWebinar."],[6220,"**The contact box is separate.** Contact box questions go to an email address, not to the **Question** panel."],[6563,"**The copy's type is fixed once created.** Check the summary at the bottom of the dialog before you click **Clone Webinar**."],[9187,"**The countdown is native, not a widget.** EasyWebinar builds it into the page, while eWebinar delivers its countdown through widgets on your own landing page. Read EasyWebinar vs eWebinar."],[5744,"**The countdown is on the registration page.** EasyWebinar's countdown is a block on the page people sign up on. WebinarJam's help docs describe its countdown on a separate holding page for people who open the live link early. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam and EverWebinar."],[6407,"**The countdown is per offer.** Polls have no countdown setting."],[9184,"**The countdown sits on the page you promote.** EasyWebinar adds it to every new registration page, while WebinarJam shows its start countdown on a separate holding page. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam."],[3448,"**The date range applies to everything on the page.** Widen it if a webinar looks emptier than you expected."],[4682,"**The date range covers the whole page.** Widen it if numbers look low."],[4370,"**The device check is part of entering.** EasyWebinar won't let you into the green room until it can see a camera and a microphone. Demio's device troubleshooting starts with running a System Check as a separate step. See EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[4265,"**The ending is planned.** Attendees are sent to a page you chose, and the recording is waiting in your library."],[3744,"**The first email can go today.** EasyWebinar's follow-ups can send right after the webinar ends. Zoom's follow-up email can be sent 1 to 7 days after the webinar start time. See EasyWebinar vs Zoom."],[8742,"**The full webinar, inside the same event.** EasyWebinar's **On Demand** plays the webinar's own recording from the evergreen schedule. StealthSeminar's in-event choice, Watch Yesterday's Replay, plays the previous session, and fully on-demand viewing is its own event type. Compare EasyWebinar vs StealthSeminar."],[7297,"**The green room broadcasts nothing.** The header reads **Not Live** until you go live."],[7110,"**The interval options are fixed:** 2, 15, 30, 45 or 60 minutes."],[2909,"**The invitation happens in the room.** EasyWebinar shows your booking or application button during the session. Kajabi's Zoom webinar funnel makes the pitch afterwards, with follow-up emails that link to the sales page. See EasyWebinar vs Kajabi."],[8547,"**The last reminder does most of the work.** In EasyWebinar's guidance, the one fifteen minutes before matters most."],[7833,"**The Library:** finished sessions land on its **Recordings** tab, next to your videos, images and files."],[3265,"**The Library.** Recordings of past live sessions sit in the Library, ready for an evergreen copy."],[8168,"**The link is public while the page is enabled.** Anyone with the **Replay Page Link** can watch."],[1621,"**The list is the right one.** Open the list tab and check who is on it, especially the no-show list."],[5216,"**The live recording is already in your library.** EasyWebinar records live sessions for reuse when **Auto Recording** is on, while StealthSeminar says you must manually upload the recording. See EasyWebinar vs StealthSeminar."],[7832,"**The live room:** recording state shows in the header, and the setting sits under **Settings** in the live room."],[5128,"**The live webinar stays as it was.** Its registrants, attendees and results are not touched."],[427,"**The merge tags.** After you rewrite a sentence, make sure the date, time and join link tags are still in it."],[2604,"**The money lands in your own account.** Stripe pays out to your bank on its usual schedule."],[2802,"**The next step is in the room.** An offer button opens your booking page or application while interest is highest."],[6222,"**The Not Answered Rate is after the fact.** Use **Active** in the room to see what's waiting while you're live."],[424,"**The offer and the price.** EasyWebinar's own guidance is to check that pages and emails say what you want, especially around pricing and what's included."],[5748,"**The offer countdown is set per offer.** Each offer has its own **Countdown timer** switch."],[4050,"**The offer gets its room.** Planning the bridge and the offer as real sections stops them shrinking to a final slide."],[6403,"**The offer inside the webinar room.** EasyWebinar pushes the card to attendees from the room's **Offers** panel. Kajabi's webinar funnel can run on any webinar host, such as Zoom, linked into the funnel. More detail in EasyWebinar vs Kajabi."],[2336,"**The offer sits in the room.** Attendees click a button while they're still watching."],[9329,"**The one-click link only works for known contacts.** It carries name and email in the URL."],[9019,"**The one-click link sits beside the widget.** EasyWebinar's **Share** dialog holds both, while Demio describes one-click links as part of its CRM integrations. More in EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[428,"**The opening line.** Start each email with what the reader needs, such as the time and the link, before any sales copy."],[1061,"**The output is a draft.** Everything is editable, and you still review the script, prices and inclusions before publishing."],[121,"**The Owner can't be changed from the Team screen.** Contact support if ownership needs to move."],[3284,"**The Owner can't be changed from the Team screen.** Contact support if ownership needs to move."],[597,"**The pages match the session.** The copy comes from your script, so the headline and learning points describe the talk you'll give."],[821,"**The pages say the same thing.** When the registration page is written from the script, what you promise matches what you teach."],[3101,"**The pitch happens in the room.** EasyWebinar shows the enrolment offer during the session. Kajabi's Zoom funnel makes the pitch afterwards, through follow-up emails that link to the sales page. See EasyWebinar vs Kajabi."],[6310,"**The pitch keeps working on the replay.** With a **Webinar Replica** replay, the same offer appears on the recording."],[9192,"**The price block is added at creation.** Converting a free webinar to paid later doesn't add it."],[9635,"**The pricing is right.** **Registration Pricing** shows **Free**, or your pricing title, price and a connected **Payment Gateway**."],[4372,"**The private room is a standard step.** Every EasyWebinar live session starts in a green room that broadcasts nothing. WebinarNinja lists a practice session on its plans. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarNinja."],[300,"**The prompt sets the quality.** Vague prompts produce generic webinars."],[5126,"**The proven version runs.** The recording is the session that already worked, not a fresh take that might not."],[9426,"**The recording can be sold too.** A **Live + Replay bundle** gives buyers a further choice that includes the recording, priced separately."],[7437,"**The recording is automatic.** With recording on, the session lands in your Library without an extra step."],[8747,"**The recording is the webinar's.** An evergreen webinar plays the recording chosen on its video step; change it from the **Webinar Video** panel on the **Content** tab."],[682,"**The registration form.** Add custom registration fields, turn on **GDPR Compliance** for a consent checkbox, or turn on **UTM Params** so each registration records the campaign behind it."],[9328,"**The registration link needs a published page.** Publish the registration page before you promote the link."],[8467,"**The registration page must be published.** Until it is, the registration link doesn't work and no confirmations go out."],[5750,"**The registration-page countdown is a page block.** It can be hidden on mobile with **Desktop Only** visibility, styled, or removed like any other block."],[2605,"**The replay becomes a second product.** You can sell live access alone or live access with the recording."],[2701,"**The replay has its own price.** EasyWebinar's **Live + Replay bundle** sells the recording as a second option. Zoom's recording access comes as complimentary viewing included with the ticket. See EasyWebinar vs Zoom."],[9331,"**The replay link is public while the replay page is on.** Anyone with it can watch."],[5829,"**The room feels alive.** With **Everyone** selected, attendees see each other's messages and can reply to each other."],[5514,"**The room never opens empty.** Messages can appear within seconds of the video starting."],[5317,"**The room still feels shared.** Everyone watches the same moment, so chat questions make sense to the whole audience."],[3073,"**The room:** backgrounds, overlays and layout in the live room's **Design** panel."],[2420,"**The sale happens in the room.** EasyWebinar shows a timed offer card during the session, while Kajabi's webinar funnel runs on a host such as Zoom. See EasyWebinar vs Kajabi."],[4778,"**The same room tools.** Chat, Q&A, polls, offers, emails and analytics work as they do on a live webinar."],[6557,"**The schedule can travel with it.** Ticking **Webinar schedule** in EasyWebinar brings the sessions to the copy. Demio says none of the sessions are copied, which leaves a blank schedule. See EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[9634,"**The schedule is right.** **Scheduling Options** shows the frequency, start date and timezone you expect, and the **Upcoming** tab lists the sittings you meant to run."],[7070,"**The schedule maintains itself.** A **Daily** or **Weekly** schedule keeps generating sessions from its **Start Date**, with no end unless you set one."],[5034,"**The schedule step's timezone message is broader than the behaviour.** Rely on the table above, not the in-app message."],[922,"**The script feeds your pages.** WebinarKit documents building a slide deck from the script. EasyWebinar writes the registration, thank-you and waiting pages from the script as well. EasyWebinar vs WebinarKit"],[926,"**The script is a draft.** The AI writes from your prompt, so a vague prompt produces a generic script. Read every line, especially anything about pricing and what your offer includes."],[201,"**The script is presentation-ready.** It comes in named sections, each with a timing and speaker notes, and downloads as a PDF."],[928,"**The script step costs credits.** It uses 10 credits, and the script and landing pages are the most expensive steps of a full build."],[8465,"**The sender name is a display name.** Replies go to the **Reply-to email** you set."],[425,"**The sender.** Set a sender name people will recognise in **Email Settings**. Nielsen Norman Group found that unrecognisable sender information was the top reason people gave for not opening email."],[9424,"**The session earns in its own right.** Every attendee has bought a seat, so the webinar brings in money before it starts."],[2337,"**The session keeps working.** A live session can be cloned into an automated one that runs on a schedule."],[7059,"**The Sessions list fills itself.** A daily schedule produces a long run of upcoming sessions with no manual entry."],[7232,"**The stage changes on your cue.** You decide when each person appears, so handovers between speakers look planned."],[7435,"**The start is controlled.** Nothing is broadcast until you confirm **Go Live**, and people in the waiting area are moved in automatically when you do."],[7233,"**The start is deliberate.** The broadcast begins only when you click **Go Live** and confirm."],[5679,"**The start time counts down too.** A countdown on the registration page gives a visitor a reason to register now rather than bookmark the page."],[426,"**The subject lines.** Put the useful words first. Inboxes cut subject lines short, and Nielsen Norman Group suggests showing no more than about 40 characters."],[9636,"**The team is in place.** **Team & Moderators** lists your presenters and moderators instead of \"No presenters or moderators added yet.\""],[4264,"**The timed pieces fire.** Reminders, polls and offers are checked before they are needed."],[7058,"**The timezone reads Attendee's local timezone** when just-in-time is on, because those sessions start shortly after each person registers, in their own time."],[6406,"**The title is internal.** Attendees see the headline and sub headline."],[226,"**The tone you want.**"],[637,"**The tone you want.**"],[882,"**The tone** you want."],[7658,"**The type is fixed.** A live webinar can't become simulive or evergreen. Clone it and choose the new type on the copy."],[6739,"**The type is fixed.** Clone the webinar and choose another type on the copy."],[7107,"**The type is fixed.** To change an evergreen webinar into another type, or a live one into evergreen, clone it."],[8748,"**The type is fixed.** To offer On Demand for a live or simulive webinar, clone it as Evergreen."],[5035,"**The type is fixed.** To use just-in-time with a webinar that is currently live or simulive, clone it as Evergreen."],[4869,"**The type is fixed.** You can't change a webinar's type after creating it; clone it instead."],[5422,"**The type is fixed.** You can't convert a simulive webinar to another type. Clone it and choose a different type on the copy."],[6922,"**The type is fixed.** You can't convert a simulive webinar to live or evergreen. Clone it and choose the new type on the copy. See Clone a webinar."],[6917,"**The video lives with the webinar.** With **Local import**, EasyWebinar stores and serves the file, so no YouTube or Vimeo account is involved. EverWebinar's help centre lists an external video as its primary source. See EasyWebinar vs EverWebinar."],[1962,"**The webinar type is fixed after creation.** Clone the webinar to change it."],[9674,"**The webinar type is fixed.** It can't be changed from the Overview or anywhere else after creation. Clone the webinar instead."],[2705,"**The webinar type is fixed.** Live, simulive and evergreen can't be swapped later. Clone the webinar to change it."],[305,"**The webinar type is fixed** once the webinar is created, so set **Type** before generating."],[8320,"**The webinar video itself, from a link.** In EasyWebinar, an imported link becomes the video your sessions play. Demio's docs describe YouTube, Vimeo and Wistia URLs for the registration page video. See EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[8164,"**The whole offer, not one button.** **Webinar Replica** repeats the live video, offers, polls and chat replay. Demio's replay page carries a single Call-to-Action window. See EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[924,"**The whole script, not just the notes.** Zoom documents AI that generates speaker notes for Zoom Slides. EasyWebinar writes the full script slide by slide, in named, timed sections. EasyWebinar vs Zoom"],[9020,"**The widget has its own look.** Livestorm's form embed inherits the page's branding, while EasyWebinar's widget is customised on its own. Read EasyWebinar vs Livestorm."],[9022,"**The widget is a form, not the whole page.** When you want EasyWebinar's page to do the selling, send the registration page link instead."],[702,"**The words, not only the layout.** WebinarJam documents templates for each page type, and EasyWebinar also writes the copy that goes into the template. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam."],[2158,"**Their brand, not ours:** pages run on the client's address with no EasyWebinar branding."],[7472,"**Theme is personal.** Light, dark or system changes your view, not the attendees'."],[1851,"**There are 14 integrations**, including EasyWebinar's own EasyCRM."],[7060,"**There is a Live tab** in the Sessions panel next to **Upcoming**, **Past** and **Cancelled**. Evergreen webinars have it; it shows sessions on air at that moment."],[1968,"**There is no free plan.** The standard trial is 7 days and requires a card."],[6561,"**There is no in-place conversion.** The type of an existing webinar can't be changed; only a copy can have a different type."],[119,"**There is no per-permission matrix.** Access is set by role alone; custom roles were not available at the time of checking."],[2512,"**There's no recording yet.** Simulive and Evergreen need a recording, but Live webinars don't. If you haven't recorded anything, run it live first and use that recording later."],[8576,"**They come from an EasyWebinar number**, not your own."],[3722,"**They count people, not emails.** **Replay Watched** tells you someone watched. It can't show on its own which email brought them back."],[3846,"**They fill seats before you pay for any other promotion.** Your list costs nothing extra to email."],[3847,"**They give you a number to beat.** Opens and clicks show whether the subject or the offer is the weak part."],[8575,"**They need a phone number.** Add the **Phone** field to your registration form, or there is nobody to message."],[3845,"**They reach your warmest audience first.** People who already know your work are the likeliest to register."],[3848,"**They set up the rest of the sequence.** Every registrant they bring in gets your confirmation and reminders automatically."],[5906,"**Third party is for recorded webinars only.** A live webinar offers **Easywebinar Chat** or **No Chat**."],[5349,"**Third party** embeds an external chat tool, such as Chatroll or Intercom, from its embed snippet."],[5425,"**Third-party chat replaces the built-in chat.** With **Third party** selected, AI Moderation and simulated chat don't apply, and messages go to your chat tool rather than EasyWebinar."],[5907,"**Third-party messages stay in your tool.** EasyWebinar doesn't receive them, so reply from the tool's own dashboard."],[598,"**Three pages arrive in one pass.** The registration, thank-you and waiting pages are written together, in one voice."],[1450,"**Three SMTP providers are offered.** They are Amazon SES, SendGrid and Mailgun, and each needs your own account with that company."],[9427,"**Ticket income is kept apart.** **Revenue by Source** separates paid registrations from offers sold in the room."],[4049,"**Time stays honest.** Each section has a budget, so you can see an overrun on paper before it happens on air."],[4777,"**Times that fit your audience.** Registrants pick a session, and just-in-time sessions follow their local time."],[5604,"**Timestamps run from the start of the video**, not from the clock time of the session."],[8607,"**Timing is relative to the webinar**, not a fixed clock time. Set it in hours, minutes and seconds before the session."],[4096,"**Timing only the teaching.** If the bridge, the offer and the questions have no minutes against them, they lose out first."],[8603,"**Timing to the minute.** EasyWebinar takes timings such as *0h 15m 0s before webinar*. Zoom's reminder email offers 1 hour, 1 day or 1 week before the start, as EasyWebinar vs Zoom shows."],[7567,"**Timing you control:** you launch each poll and push each offer at the moment the talk earns it."],[6347,"**Title**: a name your team will recognise in the CTAs list, since attendees never see it."],[9581,"**To charge for registration, have Stripe ready.** Converting a webinar to paid needs a connected Stripe account. Read the warning about converting in Step 4 below before you use it."],[9582,"**To go live, have a camera and microphone.** **Enter Room** checks both before letting you in."],[9655,"**Total Attended** includes replay viewers, and the **Attendee Replay link** sits in the Share dialog. Replay availability and design are set on the **Replay** tab."],[3491,"**Tracking code is set per page**, and none of it applies until you click **Save Changes**."],[275,"**Tune the offers.** Add a countdown timer to an offer with a real deadline, or adjust the button URL."],[3659,"**Two different deadlines.** The date in your email has to match the replay page's closing date and the offer. Check all three together."],[3881,"**Two different links.** One link, repeated, gives you a click count you can trust."],[1443,"**Two routes to a verified sender.** EasyWebinar accepts a dedicated domain or a single business address on the same screen, while eWebinar's SendGrid steps run through verification in SendGrid. More in EasyWebinar vs eWebinar."],[6071,"**Two switches control visibility.** The row toggle in the CTAs list and the **Published** switch in the editor both decide whether a poll is live."],[6408,"**Two switches control visibility**: the toggle in the CTAs list and **Published** in the editor."],[7568,"**Two uses from one session:** the recording can become an evergreen webinar's video once the live run is done."],[3447,"**Untagged links show no campaign.** People who arrived by a plain link sit outside every campaign filter."],[8322,"**Upload MP4, up to 4 GB.** The **Video Selection** screen lists MP4, MOV or WebM, but the **Upload media** dialog says it supports MP4 files only, so upload MP4 to be safe."],[8015,"**Upload video as MP4, up to 4 GB.** The **Video Selection** screen lists MP4, MOV or WebM, but the **Upload media** dialog says it supports MP4 files only, so upload MP4 to be safe."],[8012,"**Uploads and links side by side.** **Add Media** offers **Local import** and **Import from URL** on every tab. WebinarKit says direct uploads apply if your plan includes them. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarKit."],[6929,"**Uploads count towards storage.** Imported links use none. Extra storage is available as an add-on."],[2004,"**Usage resets with your billing period**, so the meters show the current period only."],[5525,"**Use a simulive or evergreen webinar.** Chat simulation isn't available on live webinars."],[3403,"**Use lowercase every time.** Values are case sensitive, so \"LinkedIn\" and \"linkedin\" count as two different sources."],[3488,"**UTM filtering needs UTM capture turned on** on the registration form, and only registrations made while it was on carry a campaign."],[8893,"**UTM filtering needs UTM capture.** The **Source & UTM** filter depends on **UTM Params** being on in your registration form."],[4530,"**UTM filtering needs UTM capture** turned on in your registration form."],[3457,"**UTM Params left off.** The **Source & UTM** filter has nothing to show. Make one tagged registration of your own before launch and find it in People."],[8845,"**UTM Params** is a switch on the form block. Once it's on, each registration records the campaign that brought it in."],[1449,"**Verification comes first.** Nothing sends until your domain or address is verified, and no setting skips this step."],[7103,"**Video hosting in the same flow.** With **Local import**, EasyWebinar hosts the video itself, so you don't need a YouTube or Vimeo account. EverWebinar's help centre says an external video source is required. See EasyWebinar vs EverWebinar."],[8170,"**Viewers go nowhere at the end** unless you set **After the replay ends**."],[4684,"**Visitors are unique IPs** on your landing page."],[3445,"**Visitors counts unique IPs on the landing page.** Several colleagues on one office network may count as one visitor, so treat registration rate as a guide."],[3492,"**Visitors counts unique IPs** on the landing page, not individual people."],[1425,"**Wallet.** Email, SMS (Beta) and call minutes each have a monthly allowance, listed with the other limits and defaults. Workflows use more over time than broadcasts, because they keep sending every day."],[1635,"**Wallet.** Workflows and broadcasts draw on the same monthly allowance for emails, SMS (Beta) and call minutes."],[2803,"**Warm leads sort themselves.** Watch time and offer clicks show who stayed for the pitch."],[5027,"**Watch now, soon or at a set time.** EasyWebinar's **On Demand** starts the recording straight away, beside just-in-time and set times. StealthSeminar's instant choice, Watch Yesterday's Replay, plays the previous session. Compare EasyWebinar vs StealthSeminar."],[4526,"**Watch time as a filter.** EasyWebinar filters people by watch time and offer clicks. eWebinar's help centre doesn't describe filtering people by watch time. See EasyWebinar vs eWebinar."],[1630,"**Webinar follow-up emails.** Each webinar's own **Webinar Follow-ups** cover the first message, and a workflow carries the sequence after it. Reminder emails handle the days before the session."],[4142,"**Webinar follow-up emails** send what your close promised."],[1578,"**Webinar follow-up.** Attendees get one message and no-shows get the replay. It runs after every webinar without you touching it."],[4656,"**Webinar Follow-ups** on the **Notifications** tab can go to everyone who registered, only attendees, or only no-shows, which matches the **Missed** number directly. **Attendee Action Follow-ups** send based on engagement and whether someone clicked an offer."],[2847,"**Webinar Follow-ups** send after the webinar, to registrants, attendees or no-shows. Send no-shows the replay with its closing date."],[9166,"**Webinar Language**, **Date Display Language**, **Date Format** and **Time Format** on the webinar's **Settings** tab control how the webinar reads to attendees. Set them before you promote, so the registration page and emails match. EasyWebinar doesn't translate your own copy; the page says whatever you wrote."],[468,"**Webinar reminder emails:** the three drafted reminders, plus SMS (Beta) and WhatsApp (Beta) options."],[8532,"**Webinar Reminders** are the emails EasyWebinar sends to registrants before the session starts. Each reminder has its own timing, set as a length of time before the webinar, so the same reminders work for a one-off session, a recurring schedule or an evergreen webinar. You can add as many as you need from the **Notifications** tab, and Analytics shows whether they are working: the gap between people who registered and people who attended is the reminders' job."],[3053,"**Webinar Reminders**, timed relative to the session, so they work on evergreen schedules too. A sensible default is a day before, an hour before and fifteen minutes before."],[2668,"**Webinar Replica** gives replay viewers the same video, offers, polls and chat replay as the live session. **Custom Build** lets you design a different page. The replay page settings cover both, along with **After the replay ends**, which sends viewers on when the recording finishes."],[905,"**Webinar types.** The script works for live webinars, simulive webinars and evergreen webinars. Set **Type** before you generate."],[3289,"**Webinars are archived, not deleted.** They move to the **Archived** tab and keep their records."],[3194,"**Webinars are easy to find.** Type filters, search and archiving keep a long list short."],[635,"**What it covers.** Name the three or four things you'll actually teach."],[224,"**What it covers.** The three or four things you'll actually teach."],[880,"**What it covers.** The three or four things you'll actually teach."],[638,"**What you're selling at the end, and the price.**"],[227,"**What you're selling at the end,** and the price."],[883,"**What you're selling** at the end, and the price."],[1451,"**WhatsApp (Beta) isn't on this screen yet.** The **Whatsapp** tab in EasyCRM is marked **Coming soon**."],[8605,"**WhatsApp for the final nudge.** EasyWebinar's Beta **Reminder Message** on the **Whatsapp** tab sends before the webinar starts. WebinarJam's reminders run by email, SMS or voice call, as EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam and EverWebinar sets out."],[4094,"**Where to click when you share a link**, if you plan to show an offer or a download."],[4093,"**Whether there is a replay**, and how people will get it."],[5863,"**Whether they can see each other**: the attendee list, set with **Show Attendees** on the webinar's **Settings** tab."],[5862,"**Whether they can talk**: chat, set on the **Engagement** tab."],[7423,"**While live:** the header shows **LIVE** with a running timer and the **Recording** badge. With EasyCast on, there's one platform icon per destination."],[5910,"**Who can see messages applies to everything attendees post.**"],[5826,"**Who can see messages** decides whether the chat is a shared room or a set of private conversations with your team. It applies to everything attendees post."],[879,"**Who it's for, specifically.** \"Experienced freelance designers stuck at capacity\" works better than \"designers\"."],[223,"**Who it's for, specifically.** \"Experienced freelance designers stuck at capacity\", not \"designers\"."],[634,"**Who it's for, specifically.** \"Owners of young dogs that pull on the lead\" gives the AI more than \"dog owners\"."],[295,"**Whole pages written from the script.** EasyWebinar writes the registration, thank-you and waiting-area pages in one step. eWebinar's AI rewrites registration page sections one at a time. See EasyWebinar vs eWebinar."],[8318,"**Wistia links work as well.** EasyWebinar imports from **YouTube**, **Vimeo**, **Wistia** or a direct **MP4 link**. WebinarKit's help asks for direct Vimeo file links rather than regular Vimeo links, and its built-in hosting is a Pro feature. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarKit."],[7243,"**With a join link.** Click **Share** on the webinar and copy the link for the role:"],[1654,"**Workflows send only once published.** A draft sends nothing, by design."],[1656,"**Workflows send to saved lists.** A filtered view has to be saved as a list before a workflow can use it."],[1424,"**Workflows.** A workflow is an automated sequence, and webinar follow-up is the sensible first one to build. It keeps sending once published, so it relies on these settings for as long as it runs."],[3623,"**Write the attendee thank-you.** Reuse the replay line, then add the one idea and the offer."],[3624,"**Write the last call.** Make one version for attendees and one for no-shows."],[3622,"**Write the no-show replay email.** It's the shortest, and no-shows are usually your biggest group."],[3625,"**Write the two day-after emails.** Pull one real question from your session for the attendee version, and one strong moment from the recording for the no-show version."],[8852,"**Write the wording yourself.** Say what the person is agreeing to, in your own words."],[4052,"**Writing gets faster.** A script, a registration page and follow-up emails are all easier to write from one agreed outline."],[8577,"**You build them from templates** grouped by tone, then edit the words."],[9501,"**You can change the price later** with the pencil on **Registration Pricing** in the Overview tab."],[9105,"**You can check the phone layout.** The device toggle shows the mobile version without leaving the builder."],[5831,"**You can make it private.** **Hosts only** turns chat into one-to-one conversations with your team when attendees shouldn't see each other."],[7434,"**You can prepare in private.** The green room lets you fix audio, lighting and screen sharing with nobody watching."],[6154,"**You can see what's left.** The **Active** and **Answered** split in the room, and the **Not Answered Rate** afterwards, show what you didn't get to."],[6312,"**You can see where it loses people.** Separate counts for views, clicks and purchases show whether to fix the offer or the checkout."],[6887,"**You can still be there.** You and your moderators answer questions in the chat while the video plays."],[8578,"**You can test first.** **Send Test SMS** and **Send Test Message** send the selected template to your own number. Pick your country from the flag dropdown rather than typing a dialling code."],[6741,"**You can't schedule a session in the past.**"],[6925,"**You can't schedule a session in the past.**"],[5516,"**You choose how much control to keep.** **AI Simulation** fills a room naturally, while **Manual Simulation** plays exactly what you wrote."],[3280,"**You choose what a copy takes.** EasyWebinar lets you tick pages, schedule, replay settings, polls, offers, emails and integrations one by one. Livestorm documents that a duplicated event keeps its access settings. See EasyWebinar vs Livestorm."],[5215,"**You choose what the copy brings.** EasyWebinar's clone lets you tick pages, schedule, polls, offers, emails and integrations, while a Demio duplicate copies no sessions. See EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[5318,"**You choose when to show up.** Join the chat for the sessions that matter and skip the rest, because the recording plays either way."],[9104,"**You edit what you see.** Changes happen on the canvas, with a settings panel for the block you select."],[83,"**You know who did what.** Separate logins replace a shared one, which leaves you guessing."],[6556,"**You pick what comes across.** EasyWebinar lists eight items under **What would you like to copy?**, each one optional. StealthSeminar's help centre says its duplicate is a full copy of the original event. See EasyWebinar vs Stealth Seminar."],[2511,"**You picked the wrong format.** You can't change the type later. Clone the webinar and choose the right type on the copy. Cloning is also how you turn a live webinar into an evergreen one, as the guide to turning a live session into an evergreen one explains."],[3283,"**You set each teammate's password.** There is no invitation to accept, so you pass the login on yourself."],[5125,"**You skip the rebuild.** The clone can bring across your registration pages, polls, offers and email notifications in one step."],[818,"**You start from a draft.** A template or an AI draft gives you sections to react to, which is faster than writing the first line from nothing."],[5832,"**You stay reachable without chat.** Choose **No Chat** and attendees can still contact you through the contact box."],[5316,"**You stop presenting the same talk.** Record it once, at your best, and let every later session play that version."],[9017,"**You style the widget, not the code.** EasyWebinar's **View & Customize** changes the widget's look before you copy it. WebinarJam puts style parameters inside the embed code itself. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam."],[2514,"**Your audience speaks another language.** Language is set per webinar, so each webinar can run in its own language. Language settings don't translate your content, though, so write your pages and emails in your audience's language."],[2338,"**Your contacts stay where you keep them, in your CRM or ours.** Keep HubSpot, Salesforce Pardot (Account Engagement), ActiveCampaign, Mailchimp or Kit (formerly ConvertKit), or use EasyCRM natively."],[5200,"**Your CRM or email tool** keeps receiving data when you copy the integration settings."],[2891,"**Your CRM or ours.** EasyWebinar connects to 14 CRM and email tools, including GoHighLevel and Keap, and tags contacts by what they did. The CRM mapping guide shows the event and field mappings. If you'd rather not run a separate CRM, EasyCRM keeps contacts and follow-up beside your webinars."],[1203,"**Your CRM or ours.** eWebinar documents direct integrations with HubSpot and MailChimp. EasyWebinar connects to fourteen integrations and adds EasyCRM for teams without one. EasyWebinar vs eWebinar"],[1651,"**Your CRM or ours.** WebinarJam sends data to a connected CRM by rule, and EasyWebinar does that too while also offering its own CRM. EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam."],[1816,"**Your CRM sends the reminders.** A mapped join link gives each contact their own working link."],[3383,"**Your CRM stays the record.** Registrants and attendees sync as separate events, so each group gets its own tag."],[472,"**Your CRM:** keep the CRM you already use and pass webinar data to it."],[3264,"**Your CRM.** Integration settings come across in a clone, so each new webinar keeps sending data where the last one did. The mapping is on connect a CRM."],[3596,"**Your deadline stays visible.** A short last call tells people when the replay or offer closes."],[3074,"**Your domain:** the **C-Name** add-on puts webinar pages on your own domain."],[5129,"**Your integrations come with it.** Integration settings are one of the items you can copy."],[2515,"**Your leads stay in the webinar tool.** Plan where contacts go before you run the session. You can bring registrants and attendees into EasyCRM, or send them to the CRM you already use."],[3943,"**Your list and your send in one place.** EasyWebinar sends the invitation from EasyCRM, while Demio's one-click link is added to emails from your integrated CRM. See EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[6918,"**Your live sessions become content.** The **Recordings** filter on the video step lists your past EasyWebinar sessions. EverWebinar needs an active WebinarJam subscription to import a live session. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam and EverWebinar."],[820,"**Your notes match your slides.** Speaker notes per slide mean you know what to say when each slide appears."],[2893,"**Your own booking, application and checkout pages.** The offer button and end-of-session redirect open any link, so payment plans and booking rules stay in the tools you already use."],[5902,"**Your own chat tool in the room.** EasyWebinar's **Third party** option takes your provider's embed snippet on simulive and evergreen webinars. Demio's help centre doesn't document embedding a third-party chat tool. See EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[1187,"**Your own CRM.** Any of the fourteen integrations can take the webinar data instead. The CRM integration tracking post explains how teams track leads that way."],[1427,"**Your own CRM.** You may prefer to send from the CRM you already use. In that case, skip this setup, since you don't need EasyCRM to run webinars."],[8010,"**Your own live sessions, kept.** EasyWebinar saves recordings of your live webinars straight into the Library. eWebinar imports cloud recordings from a connected Zoom account, and notes that Zoom only surfaces recordings under a month old. See EasyWebinar vs eWebinar."],[8319,"**Your own live sessions, ready to reuse.** Recordings of your live webinars land in **Library → Recordings** and appear in the video picker. eWebinar's import route lists recent cloud recordings from a connected Zoom account. See EasyWebinar vs eWebinar."],[683,"**Your own website.** Embed the registration form on your site with the **Registration Widget** instead of sending people to the page."],[8966,"**Your page stays in charge.** The content around the form is yours: your blog post, your landing page, your sidebar."],[2912,"**Your pitch setup comes with the clone.** Clone a live webinar as evergreen and choose what comes across. Demio's Create On-Demand makes a new event without copying the original settings. See EasyWebinar vs eWebinar for recorded-only platforms."],[3103,"**Your setup comes with you.** Clone a live webinar as **Evergreen** and its offers, polls and emails can come too. Demio's **Create On-Demand** makes a new automated event, but the original settings aren't copied. EverWebinar's import of a past WebinarJam session needs an active WebinarJam subscription. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam and EverWebinar."],[9332,"**Your subdomain is in every link.** Changing it breaks links you've already sent."],[9194,"**Your subdomain is in every link.** Changing it later breaks links you've already shared."],[819,"**Your timing is planned.** Each section gets a share of the running time, so the offer doesn't get squeezed into the last two minutes."],[2894,"**YouTube and LinkedIn.** EasyCast streams a live webinar to YouTube, LinkedIn or a custom RTMP destination at the same time. Registered attendees watch in the webinar room, and everyone else can watch on YouTube or LinkedIn."],[8331,"**YouTube**, **Vimeo**, **Wistia**, or a direct **MP4 link**."],[7663,"**Zooming in is desktop only.** It isn't available on phones, in windows narrower than 768px or in automated webinars, and it resets on a new slide or share."],[6321,"*1 All · Polls · Offers · 2 Search · 3 The list · 4 Row actions.*"],[6002,"*1 All · Polls · Offers filters · 2 Search · 3 The list of CTAs · 4 Row actions.*"],[6848,"*1 All · Videos · Recordings · 2 Search and sort · 3 Add Video · 4 Drag and drop · 5 Your library.*"],[7043,"*1 All · Videos · Recordings · 2 Search and sort · 3 Add Video · 4 Drag and drop · 5 Your li