he **Paid Offer — Transaction Success** email, the receipt-style confirmation. Use that email to say what happens next. Your course stays on your own course platform, so point buyers there for their login and first lesson."],[3063,"Anyone who buys from an offer receives the **Paid Offer — Transaction Success** email."],[7390,"Anyone who joins as a co-host or moderator lands in **Backstage**, not on stage. The green room page covers backstage, the People panel and presenter links in detail."],[9342,"Anyone with the link, while the replay page is enabled."],[6574,"Archive it from its card menu. Webinars are archived rather than deleted."],[1664,"Archive it. Archiving retires the workflow so it stops running, but keeps the record, so you can look back at it or reuse its structure for the next campaign."],[3142,"Archive last month's webinars"],[1509,"Archive when the campaign ends"],[6456,"Archiving"],[7739,"Are drawings on my shared screen in the recording?"],[4588,"Are registration payments and offer sales reported together?"],[307,"Around 23 for all five parts: 10 for the script, 10 for the pages, and 1 each for emails, polls and offers."],[7259,"As co-hosts and moderators join, they appear backstage. Expand the **Backstage** panel on the left edge of the room to see who's waiting. To see everyone at once, open **People** on the side rail."],[5037,"As often as you set with **Interval**: every 2, 15, 30, 45 or 60 minutes."],[8615,"As time before the webinar, in hours, minutes and seconds, for example *1h 0m 0s before webinar*."],[4316,"Ask a colleague to register with their own email address on a different device. They should receive the registration confirmation and the reminders you set, and each link should open the right page. Their device is also where you check the attendee view of your slides and polls."],[2369,"Ask an easy question about the audience before you make the offer. A question such as \"when are you planning to start?\" also tells you who's ready to buy. Build it on the same tab, as described under polls."],[2180,"Ask each client to point a subdomain at the webinar tool with their DNS provider."],[4325,"Ask each presenter to join from the computer and browser they will use on the day."],[4327,"Ask each presenter to share their screen and show their first slide."],[8775,"Ask for consent with GDPR Compliance"],[3322,"Ask on the registration form"],[2650,"Ask only for what you'll use. Nielsen Norman Group's form research found that every field you cut increases a form's conversion rate, and a paid form already asks for a payment. The UK's data protection rules also expect personal data to be limited to only what is necessary for your purpose. A phone number earns its place only if you plan to send SMS reminders."],[2755,"Ask only what you need on the form"],[3,"At a glance"],[140,"At a glance"],[322,"At a glance"],[523,"At a glance"],[738,"At a glance"],[1082,"At a glance"],[1232,"At a glance"],[1482,"At a glance"],[1711,"At a glance"],[1870,"At a glance"],[2091,"At a glance"],[2270,"At a glance"],[2448,"At a glance"],[2532,"At a glance"],[2734,"At a glance"],[2940,"At a glance"],[3122,"At a glance"],[3314,"At a glance"],[3516,"At a glance"],[3775,"At a glance"],[3979,"At a glance"],[4188,"At a glance"],[4403,"At a glance"],[4550,"At a glance"],[4704,"At a glance"],[4901,"At a glance"],[5054,"At a glance"],[5249,"At a glance"],[5453,"At a glance"],[5626,"At a glance"],[5768,"At a glance"],[5932,"At a glance"],[6096,"At a glance"],[6241,"At a glance"],[6433,"At a glance"],[6585,"At a glance"],[6764,"At a glance"],[6948,"At a glance"],[7179,"At a glance"],[7319,"At a glance"],[7493,"At a glance"],[7691,"At a glance"],[7885,"At a glance"],[8037,"At a glance"],[8193,"At a glance"],[8346,"At a glance"],[8489,"At a glance"],[8632,"At a glance"],[8765,"At a glance"],[8913,"At a glance"],[9041,"At a glance"],[9215,"At a glance"],[9353,"At a glance"],[9523,"At a glance"],[6356,"At the offers step, start with positioning."],[6034,"At the polls step, you aren't asked what questions to write. You are asked what the polls are for."],[5612,"At the timestamp you set, measured from the start of the video."],[2686,"At these rates, 1,000 visitors fill the room with a little to spare. The bigger lever is checkout, not traffic. Raising checkout completion from 60% to 75% adds 12 paid seats from the same 1,000 visitors, while getting those 12 seats from traffic would take 250 more visitors."],[2889,"At these rates, one session fills two places. To fill eight, you'd need four sessions of the same size, or 800 registrants in total (8 ÷ 2 = 4, and 4 × 200 = 800)."],[5356,"Attendance has a weak spot on simulive. It mixes the pull of the session time with the pull of the topic, so a low figure may only mean the time was wrong. Compare attendance across sessions at different times before you change the content."],[3644,"Attendance is only the first split. **Attendee Action Follow-ups** send based on what someone actually did, including how engaged they were and whether they clicked an offer. Someone who clicked your offer and didn't buy needs a different email from someone who left after five minutes. If you want the reasoning behind these splits, our post on segmenting webinar follow-ups covers it."],[2565,"Attendance of paid buyers"],[7173,"Attendance, offer clicks and revenue appear in Analytics, and can be sent to your CRM as tags."],[1987,"Attendee capacity by plan"],[9227,"Attendee Join Link"],[9228,"Attendee Replay link"],[2212,"Attendees and no-shows need different messages. Set them per webinar, as the follow-up email guide explains, and use AI-drafted email sequences as a first draft. If the client's domain sends the emails, verify the sending domain first."],[7788,"Attendees can zoom in on a shared screen or file to read small text. The recorder doesn't turn zoom on, so recordings never include it. So make small text large enough for replay viewers to read as it is."],[2719,"Attendees go wherever you set in **End of Session** on the Settings tab. Leave it empty and they stay on the finished webinar, so point it at your booking page or next offer."],[2896,"Attendees join from any browser with nothing to install, which matters when your audience isn't used to webinar software. For how webinars fit with the rest of a coaching business, the coaching sales funnel post covers the stages before and after this page."],[7590,"Attendees on desktop can zoom in on a shared screen, video or file, up to 400%. The zoom happens only in that attendee's browser, so your stream and everyone else's view stay as they were. It isn't available on phones, in browser windows narrower than 768px, or in automated webinars. It also resets to 100% when you move to another slide or a new share starts."],[9453,"Attendees outside the US may be offered the price in their own currency alongside the dollar price. Stripe handles the conversion."],[6691,"Attendees pay through a Stripe checkout, and the money goes straight to your Stripe account. If no account is connected, a **Payments · Action required** panel offers **Connect with Stripe**. You can switch back to **Free** any time before creating the webinar."],[7422,"Attendees then go to the URL you set in **End of Session**, if you set one."],[4320,"Attendees watching on a phone can't zoom in on a shared screen or a shared file. The same is true in any browser window narrower than 768 pixels, which the room treats as a phone. So the real test is whether your slides can be read at the size a phone shows them."],[7708,"Attendees zooming in"],[1867,"Automate follow-ups with CRM tools: ideas for the sequences your tags can trigger."],[2952,"Automate it"],[4856,"Automated webinar features, from each platform's public documentation:"],[4702,"Automated Webinar: How Recordings, Schedules and Just-in-Time Sessions Work Together"],[2526,"Automated webinars"],[7758,"Automatic recording is a setting of the live room. It stays on unless you switch it off, so each live webinar you run produces a recording you can find, name and reuse. The recording is the raw material for everything that comes after the live hour: the replay for people who missed it, and the content of an evergreen version."],[513,"Automating your webinar email funnel: EasyWebinar's blog post on planning the sequence around your funnel."],[1495,"Automation in your own CRM"],[6956,"Availability"],[359,"B2B marketing teams"],[1102,"B2B marketing teams"],[1269,"B2B marketing teams"],[1517,"B2B marketing teams"],[3157,"B2B marketing teams"],[3344,"B2B marketing teams"],[3813,"B2B marketing teams"],[4017,"B2B marketing teams"],[4230,"B2B marketing teams"],[4425,"B2B marketing teams"],[4573,"B2B marketing teams"],[5956,"B2B marketing teams"],[6119,"B2B marketing teams"],[6459,"B2B marketing teams"],[6615,"B2B marketing teams"],[6792,"B2B marketing teams"],[7200,"B2B marketing teams"],[7348,"B2B marketing teams"],[7527,"B2B marketing teams"],[8063,"B2B marketing teams"],[8370,"B2B marketing teams"],[8515,"B2B marketing teams"],[8787,"B2B marketing teams"],[8933,"B2B marketing teams"],[9243,"B2B marketing teams"],[9553,"B2B marketing teams"],[2498,"B2B marketing teams and SaaS teams run webinars to bring in leads, then pass the warmest ones to sales. The lead generation guide covers capturing registrants and their source. The People view then shows who watched and who clicked. Guides to a first sales webinar and to automated product demos are planned."],[7583,"Backstage is the waiting area for your team. When a co-host or moderator joins, they land backstage, and your audience can't see or hear them. You move each person to the stage when it's their turn and back again when they're done. Presenters and moderators get their join links from **Invite People** in the **People** panel, and team members and roles explains who can do what."],[7304,"Backstage. Expand the **Backstage** panel on the left edge to see them, and move them to the stage when you want them seen."],[131,"Backstage. Move them to the stage when you want them seen and heard, and back again when they're done."],[631,"Be slow to add form fields. The same group's form guidance notes that every field you cut raises a form's conversion rate, and it suggests keeping optional fields to one or two. Add a custom registration field only when you'll actually use the answer."],[1074,"Be specific about the audience, the three or four things you cover, the length, the tone and what you sell at the end. Vague prompts produce generic webinars."],[314,"Be specific about the audience, what you'll cover, how long it runs, the tone, and what you're selling."],[943,"Be specific about who it's for, the three or four things you'll teach, how long it runs, the tone and what you're selling, with the price. A vague prompt produces a generic script."],[1620,"Because a workflow sends the same thing to everyone on its list, the checks matter more than for a single broadcast. Go through these before you publish:"],[4504,"Because People also holds attendance and watch time, this gives you campaign attribution against real viewing, not just clicks. UTM capture is easy to miss; without it, you'll know how many people registered but not which ad, email or post sent them. See Registration page builder."],[8850,"Because People also shows who attended, this gives you campaign attribution against real attendance, not just clicks. If you also use ad pixels, they tell your ad platform what happened; UTM capture shows the same story inside EasyWebinar."],[431,"Because the timing counts from the webinar rather than from a clock time, the same reminders work for recurring live sessions and evergreen schedules. You won't need to reset them when a date moves. Follow-ups are different: you choose their audience, whether that's everyone who registered, only attendees or only no-shows. For the follow-up side in depth, the follow-up email guide covers what to send each group."],[1590,"Before a workflow, most small teams follow up like this after each session:"],[892,"Before the script is written, you're asked for the number of **slides** and the **duration**. Use the running time from your invitation, and a slide count that suits how you present. Then the script is written slide by slide, which takes roughly a minute and a half."],[7241,"Before the session, decide who will present and who will moderate. You have two routes."],[1951,"Before the webinar, Create with AI drafts your script, pages, emails, polls and offers. The draft emails arrive with merge tags in place, so dates, times and join links fill themselves in. Create with AI is credit-based, and you still review and edit everything it writes."],[4,"Before you begin"],[148,"Before you begin"],[1712,"Before you begin"],[5461,"Before you begin"],[6434,"Before you begin"],[6586,"Before you begin"],[6765,"Before you begin"],[6949,"Before you begin"],[7320,"Before you begin"],[7886,"Before you begin"],[9361,"Before you begin"],[9524,"Before you begin"],[7791,"Before you click **End Session**, note the **LIVE** timer in the header. Afterwards, find the session in **Library** → **Recordings**, where each card shows its duration. A recording far shorter than the time you were live is worth opening before you send the replay link."],[2662,"Before you go live, check the header reads **Auto Recording Enabled**. That recording is what your replay page will show, as the automatic recording guide explains."],[2393,"Before you go live, run through the webinar setup checklist to test your camera, sound and offer link."],[7705,"Before you go live: check the recording"],[665,"Before you start, have a clear description of the session and your offer, including what's included. Check your credits, which show at the top right of every step: landing pages use 10, and a full build of all five parts uses about 23. For a simulive or evergreen webinar, have the video ready too, because you'll choose it after the build."],[6594,"Blackout dates"],[7404,"Blur is the quickest fix for an untidy room. A frame overlay is where your branding goes, and it carries through to the recording and anything EasyCast streams out. Upload overlays with a transparent background, otherwise they cover the video instead of framing it. Layout matters most with several presenters or a screen share, because it decides whether your slides or your faces take the space."],[4324,"Book a 30-minute call with every presenter a day or two before."],[8477,"Both are in Beta: **Welcome SMS** and the WhatsApp **Welcome Message** send immediately after someone registers. Each needs the **Phone** field on your registration form."],[8619,"Both are in Beta. **Reminder SMS** and the WhatsApp **Reminder Message** send before the webinar starts, and both need the **Phone** field on your registration form."],[8573,"Both Beta channels have a reminder of their own on the **Notifications** tab: **Reminder SMS** on the **SMS** tab and **Reminder Message** on the **Whatsapp** tab, each sent before the webinar starts. They work alongside email rather than replacing it, and suit the final reminder before a session, when an email may sit unread."],[8440,"Both Beta channels have their own message for the moment of registration: **Welcome SMS** on the **SMS** tab and **Welcome Message** on the **Whatsapp** tab, each sent immediately after someone registers. They need a phone number, so the **Phone** field has to be on your registration form, and they come from an EasyWebinar number rather than your own. Both work alongside email rather than replacing it."],[1576,"Both draw on the same allowance, and both send to lists. The difference is time: a broadcast runs once, while a workflow keeps sending for as long as it's published."],[2839,"Both end-of-session boxes are empty by default, which means attendees are left sitting on a finished webinar. Fill them in before your first run."],[5332,"Both play a recording, so the choice comes down to the room and the calendar. Simulive broadcasts at times you set, and everyone in a session watches together. Evergreen runs on a repeating schedule and lets each registrant choose a time that suits them."],[5428,"Both play a recording. A simulive webinar broadcasts it at times you set, so everyone in a session watches together. An evergreen webinar runs on a repeating schedule and lets each registrant choose a time that suits them, so attendees arrive at different times."],[4878,"Both play a recording. Simulive broadcasts it at times you set, so everyone in a session watches together and you can chat live. Evergreen runs on a repeating schedule and lets each registrant choose a time that suits them."],[7114,"Both play a recording. Simulive broadcasts it at times you set, so everyone in a session watches together. Evergreen repeats on a schedule and each registrant picks the session that suits them."],[8963,"Both register people for the same webinar."],[8239,"Both routes start from **Library → Add Media**, or from **Add Video** while you set up a simulive or evergreen webinar. Either way the video lands in your library and can be reused on other webinars."],[7993,"Both types play a recording, and both choose it from the library on the **Video Selection** step. See Create a simulive webinar and Create an evergreen webinar."],[8301,"Both types play a video from your library. Simulive plays it at times you set, so everyone in a session watches together; evergreen runs continuously and lets each registrant pick a time."],[2750,"Bring a client on camera"],[5781,"Bring in a moderator"],[6108,"Bring in a moderator"],[1231,"Broadcasts and workflows can't go out until sending is set up. This email domain authentication guide explains how to verify a domain or a business address in EasyCRM, choose EasyCRM Mail or your own SMTP provider and check sending health, so your first broadcast leaves under your own name."],[1097,"Broadcasts and workflows: send the follow-up"],[3902,"Broadcasts send to lists, so build the list first. Import your spreadsheet into EasyCRM's leads, then use **Add List** to save the group you'll invite. Every import is kept as an audience with its own name, source and member count, so you can send to it again without importing twice. Make one list per topic rather than inviting everyone to everything."],[1575,"Broadcasts sit beside workflows under Marketing, and this is where one-off sends are listed. The figures shown are sample data."],[5464,"Build a believable cast"],[2289,"Build a registration page that gets sign-ups"],[149,"Build a webinar with AI"],[6947,"Build an evergreen webinar in EasyWebinar that plays a recording on a continuous schedule, with just-in-time sessions, On Demand viewing and recurring daily or weekly times your registrants choose from."],[3406,"Build each link from your webinar's registration link and add the tags to the end. If you promote a form embedded on your own site, make one test registration through a tagged link and check that its campaign shows in **People** before launch."],[2948,"Build it"],[6240,"Build offer cards on a webinar's CTAs tab with a headline, a button, an optional price and countdown, push them to the room, carry them onto the replay, and measure views, clicks, purchases and revenue."],[5931,"Build polls on a webinar's CTAs tab, launch them to the room, have Create with AI write them from a goal, and see who answered in the People view."],[2181,"Build the first client's registration page, emails and offer, and write down every setting you chose."],[3802,"Build the list you'll invite"],[1500,"Build the lists your workflows send to"],[2748,"Build the offer that invites people to apply or book"],[1611,"Build the workflow and leave it in draft while you check it."],[196,"Building a webinar by hand means writing a presentation, designing a registration page, writing a confirmation, reminders and follow-ups, and thinking up polls and an offer. Create with AI does a first draf