dule, pages or registrations, so you can replace a recording with an improved cut while the webinar keeps running."],[7967,"Changing the video doesn't affect the webinar's schedule, pages or registrations."],[5314,"Changing the video here doesn't affect your schedule, pages or registrations. So you can re-record a weak section and drop the new file in without rebuilding anything."],[2460,"Charge for a workshop or seminar"],[5762,"Charge for webinar registration: paid workshops, where the registration-page countdown shows how long is left to register."],[7176,"Charge for webinar registration: take payment through Stripe when people register."],[9352,"Charge people to register for a webinar in EasyWebinar, take payment through Stripe, sell a live-plus-replay bundle, and track every paid registration and transaction."],[2615,"Charging changes three things, whichever of these you run. First, the promise has to be specific, because people are buying a result rather than attending out of curiosity. Second, the room has to give buyers a voice, so chat and Q&A matter more than on a free talk. Third, the replay stops being a courtesy. It becomes part of what you sell, so you need to decide who gets it before you take the first payment."],[6597,"Charging for the webinar"],[6784,"Chat and Q&A"],[6194,"Chat and Q&A are separate controls on the same tab. Chat's **Who can see messages** setting and the Q&A option are chosen separately, so you can run a public chat with private questions."],[6896,"Chat and Q&A are set up on the **Engagement** tab, as on a live webinar. You and your moderators reply in real time while the recording plays. See Live chat and Questions and answers."],[23,"Chat and Q&A moderation"],[7340,"Chat and Q&A settings"],[5346,"Chat and Q&A work normally on a simulive webinar. You set them up on the **Engagement** tab as you would for a live webinar. You and your moderators then answer in real time while the recording plays. Being in the chat is most of the value of simulive over evergreen, so plan which sessions you'll attend."],[7509,"Chat and questions"],[6973,"Chat choices for recorded webinars"],[5893,"Chat features, from each platform's public documentation:"],[6223,"Chat is a running conversation. Q&A collects questions in a list you work through, and with **Private Q&A** attendees don't see it."],[5883,"Chat is conversation; Q&A is a list of questions. A common setup is **Everyone** for chat with **Private Q&A**: the room stays sociable while questions arrive in an orderly queue."],[6144,"Chat is conversation: greetings, reactions, side remarks, attendees talking to each other. Q&A is a list. Each entry is a question, and your job is to work through the list during or at the end of the session."],[5823,"Chat is open conversation in the room, running alongside your video. It is separate from Q&A, which is a queue of questions you work through and can keep out of sight."],[5914,"Chat is open conversation. Q&A is a queue of questions you answer in order, and you can hide it from attendees."],[7584,"Chat is set on the webinar's **Engagement** tab before the session. **Everyone** lets attendees see and reply to each other. **Hosts only** makes every message a private conversation with your team, and **No Chat** removes the panel."],[5828,"Chat lets attendees respond as you present: say hello, react, ask, and talk to each other. It is how a presenter knows the room is listening, and on a simulive webinar it is how you stay present while your recording plays."],[5860,"Chat moderation preferences sit in the room's **Settings**, under **Preferences**, alongside Q&A moderation and appearance."],[5782,"Chat on simulive and evergreen webinars"],[5451,"Chat simulation"],[6944,"Chat simulation"],[4920,"Chat Simulation"],[6785,"Chat Simulation"],[6972,"Chat Simulation"],[1077,"Chat Simulation (Beta)"],[5513,"Chat simulation gives a recorded webinar the feel of an attended session. A greeting in the first seconds, a question a few minutes in and a host reply tell a newcomer the room is active. That impression keeps people watching long enough for the content to work."],[5497,"Chat simulation plays a conversation in the chat of a recorded webinar, so a session doesn't open to an empty room. In EasyWebinar you set it up on a simulive or evergreen webinar's **Engagement** tab, under **Chat Simulation**, in one of two ways. **AI Simulation** builds a cast of simulated attendees and generates their chat and questions. **Manual Simulation** plays a script you write in a CSV, with each message timed against your video. The Chat Simulation section carries a **Beta** label in the app."],[5509,"Chat simulation solves that by playing messages into the chat at set points in the video. You choose how those messages are made:"],[5579,"Chat simulation suits evergreen webinars running just-in-time or on demand sessions, where attendees arrive in ones and twos at all hours."],[5048,"Chat simulation: a chat for attendees who each arrive at a different moment."],[8761,"Chat simulation: a chat for registrants who start watching at different times."],[5924,"Chat simulation: fill the chat on an evergreen webinar, where a shared chat isn't possible."],[7127,"Chat simulation: keeping the chat active when registrants watch at different times."],[6235,"Chat simulation: the busy automated room that pairs with **Private Q&A**."],[2557,"Chat that suits the group"],[7086,"Chat, Q&A, polls, offers, emails and analytics behave as on any other webinar. In **People**, filtering by **Webinar → Evergreen** shows how the automated funnel performs against your live sessions. See Webinar analytics and People."],[8723,"Chat, Q&A, polls, offers, emails and analytics work on evergreen webinars as they do everywhere else. Where viewers watch at different times, Chat Simulation on the **Engagement** tab keeps the chat from looking empty."],[4691,"Check **Offers Performance** for views, clicks and purchases, and **Revenue by Offer** f