reen walkthrough, setting by setting."],[5046,"Create an evergreen webinar: the full setup that just-in-time is one step of."],[5928,"Create an evergreen webinar: the recorded format that offers **Third party** chat and Chat Simulation."],[6577,"Create an evergreen webinar: the schedule options to set on a copy cloned as evergreen."],[8759,"Create an evergreen webinar: the schedule step where On Demand is switched on."],[8627,"Create an evergreen webinar: the schedule where relative timing saves the most work."],[6250,"Create an offer"],[4182,"Create and schedule a live webinar"],[6583,"Create and schedule a live webinar"],[6940,"Create and schedule a live webinar"],[7686,"Create and schedule a live webinar"],[6579,"Create and schedule a live webinar: building a webinar from scratch when there is nothing to copy."],[7174,"Create and schedule a live webinar: set a one-time or recurring schedule and choose free or paid registration."],[3974,"Create and schedule a live webinar: set the date your invitation promotes."],[4396,"Create and schedule a live webinar: set the date, time and presenters this checklist starts from."],[731,"Create and schedule a live webinar: set the schedule your pages display."],[7487,"Create and schedule a live webinar: set the session time and registration before you open the room."],[2085,"Create and schedule a live webinar: set up the session you'll be entering the room for."],[2727,"Create and schedule a live webinar: the four-step builder your paid workshop starts from."],[3116,"Create and schedule a live webinar: the manual build, including the registration template step where the **Education** category sits."],[316,"Create and schedule a live webinar: the manual route, and where to set the schedule the AI build leaves to you."],[5764,"Create and schedule a live webinar: the schedule the registration-page countdown counts down to."],[7313,"Create and schedule a live webinar: the session has to exist and be scheduled before you can enter its green room."],[1855,"Create it in your CRM, then click **Refresh**."],[3803,"Create the broadcast"],[2204,"Create the client's first webinar inside their workspace. Choose a live webinar for a launch, or an evergreen webinar for a funnel that runs every day. On **Step 4 of 4 — Registration Template**, filter by **Agency** to see templates made for this work."],[4727,"Create the webinar"],[5272,"Create the webinar"],[2642,"Create the webinar from **My Webinars → Create a Webinar**, as the live webinar setup describes. On **Step 3 of 4 · Pricing**, **Free** is selected until you change it."],[1507,"Create the workflow"],[138,"Create with AI"],[4180,"Create with AI"],[5643,"Create with AI"],[8363,"Create with AI"],[9380,"Create with AI"],[270,"Create with AI drafts the content. A few things are still yours to do:"],[199,"Create with AI is for getting from an idea to a webinar funnel you can run, without starting each piece from a blank page. It suits a first webinar, a new topic, or a team that needs a launch-ready draft quickly."],[280,"Create with AI is one of several AI features in EasyWebinar. **Chat Simulation** can use AI to populate the chat on a recorded webinar; see Chat simulation. The **AI Moderator**, which answers attendee questions in the room, is in Beta."],[206,"Create with AI matters most to coaches, course creators and small teams who run their own marketing. It matters in the week before a first webinar, when the setup hours are the main thing standing between an idea and a date."],[2027,"Create with AI uses credits, shown at the top right of every step."],[2394,"Create with AI writes the script, builds the pages, drafts the emails and creates polls and offers from one description. It takes about ten minutes, and a full build of all five parts costs around 23 credits. Check every page and email before you publish, especially what they say about your offer."],[1076,"Create with AI, step by step"],[514,"Create with AI: the full AI webinar build, from prompt to finished webinar."],[6091,"Create with AI: the full build that writes polls alongside the script, pages, emails and offers."],[9211,"Create with AI: the full build that writes these pages from your script."],[3429,"Create your tags in the CRM first, then select them here. Map **Webinar Title** to a custom field so each contact shows which webinar it came from; the field has to exist in your CRM before you can map to it. The mapping guide lists all eleven events and every field."],[6702,"Creating the webinar does not publish it. Your registration page goes live only when you click **Publish**. Use **Preview** to check it and **Save** to keep a draft."],[1038,"Credits show at the top right of every step. The script and pages cost 10 credits each, and emails, polls and offers cost 1 each."],[4422,"CRM and email tools"],[4568,"CRM and email tools"],[6262,"CRM and email tools"],[8058,"CRM and email tools"],[8365,"CRM and email tools"],[9378,"CRM and email tools"],[1836,"CRM features, from each platform's public documentation:"],[1813,"CRM mapping brings your registrants and attendees into the system you already work in, without exporting anything. Each contact arrives with a tag that says what they did, so your next step can depend on it."],[1217,"CSV or XLSX. The **Map** step matches each column in your file to the right EasyCRM field."],[8821,"Custom fields let the registration form collect what your follow-up actually needs. That might be a phone number for text reminders or a question about who is attending. It might also be consent, or the campaign each person came from."],[9061,"Custom fields, consent and UTM capture"],[8763,"Custom registration fields"],[9206,"Custom registration fields: phone, your own questions, consent and UTM capture on the form block."],[9036,"Custom registration fields: the fields and consent checkbox the form asks for."],[30,"Customer success teams"],[3158,"Customer success teams"],[4229,"Customer success teams"],[4427,"Customer success teams"],[4737,"Customer success teams"],[4929,"Customer success teams"],[5795,"Customer success teams"],[6118,"Customer success teams"],[6461,"Customer success teams"],[6794,"Customer success teams"],[6982,"Customer success teams"],[7201,"Customer success teams"],[7727,"Customer success teams"],[7914,"Customer success teams"],[8064,"Customer success teams"],[8514,"Customer success teams"],[8655,"Customer success teams"],[9244,"Customer success teams"],[4267,"Customer success teams run the same onboarding or release webinar again and again, often with a different presenter each time. A shared checklist means the session works the same way whoever runs it. It matters most on the first run with a new co-host, and when the team is presenting to its largest customers."],[865,"Cut anything that pushes a section past its minutes."],[7874,"Data protection (GOV.UK): the UK rules on how organisations use personal information, including recordings of people."],[3970,"Data protection, GOV.UK: the UK principles for using personal data."],[7681,"Data protection, GOV.UK: the UK principles that apply when you record attendees' names, voices and messages."],[3787,"Date, time and time zone in one line"],[1096,"Deals and pipelines: track what's open"],[1177,"Deals show as cards in one column per stage. Each column shows how many deals it holds and its share of the pipeline. A column that fills up and never empties is where your process is stuck. The **Offers** tab holds the things you sell, so a deal records its value the same way every time."],[1219,"Deals won't work until a pipeline exists. Create one from the **Pipelines** tab, then add deals to its stages."],[2172,"Decide early whether the webinar sells something on the spot or books a sales call. An offer's **Button URL** can point to the client's own checkout, booking page or sales page. If the client charges for registration, that needs the Paid Webinars add-on and a connected Stripe account, and payouts go to that Stripe account. Leads then need a route to the client's CRM, covered in connecting a CRM and mapping webinar data."],[5186,"Decide here how quickly a new registrant can watch the live session's recording, and on which days it runs."],[57,"Decide on a role for each person. The Roles section below explains the difference."],[2552,"Decide on the replay before you publish"],[6646,"Decide the date, time and timezone you will broadcast in."],[6648,"Decide the webinar type first. **The type can't be changed after the webinar is created.**"],[4210,"Decide what attendees can see and say"],[863,"Decide what you'll offer at the end and write the transition that leads into it."],[1259,"Decide where replies go"],[6330,"Decide whether to switch on **Countdown timer**."],[2561,"Decide who gets the replay"],[7585,"Decide who sees attendee messages before you go live. A sales session often suits private messages, while a workshop suits an open room."],[3396,"Decide your tags before the first link goes out, because the campaign is recorded at the moment someone registers. Write the values down in one place and reuse the pattern for every webinar."],[3242,"Delete or hide old webinars by hand so nobody edits the wrong one."],[3248,"Demo B's registration page converted better, while Demo A's reminders brought more people in. A sensible move is to clone Demo B, then copy Demo A's reminder timing onto the new webinar before it opens. Neither webinar is simply the better one; each was stronger at a different stage."],[843,"Describe the situation your audience is in, in their words. Use words they already use. Nielsen Norman Group's plain-language guidance recommends simple, familiar words over complicated ones, and that matters even more when people hear a sentence only once."],[348,"Describe the webinar"],[772,"Describe the webinar"],[550,"Describe the webinar and keep Landing pages on"],[4005,"Describe the webinar from your outline"],[1033,"Describe the webinar: who it's for, what it covers, how long it runs, the tone, and what you're selling at the end."],[2217,"Divide **Registered** by **Visitors**. A low figure points at the registration page: the headline, the form or the promise. Its weak spot is that **Visitors** counts unique IPs on the landing page, so people sharing an office network count once, and one person on two devices counts twice."],[2218,"Divide **Total Attended** by **Registered**. **Total Attended** counts unique people who watched live, the replay or both, so each person counts once. A low figure points at reminders, not content. Its weak spot is timing: replay views keep arriving for days, so the rate rises if you report too early."],[4125,"Divide offer clicks by offer views. A low figure means the offer itself is not landing, which often points back to a thin bridge or an offer that arrived too late. Its weak spot is that it says nothing about checkout: a strong click rate with few purchases is a checkout or pricing problem, not an outline problem."],[7599,"Divide the people who joined the live broadcast by the people who registered. A low figure usually points to reminders, not content, because the people who registered never reached the room. Its weak spot is that it counts arrivals, not attention. Someone who joined for two minutes counts the same as someone who stayed."],[1328,"DKIM lets the owner of a signing domain claim some responsibility for a message. The sending system adds a cryptographic signature, and the receiver fetches the matching public key from that domain. When the signature checks out, the message is tied to your domain."],[1244,"DKIM: a signature on each message"],[1329,"DMARC lets a domain owner state policies for validation, handling and reporting, which receiving systems can use. It also brings in alignment, which means the domain in your From address has to match a domain that SPF or DKIM has validated. A policy of `none` requests no specific action on delivery, so it's a gentle place to start."],[1245,"DMARC: your policy when checks fail"],[1889,"Do attendees need to download anything?"],[2318,"Do attendees need to download anything?"],[2786,"Do attendees need to download anything?"],[4937,"Do attendees see just-in-time sessions in their own timezone?"],[5106,"Do attendees see session times in their own timezone?"],[6805,"Do attendees see session times in their own timezone?"],[1287,"Do broadcasts and workflows need separate setup?"],[6800,"Do I have to be in the room during a simulive session?"],[6625,"Do I have to be the account owner?"],[5289,"Do I have to be there for a simulive session?"],[1748,"Do I have to connect every webinar separately?"],[3359,"Do I have to connect my CRM for every webinar?"],[9079,"Do I have to customise all five pages?"],[2470,"Do I have to give up my CRM?"],[6631,"Do I have to pick a registration template now?"],[9081,"Do I have to pick a template when I create the webinar?"],[7741,"Do I need a camera and microphone to record?"],[5664,"Do I need a separate countdown tool?"],[1110,"Do I need a separate CRM for my webinars?"],[1281,"Do I need an account with the SMTP provider?"],[9392,"Do I need an add-on?"],[1280,"Do I need EasyCRM if I already use HubSpot?"],[1531,"Do I need EasyCRM to automate webinar follow-up?"],[3364,"Do I need EasyCRM to follow up webinar leads?"],[1752,"Do I need EasyCRM to run webinars?"],[3829,"Do I need EasyCRM to send invitations?"],[1277,"Do I need my own domain to send broadcasts?"],[5291,"Do I need to host the video on YouTube or Vimeo first?"],[8803,"Do I need to publish after changing the form?"],[2469,"Do I need to record something before I start?"],[572,"Do I need to type the date and time into the page?"],[2977,"Do I need YouTube or Vimeo to host my recording?"],[6995,"Do I need YouTube or Vimeo to host the recording?"],[4748,"Do I need YouTube or Vimeo to run an automated webinar?"],[8948,"Do I still need a registration page if I use the widget?"],[987,"Do I still need to edit what the AI writes?"],[1025,"Do I still need to edit what the AI writes? Yes. The output is a draft, not a finished product, so work through this list before you publish."],[7922,"Do imported videos use my storage?"],[8224,"Do imported videos use my storage?"],[3830,"Do invitations count against my email allowance?"],[3674,"Do it all again after your next session, with new dates and links."],[1289,"Do mailbox providers require email authentication?"],[6992,"Do my attendees see times in their own timezone?"],[4938,"Do my daily and weekly sessions follow local time too?"],[5970,"Do my polls come across when I clone a webinar?"],[2578,"Do paid attendees get the replay?"],[6471,"Do polls and offers come across?"],[5107,"Do polls and offers still work in the evergreen version?"],[7359,"Do polls appear on their own during a live webinar?"],[7738,"Do recordings use my storage?"],[6468,"Do registrants come with the copy?"],[8523,"Do reminders work on recurring and evergreen webinars?"],[371,"Do the merge tags fill in automatically?"],[2842,"Do the same for **Expired Session**, which catches anyone arriving at a link that has expired."],[3417,"Do these in order for each webinar you promote. The first three happen before any link goes out."],[1278,"Do these settings change my webinar reminder emails?"],[3579,"Do webinar follow-up emails need an unsubscribe link?"],[2775,"Do webinars work for coaches?"],[1527,"Do workflow emails count against my allowance?"],[44,"Does a client workspace use one of my team seats?"],[2132,"Does a client workspace use one of my team seats?"],[9254,"Does a co-presenter need an EasyWebinar account?"],[3169,"Does a guest presenter need an account?"],[7211,"Does a guest presenter need an EasyWebinar account?"],[36,"Does a new team member get an email?"],[8383,"Does a webinar built with AI have a confirmation email?"],[8528,"Does a webinar built with AI include reminders?"],[6278,"Does an offer have to have a price?"],[7208,"Does anything I do in the green room get broadcast?"],[7535,"Does anything in the green room get broadcast?"],[5486,"Does chat simulation work on a live webinar?"],[8947,"Does cloning a webinar copy its widget?"],[5099,"Does cloning change my original live webinar?"],[6469,"Does cloning change the original?"],[5098,"Does cloning copy my registrants?"],[3173,"Does cloning copy registrants?"],[788,"Does EasyWebinar give me a script template?"],[2971,"Does EasyWebinar host my course?"],[8220,"Does EasyWebinar host videos, or do I need YouTube or Vimeo?"],[2140,"Does EasyWebinar work with GoHighLevel?"],[5663,"Does EasyWebinar write the offer for me?"],[5657,"Does every offer need a countdown?"],[4437,"Does Export include only the filtered people?"],[374,"Does it work for evergreen and simulive webinars?"],[576,"Does it work for evergreen and simulive webinars?"],[798,"Does it work for evergreen and simulive webinars?"],[990,"Does it work for evergreen and simulive webinars?"],[180,"Does it work for simulive and evergreen webinars?"],[5495,"Does it work with a third-party chat tool?"],[45,"Does my client get an email when I create their workspace?"],[2135,"Does my client get an email when I create their workspace?"],[1288,"Does my custom webinar page domain count for email?"],[6802,"Does my video need to be on YouTube or Vimeo first?"],[6132,"Does Q&A work on simulive webinars?"],[4590,"Does replay viewing count as attendance?"],[367,"Does the AI write a webinar invitation email?"],[4033,"Does the same outline work for a simulive or evergreen webinar?"],[6994,"Does the webinar ever stop running?"],[1248,"Domain or single address: which to verify"],[3241,"Download each webinar's registrant list and merge them in a spreadsheet."],[2876,"Download the attendee list and copy it into a spreadsheet."],[3669,"Download the list of registrants and the attendance report from the tool that ran your webinar."],[5152,"Download the recording of the live session and trim the waiting time at the start."],[776,"Download the script and continue"],[864,"Draft each section in plain spoken English, then read it aloud with a timer."],[4007,"Draft polls from their purpose"],[335,"Drafting from the webinar's own script"],[1022,"Drafting is only half of it. Two features work while attendees are watching."],[5551,"Drag the file onto the upload area, or use **Choose File**."],[7707,"Drawings on a shared screen"],[8260,"Drop your file onto the box, or click it to browse."],[595,"During the build, the pages open in an editor with four tabs: **Edit**, **Preview**, **SEO** and **Scripts**. A desktop and mobile view lets you check both layouts before you move on. When the build ends, you land on the finished webinar's **Overview**, and the webinar carries an **AI** badge in **My Webinars**. From then on, its pages sit on the **Content** tab and open in the registration page builder, exactly as they would on a webinar you built by hand."],[2670,"During the session, an offer can show a button that opens your own checkout or booking page. Offer sales show under **Paid Offer** in the Revenue view, apart from ticket sales."],[1952,"During the webinar, the AI Moderator answers attendee questions from documents you give it, such as PDFs and other files. It is available from the Pro plan onward. The AI overview explains what AI drafts, what it answers and what you still check."],[2225,"Each client has a different leak. The language tutor's page converts weakly, so the fix is the headline or form. The insulation installer fills well but loses people before the session, so the reminders need work. The physiotherapy clinic needs no change this month."],[2240,"Each client workspace is billed on its own plan, chosen when you create it, so there is no single combined bill across clients. Workspaces are separate from team seats: a workspace gives a client their own account, and a team seat gives a colleague a login on yours."],[6534,"Each copy starts with no registrants, so every month's figures belong to that month, and the original stays untouched. The full list of items sits under **What would you like to copy?** in the dialog. How this compares with other platforms is covered in How cloning compares, below."],[8560,"Each entry shows its **trigger**, the audience it goes **to**, and its **subject**, so the group reads as a timeline of what registrants will receive."],[708,"Each generation uses credits: 10 for landing pages, and about 23 for a full build."],[56,"Each member needs their own email address."],[6301,"Each offer has:"],[9101,"Each page has a working default, so you don't have to design any of them. If you only have time for two, make them the registration page and the replay page."],[2852,"Each person also carries a **Lead score**, calculated from engagement, which makes it a quick way to sort a long list. **Export** downloads the filtered list, so you can take that segment into your own tool."],[1958,"Each person gets their own login rather than sharing one. Sharing a login means you can't tell who did what, and only one of you can be in the live room as a host. The team members guide covers the Admin and User roles."],[7871,"Each recording carries its webinar's name and the date it was recorded. Match the date to the session you want."],[7793,"Each recording is named after its webinar and dated. If you ran a session and there is no card with that webinar's name and date, recording was off. Check **Recording Settings** before your next session."],[4468,"Each row is one person on one webinar, with columns including:"],[9613,"Each row shows the date, time, timezone and registration count for that sitting. A one-time webinar has a single upcoming session. A daily or weekly webinar fills the list from its recurrence, and a daily evergreen schedule generates a long run of upcoming sessions without you adding any."],[895,"Each section's timing is the number to check against your rehearsal, and the speaker notes are what you'll say on each slide."],[1596,"Each step is a chance to slip. The split is redone every month, and the reminder in step 4 is the one most often missed."],[7611,"Each step lives in a different place, and steps 4 and 5 are where sessions most often go wrong. An audience that arrives during a sound check, or a session nobody remembered to record, can't be fixed afterwards."],[3627,"Each template below is a complete email. Replace the words in square brackets, then cut anything that doesn't sound like you. Any version that promotes your offer also needs the opt-out notice and postal address described under What the law says, below. The examples assume a course offer, and the table further down shows what to swap for other kinds of webinar."],[9468,"Each transaction shows one of these statuses: **Pending**, **Processing**, **Success**, **Failed**, **Canceled**, **Refunded** or **Partially Refunded**. An attendee is registered once their payment succeeds."],[6535,"Each type delivers content differently, but pages, emails, polls, offers and analytics are shared across all three. That's why a clone can carry those assets into a different type."],[1565,"Each webinar has its own notifications, including **Webinar Follow-ups** sent after the session to registrants, attendees or no-shows. These catch the first message well and are the quickest way to send the replay to no-shows. They're tied to one webinar, so they don't carry a lead through a longer sequence afterwards."],[3205,"Each webinar has one owner who builds it, checks it and answers for it, while others help in set roles. The UK government's service manual makes the same point about service teams: one person should have the decision-making authority to deliver on all aspects of a project. This catches the \"I thought you sent it\" gap, but it still needs everyone to have access."],[399,"Each webinar starts with a blank set of notifications. Someone has to write the confirmation, every reminder and every follow-up from scratch, and set each send time by hand. Under deadline, the fifteen-minute reminder or the replay follow-up is usually the email that gets dropped."],[94,"Each webinar's **Team & Moderators** panel shows everyone who can run that webinar. **Add presenter** adds someone who appears on camera and presents. **Invite** sends an invitation to join the webinar team. The Overview page explains how presenters differ from team members."],[1414,"Each webinar's registration confirmation, reminders and follow-ups live on its **Notifications** tab. Their **Email Settings** button holds the **Sender name**, **Reply-to email** and **Notify admin** settings. So if your reminder shows the wrong sender name, look there rather than in **Configurations**."],[2245,"Each workspace has its own plan, and selecting a plan starts a subscription. Agree with the client before you create it whether they pay directly or you re-bill the cost as part of your fee."],[7197,"EasyCast"],[7344,"EasyCast"],[7276,"EasyCast destinations are switched on in the green room, before you go live. Once the broadcast starts, a platform icon for each destination appears in the top bar. Connections are made once, under **Integrations → EasyCast** in the sidebar, and work across every webinar."],[7406,"EasyCast is set up per account, so a destination connected once is available on every webinar. It covers **YouTube**, **LinkedIn**, **LinkedIn Organisation** and **Custom RTMP**."],[7450,"EasyCast multistreaming sends the live session to YouTube, LinkedIn, LinkedIn Organisation pages and custom RTMP destinations, connected once under **Integrations → EasyCast** and switched on per session in the room. Facebook isn't offered as a destination; its RTMP details may work under **Custom RTMP**."],[4348,"EasyCast, on Growth plans and above (see pricing), streams a live webinar to YouTube, LinkedIn or a custom RTMP destination at the same time. Connect each destination the day before. For YouTube, connect the Google account that actually owns the channel."],[1733,"EasyCRM"],[3897,"EasyCRM is built into EasyWebinar from the Growth plan; compare plans to see what each one includes. If your list already lives in another tool, skip to the last step below."],[1133,"EasyCRM is the CRM built into EasyWebinar for that job. Webinars generate leads, and EasyCRM is where you work them. You organise contacts, track deals, send campaigns and keep follow-up from slipping. You don't need it to run webinars. You need it when the number of people coming out of your webinars is more than a spreadsheet can handle."],[1957,"EasyCRM is the CRM built into EasyWebinar, and the two share one login. It holds leads, clients, deals, tasks, broadcasts and workflows. You don't need it to run webinars; it helps when your webinar leads outgrow a spreadsheet."],[1138,"EasyCRM is the option if you'd rather not run a separate tool. It suits teams that don't have a CRM yet, and it adds lead scoring and an auto-dialer beside your webinars. The webinar CRM vs traditional CRM post walks through how the two approaches differ."],[1550,"EasyCRM is the option when you'd rather not run a separate tool, or when your list has outgrown a spreadsheet. It shares one login with EasyWebinar, and registrants come across with **Import from EasyWebinar**."],[1992,"EasyCRM sending allowance"],[1380,"EasyCRM starts at Growth, and plans and add-ons are on the pricing page. You reach it by clicking **EasyCRM** under **Other Products** in the EasyWebinar sidebar, using the same login."],[1670,"EasyCRM, sequences and automated follow-up start at the Growth plan. The EasyWebinar pricing page lists what each plan includes, so check it before you choose."],[1152,"EasyCRM's sidebar lists every section. Here is what each one is for and the order most teams use them in."],[1568,"EasyCRM's sources confirm the workflow states (draft, published, archived), that a draft sends nothing, that workflows send to saved lists, and that sends draw on the Wallet allowance. Which triggers and steps the workflow builder offers is not covered here; those details are listed for confirmation with EasyWebinar."],[4278,"EasyWebinar asks every presenter to check their camera, microphone and speakers before entering, and keeps the green room private. **Send Test SMS** (Beta) sends a text message to a number you choose, and WhatsApp (Beta) messages can be tested the same way. The full test run and the phone check are things you do yourself, with a colleague."],[6726,"EasyWebinar builds live, simulive and evergreen webinars from one create dialog. A live webinar can repeat on a **Weekly** schedule and charge at sign-up through a Stripe checkout. EasyWebinar is the only platform in this table that does all three."],[4058,"EasyWebinar builds on that order. Its **Create with AI** flow starts from your description of the webinar. That covers who it is for, what it teaches, its length, its tone and what you sell. It then writes the script slide by slide. It drafts the pages and emails from that script, and writes polls and offers you can edit on the **CTAs** tab."],[4271,"EasyWebinar builds that test into the way you enter a live session. It asks you to check your camera, microphone and speakers before you reach the green room. It then keeps you in a green room where nothing is broadcast. Co-hosts wait backstage until you bring them on. Polls and offers can be switched on and off without deleting them, and reminders can be timed relative to the start."],[5685,"EasyWebinar builds the countdown into the offer card itself. On the **CTAs** tab, the coach opens the programme offer and switches on **Countdown timer**. The bonus goes in the **Headline**, so the card says what ends. Because the timer is part of the offer, it appears in every session that shows that offer. With the replay page set to **Webinar Replica**, the offer carries over to the replay too."],[9113,"EasyWebinar builds the registration page inside the webinar itself. EasyWebinar fills in the date, time, timezone and a countdown when the webinar is created. It also puts a name and email form in place. EasyWebinar keeps templates you've saved under **My Templates**, so each month's workshop can start from her own styled design."],[1015,"EasyWebinar builds the whole webinar from one description through **Create with AI**. It writes the script slide by slide, builds the pages from that script, drafts the emails, and creates polls and offers. During the session, AI Moderator answers attendee questions from uploaded context from Pro onward."],[8278,"EasyWebinar can't read the length of a video hosted elsewhere, and it uses the duration to schedule sessions and work out when the webinar ends. A wrong figure cuts the video short or leaves attendees waiting on a finished one."],[2255,"EasyWebinar carries a 99.9% uptime guarantee, and it doesn't cut a webinar off at the plan limit. Every session is recorded automatically, so a replay is ready for no-shows."],[2640,"EasyWebinar collapses steps 3, 4 and 6 into one. The buyer's email carries over from the registration form to the Stripe checkout, and they are registered only once the payment goes through. Reminders are set once on the **Notifications** tab. Recording shows as **Auto Recording Enabled** in the live room when it's switched on. The **Replay** tab handles step 8, and **Analytics → Revenue** answers step 9."],[1823,"EasyWebinar connects HubSpot on the webinar's **Integrations** tab. The team maps **Watched full** to an engaged tag that alerts the reps, and **Missed** to a no-show tag for the replay sequence. On the **Custom fields** tab they map **Webinar Join Link**, so HubSpot can send its own reminders with each person's link."],[2395,"EasyWebinar connects to email tools including HubSpot, ActiveCampaign, Mailchimp, AWeber and Kit (formerly ConvertKit). It can tag contacts by what they did, such as **Attended**, **Missed** or **Clicked offer**. The steps are under connect a CRM and map your webinar data. If you'd rather not run a separate tool, EasyCRM keeps contacts beside your webinars."],[2433,"EasyWebinar connects to tools including HubSpot, ActiveCampaign, Mailchimp, AWeber and Kit (formerly ConvertKit). It can tag contacts as attended, missed or clicked offer. You can also keep contacts in EasyCRM instead."],[3112,"EasyWebinar connects with Kit (ConvertKit), ActiveCampaign, Mailchimp, Drip, AWeber, Keap, Ontraport, GetResponse, Constant Contact and GoHighLevel, and tags people by what they did in the webinar."],[4816,"EasyWebinar does steps 2 to 6 from the schedule step. You choose the recording once, switch on the ways to watch, and set a start date with **No end date** if it should run indefinitely. The sessions list then fills itself: a daily schedule generates a long run of upcoming sessions without you adding any. **Blackout Dates** handles the holidays, and On Demand covers the person who would otherwise wait."],[2622,"EasyWebinar does the first and fourth natively. Paid registration takes payment through Stripe before registering the buyer. Offers shown during the session open the button URL you set, which can be your own checkout or booking page. Its paid webinar features cover live, simulive and evergreen webinars."],[2423,"EasyWebinar doesn't hold the money from your offer. The offer button opens your own checkout URL, and paid registration runs through your Stripe account. A webinar's type is fixed once it exists, so moving from live to evergreen means cloning it. Reminders and follow-ups are set per webinar, so a new webinar needs its own set or a clone of an earlier one. The replay link is public while the replay page is on."],[404,"EasyWebinar drafts the sequence inside its AI webinar build, straight after the script and pages. It writes a welcome email, reminders a day, an hour and fifteen minutes before, and two follow-ups. Merge tags are already in place. Each email opens on the **Notifications** tab for editing, so the agency reviews six drafts rather than writing them."],[477,"EasyWebinar drafts the whole email sequence inside the same AI build that writes the webinar's script and pages, so the emails describe the session you're about to run. The drafts are timed before and after the webinar, and you can add follow-ups for no-shows and for people who clicked an offer."],[2226,"EasyWebinar gives each client a separate workspace on its own plan, puts their pages on their own domain and removes its branding with an add-on. It also keeps a CRM with a deal pipeline beside the webinars for clients who don't have one, while connecting to the CRM they do have."],[105,"EasyWebinar gives each colleague their own login, lets a guest present or moderate one webinar from a link with no account, and keeps each agency client in a separate workspace on its own plan. EasyWebinar is the only platform in this table that does all three."],[3200,"EasyWebinar gives each teammate their own login with an Admin or User role, set by the Owner or an Admin. Guests join a single webinar with a Co-presenter or Moderator link, with no account needed. It clones a webinar with the parts you choose. It can also change the copy's type on the way, so a live session can become evergreen."],[8974,"EasyWebinar gives each webinar a **Registration Widget** on its **Content** tab. EasyWebinar lets you change the widget's look with **View & Customize**, then copy its **Embed Code** and paste it wherever the form should appear. The same snippet sits in the **Share** dialog, next to the webinar's links."],[3854,"EasyWebinar gives each webinar a **Share** dialog with its registration links, and EasyCRM sends the invitation as a one-off broadcast to a saved list. Registrants and attendees can then be imported back into EasyCRM, tagged with the webinar they came from. If you already run HubSpot, Mailchimp or another tool, EasyWebinar connects to it instead."],[6160,"EasyWebinar gives questions their own queue, set on the webinar's **Engagement** tab. The team keeps chat on **Everyone**, so the room stays sociable, and sets Q&A to **Private Q&A**, so account questions reach only hosts and moderators. The two success managers join with the **Moderator Join Link for Live room** and answer from the **Question** panel while the product manager presents."],[1561,"EasyWebinar gives the owner a CRM that sits under the same login as the webinars. They import registrants and attendees, save one list for attendees and one for no-shows, and build a workflow for each. Each stays in draft until it's checked, and is published once the first webinar's lists are in place."],[7283,"EasyWebinar gives you a private green room before the broadcast and a backstage where guests wait, both before and during the session. From the same room you can switch on several streaming destinations at once. EasyWebinar is the only platform in this table that does all three."],[3619,"EasyWebinar gives you each of these controls on the webinar itself. **Email Settings** holds the **Sender name** and **Reply-to email**. Each email has its own subject, content, timing and audience."],[5983,"EasyWebinar groups the things you put in front of an audience under **CTAs**, and there are two kinds. An offer sells something. A poll asks something. Both appear in the room only when you decide to show them."],[92,"EasyWebinar handles both from **Settings**. The agency owner adds the producers and the moderator with **Add user** as **User**, and gives the account manager **Admin**. Each accounting firm then gets a client workspace: a separate account the agency manages, on its own plan. Workspaces don't use team seats, so adding a fifth firm leaves the staff logins as they are."],[3001,"EasyWebinar handles both halves of that launch. The creator runs a **Live** webinar with recording on, then clones it as an **Evergreen** webinar. The copy plays the recording at a time each registrant picks. The live original is untouched, and the evergreen copy takes over for everyone who joins the list later."],[6533,"EasyWebinar handles both with **Clone Webinar**. For each monthly kick-off, the coach clones the webinar as **Live Webinar** and leaves **Registration pages**, **Offers** and **Email notifications** ticked. For the in-between version, she clones it as **Evergreen Webinar** and picks her strongest kick-off recording on the copy's **Content** tab."],[3603,"EasyWebinar handles that split on the webinar's **Notifications** tab. She adds a **Webinar Follow-up** for attendees and another for no-shows, each with its own timing. An **Attendee Action Follow-up** covers people who clicked the offer. She also sets the replay to close on Friday, so her emails and the page tell the same story."],[6714,"EasyWebinar handles this as a single live webinar. The team picks **Weekly**, ticks Tuesday and Thursday, and sets the course dates as the **Start Date** and **End Date (Optional)**. Holidays go in as **Blackout Dates**, and every trainee signs up on the same registration page."],[5135,"EasyWebinar handles this by cloning. She clones the live masterclass, picks **Evergreen** as the copy's type, ticks what to bring across and selects the session's recording. EasyWebinar then generates sessions from the schedule she sets, and the original live webinar is left as it was."],[4465,"EasyWebinar handles this in the **People** view. The team filters **Behavior** for high watch time and offer clicks, then adds **Source & UTM** to see which campaign each person came from. **Lead score** sorts the result, and **Export** hands the filtered list to the agents."],[7444,"EasyWebinar handles this inside the live room. EasyWebinar puts co-hosts and moderators backstage when they join, so the student can sort out their audio unseen and come on stage when called. EasyWebinar keeps questions in their own **Question** panel, split into **Active** and **Answered**, and with recording on the session lands in **Library → Recordings**."],[4971,"EasyWebinar handles this on the schedule step of an evergreen webinar. The brand switches on **Just-in-time Registration** and picks a 15-minute **Interval**, so a session is never far away. **Exclude specific time** keeps chosen hours clear, and each session runs in the shopper's own local time. **On Demand** can sit alongside it for anyone who wants to start straight away."],[8702,"EasyWebinar handles this on the schedule step of an evergreen webinar. The team switches on **On Demand**, and the registration page offers an instant start beside any other options. They change **Instant replay text** to wording such as \"Start the explainer now\". A **Recurring Schedule** can stay on for managers who prefer to book a time."],[8416,"EasyWebinar handles this on the webinar's **Notifications** tab. In **Email Settings**, the broker sets the **Sender name** to their own name and the **Reply-to email** to the office inbox. **Notify admin** sends them a copy of each sign-up. The **Registration Confirmation** then goes out at once, with each person's join link."],[8109,"EasyWebinar handles this on the webinar's **Replay** tab. The educator switches on **Enable replay page** and keeps **Webinar Replica**, so the offer and polls play as they did live. **Expire after days** gives the replay a closing point, and **After the replay ends** sends viewers to the programme's enrolment page. A **Webinar Follow-up** to no-shows carries the link."],[6318,"EasyWebinar handles this with an offer card built on the webinar's **CTAs** tab. The company writes a headline for the bundle, sets its **Offer Price** and switches on **Countdown timer**. The instructor pushes the card from the room's **Offers** panel during the pitch. Afterwards, **Offers Performance** shows the bundle's views, clicks and purchases."],[5523,"EasyWebinar handles this with Chat Simulation (Beta) on the webinar's **Engagement** tab. The author picks **Manual Simulation** and uploads a CSV of timed messages. In the script, `Attendee` lines ask about pace and meeting times, and `Admin` lines answer as the host. **Preview Simulated Chat** shows the whole conversation before she saves."],[2166,"EasyWebinar handles this with client workspaces. Each one is a separate EasyWebinar account that you manage, on its own plan, and it doesn't use one of your team seats. EasyWebinar then pairs a workspace with two add-ons: C-Name for the client's domain and White Label to remove its own branding."],[7239,"EasyWebinar handles this with the green room and backstage. The partners click **Enter Room** and land in the room in a **Not Live** state. Each guest joins with the **Co-presenter Join Link**, waits backstage, and moves to the stage when their topic comes up. The broadcast starts only when a partner clicks **Go Live**."],[2434,"EasyWebinar has no free plan. The standard trial is 7 days and requires a card. Plans are priced flat monthly, with no per-attendee fees, and current prices are on the pricing page."],[2429,"EasyWebinar has registration page templates in categories such as Coach, Lead Magnet and Marketing. Its AI can also draft the script, pages, emails, polls and offers from one description of your webinar."],[6877,"EasyWebinar has three webinar types, and they differ only in how the content is delivered. Pages, emails, polls, offers and analytics are the same across all three."],[5666,"EasyWebinar has two countdowns. An **offer countdown** sits on an offer card in the webinar room and shows how long that offer stays open. A **registration-page countdown** shows how long is left until the session starts. Both are built in, and neither needs a separate timer tool or embedded widget."],[1978,"EasyWebinar holds a SOC 2 Type II report and follows GDPR-aligned data practices. Ask EasyWebinar directly for any detail beyond that."],[8266,"EasyWebinar hosts the file from then on. Upload **MP4** files up to **4 GB**, and EasyWebinar reads the video's length automatically."],[8255,"EasyWebinar hosts the video itself. EasyWebinar lets her upload the file with **Local import**, then stores and serves it the way Vimeo or Wistia would. EasyWebinar reads the length from the file, so she has no duration to type, and the class sits in her Library ready for any webinar."],[8330,"EasyWebinar hosts them. **Local import** uploads your file and serves it, with no other video host involved. Importing from a URL is an option, not a requirement."],[8309,"EasyWebinar hosts your uploads itself, imports links from YouTube, Vimeo and Wistia, and keeps recordings of your live webinars ready to reuse. EasyWebinar is the only platform in this table that does all three."],[1969,"EasyWebinar is a webinar platform for live, simulive and evergreen webinars that collect leads and sell. You build pages, emails, polls and offers, run the webinar live or from a recording, then follow up through analytics and your CRM."],[1692,"EasyWebinar is a webinar platform for running live and recorded webinars that collect leads and sell. You build a webinar with a registration page, emails, polls and offers, run it live or from a recording, and follow up through analytics, integrations and the built-in EasyCRM."],[1944,"EasyWebinar is built around webinars that sell, so the selling tools sit inside the room rather than after it."],[4792,"EasyWebinar is confirmed to run simulive webinars, and evergreen webinars with any mix of just-in-time, on-demand and recurring sessions. In an evergreen webinar, your registrant picks from the options you switch on."],[1003,"EasyWebinar is the webinar platform in front of your course, not the place the course lives. Its AI covers the parts of the webinar that sell it: the script you present, the registration and thank-you pages, the emails, the polls and the offers. You can see the whole flow in the short video below, which walks through an AI-built webinar for live and evergreen sessions."],[1193,"EasyWebinar keeps contacts, a deal pipeline and email broadcasts beside the webinars that produce the leads. It also sends webinar data to an outside CRM when a team prefers its own. You get to choose either route without changing platforms."],[6203,"EasyWebinar keeps questions in their own queue, lets you make that queue public or private, and reports how many questions went unanswered. The same Q&A setting runs on live, simulive and evergreen webinars. EasyWebinar is the only platform in this table that does all four."],[7988,"EasyWebinar keeps recordings, uploads and documents in one Library for the whole account. EasyWebinar saves each recorded live session to the **Recordings** tab, named after its webinar, with its duration and date. The team can then pick that recording as the video for an evergreen webinar, so each new manager registers and watches in their first week."],[5999,"EasyWebinar keeps the agency's polls on the webinar's **CTAs** tab, beside its offer of a free audit. The partners run **Create with AI** with the goals \"qualifying leads\" and \"segmenting for follow-up\", then edit the five polls it writes. During the workshop, one partner launches each poll from the **Polls** panel when it fits the talk. After the session, **People** shows how many polls each attendee answered, next to **Offer clicked**."],[2344,"EasyWebinar keeps the registration page, the reminders, the offer and the follow-up inside one webinar. It shows the offer as a card in the room, with a button that opens your own checkout. It then sends different emails to attendees and no-shows, and it can turn the live session into an evergreen one by cloning it."],[9650,"EasyWebinar keeps those details on the webinar's **Overview** tab. **Scheduling Options** and **Sessions** show each month's sitting, and a sitting that is called off moves to **Cancelled**. The team copies the **Co-presenter Join Link** from **Share** for the guest, who joins without an EasyWebinar account. **Registrants** shows sign-ups on the same screen."],[8878,"EasyWebinar keeps your own questions, a consent checkbox and campaign capture together on one form block. Its **Phone** field also feeds SMS reminders (Beta), sent from an EasyWebinar number. EasyWebinar is the only platform in this table that does all four."],[6055,"EasyWebinar launches polls live, runs the same polls on recorded webinars, and can have AI write them from goals you pick. EasyWebinar is the only platform in this table that does all three."],[8155,"EasyWebinar lets the replay close after a set number of days or on a date, repeat the live offers and polls, run as a separately designed page, and report replay viewers apart from live attendees. EasyWebinar is the only platform in this table that does all four."],[4785,"EasyWebinar lets the team clone the live webinar and choose **Evergreen** on the copy. On the video step, they pick the recording of a past Thursday session. EasyWebinar then offers each registrant a just-in-time session, instant viewing or set weekly times. The polls, offers and emails carry on working as before."],[5892,"EasyWebinar lets you choose whether attendees see each other's messages, embed your own chat tool on recorded webinars, and keep a contact form open with chat switched off. EasyWebinar is the only platform in this table that does all three."],[6547,"EasyWebinar lets you choose, item by item, what comes across to the copy. The webinar schedule can come with it, and so can the integration settings. EasyWebinar is the only platform in this table that does all three."],[9007,"EasyWebinar lets you style the Registration Widget inside the app before you copy it, with no code to edit. The Share dialog holds a one-click registration link, and **Clone Webinar** can copy the widget into a new webinar. EasyWebinar is the only platform in this table that does all four."],[8595,"EasyWebinar lets you time each reminder in hours, minutes and seconds before the session. You can also add a reminder by text or by WhatsApp, both in Beta. EasyWebinar is the only platform in this table that does all three."],[9433,"EasyWebinar makes checkout the final step of signing up. The consultant chooses **Paid** on the pricing step while creating the webinar, and **Register Now** on the registration page then opens a Stripe checkout. EasyWebinar registers a founder only once their payment goes through. It then sends them to the thank-you page, which shows their personal join link."],[5331,"EasyWebinar offers all three as webinar types: **Live**, **Simulive** and **Evergreen**. Simulive and evergreen both need a recording, and live doesn't. All three use the same pages, emails, polls, offers and analytics, so only the delivery differs. You pick the type when you create the webinar, and you can't change it afterwards. The automated webinar overview covers how recordings, schedules and just-in-time sessions fit together across the recorded types."],[7580,"EasyWebinar offers all three types, and you pick one when you create the webinar. All three use the same pages, emails, polls, offers and analytics, and only the delivery differs. The type can't be changed afterwards, so cloning a webinar is how you move a live session to another format."],[2517,"EasyWebinar offers three: Live, Simulive and Evergreen. Live is presented in real time. Simulive plays a recording at set times, with you in the chat. Evergreen plays a recording on a repeating schedule, and each registrant picks their own time."],[3271,"EasyWebinar pairs individual logins with guest join links, so a team pays for seats only for staff. Its clone lets you tick each part a copy includes, and agencies get a separate workspace per client. Together that keeps a monthly calendar moving without rebuilds."],[5408,"EasyWebinar plays a recording at set times with a shared chat you can answer in, and keeps live webinars in the same product. On recorded webinars it can also embed your own chat tool in place of its built-in panel. That lets you keep conversations in the software your team already answers."],[5325,"EasyWebinar plays her best recording as a simulive webinar at the times she sets, every Thursday at the same hour. It keeps the chat as one shared room, so she can join and answer questions while the video plays. On weeks she can't attend, the session still runs. Its offers, polls and pages work exactly as they would on a live webinar."],[6909,"EasyWebinar plays your recording at the times you set while you staff the chat. It hosts an uploaded video itself, plays one linked from YouTube, Vimeo or Wistia, and lists recordings of your past webinars as ready-made content. EasyWebinar is the only platform in this table that does all four."],[1079,"EasyWebinar product documentation"],[1229,"EasyWebinar product documentation"],[1682,"EasyWebinar product documentation"],[1684,"EasyWebinar product documentation"],[1984,"EasyWebinar product documentation"],[1478,"EasyWebinar product documentation: the full library, for the steps before and after your first send."],[519,"EasyWebinar product documentation: the full library."],[5735,"EasyWebinar puts a countdown on the offer and another on the registration page itself. The offer countdown works the same way on live, simulive and evergreen webinars. EasyWebinar is the only platform in this table that does all three."],[6392,"EasyWebinar puts a countdown on the offer card itself and reports views, clicks and purchases for every offer. The same offers run on live, simulive and evergreen webinars in one product. EasyWebinar is the only platform in this table that does all three."],[9286,"EasyWebinar puts each of those links in the webinar's **Share** dialog. The producer sends the guest the **Co-presenter Join Link** and a colleague the **Moderator Join Link for Live room**. Both join without a login and wait backstage until they're brought on. The producer turns on **Shorten URL's** for the show notes and emails the **One-Click Registration Link** to subscribers."],[4515,"EasyWebinar puts everyone from every webinar in one table, filters it by what people did and which campaign brought them, and exports exactly the filtered list. EasyWebinar is the only platform in this table that does all four."],[5016,"EasyWebinar puts just-in-time sessions, instant viewing and set daily or weekly times on one evergreen webinar. It also keeps chosen hours free of just-in-time sessions with **Exclude specific time**, and runs live webinars in the same product. EasyWebinar is the only platform in this table that does all four."],[9316,"EasyWebinar puts one-click registration, join links for co-presenters and moderators, and a toggle for shorter links in the same Share dialog. EasyWebinar is the only platform in this table that does all three."],[1324,"EasyWebinar puts that job on one screen, **Configurations**, inside its CRM. It lists your email services, asks you to verify a domain or a single business address, and lets you choose where replies go. The garden centre's admin could validate the office address for Monday's send and plan the domain work for when volume grows."],[2901,"EasyWebinar puts the booking or application button inside the room, with an optional countdown, and runs the same session live or on repeat. That keeps the next step on screen at the moment a prospect decides, whichever way you deliver the session."],[1150,"EasyWebinar puts the CRM next to the webinars. EasyCRM imports registrants and attendees with **Import from EasyWebinar** and tags each lead with its webinar. It keeps leads, clients and deals in one place, and it sends broadcasts and workflows to saved lists. A team that already has a CRM can connect it instead and skip all of this."],[2612,"EasyWebinar puts the price on the registration page and sends the buyer to a Stripe checkout when they click **Register Now**. Once payment goes through, it registers them and shows their personal join link. It also lets the nutritionist add a **Live + Replay bundle** with its own price, so the recording is sold rather than given away."],[3935,"EasyWebinar puts the registration links, the list and the send under one login. Its Broadcasts screen sets your average open and click rates beside benchmarks, so you know at a glance whether an invitation needs work."],[8832,"EasyWebinar puts those options on the registration form block itself. EasyWebinar lets you add custom fields and a **Phone** field, turn on **GDPR Compliance** with your own wording, and turn on **UTM Params**. What people enter then shows up in the **People** view, ready to filter and export."],[4361,"EasyWebinar puts three of the day-of checks into the way you enter a live session: a device check, a private green room, and a backstage area for co-hosts. It also lets you test AI answers in private before the session. Each of these turns a step on your checklist into something the room does with you."],[8333,"EasyWebinar reads the length of an uploaded file automatically, but not of one hosted elsewhere. It needs the duration to schedule sessions correctly."],[6862,"EasyWebinar reads the length of an uploaded file itself, but not of a linked one. It uses the duration to schedule sessions and to know when the webinar ends, so a wrong figure can cut the video short or leave attendees waiting after it has finished."],[7841,"EasyWebinar records each live session you host by default, keeps the result on a **Recordings** tab in the Library, and lets you pick it as an evergreen webinar's video. The recording state is visible in the room header before you broadcast anything."],[3473,"EasyWebinar records the campaign on each registration and keeps it beside attendance, watch time and offer clicks for every person. It follows up attendees, no-shows and offer clickers with separate emails, and it gives each person a lead score from their engagement."],[3389,"EasyWebinar records the campaign on the registration itself when **UTM Params** is on. It keeps that campaign next to each person's status, watch percentage and offer clicks, and it sends follow-ups to attendees and no-shows separately. Its integrations pass each group to your CRM or email tool as its own event, so tagging happens without an export."],[7772,"EasyWebinar records the live session you host by default. It shows the recording state in the room header before you broadcast anything. It then saves the finished session to your Library under **Recordings**, named after its webinar. From there you can use it as the replay or pick it as the video for an evergreen webinar."],[8001,"EasyWebinar records your live sessions into the same Library that holds your uploads and imported links. Any of those recordings can then become the video for a simulive or evergreen webinar."],[2409,"EasyWebinar runs live and automated sales webinars in one product, with the offer card and its countdown inside the room. It also reports each offer's views, clicks and purchases, so you can see which step of the sale lost people."],[5206,"EasyWebinar runs live and evergreen webinars in one product, and turns a live session into an evergreen one by cloning it with the items you choose. The recording of the live session is ready in the same library, so the evergreen copy plays the version that worked."],[4855,"EasyWebinar runs simulive and evergreen webinars on the same recording, and an evergreen webinar can offer just-in-time, instant and set-time sessions together. It also runs live webinars in the same product, so a live session can be cloned straight into an automated one."],[2810,"EasyWebinar runs that explanation as a webinar. She teaches it live once and puts an offer card in the room with a button to her application form. When the session ends, everyone lands on her booking page. EasyWebinar then lets her clone the session as an evergreen webinar, so new registrants can watch it on a schedule."],[2914,"EasyWebinar runs the session and the step in front of your programme; it doesn't deliver the coaching itself. Your calendar, application form and client sessions stay in the tools you use now. The offer button opens your own page, so booking rules and payment plans are set there."],[3091,"EasyWebinar runs the webinar that sells your course, live or automated, in one product. The enrolment offer appears inside the room, and it can carry a countdown. EasyWebinar is the only platform in this table that does all three."],[6894,"EasyWebinar runs this as one simulive webinar. The school records its strongest taster lesson, uploads it with **Local import**, and sets a **Weekly** schedule for Saturday and Wednesday. A teacher joins each sitting's chat and answers questions about levels, class times and placement while the recording plays."],[3105,"EasyWebinar sells your course; it doesn't host or deliver it. Lessons, student logins and course progress stay on your course platform. The offer button and replay redirect send buyers there."],[1640,"EasyWebinar sends follow-up from the webinar itself and runs longer sequences in a CRM under the same login. You can also pass webinar activity to your own CRM's automation. Either way, follow-up keeps running after every session."],[3734,"EasyWebinar sends one follow-up to attendees and another to no-shows, and a further email when someone clicks your offer. Its built-in CRM can then run a longer sequence under the same login. Every attendee gets the next message their behaviour earned."],[7574,"EasyWebinar separates those jobs inside one live room. The coaches arrive in a green room that broadcasts nothing. The partner waits backstage until moved to the stage, and questions sit in their own queue. Recording is on by default, and an offer card can open the coaches' own application or checkout page."],[8555,"EasyWebinar sets each reminder as time before the webinar, on the **Notifications** tab. The school keeps three: a day, an hour and fifteen minutes before. Each one follows every session on the evergreen schedule. For the final nudge, the school adds a **Reminder SMS**, in Beta, because its audience reads texts quickly."],[1432,"EasyWebinar sets the email service, the sending identity and the reply address on one screen in its own CRM. Those settings then serve broadcasts and workflows, with calling on the next tab. And it's your CRM or ours: keep the CRM you have, or use EasyCRM natively."],[5839,"EasyWebinar sets this on the webinar's **Engagement** tab before the session. The firm keeps **Easywebinar Chat** and sets **Who can see messages** to **Hosts only**. Each attendee then talks privately to the team, and nobody sees anyone else. The colleague joins with the **Moderator Join Link for Live room** and answers from the **Chat** panel in the room."],[1914,"EasyWebinar suits people whose webinars have to keep working after the live hour. That covers creators, coaches, consultants, small businesses and marketing teams. In practice, these are the groups that use it most:"],[3395,"EasyWebinar supports all three. The form takes your own custom fields, **UTM Params** records the campaign on each registration, and the **Tracking Code** settings hold pixels and analytics tags for five webinar pages. Only UTM capture puts the source inside EasyWebinar, where you can read it against real attendance and watch time rather than clicks."],[3207,"EasyWebinar supports the last two directly. Each teammate gets their own login and role, presenters and moderators can be added per webinar, and **Clone Webinar** copies a webinar with the parts you tick."],[5141,"EasyWebinar supports the third way directly. A webinar's type can only be changed by cloning it, and recordings of live sessions are captured automatically when **Auto Recording** is on. They appear on the **Recordings** tab of the video picker, so the copy can play them."],[2177,"EasyWebinar supports the third way. Client workspaces are separate accounts you manage from one place, each on its own plan, and the client gets a confirmation email to join. The custom domain screen under **Settings** manages clients' access to custom domains, and the White Label add-on removes EasyWebinar branding from pages and the room."],[1835,"EasyWebinar tags contacts by what they did in the session, sends each person's join link into a CRM field, and offers its own CRM, EasyCRM, that connects the same way. EasyWebinar is the only platform in this table that does all three."],[9482,"EasyWebinar takes payment as part of sign-up: **Register Now** opens a Stripe checkout, and the person is registered once they've paid. It can also sell the replay at its own price, and it lists every payment against the webinar. EasyWebinar is the only platform in this table that does all three."],[2691,"EasyWebinar takes payment through Stripe inside the registration step and can sell the replay as its own option. It then shows the workshop's revenue on the webinar itself. Buyers pay once, get their link at once, and you see the result in one place."],[834,"EasyWebinar takes the fourth route. It asks for the number of slides and the duration, writes the script slide by slide, and organises it into named sections, each with its own timing and speaker notes. You can edit all of it, regenerate a fresh version, and download it as a PDF."],[4146,"EasyWebinar turns a description of your session into a script with named, timed sections, then writes polls from the goals you choose and offers with an optional countdown. That keeps the outline, the script and the moments you ask for action in one plan."],[210,"EasyWebinar turns her description into a complete webinar through **Create with AI**. She sets **Type** to **Live**, adds the **Polls** and **Offers** chips and clicks **Generate**. The script comes first, and the pages are written from it. She chooses **Balanced Approach** for the offer and downloads the script as a PDF to rehearse."],[606,"EasyWebinar turns her description into a script, then writes her registration page, thank-you page and waiting area from that script. It picks a template unless she chooses one, and it opens every page for editing. She reads the copy, corrects anything about the offer, sets the schedule and publishes."],[7078,"EasyWebinar turns that recording into one evergreen webinar with a single schedule. The team keeps its Tuesday slot as a **Weekly** **Recurring Schedule** and switches on **Just-in-time Registration** beside it. The registration page offers both as choices, so the Wednesday prospect can take a session that begins minutes later instead of next week."],[3912,"EasyWebinar works with your CRM or ours. Keep HubSpot, Salesforce Pardot (Account Engagement), ActiveCampaign, Mailchimp or Kit (formerly ConvertKit), or use EasyCRM natively. Paste the same registration link into your tool's campaign. Then connect that tool to EasyWebinar so registrants are tagged by what they did."],[4170,"EasyWebinar writes a timed script from a description you give it, in named sections with speaker notes. It does not hand you a blank outline, so fill in a template like the one on this page and use it as your description."],[827,"EasyWebinar writes that draft. She describes the session, its audience, its tone and the offer, then sets the number of slides and the duration. EasyWebinar writes the script slide by slide, in named sections with their own timings and speaker notes. If the draft runs long or sounds wrong, she changes the slides or duration and regenerates."],[912,"EasyWebinar writes the webinar script slide by slide from your description, after you set the slide count and duration. Each section comes with its own timing and speaker notes, and the registration, thank-you and waiting pages are written from the same script, so what you promise matches what you teach."],[692,"EasyWebinar writes your registration, thank-you and waiting pages from the script it has just drafted, in the same build as your emails. The page then promises what the session actually covers, and you edit it in the same builder as every other page."],[4616,"EasyWebinar's **Analytics** tab does that count for each webinar. Its **Overview** view runs from **Visitors** and **Registered** through **Live Attended** and **Replay Watched**. Further down, **Offers Performance** reports each offer's views and clicks. For this team, that shows whether the extra registrants stopped before the session, during it, or at the demo button."],[4666,"EasyWebinar's **Analytics** tab follows one webinar from page visits to offer sales and revenue. It reports each offer's purchases next to its views and clicks, and counts live and replay viewers without double counting. EasyWebinar is the only platform in this table that does all four."],[1047,"EasyWebinar's AI covers the webinar before and during the session. It drafts the script, pages, emails and polls from one prompt, writes simulated chat (Beta) for recorded webinars, and answers attendee questions from Pro onward."],[411,"EasyWebinar's AI drafts the email sequence using the script as source material, as part of building the webinar. The build also writes the script first, and the AI's help text warns that fixing the script then is much easier than fixing the pages and emails built from it. So the quality of your emails starts with your prompt and your script."],[9174,"EasyWebinar's builder starts you from a ready-made template, can have AI write the page copy from your script, and puts a countdown on the registration page itself. EasyWebinar is the only platform in this table that does all three."],[5586,"EasyWebinar's Chat Simulation (Beta) can write the chat with AI or play a script you upload as a CSV. It can also add simulated names to the attendee list. EasyWebinar is the only platform in this table that does all three."],[8451,"EasyWebinar's confirmation goes out from a sender name and reply-to address you set for each webinar, and **Notify admin** can copy every registration to your inbox. A WhatsApp welcome message, in Beta, can go out at the same moment. EasyWebinar is the only platform in this table that does all four."],[286,"EasyWebinar's Create with AI writes the presentation script, the registration pages, the email sequence, and the polls and offers from one description. EasyWebinar is the only platform in this table that does all four."],[1346,"EasyWebinar's guidance is that a verified domain is worth the DNS work if you send in any volume. If your first send is a small list and it's due soon, the single address is the quicker way to start. Neither route can promise that a given message lands in the inbox, since the receiving mail system makes that decision. For the wider picture, our guide to webinar email marketing covers what happens after your mail is sending."],[7456,"EasyWebinar's live room gives you a private green room, a backstage for co-hosts, and streaming out to YouTube and LinkedIn from the same screen you present from. EasyWebinar is the only platform in this table that does all three."],[7645,"EasyWebinar's live room gives you a private green room, drawing on your own share and streaming out, and the same product runs your recorded webinars. Its strength is that the live session and its automated afterlife sit together."],[2816,"EasyWebinar's offer button opens any URL you paste, so all three routes work: your booking page, your application form or your checkout. The **End of Session** setting and the replay redirect can send people to the same page. EasyWebinar can also charge for registration itself through your Stripe account, which suits a paid workshop."],[8731,"EasyWebinar's On Demand puts a watch-now button on the same registration page as just-in-time sessions and set daily or weekly times. You also choose the button's wording with **Instant replay text**, and you run live webinars in the same product. EasyWebinar is the only platform in this table that does all four."],[9662,"EasyWebinar's Overview gives each webinar private join links for guest presenters, a one-click registration link for known contacts and a **Revenue** figure. Sessions that are called off stay on their own **Cancelled** tab. EasyWebinar is the only platform in this table that does all four."],[1577,"EasyWebinar's own guidance names three workflows that earn their place. Build one, publish it, and watch it for a full cycle before adding the next. A workflow that sends the wrong thing sends it to everyone."],[8499,"Edit a reminder"],[9053,"Edit blocks"],[351,"Edit the emails on the Notifications tab"],[553,"Edit the generated pages"],[2389,"Edit the headline and promise in the builder, check the mobile view, then click **Publish**."],[339,"Edit the wording before anything sends"],[9480,"Educators in fields such as real estate, finance or wellness run paid seminars. Paid registration keeps the attendee list limited to people who paid, and the transaction list gives a record of every purchase."],[4690,"Either the webinar hasn't run yet, or your date range doesn't cover the period when it did."],[6861,"Either way, the video is saved to your library and can be reused on other webinars. For the full upload and import walkthrough, see Video hosting."],[1854,"Eleven, from **Registered** to **Clicked offer**. Each mapping applies the tag you choose when its event fires."],[1676,"Email domain authentication and CRM sending setup"],[1224,"Email domain authentication for EasyCRM"],[1292,"Email domain authentication, or verifying one business address instead, has to be done before any broadcast or workflow can leave your account. The job has three parts: choose an email service, verify the domain or business address you send as, and decide where replies go. In EasyWebinar you do all of it once, on the **Configurations** screen of its built-in CRM, EasyCRM. A webinar's own confirmation and reminder emails aren't part of this setup, because each webinar has separate settings for them. It's your CRM or ours, so if you already run HubSpot, Salesforce Pardot or ActiveCampaign, you can keep it and skip this setup."],[1230,"Email Domain Authentication: Verify a Domain or Address and Choose How You Send"],[2185,"Email each client their numbers and import the leads into their CRM yourself."],[3240,"Email guest presenters the account password, then change it afterwards."],[2878,"Email no-shows the recording link by hand, with a closing date you'll have to remember."],[1673,"Email sender guidelines, Gmail Help: what Gmail asks of bulk senders, including one-click unsubscribe and the spam rate to stay under."],[3971,"Email sender guidelines, Gmail Help: what Gmail requires of every sender and of bulk senders."],[512,"Email Subject Lines: 5 Tips to Attract Readers (Nielsen Norman Group): how to front-load subject lines and keep them short enough to show in full."],[3764,"Email Subject Lines: 5 Tips to Attract Readers, Nielsen Norman Group, 2014: why useful words go first, and why names and symbols rarely help."],[3968,"Email subject lines: 5 tips, Nielsen Norman Group (2014): how long a subject line can be before it's cut off."],[1181,"Email, SMS (Beta) and calling need setting up in **Configurations** before anything sends. That includes verifying who you send as. Nothing goes out until it's done. The steps are in email domain authentication for EasyCRM."],[162,"Emails"],[8652,"Emails"],[9377,"Emails"],[4922,"Emails and reminders"],[6786,"Emails and reminders"],[6975,"Emails and reminders"],[5785,"Embed a third-party chat tool"],[9062,"Embedding the form on your own site"],[7610,"End the session, find the recording file and send the replay to everyone who missed it."],[6187,"Ending the session disconnects everyone and nobody can rejoin, so finish the questions you want to answer before you click **End Session**."],[6612,"Engagement in the room"],[8431,"Enter a **Reply-to email**."],[8430,"Enter a **Sender name**."],[8271,"Enter the **Video duration** in hours, minutes and seconds."],[7018,"Enter the **Webinar Name** your registrants will see."],[2202,"Enter the domain once the record is in place. DNS changes can take a few hours to spread, so give it time before assuming something is wrong. Set the domain before you promote anything, because changing a subdomain later breaks every link already shared."],[7318,"Enter the EasyWebinar webinar room, prepare in the green room, go live, present with chat, polls, offers and Q&A, then end the session and find your recording."],[6029,"Enter the room from the webinar's **Overview** with **Enter Room**."],[2079,"Enter the room well before your start time. The green room broadcasts nothing, so you can pass the device check, finish your checks and test **Share** before anyone is watching. Close other video-call tools before you click **Enter Room**, so nothing else is holding the camera. For the kit itself, see the webinar equipment guide and this host preparation guide."],[4381,"Enter the room, pick your camera, microphone and speakers, and continue to the green room. Check your framing and screen share, make sure co-hosts are backstage and recording is on, then go live."],[63,"Enter their **Name** and **Email**, and optionally a **Photo**."],[9535,"Entering a running session on a recorded webinar"],[5395,"Entering as an admin from Overview shows your own host tools, not the attendee view, so an embedded widget won't appear there. The Overview tab page explains the Sessions panel in full."],[1877,"Evergreen"],[2280,"Evergreen"],[2452,"Evergreen"],[7134,"Evergreen"],[8506,"Evergreen and just-in-time sessions"],[3860,"Evergreen and just-in-time webinars change the timing. A recorded webinar that runs every day, like an evergreen webinar, doesn't need a countdown. Invite people when you launch it, then again when you change the topic or the offer."],[7094,"Evergreen features, from each platform's public documentation:"],[7343,"Evergreen from a live session"],[2349,"Evergreen makes the recording available around the clock, and each registrant picks a time that suits them. It suits an offer you sell all year. When your live session has gone well, you can turn it into an evergreen webinar by cloning it and choosing **Evergreen** on the copy."],[9384,"Evergreen paid trainings"],[4715,"Evergreen recurring schedule: set times that repeat"],[5474,"Evergreen schedules"],[7068,"Evergreen suits a webinar that belongs to a funnel and should work whether or not you're free. Typical examples are a product demo, customer onboarding or a year-round offer. People reach it at all hours, so it has to be ready whenever they do."],[5207,"Evergreen webinar features for reusing a live session, from each platform's public documentation:"],[5052,"Evergreen Webinar: Turn a Live Session Into One by Cloning It and Setting a Schedule"],[7082,"Evergreen webinars can use **Easywebinar Chat**, embed an external chat tool with **Third party**, or turn chat off with **No Chat** while keeping the **EW Contact Box** for questions sent by email."],[5005,"Evergreen webinars have a **Live** tab in the Sessions panel, alongside **Upcoming**, **Past** and **Cancelled**, showing sessions currently on air. The webinar Overview tab explains the rest of that screen."],[2518,"Evergreen, in most cases, because it runs without you being there. Many people run the session live a few times first to sharpen it. Then they clone it as Evergreen and use the recording."],[7505,"Evergreen: a recording on a repeating schedule"],[5261,"Evergreen: a time each registrant picks"],[5784,"Evergreen: simulate the room"],[463,"Every AI draft lands in one of these five groups, so this is where you change wording, adjust timing and add the follow-ups your goal needs."],[4787,"Every automated webinar plays a recording. What differs is when each session starts and who watches it together. Each way below catches a different kind of registrant and misses another."],[3226,"Every card shows the webinar's type, its name, the next session's date, time and timezone, and its registrant count. Webinars built with **Create with AI** also carry an **AI** badge, so the team can see which drafts still need a human edit."],[2161,"Every client sees a stranger's name in their links, and some will hesitate to register. Clients' registrant lists sit side by side in one account. Reporting turns into a guessing game about which numbers belong to whom."],[2435,"Every EasyWebinar plan includes live webinars. Automation, EasyCRM and checkout start at the Growth plan, so an evergreen or simulive sales webinar needs Growth or above."],[9262,"Every EasyWebinar webinar generates seven links, and the **Share** button on the webinar's header shows them all in one dialog. One is the public registration link you promote; others let a known contact register in one click, let attendees join, let a co-presenter or moderator into the room, and send people to the replay. The dialog also holds the **Registration Widget** embed code, a **Share on social media** section, and a **Shorten URL's** toggle for shorter versions of every link."],[4592,"Every EasyWebinar webinar has an **Analytics** tab that shows how many people reached each stage of that webinar and where the rest dropped away. It has three views: **Overview** for the funnel, engagement and offer numbers, **People** for the individuals behind those numbers, and **Revenue** for what the webinar earned. A date range at the top limits everything on the page to the period you choose."],[9571,"Every EasyWebinar webinar opens on its **Overview** tab. From this one screen you can see how the webinar is doing, check and change when it runs, act on a single session, switch between free and paid registration, add the people who present or moderate, and get to the share links and the room. This page walks through each panel in the order you'll usually need it. When you're done, you'll know where every webinar-level control on the Overview lives and what each number means."],[1171,"Every import is kept as an **audience** with its source, member count and status. If an import fails, open the audience's **Details**. It's usually a column that didn't map to a field."],[1986,"Every limit, allowance and default setting in EasyWebinar in one place, with its unit and where it applies."],[3861,"Every line of an invitation has a job. If a line doesn't help someone decide to register, cut it."],[7825,"Every live session you record lands on this tab, so match the card's name and date to the session you ran."],[1708,"Every page shows who it applies to, its status and the date it was last checked against the product. Each heading has a permanent link you can copy and share."],[2366,"Every part of your in-room offer is set on this one screen, from the countdown to where the button goes. The price shown is sample data for a demo brand."],[2396,"Every plan includes live webinars with browser join, so attendees click a link and watch without installing anything. Automation, EasyCRM and checkout start at the Growth plan. There's no free plan: the standard trial is 7 days and requires a card. Pricing is flat monthly, with no per-attendee fees, and monthly plans are available. Current plans are on the pricing page."],[4122,"Every poll and offer from your outline sits on this one list. The offer titles and prices shown are sample data for a demo webinar."],[5988,"Every poll on a webinar sits in one list on the CTAs tab. Each one can be switched on or off from that list without being deleted, so a poll can wait in reserve until the point in the session where it fits."],[9309,"Every public link includes your subdomain, ending in `.easywebinar.live`, including the links in your emails. The **C-Name** add-on lets links use your own domain instead. Changing your subdomain changes your existing links, so anything already shared will break; set it before you promote."],[430,"Every reminder's timing is set as a period before the webinar, shown as, for example, *1h 0m 0s before webinar* or *0h 15m 0s before webinar*. Open a reminder on the **Notifications** tab to change it."],[8551,"Every result that matters to the business, from offer clicks to booked calls, depends on people actually watching. That makes reminders matter most to teams that sell or book calls at the end of a session. It matters even more on automated webinars, where sessions run without anyone checking the emails."],[4780,"Every session needs you live, at one fixed time. Someone who registers on a Tuesday for a Thursday slot has two days to lose interest. Anyone in a distant timezone may never find a slot at all. Your reach stops at the number of hours you can present."],[5386,"Every session plays the video you click here, so pick the cut you'd be happy to show every audience."],[4615,"Every stage up to the demo button happens on the webinar platform: the page visit, the sign-up, the session, the recording and the click. A platform that runs all of those can count every stage for the same webinar, so nobody has to merge lists by hand."],[4815,"Every step repeats for every session, and anyone who arrives between slots waits for the next one."],[3714,"Every tile reads zero here because this sample webinar hasn't run. After your session, Replay Watched and Missed are the two to compare once the no-show emails have gone."],[6901,"Every video you add, and every recording of a past webinar, lands in the **Library**. Recordings appear there automatically when **Auto Recording** is on in the live room. See The Library."],[8300,"Every video you add, by either route, appears on the Library's **Videos** tab with a badge in its corner: **EasyWebinar** for a hosted file, or the platform's logo for an imported link. Recordings of live sessions appear on the **Recordings** tab."],[5327,"Every webinar answers two questions: who supplies the content, and who decides when it plays. The three ways of running one answer them differently, and each one catches or misses something for a repeated session."],[1928,"Every webinar follows the same order, whichever type you choose. Here is what you do, and what to check at each step."],[8958,"Every webinar has a registration page hosted by EasyWebinar, and a **Registration Page Link** that sends people to it. The Registration Widget is the other route: instead of sending visitors to EasyWebinar, you bring the form to them, on a page you already control."],[9099,"Every webinar has five pages that its audience moves through: **Registration Page**, **Thank you Page**, **Waiting Area**, **Webinar Page** and **Replay Page**. All five open in the same builder, and all five already know when your webinar runs."],[1010,"Every webinar starts from nothing. The script, pages and emails get written one after another, often by the same tired person, and the offer copy drifts away from what the session teaches."],[8398,"Every webinar's **Notifications** tab has three channels: **Emails**, **SMS** and **Whatsapp**. SMS and WhatsApp are in Beta. The **Emails** channel groups everything your webinar sends into five kinds of email:"],[4308,"Every webinar's Overview tab has its own share links, including a **Co-presenter Join Link** and a **Moderator Join Link for Live room**. Send each person the link for their role, and keep the **Attendee Join Link** for registrants. A co-host who joins on an attendee link watches the session instead of joining it. The sharing links page lists every link and who it is for."],[1818,"Everyone on the list gets the same follow-up, whether they watched to the end or never turned up. Interested people wait in a spreadsheet while the moment passes. Sales has no way to tell a casual sign-up from someone who clicked the offer."],[3203,"Everyone signs in with the same email and password. It is quick to set up, but you can't tell who changed what, and only one of you can host in the live room. When someone leaves, the password has to change for everyone."],[87,"Everyone works from one login. Nobody can tell who changed a webinar or a setting, and only one person can host the live room at a time. Anyone holding that password can also reach billing and every account setting, whether their job needs it or not."],[1477,"Everything EasyCRM includes: the leads, deals and marketing tools these sending settings serve."],[1182,"Everything EasyCRM sends draws on a monthly allowance, and **Wallet** shows what's left. The Wallet screen lists 1,000 emails, 100 SMS (Beta) messages and 100 call minutes a month. The cycle resets on your signup date, not the first of the month. Workflows use more than broadcasts over time, because they keep sending every day."],[2038,"Everything EasyCRM sends draws on this monthly allowance, and its **Wallet** screen shows what's left. The allowance resets on your **signup date**, not the first of the month. Broadcasts and workflows draw on the same allowance, and each channel is counted separately."],[4339,"Everything in the green room stays private, so this is where the day-of half of the checklist gets done."],[1037,"Everything the AI drafts comes from this one prompt, so a specific description here saves editing in every later step."],[1004,"Everything the AI produces stays editable. The finished webinar behaves exactly like one you built by hand, with the same tabs and settings, so nothing locks you into the draft."],[4121,"Everything the outline planned for the audience to answer or click lives on the **CTAs** tab. Open the webinar and click **CTAs** to see every poll and offer, filter by **All**, **Polls** or **Offers**, and switch each one on or off from its row."],[891,"Everything the script says starts from this prompt, so the audience, the three teaching points and the offer should all be written here."],[7411,"Everything you use while presenting sits on the right-hand rail:"],[622,"Expect to edit, not rebuild. The product's own guidance treats the generated pages as a strong first draft, and it singles out pricing and what's included as the things to read closely. The checks below take most people well under an hour, because the layout and most of the copy are already there."],[9240,"Expired links"],[2183,"Export each client's registrant and attendee lists after every webinar."],[2379,"Export the call's attendance list and match it against the sign-up sheet."],[1591,"Export the registrant list from the webinar's People view."],[3889,"Export your contacts to a spreadsheet and remove anyone who has unsubscribed."],[726,"F-Shaped Pattern of Reading on the Web, Nielsen Norman Group: where eyes land on a page and how headings change it."],[3528,"Few messages, each with its own job"],[2457,"Fill a sales pipeline"],[6011,"Fill in the **Response Options**. Click **Add another option** for each extra answer, and click the bin beside any option to remove it."],[4106,"Fill in the minutes column of the template so the total matches your slot exactly."],[5690,"Fill in the rest of the offer: **Offer Style** (**Text Offer** or **Image Offer**), **Offer Price** (or switch on **Free**), the **Headline** and **Sub Headline**, and the **Button** text and URL."],[4209,"Fill in where attendees go at the end"],[5452,"Fill the chat on a simulive or evergreen webinar with a conversation generated by AI from a cast of simulated attendees, or scripted by you in a timed CSV."],[4541,"Filter **Behavior** for high watch time and offer clicks. Those are people who were interested and haven't bought yet."],[4503,"Filter **People** by **Source & UTM** to see which campaign each registrant came from."],[4534,"Filter by **Behavior** for no-shows, add a **Webinar** filter for a single event, then click **Export**."],[4536,"Filter by **Source & UTM**. You need **UTM Params** turned on in your registration form first."],[9117,"Filter by category: **All Templates**, **Agency**, **Coach**, **Education**, **Health & Wellness**, **Lead Magnet** or **Marketing**. **My Templates** holds templates you've saved yourself."],[6694,"Filter by category: **All Templates**, **Agency**, **Coach**, **Education**, **Health & Wellness**, **Lead Magnet**, **Marketing**, or **My Templates** for ones you have saved."],[4498,"Filter first, then export. Exporting everything and cutting it down in a spreadsheet repeats work the filters already do, and **Export** respects whatever filters are applied."],[3334,"Filter People by source after the session"],[5183,"Filter to Recordings to find the live session by its webinar name and date, so the copy plays the version that worked."],[2205,"Filtering by Agency narrows the template grid to layouts built for client work, and Skip & Create Webinar lets you choose a design later."],[3259,"Filters, search and the card menu are how a busy team finds the right webinar, clones it or archives it."],[2571,"Financial education for the public"],[3141,"Find any webinar in a busy account"],[2674,"Find it in the webinar's **Analytics** tab under **Revenue**, then **Paid Webinar**. It lists completed, pending and abandoned checkouts, and a searchable list of every transaction with its status."],[1357,"Find out who controls the domain's DNS, and agree a time to make the changes."],[3770,"Find people by what they did: the filters to use when you want to write to one group by hand."],[8424,"Find the **Registration Confirmation** group at the top of the list."],[7803,"Find the file. Chromebook recordings save to the Downloads folder unless you choose another folder."],[7720,"Find the recording"],[2475,"Find the row closest to what you're trying to do. The format column tells you what to pick when you create the webinar, and the last column is where to go next."],[6490,"Find the webinar to copy. The type filters (**All**, **Live**, **Simulive**, **Evergreen**, **Archived**) and search help with a long list."],[1688,"Find what you need by role"],[6249,"Find your offers"],[5940,"Find your polls"],[8498,"Find your reminders"],[1774,"Find your tool under **Available integrations** and click **Connect**."],[7884,"Find, add and manage the videos, webinar recordings, images and documents your webinars use, see which files count towards your storage, and put a library video to work in a simulive or evergreen webinar."],[554,"Finish the build and find your pages"],[255,"First choose how you want to position the offer:"],[2056,"Fix it"],[2959,"Follow up"],[4547,"Follow up after a course webinar: how a course creator acts on the people who clicked but didn't enrol."],[2753,"Follow up by what each person did"],[2296,"Follow up with attendees and no-shows"],[6114,"Follow-up"],[5645,"Follow-up and CRM tags"],[2118,"Follow-up and lead handoff for each client"],[4421,"Follow-up emails"],[4567,"Follow-up emails"],[6261,"Follow-up emails"],[8054,"Follow-up emails"],[3061,"Follow-up emails send after the webinar to the audience you choose: everyone who registered, only those who attended, or only the no-shows. No-shows are usually the biggest group, and the replay link is what they want."],[3545,"Follow-up mistakes that are easy to make today"],[3540,"Follow-up templates for people who clicked or left early"],[1882,"Follow-up: analytics and your CRM or ours"],[3748,"Follow-ups are set per webinar, so a new webinar needs its own set or a clone of an earlier one. The replay link is public while the replay page is on, so anyone you forward it to can watch. EasyWebinar also doesn't host or deliver your course: the offer button and any redirect send people to your own checkout or sales page. SMS (Beta) and WhatsApp (Beta) messages come from an EasyWebinar number, so replies don't reach your phone."],[3700,"Follow-ups belong to one webinar, so your next session needs its own set. Cloning the webinar can bring its email notifications with it, as well as its polls and offers. After cloning, update the dates, the replay link and the deadline in every email."],[8508,"Follow-ups for people the reminders didn't reach"],[2220,"For a client report, filter the People list by webinar or behaviour, then click **Export**. Filter first, then export, so the spreadsheet holds only what the client needs. There are no scheduled report emails, so build the monthly note from these two sources."],[3850,"For a coach or consultant, a webinar is often the start of a booked call or a new client. A room of people who already trust you is worth more than a room of strangers. The invitation decides how full that room gets."],[1430,"For a coach, the reply is often the point of the email, because a reply can start a client conversation. Set **Reply & forwarding settings** with the same care as the identity, and use an address you check daily. A single business address often suits this kind of low-volume sending."],[7806,"For a live webinar you run in EasyWebinar, you skip steps 2 to 7. You check that the header reads **Auto Recording Enabled**, go live, and find the session in **Library** → **Recordings** afterwards. If you do have a video file of your own, **Add Media** → **Local import** uploads it to the Library, where EasyWebinar hosts it like any other video. Video hosting covers that."],[9300,"For a moderator, to handle chat and questions. Like the co-presenter link, it works without an account. It's also a handy way to check your own webinar from the inside: on a recorded webinar with an embedded third-party chat, joining with the **Moderator Join Link** lets you look at the side panel."],[5729,"For a paid workshop, the registration-page countdown shows how long is left to register before the session starts. Inside the workshop, a countdown on an offer can mark a follow-on programme available to attendees only."],[9299,"For a presenter, so they can join the room. They don't need an EasyWebinar account to use it. When a co-host or moderator joins a live session, they land backstage, not on stage, and your audience doesn't see or hear them until you move them to the stage."],[4605,"For a quick read without opening the tab, the webinar's **Overview** tab shows four live stats (**Registrants**, **Live Attended**, **Total Attended** and **Revenue**) that update as the webinar runs. See The Overview tab."],[5578,"For an automated webinar that should still feel busy, pair **Everyone** chat and Chat Simulation with **Private Q&A**, so real questions reach your team in a queue."],[7962,"For an imported video you also enter its length, because EasyWebinar needs the duration to schedule sessions. See Video hosting for both routes step by step."],[7795,"For audience numbers once the replay is out, use Webinar analytics."],[228,"For example: a 45-minute live masterclass for experienced freelance designers who want recurring revenue without hiring, covering why hourly billing caps growth, how to turn a repeatable service into a fixed-scope offer, and how to price it. Warm and practical, no hype. End with an offer for a six-week group programme with templates and weekly calls, plus its price."],[7118,"For just-in-time sessions, yes. Daily and weekly sessions run in the webinar's timezone."],[4830,"For just-in-time, set the **Interval** to every 2, 15, 30, 45 or 60 minutes, and use **Exclude specific time** for hours to keep clear."],[632,"For layout ideas beyond the generated draft, the blog's webinar landing page examples and its guide to high-conversion landing page essentials are worth a look before you edit."],[7778,"For live webinars you run in EasyWebinar, the confirmed method is the first one. Auto Recording is on by default, its state shows in the room header, and recorded sessions land in **Library** → **Recordings**. Two things are confirmed as never in the recording: drawings on a shared screen, and an attendee zooming in on a shared screen or file."],[3438,"For next quarter's live session, clone this webinar and choose to copy its integration settings, so the new webinar feeds the same CRM."],[4659,"For paid webinars, the **Revenue** view is where every registration payment and its status appear. See Paid webinars."],[9296,"For people watching the recording afterwards. It's the same link as the **Replay Page Link** on the webinar's **Replay** tab, where you also turn the replay page on with **Enable replay page**."],[1021,"For polls, you pick goals such as gauging interest in your offer, and the AI writes five, each with a note on where it fits. For offers, you choose a soft, balanced or direct pitch, and the AI writes the title, headline and button text. You then manage them as polls and offers like any others."],[9295,"For registered attendees, to enter the live session. Registrants also receive a join link in the **Registration Confirmation** email, which is sent the moment someone registers. That's why it's the one email you shouldn't turn off."],[4386,"For SMS (Beta), yes: select a template and click **Send Test SMS**. WhatsApp (Beta) can be tested on your own number too. For email reminders, register with your own address and check what arrives."],[8828,"For teams that run webinars to generate leads or sell, the registration form is where first-party data starts. It matters most to whoever follows up, in the first days after a session. That's when a role, a phone number or a campaign tag decides who hears from you first."],[1956,"For the CRM, the rule is your CRM or ours. Keep HubSpot, Salesforce Pardot (Account Engagement), ActiveCampaign, Mailchimp or Kit (formerly ConvertKit), or use EasyCRM natively. Other connections include GoHighLevel, Keap, AWeber, Drip, Ontraport and Zapier. You map your webinar data as rules: when an event happens, then take an action, with a value such as a tag."],[4831,"For the recurring schedule, choose **Daily** or **Weekly** and add times with **Add Time**."],[7067,"For the scheduled-broadcast version, see Create a simulive webinar."],[907,"For the wider planning around a session, the blog's guide on how to create webinars covers topic, format and promotion."],[2373,"For warmer leads, **Attendee Action Follow-ups** send based on what someone did, such as clicking your offer. In People, the filter for high watch time plus an offer click shows who was interested and didn't buy."],[1582,"For what to write in each message, the guide to automating webinar follow-ups with CRM tools walks through the timing and content."],[8844,"Form changes reach visitors only once the page is published. **Save** keeps a draft; **Publish** makes it public."],[5610,"Four columns, `HH:MM:SS,Name,Role,Message`, saved as UTF-8 CSV. **Download sample CSV** gives you the exact layout."],[4166,"Four things: how to ask a question, how long the session runs, whether there is a replay, and where to click when you share a link. Say them aloud too, because people who join late miss the slide."],[748,"From a blank page"],[749,"From a fill-in template"],[1023,"From Pro onward, AI Moderator answers attendee questions using context you upload, including PDFs and other files. It works during live, simulive, automated and other webinar types. Upload the files that hold the answers people actually ask for, such as what the course includes. Questions you take yourself still run through questions and answers."],[7138,"From registration to follow-up"],[8922,"From the Content tab"],[8923,"From the Share dialog"],[4335,"From the webinar's **Overview**, click **Enter Room**. You're asked to check your camera, microphone and speakers, then click **Continue to Green Room**."],[7780,"From the webinar's Overview, click **Enter Room**."],[750,"From your slides first"],[4632,"Further down the **Overview**:"],[378,"Further reading"],[580,"Further reading"],[801,"Further reading"],[1290,"Further reading"],[1535,"Further reading"],[2145,"Further reading"],[2324,"Further reading"],[2591,"Further reading"],[2789,"Further reading"],[3179,"Further reading"],[3366,"Further reading"],[3581,"Further reading"],[3833,"Further reading"],[4038,"Further reading"],[4250,"Further reading"],[4757,"Further reading"],[5109,"Further reading"],[5299,"Further reading"],[7546,"Further reading"],[7745,"Further reading"],[251,"gathering background"],[249,"gauging interest in your offer"],[6361,"Generated offers appear on the CTAs tab and are edited like any other. Read the copy before you publish, particularly anything about price and what's included."],[681,"Generated pages are ordinary webinar pages once the build ends, so everything else in the page builder applies to them."],[276,"Generated pages open in the same drag-and-drop builder as any other, on the webinar's **Content** tab. Change templates, edit blocks, add **UTM Params** to the form, then publish. See Registration page builder."],[676,"Generated pages open in this builder, so you can change any block, swap the template or check the mobile view before you publish."],[278,"Generated polls and offers appear on the **CTAs** tab, already written and editable like any other. See Polls and Offers."],[6044,"Generated polls land on the CTAs tab and are edited like any poll you wrote yourself. Read them against your script before the webinar."],[2290,"Get people to turn up"],[8921,"Get the embed code"],[7784,"Get your offers and polls ready, because the **Go Live** confirmation reminds you to."],[252,"getting feedback on delivery"],[8545,"Getting people to register is the easy part; getting them to turn up is what notifications are for. Reminders bring the date, the time and the way in back to each registrant. They land the day before, when people can still plan, and in the final minutes, when they need a nudge to click."],[2363,"Getting people to register is the easy part. Getting them to turn up is what reminders are for. A common pattern is three reminder emails: a day before, an hour before and fifteen minutes before. The last one does most of the work."],[2957,"Getting people to turn up"],[3214,"Give **Admin** only to people who need to change billing, team or account settings. Everyone else who builds or runs webinars can be a **User**. The full set-up is on team members and roles."],[71,"Give **Admin** to people who need to change billing, team or account settings. **User** suits presenters and moderators and anyone who works on webinars without touching the account."],[3867,"Give an honest reason to act this week: a live question-and-answer slot, a limited number of seats, or a handout for people who attend. Don't invent scarcity you won't keep."],[2,"Give colleagues their own EasyWebinar login, choose Admin or User, and understand how team members differ from presenters, moderators and client workspaces."],[47,"Give each colleague who builds webinars or reads your analytics their own EasyWebinar login, as an **Admin** or a **User**. Sharing one login means you can't tell who did what, and only one of you can be in the live room as host. When you finish, the new member is listed under **Settings → Team** and can sign in with the details you give them."],[845,"Give each point its own block of time, roughly six to seven minutes each for three points. For each one, say the idea, give an example, then say what the viewer can do this week."],[3291,"Give every person their own login with the right role, and name one owner per webinar. Start each new webinar as a copy of the last good one, then archive old webinars once their follow-up ends."],[4176,"Give every section a fixed end time in the outline, treat questions as protected time, and rehearse with a timer. If you run long on the day, shorten the last teaching point rather than the offer or questions."],[5379,"Give it a name and choose **Simulive Webinar**. Click **Continue to Schedule**."],[4828,"Give it a name, choose **Evergreen Webinar**, and click **Continue to Schedule**."],[5870,"Give the box a **Box title**. Attendees see it above the widget, so a plain label such as \"Live Chat\" or \"Ask the team\" works better than the tool's name."],[6332,"Give the offer an internal **Title**, then write the **Headline** and **Sub Headline**."],[2752,"Give the replay a deadline"],[8270,"Give the video a title and paste the **Video URL**."],[8259,"Give the video a title. This is the name you'll see in your library."],[3796,"Gmail: unsubscribe and spam rates"],[1467,"Gmail's email sender guidelines: the full requirements for all senders and for those above 5,000 messages a day."],[1472,"Gmail's guide to full headers: how to open the header of a test message."],[7719,"Go live and end the session"],[3704,"Go to **Marketing → Campaign** and click **Create Workflow**. Nothing sends while a workflow is in draft, and nothing sends until sending is set up, including a connected email provider and a verified sender. For a one-off message, such as a replay link after a webinar or an offer closing on Friday, use **Marketing → Broadcasts** instead. A broadcast goes to a list you pick, and it can go now or on a schedule. EasyCRM is a plan add-on, and sends count against your **Wallet** allowance, so check plans and add-ons first."],[3886,"Google's email sender guidelines say marketing messages must support one-click unsubscribe and show a visible unsubscribe link. Every sender should keep the spam rate in Postmaster Tools below 0.3%. Extra rules apply above 5,000 messages a day to Gmail accounts."],[7284,"Green room features, from each platform's public documentation:"],[2200,"Guest presenters don't need an account at all. They join with a presenter link from the webinar, and you should treat that link as private."],[3136,"Guests who present once"],[2120,"Hand warm leads to the client's sales team fast"],[4326,"Have each one turn on their camera and microphone, and fix any the browser blocks."],[4059,"Here is one detail you can check. The script step asks for the number of slides and the duration before it writes anything. The script then comes back in named sections, each with its own timing and speaker notes. How this compares with other platforms is covered in How EasyWebinar compares for webinar planning, below."],[647,"Here's the manual method, so you can see which steps the AI takes on."],[2690,"Hiring teams and charities use the same set-up for paid assessment sessions or ticketed donor briefings. **Show Attendees** can be switched off so guests don't see each other."],[4802,"Holidays are the other check. GOV.UK lists 25 and 28 December 2026 as bank holidays in England and Wales, with 28 December as the Boxing Day substitute day. If nobody will attend then, add those dates under **Blackout Dates** so the webinar doesn't run."],[8201,"Host a video on EasyWebinar"],[8192,"Host a webinar video on EasyWebinar with Local import, or play one from YouTube, Vimeo, Wistia or a direct MP4 link, with the formats, size limit, storage rules and duration setting for each route."],[8303,"Hosted videos and recordings count towards your storage, metered on the **Plan** tab under **Settings** → **Manage Plan**, with **Buy More**. **Additional Storage (5GB)** is available as an add-on. See storage and upload limits."],[8244,"Hosting is what lets a recorded webinar run. Simulive webinars play the video at times you set. Evergreen webinars play it whenever a registrant's session comes round, and neither works until the video is in the library."],[8299,"Hosting on EasyWebinar is the simpler route for a webinar recording you don't want public. Importing is the quicker route when the video already lives on a platform you control."],[7591,"Hosts and co-hosts can draw on their own shared screen or slides, and everyone in the session sees each line as it's drawn. Only the person sharing can draw. Drawings disappear for everyone when the share stops, and they aren't in the recording. Drawing isn't available on video shares."],[5063,"How a live session becomes an evergreen webinar"],[2282,"How a sales webinar leads to the sale"],[331,"How a webinar email sequence gets written"],[5258,"How a webinar reaches its audience: live, simulated live and evergreen"],[2103,"How agencies white label webinars for clients"],[733,"How AI builds a webinar registration page: the blog's take on AI-written registration pages."],[1881,"How AI helps"],[4713,"How an automated webinar delivers a session"],[47