art from scratch?"],[7265,"If a guest hasn't received their link, **Invite People** gives you the presenter and moderator links from inside the room."],[3555,"If AI drafted your emails"],[3804,"If AI drafted your invitation"],[2300,"If AI drafts it for you"],[7740,"If an attendee zooms in on my shared screen, is that recorded?"],[7387,"If another of your webinars is already live, **Enter Room** shows **\"You can only have one event live at a time.\"** Join the session that's running, or go live with the new one."],[9631,"If another webinar is already on air, you'll see \"You can only have one event live at a time.\" Join that one, or go live with the new one."],[7783,"If it doesn't, open **Settings** → **Recording Settings** and switch recording on."],[8286,"If it isn't there yet, click **Add Video** for both routes, **Local import** and **Import from URL**, or drop a file onto the page."],[4839,"If it isn't there yet, click **Add Video**, or drag a file straight on to the page."],[9432,"If paying and registering happen in one step, there is nothing to copy. The seat is what the consultant sells, so buying it can create the registration. The list of buyers and the list of registrants then become the same list."],[4343,"If someone is missing, use **Invite People** to share their join link again. Move each person to the stage when it is their turn, and back when they're done."],[9444,"If Stripe isn't connected yet, a **Payments · Action required** panel appears with **Connect with Stripe**."],[2647,"If Stripe isn't connected, a **Payments · Action required** panel shows a **Connect with Stripe** button. Payouts go directly to your own bank account, and EasyWebinar never holds your funds. If the paid option isn't behaving as expected, check that **Paid Webinars** shows as active on the **Add-ons** tab under **Settings → Manage Plan**."],[6416,"If the button has no URL, the editor shows **\"Button link is required\"**. Any other invalid field shows **\"Please fix the highlighted fields before saving.\"**"],[896,"If the draft is the wrong length, change **Slides and duration**. If it misses your audience or your tone, edit the **Webinar topic** to be more specific. Then click **Regenerate**. It writes a fresh script, not a patched version of the old one, so copy any lines you want to keep before you regenerate."],[3761,"If the email promotes something and goes to US recipients, the CAN-SPAM Act requires a clear way to opt out and a postal address. Other countries have their own rules, so take advice if you're unsure."],[7785,"If the room won't let you in at step 2, the camera or microphone isn't being detected. The fix is in Camera not detected."],[6771,"If the video isn't in your library yet"],[7050,"If the video isn't in your library, **Add Video** gives you **Local import**, where EasyWebinar hosts the file, or **Import from URL** for YouTube, Vimeo, Wistia or a direct MP4 link. An imported video needs its length as well as its link. Uploads can be MP4, MOV or WebM, up to 4 GB. See Video hosting for both routes in detail."],[5387,"If the video isn't there yet, **Add Video** offers two routes. **Local import** uploads from your computer, and EasyWebinar hosts the video itself, so you don't need a YouTube or Vimeo account. **Import from URL** plays a video already on YouTube, Vimeo, Wistia or a direct MP4 link, and asks for its length as well as the link. Either way, the video is saved to your library for reuse. This video shows how to upload webinar videos to the library in EasyWebinar."],[2482,"If you already use a CRM, you can keep it. Keep HubSpot, Salesforce Pardot (Account Engagement), ActiveCampaign, Mailchimp or Kit, or use EasyCRM natively. The CRM mapping guide shows how webinar data reaches the CRM you already have."],[437,"If you build the webinar yourself, the sequence still follows the same order."],[9585,"If you built the webinar with **Create with AI**, the flow ends here too: it drops you on the finished webinar's Overview, and the webinar carries an **AI** badge in My Webinars. From then on it behaves like one you built by hand."],[3911,"If you built the webinar with Create with AI, it can draft your emails as well. Treat the draft as a first pass: check the date, time zone and link, then rewrite the opening in your own words."],[2295,"If you charge to register"],[7041,"If you choose **Paid**, you'll need a connected Stripe account. See Paid webinars."],[2510,"If you choose AI, Create with AI builds a complete webinar from a description. You then review and edit what it drafted before anyone sees it."],[5144,"If you circled numbers or underlined points on your shared screen or slides, those marks are not in the recording. Drawings are removed when you stop sharing, so viewers of the evergreen version won't see them. Listen for lines like \"as I've circled here\" and plan to explain the point another way."],[7405,"If you connected destinations in **Integrations → EasyCast**, click **EasyCast** in the top bar of the room. Switch **Stream** on for each destination you want this session to reach. The pencil beside a destination sets the title and description shown on that platform, so your public stream doesn't carry your internal webinar name. **Connect More Channels** takes you to the Integrations page to add another."],[7787,"If you draw on a screen or slides you're sharing, attendees see the drawings live. They are removed when you stop sharing, and they are not in the recording. If a diagram matters to replay viewers, put it on the slide itself rather than drawing it during the session."],[5394,"If you embedded a third-party chat, open **Contact** in the right-hand rail and its **Chat** tab, then reply from your chat tool's own dashboard."],[1313,"If you keep your own, connect it on a webinar's **Integrations** tab. Attendee engagement then flows into your system of record, with each contact tagged by what they did, such as attending or missing the session. Your broadcasts go out from that tool, so you don't need this setup. Your webinar's own confirmation, reminder and follow-up emails still go out from EasyWebinar either way."],[7796,"If you need a copy of a session you're watching or presenting outside EasyWebinar, a screen recorder on your own device is the general method. This records only what is on your screen. On a Chromebook, for example:"],[7814,"If you need to change it, open **Settings** → **Recording Settings**."],[8129,"If you only have time to style two of the five pages, EasyWebinar's guidance is to make them the registration page and the replay page: one carries your signups, the other carries the long tail of views."],[4507,"If you only need to email no-shows or attendees of one webinar, **Webinar Follow-ups** on the **Notifications** tab can target those audiences directly, and **Attendee Action Follow-ups** send based on engagement and offer clicks. People is for when you want to see the list, combine conditions, or take it elsewhere."],[5388,"If you play a YouTube video and later trim it, YouTube Help says the video's URL, view count and comments stay the same. The length you gave EasyWebinar at import no longer matches, though, so check it before the next session. The video hosting page compares hosting the file yourself with importing a link."],[646,"If you run search ads to the page, Google Ads rates landing page experience as one of three parts of Quality Score: how relevant and useful the page is to people who click the ad. Google calls Quality Score a diagnostic tool, not a key performance indicator. Treat it as a hint about the page, and keep registration rate as your main number."],[3557,"If you run the sequence in EasyCRM"],[99,"If you run webinars for clients, a client workspace gives each one a separate EasyWebinar account that you manage, on its own plan. It is the setup for marketing agencies running client webinars. Unlike adding a team member, the client does get an email confirmation to set their password, so use an address they read."],[9448,"If you sell replay access, set how long the replay stays open on the **Replay** tab: **Always Available**, **Expire after days** or a **Specific date**. Make sure the bundle's description matches that setting."],[4311,"If you send text reminders, SMS (Beta) needs the **Phone** field on your registration form, added in the registration page builder, or there is nobody to text. The reminder emails page covers each setting, and confirmation emails covers the first message registrants get."],[2872,"If you share your registration link in different places, tag each one with UTM parameters. Google's guidance is to always use utm_source, utm_medium and utm_campaign. UTM filtering in the People view needs UTM capture turned on in your registration form."],[4225,"If you stream to YouTube or LinkedIn"],[5184,"If you trimmed the recording outside EasyWebinar, click **Add Video**. **Local import** uploads your file and EasyWebinar hosts it. **Import from URL** plays a video on YouTube, Vimeo, Wistia or a direct MP4 link, and asks for its length. Video hosting covers both routes. You can swap the recording later from the **Webinar Video** panel on the Content tab, without disturbing the schedule or registrations."],[4319,"If you use AI moderation, open **Test Chat Moderation** and ask it the hard questions your customers ask. It opens a private conversation, so nothing reaches attendees. It retrains each time you add a document to its knowledge base, so give it a moment after an upload before you test."],[4317,"If you use SMS (Beta), select a template, click **Send Test SMS**, pick your country from the flag dropdown and type your number. Choose the country from the list rather than typing a dialling code. The message arrives from your EasyWebinar number, exactly as a registrant would see it. WhatsApp (Beta) messages can be tested on your own number in the same way."],[8136,"If you want people to watch the moment they register, you want **On Demand** on an evergreen webinar. If you want people who missed a session to catch up, you want the replay page. See On Demand."],[8978,"If you want to change how the form looks, click **View & Customize** first."],[3223,"If you want to try a new registration page or offer on a webinar that's already running, clone it and change the copy. When a live session worked well, clone it as evergreen; it then needs a recording, which you pick on the new webinar's **Content** tab. That route is covered in turning a live webinar into an evergreen one."],[6647,"If you will charge for the webinar, connect a **Stripe** account. You can complete everything without one by leaving pricing on **Free**."],[6653,"If you would rather have EasyWebinar write the script, pages, emails, offers and polls for you, choose **Create with AI** instead of **Create Manually** in step 1."],[8588,"If you would rather send reminders from your CRM or email tool, map the **Webinar Join Link** into one of its custom fields. Each contact then holds their own working link, which is what lets your system send the reminder instead of EasyWebinar."],[6830,"If you'd rather have the script, pages, emails, polls and offers written for you, choose **Create with AI** and set **Type** to Simulive before generating. You still pick the video afterwards. See Create with AI."],[3701,"If you'd rather run follow-ups as an automated sequence, EasyCRM has **Workflows**. Our guide to automating webinar follow-ups with CRM tools walks through the thinking. The simplest version gives attendees one message and no-shows the replay, and it runs after every webinar."],[2358,"If you'd rather start from a draft, EasyWebinar can generate a sales webinar script from a description of your audience, your topic and your offer. The script comes back in named sections with timings and speaker notes. Read it before you move on, because the pages and emails are built from it."],[5354,"If you'd rather take questions without an open chat, the Q&A queue keeps questions apart from conversation. The contact box is another option, with **Pin in the room** on and an email address you actually monitor."],[859,"If you'd rather write the script yourself, this order keeps the work moving."],[3887,"If you're not using a CRM yet, this is the manual way to do the job."],[3071,"If your audience already watches you on YouTube or LinkedIn, **EasyCast** streams a live webinar to **YouTube**, **LinkedIn** and **LinkedIn Organisation** pages at the same time, and to any other platform that accepts a **custom RTMP** stream."],[2301,"If your list lives in an email tool"],[3558,"If your list lives in an email tool"],[3064,"If your list lives in an email tool, connect it per webinar from the **Integrations** tab. Supported tools include **Kit (ConvertKit)**, **ActiveCampaign**, **Mailchimp**, **Drip**, **AWeber**, **Keap**, **Ontraport**, **GetResponse**, **Constant Contact** and **GoHighLevel**, alongside EasyWebinar's own **EasyCRM**."],[3805,"If your list lives in another email tool"],[5151,"If your platform can't copy a webinar, the job looks like this:"],[1137,"If your team already runs a CRM, keep it. EasyWebinar connects to fourteen integrations, including HubSpot, ActiveCampaign, Mailchimp, Kit (formerly ConvertKit), GoHighLevel and AWeber. You map your webinar data to that CRM's fields, which is covered in connecting a CRM and mapping your webinar data. The full list is on the integrations page."],[3154,"If your team needs enterprise checks"],[3216,"If your team runs webinars for clients, a client workspace keeps each client's webinars, registrants and settings apart. Each workspace runs on its own plan, and adding one doesn't use a team seat. If you run webinars only for your own business, team members and seats cover what you need."],[3668,"If your webinar ran somewhere with no follow-up settings, the job looks like this."],[4259,"If your webinar starts within the hour, skip to the day-of part of the checklist below and work down it."],[3407,"If your webinar tool doesn't record the source, the job is still possible with a spreadsheet. It usually runs like this:"],[2651,"If your workshop needs a disclaimer, for example on financial or health topics, add it as a text block in the registration page builder. Its templates include **Coach**, **Education** and **Health & Wellness** categories."],[436,"Illustrative calculation with sample figures, not an EasyWebinar output: 400 people register and 160 attend live. Registered to attended is 160 ÷ 400 = 40%, and the missed group is 400 − 160 = 240 people. That 240 is the list your replay follow-up needs to reach. The webinar analytics page explains each funnel metric."],[446,"Illustrative calculation with sample figures, not an EasyWebinar output. The four-person agency from earlier runs one webinar a month for each of five clients."],[8470,"Immediately after someone registers. The entry on the **Notifications** tab shows this as its trigger."],[3672,"Import each group into your email tool as its own list."],[8202,"Import from YouTube, Vimeo, Wistia or an MP4 link"],[1660,"Import your registrants into EasyCRM, save a list for attendees and one for no-shows, then build a workflow for each under Marketing → Campaign. Publish each workflow when it's ready, and it runs after every webinar."],[1608,"Import your webinar's registrants and attendees into **Leads**."],[8707,"In **Instant replay text**, keep *Watch instant replay* or type your own wording."],[6575,"In **Library → Recordings**, if **Auto Recording** was on during the session."],[7626,"In **My Webinars**, click **Create a Webinar** and choose **Create Manually**. Create with AI is the other route if you'd like a draft to start from."],[3501,"In **People**, filter by **Behavior** for high watch time plus an offer click. Those people stayed and clicked but didn't buy, which makes them a strong list for a personal follow-up."],[6084,"In **People**, the **Polls** column shows how many polls each person answered."],[3693,"In **Webinar Follow-ups**, click **Create New**."],[6659,"In **Webinar Name**, type the title attendees will see."],[4165,"In a 45-minute session, try 4 minutes of opening, 2 for the promise, 8 for each of three teaching points, 2 for the bridge, 6 for the offer and 7 for questions. Adjust the split, but keep the total fixed."],[5725,"In a connected CRM, the **Clicked offer** event can apply a tag, for example `webinar-hot`, so sales can follow up."],[5429,"In a live webinar you present in real time, and chat and Q&A happen as they happen. A pre-recorded webinar, simulive or evergreen, plays a video you made earlier. In EasyWebinar all three types use the same pages, emails, polls, offers and analytics."],[9371,"In Analytics"],[1546,"In EasyCRM, a **workflow** is an automated sequence. Where a broadcast goes out once, a workflow keeps running and sends the right message when someone does something, without you being there. You build it in draft, publish it when it's ready, and archive it when the campaign ends."],[1663,"In EasyCRM, click Marketing → Campaign in the sidebar, then Create Workflow. The Workflows screen also shows every workflow you have under the All, Published, Draft and Archived tabs."],[1597,"In EasyCRM, steps 1 and 2 become **Import from EasyWebinar** and two saved lists. Steps 3 and 4 become a workflow for each list, built once in draft and then published. Step 5 disappears, because a published workflow keeps running after every webinar until you archive it."],[1629,"In EasyCRM, the Wallet's **Recent activity** log shows what was sent and when, split by channel. It's the place to look when a meter has moved more than you expected, which is usually a workflow running on its own. Open and click averages, with benchmarks of 21% and 2.6% beside them, appear on the **Broadcasts** screen."],[1363,"In EasyWebinar the job starts on **Configurations** rather than in your DNS settings. Steps 1 and 2 still apply, because they're about your own company. From there, you complete **Domain Configuration** or validate a single business email address, following what the screen asks for. The set-up steps below cover the rest, including replies."],[7612,"In EasyWebinar the same steps happen in one product. The builder sets the schedule and opens the registration page builder. Reminder emails go out from the webinar's own settings. The green room covers step 4, and recording is on by default, which covers step 5. Polls and offers are built ahead on the **CTAs** tab, and the recording lands in the Library when you end."],[2382,"In EasyWebinar the same steps sit in one webinar. The registration page, reminders and follow-ups are built in, and the offer card shows inside the room. Analytics count visitors, registrations, attendance and each offer's views, clicks and purchases, so you don't match lists by hand."],[3416,"In EasyWebinar the seven steps shrink to set-up you do once per webinar. **UTM Params** records the campaign at registration, so steps 3 and 4 disappear. **People** holds every registrant with their status, watch percentage and offer clicks, and its **Source & UTM** filter does the counting in step 5. Follow-ups to attendees and no-shows send on their own, and the integration tags each group in your CRM without an export."],[7560,"In EasyWebinar you choose **Live Webinar** when you create the webinar, and it's selected by default. You set a date, time and timezone, publish a registration page, and present from the live room on the day. Our blog covers the format in more depth in its guide to live webinars."],[2428,"In EasyWebinar you set the duration and slide count before AI writes the script, so decide how long you need to teach, make the offer and answer questions before you generate it."],[1066,"In EasyWebinar, AI drafts the script, registration and thank-you pages, emails, polls and offers from one prompt. It can write a simulated chat (Beta) for recorded webinars and, from Pro onward, answer attendee questions from your uploaded files."],[5150,"In EasyWebinar, analytics work on an evergreen webinar as they do on every other type. Webinar analytics shows **Offers Performance**: offers, views, clicks and purchases, with a click rate. Low views-to-clicks means the offer itself isn't landing. Replay views are counted separately from live attendance, so the original live results stay readable."],[858,"In EasyWebinar, every section of the generated script carries its own timing. You set the overall duration before the script is written, and changing it and regenerating changes the result. Compare your read-through times with those section timings to see where the draft runs long."],[7093,"In EasyWebinar, one evergreen webinar can offer just-in-time sessions, On Demand viewing and set times, all on one page. It can host the video itself, and live webinars run in the same product. EasyWebinar is the only platform in this table that does all three."],[593,"In EasyWebinar, page generation is one part of a larger AI build that starts from a single prompt. The AI writes your presentation script first. It then writes the pages, using that script as its source material. Because the build starts from one description, the pages and the talk describe the same session."],[868,"In EasyWebinar, steps 1 to 5 collapse into a prompt and two numbers. You describe who the webinar is for, what it covers, how long it runs, the tone and what you're selling. Then you set the slides and duration, and the AI writes the script slide by slide, with timings and speaker notes per section. Steps 6 to 8 stay yours: read it, cut what runs long, regenerate if needed and rehearse."],[5159,"In EasyWebinar, steps 3 to 6 become ticks in the clone dialog, and step 2 becomes a choice on the **Recordings** tab. You still check the recording and set the schedule yourself. The original live webinar keeps its own registrants and results."],[4333,"In EasyWebinar, steps 3, 4 and 8 happen in the live room itself. From the webinar's **Overview**, click **Enter Room**, check your devices, and continue to the green room. Your co-hosts join backstage on their own link and sort out their audio there. A guest co-host needs only a join link, not an account, while regular presenters can be added as team members. Steps 5 and 6 stay the same, and SMS (Beta) adds a test send to your own number."],[2881,"In EasyWebinar, the offer card stays on screen with your booking link, and it can carry a countdown. The People view shows watch percentage and offer clicks without a spreadsheet. Follow-ups send to attendees, no-shows and clickers on their own. Once the session works, you clone it as evergreen so it runs without you presenting."],[4807,"In EasyWebinar, the Overview tab shows your scheduling options and every session the schedule generated, with **Live**, **Upcoming**, **Past** and **Cancelled** tabs. Attendance, offers and watch behaviour sit in webinar analytics, which works on automated webinars as it does on live ones. To see which channel each registration came from, tag your shared links with campaign parameters such as utm_source and utm_campaign, which Google Analytics reads."],[5367,"In EasyWebinar, the recording is part of the webinar itself, and the schedule plays it. You set the sessions once, as dates or a daily or weekly schedule. Each session plays the chosen video on time, whether or not you join. The registration page, emails, polls and offers all belong to the same webinar, so there's one set of links and one place to read the results."],[3896,"In EasyWebinar, the registration link comes from the webinar's **Share** dialog, and your list lives in EasyCRM. You send the invitation as a broadcast, and the Broadcasts screen keeps the totals and average rates for you. Registrants arrive on the webinar, and **Import from EasyWebinar** brings registrants and attendees back into EasyCRM."],[1405,"In EasyWebinar, two places help. The **Broadcasts** screen shows your open and click rates beside industry averages, and **Sending health** sits beside **EasyCRM Mail** on the service list. Outside the product, Google's guidelines point to Postmaster Tools for monitoring your domain's spam rate with Gmail."],[3614,"In Nielsen Norman Group's 2008 study of transactional email, an unrecognised sender was the main reason people gave for leaving a message unread. The study also advises a descriptive sender name alongside the address. So use the name people saw when they registered, whether that's yours or your company's."],[8574,"In short:"],[4692,"In the **People** view on the Analytics tab, or in People in the sidebar for every webinar at once."],[6227,"In the **Question** panel on the room's side rail, split into **Active** and **Answered**."],[9027,"In the **Share** dialog, under **Registration Widget**. It's the same snippet."],[6512,"In the **Webinar Video** panel, choose the video. The recording of the original live session is in your library under **Recordings**, named after its webinar, with its duration and recording date."],[8291,"In the **Webinar Video** panel, click **Preview** to play the current video."],[5376,"In the first month she saves 80 minutes, and from the second month 140 minutes, a cut of about 64%. She can spend part of that time answering chat in the sessions she does attend."],[7773,"In the green room, the header reads **Auto Recording Enabled** before you click **Go Live**, and **Recording** afterwards. How that compares with other platforms is covered in How EasyWebinar compares for webinar recording, below."],[6654,"In the left sidebar, click **My Webinars**."],[6827,"In the left sidebar, click **My Webinars**."],[5230,"In the Library, on the Recordings tab, named after its webinar with its duration and date. It also appears on the Recordings tab of the video picker when you set up the copy."],[7820,"In the live room, click **Settings**, then **Recording Settings**. The settings dialog also holds your device settings and room preferences such as chat and Q&A moderation."],[7864,"In the live room, open **Settings** → **Recording Settings** and switch recording off before you go live. Leave it on unless you have a reason not to."],[6362,"In the live room, the side rail has an **Offers** panel. Open it and push the offer to the room when you reach your pitch. When you click **Go Live**, the confirmation reminds you that offers and polls should be ready, so check them in the green room before you start."],[5686,"In the numbered editor screenshot further down, **Countdown timer** is item 2, after **Offer Style** and before **Offer Price**. It is a switch on each offer, so a free workbook offer can run with no timer while the programme offer keeps one. For other platforms' countdowns, see How countdown timers compare, below."],[9434,"In the Revenue screenshot below, the **Paid Webinar** view splits registration payments into completed, pending and abandoned checkouts. A founder who closes the checkout without paying is counted under **Checkout abandoned** and is never added as a registrant. How other tools take payment is covered in How paid webinars compare, further down."],[9341,"In the Share dialog, as **Attendee Replay link**, and on the **Replay** tab as **Replay Page Link**. Turn on **Enable replay page** first."],[7419,"In the top bar, **Share** shares your screen, **Full Screen** expands the stage, and **Reactions** enables emoji reactions from the room."],[1625,"In the United States, the CAN-SPAM Act bars commercial email to someone more than 10 business days after they opt out. A sequence that keeps running is where a missed opt-out is most likely, so check how your list handles them."],[464,"In this EasyWebinar video, you'll see how reminder emails are set up and timed on a webinar's Notifications tab."],[1581,"In this EasyWebinar video, you'll see webinar follow-up that changes with what each attendee did during the session."],[1953,"In this video, EasyWebinar shows how AI fits into running live and evergreen webinars."],[1912,"In this video, EasyWebinar shows its webinar platform running live and evergreen webinars from one account."],[247,"increasing engagement"],[780,"Independent consultants"],[443,"Insert the merge tags for name, date, time and join link, then send yourself a test."],[2251,"Inside one account, use Clone Webinar from the card menu on My Webinars, then change the copy. Registration templates under the Agency filter, and your own under My Templates, give each new funnel a starting point."],[9122,"Inside the builder, **Templates** in the top bar swaps the design for a different one. Templates are chosen per page, so each of the five pages can use a different one. Changing a template replaces that page's layout, so settle on one before you do detailed editing."],[9305,"Inside the room, the **People** panel's **Invite People** shares join links for presenters and moderators, so you can bring someone in after you've entered the green room. See Run a live webinar."],[8732,"Instant viewing, from each platform's public documentation:"],[246,"Instead of asking what questions you want, this step asks what the polls are for. Choose any combination of goals:"],[6454,"Integrations"],[1766,"Integrations are set **per webinar**, so connecting one doesn't connect the rest. Different webinars can feed different lists."],[3428,"Integrations are set per webinar, so connect your CRM or email tool on every webinar you promote."],[5918,"Into your chat tool, not EasyWebinar. You read and moderate them there."],[4177,"Inverted Pyramid: Writing for Comprehension (Nielsen Norman Group, 2018) explains why the main point should come first, which is how each section of an outline should open."],[944,"Inverted Pyramid: Writing for Comprehension: Nielsen Norman Group on putting the main point first, which suits a webinar opening."],[3792,"Invitation mistakes that are easy to make"],[2743,"Invite attendees to apply"],[2742,"Invite attendees to book a call"],[2925,"Invite your volunteer as a presenter before the session, using the join links on the People panel. Presenters wait backstage, unseen by the audience, until you move them to the stage."],[7537,"Is a live webinar recorded automatically?"],[5286,"Is a simulive webinar live?"],[7533,"Is a webinar live or recorded?"],[8229,"Is a YouTube-hosted webinar video private?"],[7354,"Is anything broadcast while I'm in the green room?"],[4239,"Is anything in the green room broadcast?"],[1895,"Is EasyWebinar secure?"],[2138,"Is EasyWebinar white label webinar software for live and automated webinars?"],[4943,"Is just-in-time the same as JIT?"],[4246,"Is my live webinar recorded automatically?"],[573,"Is my registration link live as soon as the build finishes?"],[6626,"Is my registration page live as soon as I create the webinar?"],[4756,"Is my registration page public as soon as I create the webinar?"],[7357,"Is my webinar recorded automatically?"],[7732,"Is my webinar recorded automatically?"],[8664,"Is On Demand the same as instant replay?"],[6991,"Is On Demand the same as the replay page?"],[993,"Is simulated chat available on live webinars?"],[9398,"Is someone registered if they close checkout without paying?"],[2581,"Is someone registered if they close the checkout without paying?"],[8386,"Is the confirmation the same as the thank-you page?"],[7217,"Is the green room the same as the waiting area?"],[8077,"Is the replay link private?"],[5659,"Is there a countdown on my registration page?"],[2320,"Is there a free trial, and do I need a card?"],[2315,"Is there a sales webinar template I can start from?"],[3822,"Is there a webinar invitation template I can copy?"],[4249,"Is this checklist built into EasyWebinar?"],[7667,"It can be either. A live webinar has someone presenting in real time. Simulive and evergreen webinars play a recording, at set times or on a repeating schedule."],[2524,"It can draft it. The AI webinar overview explains what AI drafts before the session and what you still review. You stay in charge of the final wording."],[5759,"It can. **Create with AI** generates offers with a title, headline, sub headline, button text and link, and you can add a countdown to any of them."],[9032,"It can. **Embed widgets** is one of the assets listed under **Webinar assets** in the clone dialog."],[2924,"It can. Simulive plays your recording at set times while you answer in the chat. On evergreen, Chat Simulation (Beta) can fill the chat, and offers appear on the recording as they did in your live session."],[6938,"It can't read the length of a video hosted elsewhere, and it needs that length to schedule sessions and end the webinar at the right time."],[4697,"It counts towards **Total Attended**. **Live Attended** counts the broadcast only."],[3297,"It depends on your plan. The Settings overview shows how many seats you've used out of your allowance, and adding people only costs more once that allowance is used up."],[128,"It depends on your plan. The Settings overview shows seats used out of your allowance."],[1971,"It does not host or deliver courses, and it is not a free tool: there is no free plan. Automation, EasyCRM, checkout and EasyCast start at the Growth plan, and the AI Moderator starts at Pro."],[7768,"It falls to whoever hosts or produces the session, usually in the minutes before going live. It matters most to anyone who sells from a replay or turns a good live session into an evergreen one. A course creator opening enrolment is a typical case."],[4054,"It falls to whoever owns the session, usually the presenter or the marketer running the programme. The moment is before any slide or page exists, when moving a section costs nothing."],[823,"It falls to whoever presents. For a coach or consultant working alone, that means the same person who books the date also writes the script, the pages and the emails. The pressure peaks in the week before the session, when the date is fixed and the registration page has to go live."],[1005,"It gets you from an idea to a webinar you can actually run without starting from a blank page. The AI writes the drafts, and your time goes into checking that they say what you mean."],[393,"It gives every webinar a complete, timed webinar email sequence before the first person registers. You start from six working drafts instead of a blank editor, then spend your time on the wording."],[2629,"It helps to see the full job without any webinar platform, because each step is something that can go wrong."],[8405,"It is a different thing from the **Thank you Page**. The thank-you page is what the browser shows straight after registering, with confirmation and what happens next. The email is what stays in the registrant's inbox after they have closed that tab, and it is where they go looking for the link on the day."],[9416,"It is different from **selling an offer during a webinar**:"],[3292,"It is the work of planning, building, running and following up each webinar: access, pages, reminders, presenters and results. For a team it also means agreeing who owns each step, so nothing is done twice or missed."],[8749,"It lets someone watch immediately, with no session to wait for."],[5124,"It lets the live session you have already tested keep running for new registrants, without you presenting it again. You reuse the recording and the setup instead of rebuilding them."],[2156,"It lets you deliver webinars as a service without your clients seeing the tool behind them. Each client gets pages on their own domain, a funnel built for their offer and numbers they can check."],[3599,"It matters most on the day of the session, when you have to write several emails at once. A course creator needs them out before an enrolment window closes. A marketing manager needs them out before interest cools and new leads go quiet."],[2162,"It matters most to agency owners who sell webinars as a monthly retainer, and to account leads who answer to several clients at once. It matters most at the moment a client asks to see results before renewing."],[2997,"It matters most to creators selling a new course, and to educators and trainers who sell cohorts or workshops. It counts most with cold traffic: people who found you through an ad or a search and have never heard you teach."],[2340,"It matters most to owners and solo operators who sell something that takes ten minutes or more to explain. It matters most in the weeks before a launch or a seasonal push, when you need many conversations at once."],[8251,"It matters most to people who teach or sell through automated webinars, such as trainers and course creators. The question comes up early, usually before the first recording is made, because it decides where the file will live."],[7074,"It matters most to SaaS, customer success and course teams who run a webinar as a standing channel rather than a launch-day event. The moment that counts is the first visit, when someone is interested enough to register."],[1146,"It matters most to small teams that sell through webinars and don't have a CRM yet. It also matters at the point a team's monthly webinars produce more contacts than a spreadsheet can track."],[7235,"It matters most to teams that run live webinars with several speakers, such as panels, interviews and demos with a moderator. Those sessions depend on guests joining without interrupting, and on handovers that look rehearsed."],[7984,"It matters most to teams that run recorded webinars and train or sell with the same content again and again. The question tends to come up once the first few sessions are recorded and someone asks where they all went."],[7440,"It matters most to teams whose live session is a public moment: a launch, a recruitment event or a sales presentation. Those teams are choosing a live webinar platform, and the test comes in the first five minutes of the first session."],[3196,"It matters most to the lead who signs off the calendar and answers for the numbers. It starts to bite once you run more than two webinars a month, or once a new colleague joins and needs access on day one."],[602,"It matters most to the person who runs webinars alone or with one helper: an owner, a marketer or a consultant. The pressure point is the week before promotion starts. No ad, email or social post can go out until the registration page exists."],[6710,"It matters most to trainers, educators and sales teams whose value comes from talking with people in real time. The key moment is the week before a session, when people decide whether to register and keep the date free."],[3385,"It matters most to whoever owns the pipeline number. A demand generation lead has to show which webinars produce leads, and that question comes up whenever next quarter's budget is set. It comes up again each time a new channel is tested."],[400,"It matters most to whoever runs several webinars a month, such as an agency team running sessions for different clients. Each new webinar needs its own sequence in its own voice. Drafting it in the build saves that writing every time."],[4612,"It matters most when a webinar carries a target. That might be sign-ups for a marketing team, enrolments for a course creator or paid seats for a workshop host. It earns its keep in the days after a session, when you choose what to change before promoting the next one."],[5519,"It matters to anyone who relies on evergreen webinars inside a funnel, where nobody presents live. Those teams need the automated session to hold attention the way a live one does, most of all when it plays many times a day."],[6890,"It matters to teams that repeat one webinar on a cycle, such as a weekly walkthrough or a monthly onboarding session. They want the same polished delivery each time, with a real audience and a chat they can staff."],[1819,"It matters to teams whose pipeline already lives in a CRM. A webinar only counts there once its people show up in that CRM, tagged in a way that sales and marketing automation can act on. That is the point of tracking webinar leads in your CRM."],[1776,"It moves up to **Connected apps**, marked **Ready to use**."],[1922,"It sits between a simple meeting room and an enterprise event platform. It is simple enough for a first webinar, and it can run your whole webinar funnel."],[7116,"It starts a few minutes after someone registers rather than at a fixed future time."],[6573,"It starts with the original's name plus \"(Copy)\". You can change it in the dialog."],[1970,"It suits creators, coaches, consultants, small businesses and marketing teams whose webinars have to keep working after the live hour. Agencies use client workspaces, and SaaS and customer success teams run demos and training as evergreen sessions."],[3379,"It turns a webinar from a one-off event into a lead source you can measure. Each registrant arrives with a name, an email and the campaign that sent them. After the session you know who attended, who missed it and who clicked your offer."],[197,"It works in sequence, one step after another. Your prompt becomes a script, and the AI then uses that script as source material when it writes your pages. That ordering matters: the script is the foundation, so getting it right first improves everything built after it."],[938,"It writes a fresh script. If you change the slides or the duration first, the new script changes to match. Copy any lines you want to keep before you regenerate."],[714,"It writes the headline, what attendees will learn and an instructor bio, using your script as its source. The default form asks for full name and email, both required."],[713,"It writes three: the registration page, the thank-you page and the waiting area. The webinar page and the replay page keep their working defaults, which you can edit in the same builder."],[3502,"It's a rating of how engaged someone was, based on attendance, watch time and interaction, for example Hot. Sorting by it is a 