,[7887,"Manage your media"],[2178,"Many agencies start without a dedicated set-up. If that's you today, this is the order that keeps the mess down."],[3007,"Many creators run the same webinar live a few times to sharpen it, then turn the best version into an evergreen funnel."],[5338,"Many people run a session live a few times first to sharpen it. The recording of a past webinar then becomes the simulive video, picked from the **Recordings** tab on the video step. If you later want each registrant to choose their own time, turn the session into an evergreen webinar by cloning it. For a full walk-through of the evergreen build, see creating an evergreen webinar."],[1718,"Map custom fields"],[1715,"Map events to tags"],[4544,"Map webinar behaviour to CRM tags: send the same behaviour People shows into your CRM automatically."],[4699,"Map webinar events to CRM tags: act on **Missed**, **Attended** and **Clicked offer** outside EasyWebinar."],[3065,"Map webinar events to tags so your email tool knows what each person did:"],[1806,"Mapping the **join link** lets you send reminders from your CRM instead of EasyWebinar's own reminder emails, because each contact gets their own working link."],[2877,"Mark who stayed to the end and who mentioned your offer."],[28,"Marketing teams"],[1737,"Marketing teams"],[5779,"Match chat to the webinar you're running"],[3754,"Match it to your offer. Use **Expire after days** or **Specific date** when a deadline applies, and **Always Available** for training or anything that keeps its value. Your emails should state the same closing time."],[3670,"Match the two lists to sort people into attended and missed."],[7711,"Measure 1: duration against time live"],[7712,"Measure 2: a card for every session"],[2963,"Measure it"],[5238,"Measure key moments for audience retention (YouTube Help): how intros, dips and spikes show where viewers stay or leave a video."],[5442,"Measure key moments for audience retention (YouTube Help): how to read flat lines, dips and spikes in a recording's watch time."],[2303,"Measure your first sales webinar"],[6259,"Measure your offers"],[245,"Merge tags are already in place, so dates, times and join links fill in automatically. **Add email** adds another. Click **Continue**."],[5874,"Messages then go to your chat tool, not to EasyWebinar, and you read and answer them from that tool's own dashboard."],[9230,"Moderator Join Link for Live room"],[136,"Moderators in the Q&A queue: how a moderator works through questions during a session."],[97,"Moderators work with the settings on the **Engagement** tab. With Private Q&A, questions are visible only to hosts and moderators. With chat set to Hosts only, each attendee talks privately to your team. AI Moderation (Beta) doesn't replace a human moderator on a live session; someone still spots the question worth answering on air."],[2408,"More than half the registrants never showed up, so the replay email to 66 no-shows is the biggest next step. For the next webinar, the reminders deserve attention before the offer does, because the offer converted a fair share of the people who saw it."],[2799,"Most coaches fill their first programmes through people who already know them. Then the referrals slow down, and every new client means another coffee call that may go nowhere. A coaching webinar is a free or paid teaching session that holds the first conversation at scale. The calls you take afterwards are with people who already want help."],[2991,"Most course businesses have three parts: a way to attract people, a way to turn interest into a purchase, and a place to deliver lessons. EasyWebinar is the middle part. People register for your webinar, watch it and click through to buy, while your course platform keeps hosting lessons and managing students."],[1406,"Most failures trace back to one of a few causes, and each has a place to look:"],[2474,"Most guides to the types of webinars sort them by format, but you start with a job: fill a course, 