s fixed once the webinar exists."],[9138,"New registration pages show the date, time and timezone with a countdown to the session. Selecting that block gives you its visibility (including a **Desktop Only** option), its margins and width, and the fonts, sizes and alignment for the date, time and timezone."],[2067,"Next steps"],[6634,"Next steps"],[7139,"Next steps"],[3615,"Nielsen Norman Group's 2014 subject line guidance puts the useful words first and recommends about 40 characters, because inboxes cut long lines off. It also advises against putting the recipient's name in the subject. That's why the templates on this page start with the replay, the course or the deadline. If your webinar title is long, use a shorter version."],[1400,"No single number proves your email setup is healthy, so it helps to know what each common measure can and can't tell you:"],[3732,"No-shows take 360 of the 635 sends, which is about 57%. So the no-show emails deserve as much care as the attendee thank-you, and they're the ones to write first. If you send through EasyCRM, this total also tells you what the sequence will use from your **Wallet** allowance."],[1465,"No. **Custom domain (C-Name)** points your own domain at your webinar pages, and **Domain Configuration** concerns the email your CRM sends. They are separate settings on separate screens, so finishing one doesn't complete the other, even with the same company domain."],[4695,"No. **Revenue by Source** splits them, and the section below switches between **Paid Webinar** and **Paid Offer**."],[9204,"No. **Webinar Language** changes the interface language attendees see; your own copy stays as you wrote it."],[9339,"No. A co-host or moderator who joins lands backstage. Your audience doesn't see or hear them until you move them to the stage."],[5427,"No. A simulive webinar plays a recording you made in advance at the times you set. What's shared in real time is the room: attendees watch the same moment together, and you and your