heckout"],[4569,"Offers and countdowns"],[8052,"Offers and polls"],[2868,"Offers and polls carry over to the replay when it uses **Webinar Replica**, and the offer on the recording appears as it did live. So the evergreen version sells the same way your best live session did."],[8137,"Offers and polls carry over to the replay when the replay uses **Webinar Replica**. If an offer's headline or countdown talks about a deadline, check it still makes sense to someone watching later, and use **Preview** on the replay page to see what viewers get. See Offers and Polls."],[7175,"Offers and the countdown timer: build the offers you sell during the webinar, with an optional countdown."],[6759,"Offers and the countdown timer: put a call to action in front of the room while you present."],[1863,"Offers and the countdown timer: the offers behind the **Clicked offer** event."],[5756,"Offers carry over to the replay when the replay page uses **Webinar Replica**. Use **Preview** on the replay page to check it looks the way you want."],[9375,"Offers inside a paid webinar"],[6314,"Offers matter most to teams whose webinars have to pay for themselves, such as course creators, coaches, training companies and product teams. They matter most in launch weeks and on automated webinars, where the card does the selling while nobody is presenting."],[6258,"Offers on the replay"],[2263,"Offers shown in the webinar room"],[5761,"Offers: build the offer card that carries the countdown."],[8187,"Offers: the offers that carry onto a Webinar Replica replay."],[6087,"Offers: the other kind of CTA, built in the same list as your polls."],[1462,"On **Configurations**, under **Email Integration** and **Email provider**. **Sending health** sits beside **EasyCRM Mail** on the service list. Look there before your first send, then watch your open rate on the **Broadcasts** screen once mail has gone out."],[2391,"On **CTAs**, build your offer, set the **Button URL** to your checkout and leave its toggle off."],[5869,"On **Engagement** → **Chat**, choose **Third party**."],[3035,"On **My Webinars**, click **⋮** on the webinar's card and choose **Clone Webinar**."],[4827,"On **My Webinars**, click **Create a Webinar**, then **Create Manually**."],[4973,"On **My Webinars**, click **Create a Webinar**, then **Create Manually**."],[5378,"On **My Webinars**, click **Create a Webinar**, then **Create Manually**."],[8704,"On **My Webinars**, click **Create a Webinar**, then **Create Manually**."],[4877,"On **My Webinars**, click **Create a Webinar**, then **Create Manually**. Choose **Evergreen Webinar** or **Simulive Webinar**, set the schedule and pricing, pick the recording on the video step, then choose a registration template and publish the page."],[2855,"On **My Webinars**, click the **⋮** on the live webinar's card and choose **Clone Webinar**."],[5173,"On **My Webinars**, click the **⋮** on the live webinar's card and choose **Clone Webinar**."],[2385,"On **My Webinars**, create a webinar, give it a name and choose **Live**."],[2390,"On **Notifications**, set three reminders and two **Webinar Follow-ups**: one for attendees, one for no-shows."],[6665,"On **Step 2 of 4: Schedule**:"],[6683,"On **Step 3 of 4: Pricing**, choose one:"],[6693,"On **Step 4 of 4: Registration Template**:"],[6189,"On a **simulive** webinar, chat and Q&A work normally. Everyone in a session sees the same moment of the video, and you and your moderators answer in real time while the recording plays."],[5865,"On a busy webinar, one presenter can't watch the chat and present at the same time. The webinar's **Share** dialog includes a **Moderator Join Link for Live room**, which lets a moderator join to handle chat and questions. Treat it as private: anyone holding it can join the room in that role."],[6188,"On a large webinar, a moderator can work the queue while the presenter keeps presenting. Send them the **Moderator Join Link for Live room** from the webinar's **Share** dialog; it is the link for someone handling chat and questions. Keep it private, because anyone holding it can join in that role."],[5718,"On a live webinar you choose the moment to show the offer from the **Offers** panel in the room. Before you go live, **Go Live** reminds you to have offers and polls ready."],[7587,"On a live webinar you launch polls by hand from the **Polls** panel, at the moment you choose. You build polls and offers in advance on the webinar's **CTAs** tab, then push them to the room during the session. An offer's **Button URL** is where attendees land when they click, such as your checkout, booking page or sales page. This video shows an offer being made to attendees during a webinar."],[9627,"On a live webinar, **Enter Room** takes you into the webinar room."],[6032,"On a live webinar, polls don't appear on their own: you launch each one manually. When you click **Go Live**, the confirmation reminds you that offers and polls should be ready, so check your poll list in the green room first."],[8138,"On a live webinar, the room header shows **Auto Recording Enabled** when recording is on, and recorded sessions land in **Library → Recordings**. Recording can be changed in the room under **Settings → Recording Settings**. See Run a live webinar and The Library."],[4910,"On a new evergreen webinar"],[8642,"On a new evergreen webinar"],[5755,"On a new live webinar, yes: the registration page builder opens with a countdown to the session. On other types, check the page in the builder. You can restyle the block, hide it on mobile with **Desktop Only**, or remove it."],[9653,"On a paid webinar, **Registrants** counts everyone who has registered and paid, and **Revenue** is the total taken. Every transaction is listed under **Analytics → Revenue → Paid Webinar**."],[8442,"On a paid webinar, the attendee is registered once payment goes through and is then sent to your thank-you page. Purchases of an offer inside the webinar have their own email, **Paid Offer — Transaction Success**, the receipt-style confirmation for anyone who bought. See Paid webinars."],[9121,"On a paid webinar, the template you pick includes the price automatically."],[1024,"On a recorded webinar there is no shared conversation, and an empty chat panel looks abandoned. Chat Simulation (Beta) fills it, either with a conversation the AI generates or with messages you script yourself. It works on simulive and evergreen webinars, and the Chat Simulation (Beta) guide covers the setup."],[5518,"On a recorded webinar with an empty chat, the first impression is a room nobody else came to. Attendees already suspect they may be watching a recording, and a silent panel confirms it. Many leave before the content has had a chance to work."],[3029,"On a recorded webinar, attendees arrive at different times, so there's no shared conversation, and an empty chat panel makes the room look abandoned. **Chat Simulation** (Beta) fills it, on simulive and evergreen webinars:"],[5580,"On a simulive webinar, everyone in a session watches the same moment, so real chat works and you can answer live while the recording plays. Chat Simulation is available on simulive webinars as well as evergreen ones."],[1557,"On a small team, the person who presents the webinar usually sends the follow-up too. It matters most in the week after a session, when that person is also answering questions and planning the next one. A published workflow takes the follow-up off their list."],[6190,"On an **evergreen** webinar, Q&A is set up the same way on the Engagement tab. There is also a separate built-in contact form, the **EW Contact Box**, which sends submitted questions to an email address you choose. On a recorded webinar, attendees find it under **Contact** in the room, on its **Question** tab. It is a different thing from the Q&A queue: questions arrive by email rather than in the room's **Question** panel."],[7804,"On an Android phone, the Screen record tile in Quick Settings does the same job, and recordings appear in the Photos app."],[5607,"On an automated webinar, attendees arrive at different times, so a genuine shared chat isn't possible. An empty panel makes the room look deserted."],[7081,"On an automated webinar, people arrive at different times, so a shared live conversation isn't possible. Turn on **Chat Simulation** on the **Engagement** tab to fill the chat with an AI-generated or CSV-scripted conversation. See Chat simulation."],[9606,"On an evergreen webinar with just-in-time switched on, the timezone line reads **Attendee's local timezone**. That's because a just-in-time session starts shortly after each person registers, in their own local time."],[5867,"On an evergreen webinar, a real shared chat isn't possible because attendees arrive at different times. **Chat Simulation** plays back a conversation, either generated by AI or scripted by you in a CSV, so the room doesn't look empty. It needs **Easywebinar Chat**."],[4911,"On an existing evergreen webinar"],[8643,"On an existing evergreen webinar"],[4917,"On Demand"],[6954,"On Demand"],[8630,"On Demand (instant replay)"],[4895,"On Demand (instant replay): letting registrants watch straight away."],[5445,"On Demand (instant replay): letting registrants watch straight away."],[8634,"On Demand and the replay page are different"],[8692,"On Demand is for evergreen webinars where the content is the point, not the occasion. Think of training, product explainers and onboarding material. People want to get through these on their own timetable."],[4791,"On Demand lets a registrant start the recording immediately, with no session to wait for. The button reads *Watch instant replay* by default, and you can reword it. It catches people who want the content and nothing else. It gives up the sense of a scheduled event, so leave it off when you want people to turn up."],[8698,"On Demand matters to teams using evergreen webinars for education and onboarding. It matters most when the audience is busy and the content is the reason they came. Those registrants get immediate access from the same page, recording and webinar setup."],[8184,"On Demand: instant replay on evergreen webinars, which is often confused with the replay page."],[5047,"On Demand: the option for registrants who want to watch now rather than in a few minutes."],[4717,"On demand: watch straight away"],[7125,"On Demand: wording the instant replay button and how it differs from the replay page."],[1960,"On security, EasyWebinar holds a SOC 2 Type II report and follows GDPR-aligned data practices."],[5868,"On simulive and evergreen webinars you can replace the built-in panel with a chat tool you already use, such as Chatroll, Intercom or anything that gives you an embed snippet."],[6421,"On the **Analytics** Overview. **Offers Performance** gives views, clicks and purchases with a click rate, and **Revenue by Offer** gives total revenue and payment count."],[9167,"On the **Analytics** tab, **Visitors** counts unique IPs on your landing page and **Registered** counts unique sign-ups. A low **Visitors to Registered** rate points at the page itself: the headline, the form, the promise."],[2399,"On the **Analytics** tab, **Visitors** to **Registered** shows whether your registration page is doing its job. **Registered** to **Attended** shows whether your reminders are. Lower down, **Views to Clicks** and **Clicks to Purchases** separate the two offer problems. Low views to clicks means the offer isn't landing, and low clicks to purchases points to your checkout or pricing. The webinar analytics page explains each figure."],[8126,"On the **Content** tab, click **Edit** on the **Replay Page** card."],[6327,"On the **CTAs** tab, open an existing offer."],[6008,"On the **CTAs** tab, open an existing poll."],[4318,"On the **CTAs** tab, the poll editor previews each poll exactly as attendees will see it. Use the toggle on each row to keep an offer ready but switched off until you need it. On a live webinar you launch polls by hand, so decide in the test run who launches each one and when. The polls and offers pages cover the settings."],[4388,"On the **CTAs** tab, turn the toggle on that offer's row off. The offer is kept but not shown, so you can switch it on when you reach it in the session."],[8429,"On the **Emails** channel, click **Email Settings**."],[5920,"On the **Engagement** tab, set chat to **Hosts only**, or choose **No Chat**."],[8028,"On the **Files** tab. It's also where the AI Moderator (Beta) keeps the documents it answers from."],[2671,"On the **Notifications** tab, **Webinar Follow-ups** go to registrants, attendees or no-shows after the session. **Attendee Action Follow-ups** respond to what someone did, such as clicking an offer. The webinar follow-up email templates give wording for each group."],[9289,"On the **Overview** tab, click **Share** on the webinar's header, next to **Registration Page**."],[8021,"On the **Recordings** tab of the **Library**. Each is named after its webinar, with its duration and recording date."],[8285,"On the **Video Selection** step, click the video you want."],[4331,"On the day, join early and repeat steps 3 and 4."],[5347,"On the Engagement tab, under **Chat**, a recorded webinar offers more than a live one does:"],[2191,"On the first step, enter the client's **Full Name**, **Work email**, **Company Name** and **Phone Number**, and set a **Password**. **Job Title** and **Profile photo** are optional. Click **Continue**."],[3038,"On the new webinar's **Content** tab, select the recording of your live session."],[9370,"On the Overview tab"],[4357,"On the phone, the footnote ends up a quarter of its slide size, and the attendee can't zoom in to read it. Size every line of text you need people to read as if it will be shown four times smaller, and cut the rest."],[2387,"On the pricing step, leave the webinar **Free** unless you're charging to register."],[8754,"On the schedule step when you set up an evergreen webinar, not on the **Replay** tab."],[4786,"On the schedule step, **Just-in-time Registration**, **On Demand** and **Recurring Schedule** sit side by side and can all be on at once. How that set-up stands against other platforms is covered in How EasyWebinar compares for automated webinars, below."],[4996,"On the schedule step, EasyWebinar shows a message saying attendees will see times in their local time based on the selected timezone. On an evergreen webinar, that's true of just-in-time sessions only. Recurring daily and weekly sessions run at the times you set in the webinar's timezone."],[2192,"On the second step, choose a plan. Each workspace runs on its own plan, billed monthly or yearly:"],[501,"On the webinar's **Notifications** tab. The drafts sit in their groups, and you can open any one to change its subject, content and timing, just like an email you wrote yourself."],[8712,"On the webinar's **Overview** tab, the options menu on the **Scheduling Options** panel changes the schedule for the whole webinar. The same panel shows the frequency, start date, timezone and the preference you chose."],[7247,"On the webinar's **Overview**, click **Enter Room**."],[8980,"On the webinar's **Overview**, click **Share**."],[5000,"On the webinar's **Overview**, open the **Live** tab in the **Sessions** panel. A session on air appears there marked *Live now*, with **Enter room**."],[3757,"On the webinar's **Replay** tab, under **Replay Page Link**, once **Enable replay page** is on. It's also in the Share dialog as **Attendee Replay link**."],[9164,"On the webinar's **Settings → Tracking Code** sub-tab, you pick a page and paste code into **Header Code**, **Body Code** or **Footer Code**. Tracking code is set per page. The registration page tells your ad platform who was interested; the thank-you page, which only loads after someone registers, is the reliable conversion signal."],[8148,"On the webinar's **Settings** tab, the **Tracking Code** sub-tab lets you add scripts to each of the five pages, including the **Replay Page**, so your analytics or ad platform can count people who watched afterwards."],[1397,"Once a broadcast has gone out, **Marketing → Broadcasts** is the first place a sending problem shows. The screen sets your average open rate against an industry average of 21%, and your average click rate against 2.6%."],[2209,"Once connected, the app moves to **Connected apps**, where you choose which list or tag people land in. If the client has no CRM, EasyCRM keeps contacts, deals and follow-up in the same product. If you run follow-up for them, build CRM workflows for attendees and no-shows."],[9454,"Once payment goes through, the attendee is registered and sent to your thank-you page."],[2654,"Once payment goes through, the buyer is registered and sent to your thank-you page. It shows their personal join link and the session date, with calendar buttons."],[6692,"Once people pay, the webinar's **Analytics** tab shows what you've earned under **Revenue**, with a list of every transaction and its status."],[3913,"Once people register from your invitation, reminder emails take over. This EasyWebinar video shows how to set them up."],[2854,"Once the live version has been run a few times and the pitch holds up, make it evergreen. A webinar's type can't change after you create it, so you clone it instead. The guide to cloning a webinar walks through each screen."],[4112,"Once the outline is filled in, it becomes the description you give EasyWebinar. The product then writes the script, pages, emails, polls and offers from it, and you edit each part before you go live."],[9298,"Once the page is enabled it reads *Replay page is live, anyone with the link can watch*, so treat the replay link as public. Replay emails aren't set up here: add a **Webinar Follow-up** on the **Notifications** tab and include the replay link."],[1937,"Once the webinar exists, it opens on its Overview tab. This is the home screen for one webinar, with live stats, scheduling