ations screen"],[8426,"Open the email to change its subject and content. Every email on the tab is editable in the same way."],[350,"Open the finished webinar"],[3260,"Open the new webinar and check its schedule, its reminder emails and its offer links. A clone carries the old settings, so a stale date or a last-month offer is the most common slip. Then send the registration link out."],[6511,"Open the new webinar and go to its **Content** tab."],[5192,"Open the new webinar's Overview. The **Sessions** panel should list sessions generated from your schedule. Then register yourself through the registration page and watch the opening minutes, the drawing moments and the offer."],[8355,"Open the Notifications tab"],[9525,"Open the Overview tab"],[8985,"Open the page on your site where people should register."],[3418,"Open the registration page in the page builder and select the form block. The default form collects **Full name** and **Email**, both required. On the same block you can:"],[8561,"Open the reminder you want to change."],[7813,"Open the room and confirm the header reads **Auto Recording Enabled**."],[7797,"Open the session in a window on its own, and close notifications you don't want captured."],[9223,"Open the Share dialog"],[5,"Open the Team screen"],[9114,"Open the template step of the create flow. Next to **Education**, **Coach** and the other categories, the filter row includes **My Templates**. How that setup sits against other platforms is covered in How the registration page builder compares, below."],[2219,"Open the webinar and click **Analytics**. The **Overview**, **People** and **Revenue** views share a date range, set with **Apply**. The funnel shows **Visitors**, **Registered**, **Live Attended**, **Replay Watched**, **Total Attended** and **Missed**. Webinar analytics explains each figure."],[8290,"Open the webinar and click the **Content** tab."],[2830,"Open the webinar, click **CTAs** and add an offer."],[3424,"Open the webinar, click **Se