tive to the webinar, so they work for recurring and evergreen schedules too."],[4570,"Paid registration"],[8364,"Paid registration"],[9546,"Paid registration"],[9483,"Paid registration features, from each platform's public documentation:"],[9423,"Paid registration is for webinars that are the product: workshops, masterclasses, paid trainings and ticketed seminars. People pay to attend, so the seat itself is what you sell."],[9415,"Paid registration makes payment part of signing up. Instead of a free form that registers someone straight away, the registration page shows your price, the **Register Now** button opens a checkout, and the person is registered only once payment succeeds."],[9429,"Paid registration matters most to educators, coaches and consultants whose sessions should earn money rather than cost it. It matters at the planning stage, when a session is designed to be sold rather than given away."],[3050,"Paid registration needs the **Paid Webinars** add-on and a connected Stripe account. Registration revenue and course sales from offers inside the session are reported separately under **Revenue by Source**. See Paid webinars."],[2692,"Paid webinar features, from each platform's public documentation:"],[2530,"Paid Webinar: Run a Workshop or Seminar, From Taking Payment to Sharing the Replay"],[164,"Paid webinars"],[2528,"Paid webinars"],[6264,"Paid webinars"],[6945,"Paid webinars"],[8056,"Paid webinars"],[2264,"Paid webinars and paid registration"],[9351,"Paid webinars and paid registration"],[2726,"Paid webinars and paid registration: every pricing field, the checkout and the revenue screens in full."],[6426,"Paid webinars: charging for registration, reported apart from offer sales."],[8483,"Paid webinars: registration happens only after payment, so that is when the confirmation sends."],[8189,"Paid webinars: sell replay access with a Live + Replay bundle."],[9694,"Paid webinars: set a price at creation, since a converted webinar keeps the free form."],[8342,"Paid webinars: the pricing step that comes just before Video Selection."],[9210,"Paid webinars: why the price block appears only when Paid is chosen at creation."],[2570,"Paid wellness workshops"],[2956,"Paid workshops"],[5649,"Paid workshops and live events"],[9382,"Paid workshops and masterclasses"],[6106,"Pair it with your chat setting"],[6592,"Past dates"],[5364,"Paste any offer link into the chat at the right moment, by hand."],[8986,"Paste the embed code wherever the form should appear."],[2184,"Paste the lists into a spreadsheet per client and work out registration and show-up rates."],[3673,"Paste the replay link into each email, and schedule the first email, the day-after email and the last call for each list."],[3425,"Paste the same pixel on the Registration Page and the Thank You Page, so your ad platform sees both interest and sign-ups."],[2841,"Paste the URL you want attendees sent to, such as your booking page."],[5871,"Paste your **Chat widget code**: an `<iframe>` or script snippet, exactly as your chat provider gives it to you."],[2834,"Paste your booking page, application form or checkout link into **Button URL**."],[2713,"Payments go straight to your own Stripe account, and Stripe pays out to your bank on its usual schedule. EasyWebinar never holds your funds."],[9505,"Payments go straight to your Stripe account, and Stripe pays out to your bank on its usual schedule."],[2677,"Pending checkouts haven't finished yet, so leave them out until they settle. Replay views are counted apart from live attendance, so a bundle buyer who watched both shows under **Both**. On a small workshop, a few people can swing either percentage widely, so look across several sessions before you change the price."],[4401,"People"],[6790,"People"],[3862,"People decide whether to open an email by who sent it. Nielsen Norman Group's research found that unrecognisable sender information was the top reason people gave for not opening email (2008). Send from your own name or a name your list knows, not a brand they've forgotten."],[7484,"People in the waiting area are moved into the webinar automatically when you go live."],[1826,"People is every registrant and attendee across all your webinars in one table, and you can filter it by behaviour and source and export the list. It is a quick way to check who should have received a tag, or to follow up with people outside your CRM rules."],[4455,"People is the follow-up list. It turns webinar behaviour into segments you can act on. Think of no-shows to send the replay to, or engaged viewers to invite to a call. It also shows which campaigns brought attendees rather than just sign-ups."],[4516,"People list features, from each platform's public documentation:"],[9379,"People view"],[1226,"People view in webinar analytics"],[7087,"People watching evergreen sessions count towards the **Automated attendees** meter on the **Plan** tab."],[8725,"People watching evergreen sessions count towards the **Automated attendees** meter on the **Plan** tab."],[5010,"People watching evergreen sessions, including just-in-time ones, count towards the **Automated attendees** meter on the **Plan** tab."],[3543,"People who bought"],[5723,"People who click an offer can be treated differently afterwards:"],[4696,"People who reached the checkout for a paid webinar but didn't pay. They aren't registered."],[8486,"People: check who registered and when."],[3512,"People: every registrant across your webinars, with filters by behaviour and source."],[3973,"People: see who registered and what they did."],[3309,"People: the filters and export for following up across webinars."],[6092,"People: who answered your polls, next to watch time and offer clicks."],[3338,"Per campaign"],[4542,"Phone numbers only appear if your registration form collects them. Add the **Phone** field to the form block."],[4485,"Pick a category on the left, refine it on the right, then click **Apply Filter**."],[7603,"Pick a date, time and timezone, and write them on a registration page."],[2758,"Pick a registration page"],[6868,"Pick a registration template for the page people sign up on, or click **Skip & Create Webinar** to choose one later."],[2388,"Pick a registration template, or choose **Default Register Page** for a simple one-column page."],[7630,"Pick a registration template, or click **Skip & Create Webinar** and choose one later."],[7052,"Pick a registration template, or click **Skip & Create Webinar** and choose one later. Edit and publish the page in the builder before you send anyone to it. See Registration page builder."],[4843,"Pick a registration template, or click **Skip & Create Webinar** to choose one later. The webinar opens in the registration page builder, and the page stays private until you click **Publish**."],[552,"Pick a template"],[4731,"Pick a template and publish"],[2866,"Pick a template, or click **Skip & Create Webinar** and choose one later. The registration page builder lets you edit it on desktop and mobile views."],[2427,"Pick a topic that solves the first part of the problem your product solves. A home organiser might teach how to clear one room in a weekend, then offer the full package for the whole house."],[6035,"Pick any combination of these goals:"],[4793,"Pick by what your audience came for. If the value is you being there, run it live. If the value is the content, a recording will do."],[5339,"Pick carefully, because the type is fixed once the webinar exists. If you choose wrongly, clone the webinar and pick the right type on the copy."],[4810,"Pick the days and times you will run it, and publish a page listing them."],[3906,"Pick the list to send to."],[8867,"Pick the matching CRM field beside each item. The field must already exist in your CRM; after creating one there, click **Refresh**. Integrations are set per webinar."],[1805,"Pick the matching CRM field beside each one. **Refresh** pulls in fields you have just created in the CRM."],[1035,"Pick the output chips. **Script**, **Landing pages** and **Emails** are on by default; click **Polls** and **Offers** to add them."],[2857,"Pick the recording of your best live session on the new webinar's video step."],[6498,"Pick the type for the copy:"],[8580,"Pick whichever channel your audience actually uses. Sending both tends to irritate people."],[7781,"Pick your camera, microphone and speakers, then click **Continue to Green Room**. The button stays greyed out until the room can see a working camera and microphone."],[861,"Pick your running time, then split it across the sections in the template above."],[592,"Picture a coach with a topic, an offer and a date in mind, but no registration page yet. She can write one from a blank screen tonight, or she can describe the session and let the AI draft it. An AI-generated webinar landing page is the second route: pages written by AI from a description of your webinar, which you then edit like any other page."],[1002,"Picture a course creator who sells a self-paced course on another platform and wants a free webinar in front of it. The topic is clear, but writing a script, three pages, six emails and a set of polls takes days. An AI webinar is one where the AI writes those drafts from a description, so the work shifts from writing to reviewing."],[2601,"Picture a trainer who has run free sessions for a year and now wants to charge for a deeper, hands-on one. The questions arrive at once: how do people pay, how do only buyers get in, and what happens to the recording? A paid webinar answers all three in one place."],[9430,"Picture a typical case. A pricing consultant sells tickets to a live, two-hour masterclass for SaaS founders, with seats on sale three weeks ahead. Every founder who buys needs a seat and a join link before the day. Nobody who hasn't paid should get in."],[3851,"Picture a typical case. An independent management consultant who advises family-owned manufacturers runs a quarterly live briefing on succession planning. She has about 800 contacts from past projects and events, and she wants 60 of them in the room."],[389,"Picture a webinar that's two weeks away. The registration page is live, people are signing up, and nobody has written the reminder emails yet. This feature closes that gap."],[2155,"Picture an account lead on a Monday with three client launches this month. One client asks why the registration link shows another company's address, and another asks how many people actually turned up. White label webinar software lets one agency run webinars under many brands. It keeps each client's data apart and reports on each funnel."],[4260,"Picture the hour before a live session. The host is sorting slides, a co-host is still looking for the join link, and nobody has checked that the room is recording."],[7757,"Picture the last ten minutes before a live session. Your slides are open, a co-host is waiting backstage, and you suddenly wonder whether anyone pressed record. In EasyWebinar you don't have to press anything: Auto Recording captures the live session you host, and the result appears in your Library when the session is over."],[1545,"Picture the morning after a webinar. You have a list of people who came, a longer list of people who didn't, and a day of other work. A workflow is how that follow-up happens without you sitting down to send it."],[1132,"Picture the morning after a webinar. You have a registrant list in one tool, an attendee list in another and a spreadsheet of who clicked the offer. Someone has to merge them before anyone gets a follow-up."],[3189,"Picture the third week of the month. Four webinars are booked for next month and three people are building them. Two of them have just set up the same registration page from scratch. That is the moment a team needs a way to run regular webinars without duplicated work."],[3378,"Picture the week after a webinar. Your report shows 450 registrations, and someone in sales asks which of them are worth a call and where they came from. Webinar lead generation answers that question: the form captures the person, a campaign tag records the source, and attendance decides the follow-up."],[812,"Picture the week before a free webinar. The slides are half done, the invitation needs a description, and you still don't know what you'll say in the first two minutes. A webinar script template fixes that by giving you a set order of sections, so you fill in blanks instead of facing an empty page."],[4047,"Picture the week before a webinar. You have a title, a date and a registration page, and someone asks what the second half covers. If the answer is \"we'll see how it goes\", the session will run long and the ask will be rushed. A webinar outline is the one-page plan that answers it. It sets the sections, their order, their length and the moments you ask the audience to act."],[4009,"Place polls and offers on the CTAs tab"],[4109,"Place three polls against sections 1, 4 and 6, each with its purpose written beside it."],[2440,"Plain Language Is for Everyone, Even Experts (Nielsen Norman Group): how simple words make a script easier to follow."],[945,"Plain Language Is for Everyone, Even Experts: why simple, familiar words help every audience, including experts."],[7640,"Plan details are on the pricing page, and defaults are in limits and defaults."],[2215,"Plan for the end on day one. UK data protection rules say personal data should be kept for no longer than is necessary, and the same principles cover using it only for stated purposes. Agree in writing who owns the registrant list. Then export what the client is entitled to from **People** before you close the workspace."],[4169,"Plan one poll in the opening to learn who is attending, one after the second teaching point about their experience, and one in the bridge to gauge interest in going further before you make the offer."],[4720,"Plan the schedule around your audience's calendar"],[4924,"Plan usage"],[6789,"Plan usage"],[6978,"Plan usage"],[8653,"Plan usage"],[5264,"Plan your session times"],[734,"Plans and pricing: what each plan includes."],[947,"Plans and pricing: what each plan includes."],[6056,"Poll features, from each platform's public documentation:"],[5930,"Polls"],[163,"Polls and offers"],[7341,"Polls and offers"],[7510,"Polls and offers"],[7447,"Polls and offers are created on the **CTAs** tab and shown from the room. A row's toggle in the CTAs list keeps an offer ready without showing it. Switch on **Countdown timer** in the offer editor to put a countdown on an offer."],[6045,"Polls and offers share the CTAs tab, the same list controls and the same **Published** switch. A poll asked just before an offer can show you how ready the room is."],[2559,"Polls as the hands-on moments"],[7420,"Polls don't fire on their own in a live session, so plan when each poll goes out. Offers reach the room when you push them from the **Offers** panel. The **Question** panel keeps **Active** and **Answered** apart, so you can see at a glance what's still waiting."],[2660,"Polls let you stop and ask the room something. Ask a question about the audience rather than a test, such as which step they're stuck on. The answer tells you where to spend the next ten minutes."],[5995,"Polls matter most to coaches, consultants and B2B marketing teams who follow up with attendees after the webinar. For them, an answer given just before the offer is an early sign of who is ready to talk. Course creators use polls in long teaching sessions, where steady engagement keeps people watching to the end."],[4085,"Polls work best with a job to do. Plan each one against a section in the outline, not as a break when energy dips."],[5009,"Polls, offers and analytics behave as on any webinar. In **People**, filter by **Webinar → Evergreen** to compare your automated funnel with your live sessions. The People view lists every registrant."],[8651,"Polls, offers and chat"],[6453,"Polls, offers and emails"],[6234,"Polls: ask the room a question of your own instead of waiting for theirs."],[6425,"Polls: the other kind of CTA, often asked just before the pitch."],[5925,"Polls: the other way to hear from the room, including people who never type."],[732,"Polls: the polls the same build can write."],[5393,"Post a test message in chat and confirm it appears."],[5068,"Prepare the live recording before you reuse it"],[7608,"Present, take questions from chat, and run any polls you've prepared."],[7816,"Present, then click **End Session** and confirm."],[2378,"Present, then paste a payment link into the chat when you make the offer."],[5259,"Presenting live every time"],[7798,"Press **Shift + Ctrl + Show windows**, then choose **Screen record**."],[4224,"Press Go Live"],[2060,"Prevent it next time"],[4214,"Preview every poll and offer"],[9057,"Preview, save and publish"],[1979,"Prices change, so this page doesn't list them. The pricing page has current plans, and the standard trial is 7 days with a card required."],[9363,"Pricing on simulive and evergreen webinars"],[8711,"Pricing, video selection and templates are covered in Create an evergreen webinar."],[5650,"Product and SaaS teams"],[2500,"Product teams can announce and demonstrate in one live session, then keep the recording working. Customer success teams often run the same onboarding session each week, which suits Simulive or Evergreen. You can let people watch straight after registering instead of waiting for the next slot. Guides to product launch webinars and customer onboarding webinars are still being written."],[9385,"Professional education"],[4084,"Protect this time in the plan. Answer live questions, repeat the next step once, and tell people what will arrive by email afterwards. If you are running short, cut teaching, not questions, because questions are often where buyers raise the objections your offer has to answer."],[6224,"Public if you want people to see what's already been asked. Private if you want control over what the room sees."],[6105,"Public or private?"],[1360,"Publish a DMARC record with a policy of `none`, and include a reporting address so you can monitor the initial setup."],[1612,"Publish it, then watch one full cycle before adding another."],[1359,"Publish the DKIM public key that your sending service gives you."],[8987,"Publish the page on your site."],[1508,"Publish when it's ready"],[3324,"Put ad pixels on the registration and thank-you pages"],[8912,"Put an EasyWebinar registration form on your own website with the Registration Widget embed code, and decide when to use the widget instead of the registration page link."],[3498,"Put it in **Header Code** on the **Registration Page** and the **Thank You Page**, under **Settings** and then **Tracking Code**. Add your conversion event on the **Thank You Page** only, because that page loads only after someone registers."],[4164,"Put the offer after your last teaching point, through a short bridge that names the gap it closes. Leave time for questions afterwards, because that is where attendees raise the objections the offer has to answer."],[5473,"Q&A"],[6172,"Q&A and chat are set side by side on the Engagement tab, and they work best chosen together."],[6204,"Q&A features, from each platform's public documentation:"],[6150,"Q&A gives attendees a dependable way to ask something and a reasonable expectation that the question will be seen. For the presenter, it turns scattered questions into a list that can be answered in order."],[6135,"Q&A in EasyWebinar is a question queue that runs separately from chat. Attendees submit questions, and you and your moderators work through them in the room's **Question** panel, which splits them into **Active** and **Answered**. You decide on the webinar's **Engagement** tab whether questions are visible to everyone, visible only to hosts and moderators, or switched off. After the session, Analytics shows how many questions were asked and how many you answered."],[2659,"Q&A is a separate queue from chat. **Private Q&A** shows questions only to hosts and moderators, so one person's question doesn't set the agenda. A common workshop setup is **Everyone** for chat plus **Private Q&A**."],[6156,"Q&A matters most to teams that run demos, trainings and sales webinars. They want to answer questions without losing control of the room. A sociable chat with a private question queue, plus a count of what went unanswered afterwards, gives them that control."],[6182,"Q&A moderation preferences sit in the room's **Settings**, under **Preferences**, alongside chat moderation and appearance."],[6109,"Q&A on recorded webinars"],[250,"qualifying leads"],[5788,"Questions and answers"],[6094,"Questions and answers (Q&A)"],[5619,"Questions and answers: give real questions a private queue beside the simulated chat."],[6089,"Questions and answers: the attendees' own questions, in a queue."],[5923,"Questions and answers: the question queue you set beside chat on the same tab."],[4700,"Questions and answers: the setting behind the **Questions & Answers** panel and its **Not Answered Rate**."],[3999,"Questions and close"],[6159,"Questions and conversation do different jobs, so they don't need to share one stream. A greeting needs no reply, while a question needs an owner and a record of whether it was answered. Once questions have their own list, a second person can work through it while the presenter keeps going."],[7586,"Questions arrive in the **Question** panel, split into **Active** and **Answered**, so they don't get buried in chat. The live chat and Q&A pages cover each setting. Whether attendees can see each other in the attendee list is a separate setting, **Show Attendees**, on the Settings tab."],[4012,"Questions asked and answered"],[5155,"Re-enter every poll and offer, with the same wording and timing."],[4639,"Read **Views to Clicks** and **Clicks to Purchases** together. A low views-to-clicks rate means the offer itself isn't landing. A low clicks-to-purchases rate means people want the offer but your checkout or price is stopping them."],[774,"Read and edit the script"],[856,"Read each section aloud with a timer and compare it with the minutes you planned. This is the measure that matters most, because overruns usually land at the end, where the offer and questions sit. Its weak spot is that a solo read-through runs faster than a live session. Chat, questions and pauses all add time, so leave a margin."],[4118,"Read it before you move on. It is much easier to fix the script now than to fix the pages and emails built from it. If the timings drift from your plan, change the slides or duration and click **Regenerate**. **Download PDF** takes the script away so you can present from it. The AI webinar script generator page explains the same step for people starting from a blank page."],[3410,"Read the campaign for each registration from your web analytics or form tool, and copy it into the sheet against the email address."],[724,"Read the copy for pricing and what's included, then set the schedule and confirm the date. Check the mobile layout, the form fields and the SEO and sharing settings, then publish."],[8425,"Read the entry. Each one shows its **trigger**, the audience it goes **to**, and its **subject** line, so you can check what it does without opening it."],[1262,"Read the first results"],[7761,"Read the header in two moments. Before you start it says **Auto Recording Enabled**. Once you click **Go Live**, the badge changes to **Recording**, and the header also shows **LIVE** with a timer."],[630,"Read the headline the way a visitor would. In Nielsen Norman Group's early research, 79 percent of test users always scanned a new page instead of reading word by word. Its later eyetracking work advises putting the most important points in the first two paragraphs and starting headings with the words that carry most information. If the generated headline opens with filler, move the promise to the front."],[4110,"Read the outline aloud with a timer and move minutes until the questions still have their time."],[641,"Read the script before you continue to the pages. It's much easier to fix the script at this point than to fix the pages and emails built from it. If you want the price on the page, add it to your prompt, then check it on the page before you publish."],[459,"Read the script before you continue, because the pages and emails are built from it. The page generation guide covers the step after. On the emails step, read the six drafts and use **Add email** for anything missing. Click **Continue** to move on to polls and offers."],[444,"Read the whole sequence in order and check every price, date and link."],[3232,"Read this funnel before you clone a webinar, so the copy carries a setup that worked. The figures shown are sample data for a demo account."],[5553,"Read through **Preview Simulated Chat**."],[4558,"Read your analytics"],[3771,"Reading the webinar funnel: what each figure counts, and how to tell a page problem from a reminder problem."],[5064,"Rebuild it from scratch"],[5154,"Rebuild the registration page, copying the text and images from the live version."],[2182,"Rebuild the same funnel by hand in the next client's account, working from your notes."],[5157,"Reconnect your email or CRM tool and remap the fields."],[5065,"Record a fresh, clean take"],[4809,"Record the session, or keep the recording of a live run."],[2637,"Record the session, upload it somewhere private, and send it to whoever the replay rule covers."],[5360,"Record the talk once and keep the file somewhere you can reach it."],[7873,"Record your screen on your Android device (Android Help): starting and stopping a phone screen recording and finding the file."],[7701,"Recorded automatically by the webinar platform"],[7672,"Recorded live sessions land in **Library → Recordings**, where they can become the video for an evergreen webinar if you clone the live one."],[7595,"Recorded sessions land in **Library → Recordings**. The automatic recording guide walks through the check step by step. A recording holds attendees' names, voices and messages, and UK guidance says personal data must be used fairly, lawfully and transparently, so tell people you're recording."],[4346,"Recorded sessions land in the Library, under **Recordings**. Leave recording on unless you have a reason not to, because the replay is often watched by more people than the live session. The automatic recording page shows where to find it afterwards."],[6897,"Recorded webinars also have chat options a live webinar lacks: **Third party** embeds an external chat tool, **No Chat** hides the panel, and the **EW Contact Box** collects attendee questions by email even when chat is off."],[5351,"Recorded webinars can embed your own chat tool here, so conversations stay in the software your team already answers."],[7512,"Recording"],[8053,"Recording"],[7762,"Recording a webinar gives you a copy of the live session without anyone having to remember to start it. That copy is what you send to people who missed the hour, and what an evergreen version plays later."],[7812,"Recording needs no separate setup when you leave the default alone. The steps below are what to check and where to look."],[7821,"Recording Settings sits beside your devices, so check both in the green room before you broadcast anything."],[7830,"Recordings also appear on the **Recordings** tab of the video picker during webinar setup, so you pick it where you pick any other video. Create an evergreen webinar covers the rest of that setup."],[5231,"Recordings are captured automatically only when Auto Recording is on in the live room. If it was off, upload your own video instead, and turn it on before your next live run."],[7955,"Recordings are captured automatically when **Auto Recording** is on in the live room, and appear here after the session. They also show on the **Recordings** tab of the video picker when you set up a simulive or evergreen webinar."