ter deliverability than a single address. Follow what that screen asks for, rather than copying records from another service or guide. This page names no specific EasyCRM records for that reason."],[4825,"These steps create an evergreen webinar, the type with the most scheduling choices. A simulive webinar uses the same builder with set dates; Create a simulive webinar covers it."],[878,"These steps take you from a description to a finished script you can present from. The script is the first step of an AI webinar build, and the later steps use it."],[664,"These steps take you from a prompt to published pages. The whole build takes about ten minutes, and the script is the slowest part."],[2494,"These webinar examples are grouped by what the webinar has to achieve, which is usually the way a sale works. Each one says who it suits, who it doesn't suit, and where the full steps live. For a wider view by sector, the EasyWebinar solutions for all industries cover more ground."],[9457,"They also receive your **Registration Confirmation** email, which carries their join link, and your reminders before the session."],[313,"They carry an **AI** badge on their card in **My Webinars**."],[6082,"They do when the replay page uses **Webinar Replica**, which copies the session's video, offers, polls and chat replay."],[4173,"They do when the replay page uses Webinar Replica, which duplicates the live webinar with the same video, offers, polls and chat replay. Your outline's asks then keep working for people who watch later."],[7170,"They get confirmation and reminder emails from the Notifications tab."],[7171,"They join live, or watch the recording at their session time."],[3496,"They're tags added to the end of a link that say where a click came from. The core three are utm_source, utm_medium and utm_campaign. When **UTM Params** is on, EasyWebinar records the campaign with each registration."],[2078,"This appears on **Enter Room** when another of your webinars is already live, because only one webinar can be live at a time. Join that one from its Overview tab, or go live with the new one."],[1180,"This EasyWebinar video shows EasyCRM follow-up that changes with what each attendee did."],[3705,"This EasyWebinar video shows EasyCRM follow-up that reacts to what each attendee did."],[1139,"This EasyWebinar video shows how to connect your CRM and email tools to a webinar."],[3430,"This EasyWebinar video shows how to connect your CRM and email tools to a webinar."],[677,"This EasyWebinar video shows how to customize a registration page in the page builder."],[3436,"This EasyWebinar video shows how to filter and export registrants in People."],[4835,"This EasyWebinar video shows how to set a daily or weekly schedule on a webinar."],[3690,"This EasyWebinar video shows how to set up a replay that expires."],[7831,"This EasyWebinar video shows how to set up a replay that expires."],[4842,"This EasyWebinar video shows how to upload a webinar video to the library."],[7827,"This EasyWebinar video shows the Library, where you can also upload your own webinar videos."],[3443,"This EasyWebinar video walks through a webinar's Analytics tab, including revenue."],[835,"This is a fill-in template written for this page. EasyWebinar does not supply it, and its AI writes its own sections rather than filling in these headings. Copy it into a document, replace the bracketed parts, and adjust the minutes to your running time. The shares below assume a 45-minute session."],[7807,"This is an illustrative calculation with sample figures, not an EasyWebinar output. A host checks three monthly sessions by comparing time live with the duration shown on each recording card."],[2401,"This is an illustrative calculation with sample figures, not an EasyWebinar output. A solo operator promotes a free live session and reads the funnel the next morning."],[4817,"This is an illustrative calculation with sample figures, not an EasyWebinar output. A team runs its walkthrough **Weekly** on Monday to Friday at 11:00 and 16:00, and expects 300 registrants that week."],[5368,"This is an illustrative calculation with sample figures, not an EasyWebinar output. It counts the coach's own time across four weekly sessions in a month."],[5160,"This is an illustrative calculation with sample figures, not an EasyWebinar output. It counts the setup items the woodworking masterclass would need rebuilt by hand, then the share that cloning covers."],[3450,"This is an illustrative calculation with sample figures, not an EasyWebinar output. It follows the freight software team from the approach section after one quarterly webinar. The counts come from filtering People by **Source & UTM** for each campaign."],[3245,"This is an illustrative calculation with sample figures, not an EasyWebinar output. It shows how a team might pick the master for next month's demo from last month's two demos."],[2221,"This is an illustrative calculation with sample figures, not an EasyWebinar output. It shows how an account lead turns one month's analytics into a comparison across three clients."],[2882,"This is an illustrative calculation with sample figures, not an EasyWebinar output. It shows how to work out how many runs of your webinar you need."],[4128,"This is an illustrative calculation with sample figures, not an EasyWebinar output. It takes the 60-minute column of the template, works out the running clock and share of time, then shows what a small overrun does."],[1598,"This is an illustrative calculation with sample figures, not an EasyWebinar output. It uses the bike workshop above and the 1,000 emails a month that the Wallet screen lists as included."],[1364,"This is an illustrative calculation with sample figures, not an EasyWebinar output. It uses the garden centre from earlier and asks two planning questions. Does the month fit the **Wallet** allowance, and how close is the largest day to the level Gmail treats as bulk?"],[7613,"This is an illustrative calculation with sample figures, not an EasyWebinar output. Say the coaching workshop from earlier had 400 registrants."],[4353,"This is an illustrative calculation with sample figures, not an EasyWebinar output. Shared slides arrive as images about 1,500 pixels wide. When a phone shows the whole slide across a screen 375 pixels wide, every part of it shrinks to a quarter of its size."],[870,"This is an illustrative calculation with sample figures, not an EasyWebinar output. Suppose a career coach times herself and finds she speaks at about 130 words a minute. She plans a 45-minute session and holds back 5 minutes as a margin for chat and pauses, leaving 40 scripted minutes."],[2679,"This is an illustrative calculation with sample figures, not an EasyWebinar output. Suppose you want 30 people in the live room and you know roughly how your page performs."],[3726,"This is an illustrative calculation with sample figures, not an EasyWebinar output. Take the watercolour class from earlier, with 200 registrants, and the send plan from this page. Three emails go to each main group, and one goes to each behaviour group."],[3920,"This is an illustrative calculation with sample figures, not an EasyWebinar output. The leadership coach sends two invitations to the same 800 contacts."],[657,"This is an illustrative calculation with sample figures, not an output from the product. It shows how to read the funnel once the generated pages have been live for one session."],[2485,"This is the moment the format is fixed. Pick the type that fits your job here, because the webinar keeps it from then on."],[2643,"This is the one moment to decide that your workshop is paid, because switching a free webinar later keeps the free form."],[5122,"This is the one place where a live webinar becomes evergreen: choosing Evergreen here sets the new copy's type for good."],[2817,"This is the order to work in if you're building your first coaching webinar this week. Each step links to the page that covers its settings in full."],[4111,"This is the same planning work the webinar agenda guide on our blog covers from the attendee's side, where the agenda is the promise you publish in advance."],[2675,"This is the share of paid registrants who showed up, live or on replay. Paid buyers usually care, but they still forget. A gap here is a reminder problem, not a sales problem."],[2673,"This is the share of people who reached checkout and paid. Work it out as completed checkouts divided by completed plus abandoned checkouts. A low figure points at the price, the ticket wording or a surprise at checkout rather than at your marketing."],[433,"This is the share of registrants who turned up. EasyWebinar's analytics guidance calls it your reminders doing their job, and says a low number is a notification problem, not a content one. Its weak spot is that it mixes in things the emails don't control, such as how far ahead people registered. Compare it across webinars with similar lead times."],[6847,"This is the step that makes the webinar simulive. Whatever you pick here is what plays in every session."],[2829,"This is where the coaching pitch becomes a button: write the headline, paste your booking or application link and decide whether a countdown runs."],[836,"This is your webinar opening script, and it does two jobs: it welcomes people and tells them why staying is worth it. Put the main point first. Nielsen Norman Group's guidance on the inverted pyramid says to start with the most important information, so people get the point however much they take in. The same logic suits a spoken opening, because people join late and drift in and out."],[2608,"This matters most to coaches, consultants, wellness practitioners and specialist trainers whose knowledge is the product. It matters most when the first paid session goes on sale."],[5131,"This matters most to hosts who sell from a webinar and can't present every day. It usually comes up right after a live session that converted well. The host wants the same result next week without blocking the diary again."],[5321,"This matters most to marketers and creators whose webinar already works and now needs to run on a calendar. Course creators running weekly taster sessions, coaches with a standing intro talk and product teams with a recurring demo all reach this point. It usually comes the week the session gets booked for a time zone nobody on the team lives in."],[4781,"This matters most to SaaS teams, marketers and course creators. For them, the webinar is a step in a funnel, such as a demo, an onboarding session or an offer. It matters most when a live session already works and the next question is how to run it more often."],[9282,"This matters most to teams that bring outside speakers onto their webinars and promote to lists they already own. It shows up in the week before a session, when links go out to speakers, moderators, customers and the wider audience at once."],[1320,"This matters most to the admin or marketer who owns the first send, and to the owner whose domain carries the mail. It matters at the very start, before lists and campaigns exist. Domain work can need help from whoever holds your DNS, so leave time for it."],[3441,"This new webinar still shows zeros; the cards fill in as registrations arrive, and the date range covers every card on the page."],[7869,"This page covers webinars you run in EasyWebinar. For a session hosted elsewhere, the general method is a screen recorder on your own device, which records only your screen."],[5313,"This panel is where you confirm which recording each session will play, and swap it later without touching the schedule."],[3233,"This rate shows your registration page doing its job. A low figure is a page problem: the headline, the form or the promise. Its weak spot is that **Visitors** counts unique IPs, so many people behind one office network can look like one visitor."],[3234,"This rate shows your reminders doing their job. A low figure is a notification problem, not a content one. **Total Attended** counts unique people, live or replay, so check the **Live only**, **Replay only** and **Both** split before you judge the live session."],[2383,"This recipe gets a live sales webinar ready in one sitting. The manual builder walks you through four steps and takes about two minutes, and every page has a working default you can improve later."],[4834,"This schedule step is where one recording becomes many sessions, so every option you switch on here becomes a choice on your registration page."],[1415,"This screen is the other half of the picture: emails tied to one webinar, with their own sender settings, which your CRM sending setup leaves untouched."],[3645,"This sends on the action, so it can arrive while the person is still deciding. Write it to make sense whenever it lands, and don't assume they left without buying. The offer's button decides where they went, so link the same page here."],[1314,"This setup answers one question: how do my CRM broadcasts and workflows go out from my own domain or address? It connects an email service and proves who you send as. You do it once, before you build anything."],[4770,"This short EasyWebinar video walks through how an automated webinar formula turns one recording into a repeating funnel."],[88,"This starts to matter when a second person joins the webinar work. That might be a producer building pages, a moderator in the chat, or a manager checking results. It matters most to agencies, whose own staff and each client's work need clear lines between them."],[2496,"This suits course creators, educators and trainers. It is not for hosting the course itself. EasyWebinar is the layer that sells your course, and the course stays on your own course platform."],[2499,"This suits teams with a steady flow of prospects. If you only need a quick internal meeting, a full webinar set-up is more than the job needs."],[4313,"This video shows how to set the redirects and add tracking code to the webinar."],[5191,"This video shows how to set up a daily or weekly schedule for a webinar in EasyWebinar."],[3257,"This video shows team roles being set up, then a custom domain added for your webinar pages."],[869,"This video shows the AI drafting a webinar script from a description, then carrying it into the rest of the build."],[906,"This video shows the same AI build on live and evergreen webinars."],[4310,"This video shows where reminder emails are set and how their timing works."],[1163,"Those registrants arrive in **Leads**."],[5341,"Three checks are worth doing before you publish a long schedule:"],[3612,"Three emails per group is enough for most sessions. If you can only write two, keep the first and the last. The first delivers what people signed up for, and the last tells them what is about to close. For more on how the wider sequence fits together, read our guide to webinar retention and post-webinar follow-up."],[8613,"Three is a sensible default: a day before, an hour before, and fifteen minutes before. The last one does most of the work."],[8571,"Three is a sensible default. Webinars built with **Create with AI** arrive with exactly this pattern already drafted: **Reminder — 1d**, **Reminder — 1h** and **Reminder — 15m**, with merge tags already in place so dates, times and join links fill themselves in."],[4168,"Three is enough for 45 or 60 minutes. Each point needs an idea, an example and a takeaway, and more points leave each one too little time while pushing the offer later."],[3914,"Three numbers tell you how an invitation did: opens, clicks and registrations. Each one points at a different line of the email."],[3752,"Three per group is enough for most sessions: one right after, one a day later and a last call before your deadline. If nothing is closing, you can stop at two."],[4081,"Three points are enough for 45 or 60 minutes. Each one gets an idea, an example and a takeaway. Research on memory suggests people hold a small number of chunks at once, which is a good reason to resist a fourth or fifth point. Put the point that leads most naturally to your offer last."],[3402,"Three rules keep the report clean:"],[3996,"Three teaching points"],[7057,"Three things confirm the setup worked:"],[6537,"Ticking **Registration pages** and **Embed widgets** brings the original's pages and embed widgets across to the copy. Review them on the copy before promoting it, since the copy may now be a different type with a different schedule. See Registration page builder and Registration embeds."],[4208,"Time the reminders around the start"],[2628,"Time zones work differently by type. A live session runs at one fixed time in the timezone you set, and the registration page shows that time with its timezone. If your buyers are spread across regions, add more sessions with **Add Session** rather than expecting the time to shift for each person."],[6591,"Timezone"],[4914,"Timezones: who sees which time"],[7480,"To **Library → Recordings**, named after the webinar with its duration and recording date."],[9614,"To act on one sitting without touching the rest, use the options menu on that session's row. To change every sitting at once, go back to **Scheduling Options**."],[9137,"To add a block, use the orange **+** below an existing block. The new one goes underneath."],[6328,"To add a new one, click **+** at the bottom of the offer list on the left."],[7966,"To change it later, open the webinar's **Content** tab and use the **Webinar Video** panel. **Preview** plays the current video and **Change Video** swaps it."],[5705,"To change it:"],[9605,"To change the date, time or recurrence, open the options menu on the **Scheduling Options** panel. A change made here applies to the whole webinar, not to one sitting."],[5875,"To check it, join a running session as an attendee, not as an admin. The widget sits under **Contact** in the right-hand rail, on its **Chat** tab. In the admin view the side panel shows your own host tools instead."],[4322,"To check, open your slides on your own phone at the size they fill the screen. If you have to squint, enlarge the type or split the slide in two. Do the same for any screen you plan to share, such as a spreadsheet or a product screen: zoom your own browser in before you share it, so the text is large when it arrives."],[2362,"To invite people already on your list, send the **One-Click Registration Link** from sharing links. It carries their name and email in the URL, so a known contact registers without filling in the form."],[3022,"To keep people on your own site, copy the **Registration Widget** embed code and paste the form into a landing page or blog post."],[7273,"To leave without broadcasting, click **Exit**. For what happens once you're live, see Run a live webinar."],[7366,"To run a live webinar in EasyWebinar, you open the webinar room from the webinar's **Overview**, pass a quick camera and microphone check, and arrive in the green room, where nothing reaches your audience. When you're ready you click **Go Live**, present using the panels on the right-hand rail, and finish with **End Session**. The result is a broadcast to everyone registered for the session, with the recording saved to **Library → Recordings** if recording was on."],[7432,"To run a recording at set times without presenting, see Create a simulive webinar."],[7061,"To see your evergreen webinar the way attendees do, register on your own registration page. With just-in-time on and the interval at 2 minutes, the shortest option, a session starts within minutes. When a session is running, it appears on the **Live** tab of the Sessions panel marked *Live now*, with **Enter room**."],[2206,"To speed up the draft, the AI Webinar Builder drafts scripts, pages, emails, polls and follow-up before the webinar. It works from your description of the client's offer, as explained in Create with AI. Read the drafts as the client's voice, then edit. The registration page builder handles anything the template doesn't."],[6009,"To start a new one, click **+** at the bottom of the poll list on the left."],[1619,"To stop a workflow that's running, archive it. Archive rather than delete when a campaign ends: you keep the record, and you can reuse the structure for the next one."],[8474,"To the **Reply-to email** in **Email Settings**. Use an address someone reads, because people do reply."],[5921,"To the address set in **Email address to receive questions**."],[7151,"To turn a live webinar into an evergreen one, run it live first, then clone it and choose Evergreen on the copy. Cloning is the supported path because the type is fixed."],[8059,"Tracking code"],[3426,"Tracking code is set per page, and nothing applies until you click **Save Changes**. A Google Analytics tag goes in **Header Code** in the same way, on each page you want in your reports."],[8782,"Tracking pixels"],[9064,"Tracking pixels"],[6614,"Training and education providers"],[9372,"Transaction statuses"],[3967,"Transactional and confirmation email, Nielsen Norman Group (2008): why a recognisable sender decides whether email gets opened."],[511,"Transactional Email and Confirmation Messages (Nielsen Norman Group): why recognisable senders and leading with what matters get emails opened."],[3763,"Transactional Email and Confirmation Messages, Nielsen Norman Group, 2008: how people sort a crowded inbox, and what they look for first in an email."],[4648,"Transactions show one of these statuses: **Pending**, **Processing**, **Success**, **Failed**, **Canceled**, **Refunded** or **Partially Refunded**. **Checkout abandoned** counts people who reached checkout but didn't pay; they aren't registered. A webinar with no payments shows \"No transactions yet.\""],[5072,"Trim the start and end if you need to"],[5443,"Trim your videos (YouTube Help): how to cut a YouTube video without re-uploading it."],[5239,"Trim your videos (YouTube Help): how to cut the start, middle or end of a recording before you reuse it."],[5786,"Turn chat off but stay reachable"],[7030,"Turn it on and registrants can start watching as soon as they register. **Instant replay text** sets the wording of the button they click, which reads *Watch instant replay* until you change it. On Demand is the same thing as instant replay, and it is not the replay page on the **Replay** tab. See On Demand."],[7029,"Turn it on and the registration page offers a session that starts shortly. **Interval** controls how often these sessions come round, from every 2 minutes to every 60, and **Exclude specific time** keeps chosen hours clear. Just-in-time sessions run in each attendee's own local time. Settings, timezone behaviour and testing are covered in Just-in-time webinars."],[7119,"Turn on **Blackout Dates** in **Schedule Preferences** and choose the dates."],[3684,"Turn on **Enable replay page**."],[8839,"Turn on **GDPR Compliance** if you ask for marketing consent. Write the consent wording, and choose whether ticking it is mandatory."],[8900,"Turn on **GDPR Compliance** on the form block. You write the consent wording and can make ticking it mandatory."],[3422,"turn on **GDPR Compliance**, which adds a consent checkbox you can word yourself and make mandatory."],[2648,"Turn on **Live + Replay bundle** if you want to sell a second option that includes the replay recording, with its own price. The registration page then shows two options to choose from. Make this call before the page goes live, because it changes what your first buyers are promised."],[9447,"Turn on **Live + Replay bundle** to offer two choices on the registration page: the live webinar alone, or the webinar plus its recording, each at its own price. It suits people who want to attend but also keep the session to watch again, and people who can't make the live time."],[8432,"Turn on **Notify admin** if you want a copy of each registration sent to an admin address, and give it that address."],[9290,"Turn on **Shorten URL's** if you want shorter versions."],[9303,"Turn on **Shorten URL's** in the Share dialog to get shorter versions of the links. If you send join and replay links from a connected CRM, the integration's **Custom fields** tab offers short versions there too: **Webinar Join Short Link** and **Webinar Replay Short Link**, alongside the full **Webinar Join Link** and **Webinar Replay Link**."],[8846,"Turn on **UTM Params** on the form block and publish the page."],[8901,"Turn on **UTM Params** on the form, tag your links, then filter **People** by **Source & UTM**."],[3494,"Turn on **UTM Params** on the registration form and tag every promotion link. Then open **People**, click **Add Filter** and choose **Source & UTM**. The **Webinar** column shows which webinar each person registered for."],[8840,"Turn on **UTM Params** to record the campaign behind each registration."],[3419,"turn on **UTM Params**, so each registration records the campaign that brought it in;"],[8036,"Turn on a webinar's replay page, decide how long it stays available, send viewers somewhere when it ends, choose between Webinar Replica and Custom Build, and tell a replay apart from instant replay."],[4829,"Turn on any mix of **Just-in-time Registration**, **On Demand** and **Recurring Schedule**."],[2372,"Turn on the replay page before you paste its link into an email. If the replay uses **Webinar Replica**, the same offers and polls carry over, so replay viewers can buy too. The replay pages guide covers the expiry options, and the full email set is on webinar follow-up emails."],[3330,"Turn on UTM capture on the registration form"],[649,"Turn that sentence into a headline that leads with the words carrying most information."],[6353,"Turn the editor's **Published** switch off."],[2756,"Turn the live session into one that runs on repeat"],[5701,"Turn the offer's toggle off in the **CTAs** list, or"],[2836,"Turn the offer's toggle off until you're ready to show it, then turn it on in the session."],[6026,"Turn the poll's toggle off in the **CTAs** list, or"],[5530,"Turn the simulation on with its **Active** toggle. This disables Manual Simulation."],[4004,"Turn your outline into a webinar in EasyWebinar"],[7906,"Turning a live webinar into an evergreen one"],[8851,"Turning on **GDPR Compliance** on the form block adds a consent checkbox to your form."],[4203,"Two days before"],[3002,"Two details shape this route. A webinar's type can't be changed after you create it, so there is no live-to-evergreen switch, only a clone. And a clone starts at zero: registrants and attendees remain on the live webinar, so the launch's figures stay where they were. How other platforms handle a course webinar is covered in How selling a course by webinar compares, below."],[6380,"Two email groups on the **Notifications** tab relate to offers:"],[1940,"Two features help when you share a screen or slides:"],[4628,"Two gaps tell you most of what you need:"],[1332,"Two large mailbox providers publish rules that apply to whatever your CRM sends, and both pages were checked on 2 November 2026. Gmail's requirements have applied since 1 February 2024, and they concern personal accounts ending in @gmail.com or @googlemail.com. Providers change these rules, so check the source pages before a large send."],[1626,"Two measures matter most for an automated sequence: how many people it reached, and whether those people engaged. Each has a weak spot."],[5355,"Two measures move directly with a simulated live webinar. The first is attendance: the share of registrants who turn up to a session. The second is how long attendees stay, and where in the recording they leave."],[432,"Two measures show whether the emails are doing their job. Both are on the webinar's analytics, so you can check them after every session."],[3439,"Two measures show whether webinar lead generation is working: registration rate and show-up rate. Read both for the whole webinar first, then for each campaign."],[2672,"Two measures tell you most about a paid workshop. Both sit inside the webinar, so you don't need a spreadsheet."],[2397,"Two measures tell you most of what a first sales webinar did. The first is how many registrants attended. The second is how many people who saw your offer clicked it and then bought."],[2869,"Two measures tell you most of what you need. The first is the offer click rate: clicks on your offer divided by the people who saw it. The second is how many clickers went on to book or apply, which you count in your booking tool or application form."],[642,"Two measures tell you whether a landing page is doing its job. Both are about the page itself, not about the webinar that follows."],[7598,"Two measures tell you whether a live session did its job. Neither is perfect, so read them together."],[5147,"Two measures tell you whether a reused live recording works as an evergreen webinar: how long people keep watching, and how many act on your offer."],[3231,"Two measures tell you whether a webinar's setup deserves to become next month's master. Both sit on each webinar's **Analytics** tab."],[4124,"Two measures tell you whether the plan held up, and both come from the sections you timed."],[4803,"Two measures tell you whether the schedule is doing its job."],[4988,"Two minutes is also the setting to use when you want to check the webinar yourself, because a session starts almost as soon as you register. The steps are in Test a just-in-time session, below."],[5038,"Two minutes."],[6368,"Two more replay settings support an offer:"],[5861,"Two separate controls decide what attendees can do:"],[4314,"Two settings decide what attendees can do, and both are set before the session. **Show Attendees** on the webinar's Settings tab controls whether the attendee list is visible. Chat is set on the **Engagement** tab, where **Hosts only** makes every message private to your team and **No Chat** removes the panel. The live chat page explains each option."],[5824,"Two settings shape the chat:"],[1347,"Two settings use the word \"domain\", and they do different jobs. **Domain Configuration** under **Configurations** concerns the email your CRM sends. **Custom domain (C-Name)** under **Settings** → **Edit Profile** points your own domain at your webinar pages, so links read `webinars.yourcompany.com`."],[7786,"Two things that attendees see live never reach the recording, so plan your session around them."],[6831,"Type a **Webinar Name**. The builder won't move on while the name is empty."],[6010,"Type your **Question**."],[2447,"Types of webinars sorted by the job you want done, with the format, features and step-by-step guide that fit each one in EasyWebinar."],[2446,"Types of Webinars: Pick the Job You Have, Then Find the Set-Up and Steps That Fit It"],[4889,"UK bank holidays (GOV.UK): the bank holidays to consider as blackout dates."],[5441,"UK bank holidays (GOV.UK): the upcoming bank holidays in England and Wales, for planning a weekly schedule."],[3885,"UK data protection law says personal data must be \"used for specified, explicit purposes\" and handled fairly, lawfully and transparently. Invite people whose details you collected for this kind of contact."],[3667,"UK data protection rules say personal data must be used for \"specified, explicit purposes\", and used fairly and transparently. A replay email is what people expect after registering for a session. An unrelated promotion is harder to justify, so say on your registration form what else you'll send. **GDPR Compliance** on the registration form adds a consent checkbox that you word yourself."],[6197,"Unanswered questions are a reason to follow up. **Webinar Follow-ups** on the **Notifications** tab can go to everyone who registered, only those who attended, or only no-shows."],[5529,"Under **AI Simulation**, use **Add New** to create a simulation, or pick a saved one from the selector."],[3685,"Under **Availability**, choose **Always Available**, **Expire after days** or **Specific date**."