nything?"],[2783,"Will an evergreen coaching webinar still feel live?"],[2063,"Will attendees see me while I fix my camera?"],[9087,"Will EasyWebinar translate my page?"],[2319,"Will EasyWebinar work with my email tool?"],[1113,"Will importing the same webinar twice create duplicates?"],[1750,"Will it sync people who registered but didn't attend?"],[2975,"Will it work with my email tool?"],[9255,"Will my co-presenter appear on screen as soon as they join?"],[8073,"Will my offers and polls show on the replay?"],[6283,"Will my offers show on the replay?"],[5660,"Will my offers, and their countdowns, show on the replay?"],[4034,"Will my polls and offers appear on the replay?"],[5967,"Will my polls appear on the replay?"],[5493,"Will the AI chat be the same in every session?"],[5103,"Will the drawings from my live session appear in the evergreen version?"],[574,"Will the generated pages work on phones?"],[2456,"Win clients as a coach or consultant"],[7596,"With **EasyCast**, you can broadcast the live webinar to YouTube, LinkedIn or a custom RTMP destination at the same time. Registered attendees watch in the webinar room, and everyone else can watch on those platforms. EasyCast starts on the Growth plan."],[5576,"With **Easywebinar Chat** selected, a recorded webinar's Chat screen offers **Simulated Chat**, which plays back a pre-written chat during the webinar, and **Simulated Attendees**, which shows a simulated attendee list in the room. The script, attendee count and names are set on the Chat Simulation tab. Choosing **Third party** replaces the built-in chat, so simulation stops applying."],[8242,"With **Import from URL**, the answer is somewhere else. You give EasyWebinar the platform, a link and the video's length, and the webinar plays the video from that platform. Nothing is stored on EasyWebinar, so no storage is used, but the webinar now depends on the video staying where it is."],[8241,"With **Local import**, the answer is EasyWebinar. You upload the file, EasyWebinar stores and serves it in the same way a dedicated video host would, and nothing else is needed to play it in a webinar. The upload uses part of your storage allowance, shown at the top of the Library."],[5720,"With **Webinar Replica**, the replay page shows the same video, offers, polls and chat replay as the session, so your offers keep selling after the event. The replay itself can also have a deadline: **Expire after days** closes it a set number of days after the session, and **Specific date** closes it at a time you choose. A replay deadline and an offer deadline are separate settings; keep them consistent so attendees aren't told two different end times."],[1173,"With a few hundred leads you can scroll. With a few thousand you can't. **Add Filter** narrows the table once, by status, tags, company or date created. **Add List** saves a group as a tab you can come back to and send to."],[2949,"With AI"],[751,"With AI from a prompt"],[5680,"With no countdown, an offer's end point is easy to miss or forget. People who meant to buy are left unsure whether it is still open. Many wait, and in webinar selling, waiting often means not buying. A registration page with no visible start time gives visitors little reason to sign up today."],[8719,"With On Demand off, registrants still have just-in-time or recurring sessions if you've enabled them."],[8827,"With only name and email, you know how many people registered but little else. You can't text anyone, and you can't tell which ad, email or post sent them. The registration count goes up, and the reason why is lost."],[4966,"With only set daily or weekly times, someone who arrives just after a session starts must wait for the next slot. That slot can be hours or a day away. The gap between interest and watching is where people disappear. Many who close the tab meaning to return never do."],[5352,"With the built-in chat selected, a recorded webinar can also play back a pre-written chat with **Simulated Chat**, and show a simulated attendee list. Chat Simulation is in Beta, and the chat simulation (Beta) page covers the script, attendee count and names. Use it honestly: simulated messages shouldn't impersonate real customers or invent testimonials."],[9471,"With the replay page set to **Webinar Replica**, the recording shows the same video, offers, polls and chat replay as the session. Replay availability is set on the **Replay** tab, and **After the replay ends** under Redirects can send viewers to your next offer."],[4460,"Without a behaviour-level list, every registrant gets the same follow-up. The person who watched to the end and clicked your offer gets the same email as someone who never turned up. The people closest to buying are treated like everyone else."],[1145,"Without a CRM, webinar leads sit in exports and inboxes. Nobody owns the follow-up, so attendees and no-shows get the same message or none at all. The interest a webinar created fades before anyone acts on it."],[4266,"Without a fixed list, checks happen in whatever order you remember them. The ones you forget tend to be the ones you can't fix live: an empty redirect, a co-host without a link, or recording switched off. Those cost you the replay, the next step for attendees, or the first five minutes of the session."],[7569,"Without a live session, every question waits for an email reply, and nobody hears it answered in front of the group. A launch loses its shared moment, because each viewer meets the offer alone and at a different time. You also lose the chance to hear real objections and fix the talk before you automate it."],[2607,"Without a paid route, you either give the workshop away or stitch together a payment link, a spreadsheet and a meeting invite. People who paid get missed, and people who didn't pay find the link."],[3236,"Without a platform built for teams, the job looks like this:"],[4323,"Without a private room, a test run takes more people and more steps. This is the manual method many teams use."],[7767,"Without a recording, the live hour is all you get. Registrants who couldn't attend have nothing to watch, and the talk you prepared can't run again unless you present it again. The replay is usually watched by more people than the live session, so losing it loses most of the audience."],[9108,"Without a registration page, people have nowhere to sign up. Your posts and emails create interest, but that interest never becomes a name on your list. You also lose the first number in your funnel: how many people saw the invitation and said yes."],[8104,"Without a replay page, the session is over for everyone who wasn't there. No-shows get a follow-up with nothing to watch. An offer made live never reaches a second audience. EasyWebinar's guidance is to leave live recording on because the replay is usually watched by more people than the live session."],[2339,"Without a sales webinar, every sale needs its own conversation. Your time sets the ceiling on how many people you can sell to, and interested people who can't get a call slot drift away."],[6709,"Without a scheduled live session, your audience has no fixed moment to turn up. Promotion has no date to point at, so interest fades before anyone joins. You also lose the chance to answer questions while people are still deciding."],[822,"Without a script, presenters tend to overrun the teaching and rush the close. The invitation promises one thing and the session delivers another. Each new webinar starts from a blank page again, so the prep takes days instead of an afternoon."],[1355,"Without a setup screen, this job happens directly in DNS. These steps show the general method, and they're useful for briefing whoever holds your DNS."],[7983,"Without a shared library, each recorded webinar needs its video added again. Recordings of live sessions sit apart from the webinars that could reuse them. It also gets harder to see which videos depend on an outside platform."],[5320,"Without a simulated live webinar, every repeat of a session costs you the full presenting time. The quality also varies from one session to the next, with your energy, your connection and your voice. A strong talk that you can't face giving again simply stops running."],[5359,"Without a simulive webinar type, a repeated talk is usually run from a video call tool and a calendar:"],[9645,"Without a single summary screen, the basics of a webinar get scattered. The schedule lives in one place, pricing in another and the presenter list somewhere else. It becomes easy to promote the wrong date. A co-presenter may only get their link after messaging you to ask for it."],[7439,"Without a staging area, presenters test their microphones in front of the audience, and a co-host's first words are an apology about echo. Without a confirmation step, a webinar can start before the offers exist. Without automatic recording, the replay you planned to send to no-shows may not exist at all."],[7234,"Without a staging area, the first minutes of a webinar become the rehearsal. Attendees who arrived on time watch presenters ask whether they can be heard. The recording behind your replay page then opens with the same fumbling."],[8250,"Without a video in place, a simulive or evergreen webinar has nothing to play. Registrants turn up at their session and there is no class to watch. Every webinar you meant to run on its own waits on a file."],[2996,"Without a webinar in the middle, people go straight from an email or an ad to a sales page. The page has to answer every doubt on its own, with no chance to teach or take questions. Visitors who aren't ready yet tend to leave."],[2805,"Without a webinar, every prospect hears your method one call at a time. Your calendar fills with people who were never a fit. The months between referral waves stay empty, and you only find out who was serious after you've spent the hour."],[8969,"Without an embed, every visitor on your own site has to follow a link to the EasyWebinar page to register. Each extra click is a chance for someone to get distracted and leave. The page that persuaded them, such as the article they were reading, is left behind."],[7073,"Without an evergreen schedule, a recording reaches people only on the dates it is shown. Anyone who finds the page between showings has to wait, and many lose interest before the next one comes round."],[5130,"Without an evergreen version, your best session is over once the live date passes. Every new visitor waits for the next date you can present, and many of them won't come back for it."],[3849,"Without an invitation, the people most likely to come never hear about the session. The registration page waits for search or social traffic that may not arrive, and your list goes cold while you post into feeds."],[6313,"Without an offer card, the call to action is only what the presenter says. People who arrive late miss it, and anyone watching a recording hears it once and moves on. Interest goes unrecorded, so you can't tell who came close to buying."],[4053,"Without an outline, the session grows around whatever you most enjoy explaining. Questions get cut, the offer lands when people are already leaving, and the follow-up emails promise things the session never covered."],[1556,"Without automation, follow-up depends on someone remembering to send it. The no-shows, usually the biggest group, are the first to be dropped. Leads who were interested on the day hear nothing for a week, and by then the webinar has faded from their mind."],[4808,"Without automation, keeping a session available means doing the scheduling yourself."],[5834,"Without chat, attendees have no way to speak during the session, and the presenter has no way to tell whether the message is landing. Questions go unasked while the moment passes. For a selling webinar, that is where doubts that could have been answered in a sentence turn into \"not now\"."],[6528,"Without cloning, a new format means building the second version by hand. You recreate the registration page, rewrite the emails, re-enter polls and offers and reconnect integrations. Each step is a chance to introduce a difference you didn't intend."],[3598,"Without follow-ups, the webinar ends and so does the conversation. Attendees who meant to decide later get no nudge. Registrants who couldn't make it never learn that a replay exists, even though they asked to hear from you."],[3195,"Without it, one login gets shared and nobody can say who changed the reminder timing. Each webinar is built from nothing, so small differences creep in between sessions. Last quarter's webinars clutter the list, and the replay link goes out from the wrong one."],[205,"Without it, the setup work is spread across several blank pages: a script document, a page builder, five or six emails and an offer. That's often where webinars stall, especially a first one. Pieces written on different days also tend not to match each other."],[601,"Without it, you write each page yourself, from the headline down to the instructor bio. That's an evening a solo operator may not have, so promotion starts late or the page goes out thin. A thin page shows up later as visitors who look and don't register."],[8697,"Without On Demand, every registrant has to wait for a session, even if only for a few minutes. Some content is meant to be watched the moment people find it. For that content, any wait is a chance for them to leave and not return."],[9428,"Without paid registration, the registration page signs up anyone for nothing. A workshop worth paying for becomes a free session. Its value then has to be won back later, through an offer that only some attendees buy."],[4611,"Without per-stage numbers, a disappointing webinar is just disappointing. You can't tell whether few people saw the page, the page didn't convert, the reminders failed or the offer fell flat. So you end up changing everything at once. It's easy to rewrite a talk that was fine, when the real problem was that people never turned up."],[6155,"Without Q&A, attendees have no dedicated place to ask, so many keep their questions to themselves. Those who do ask get no sign that anyone saw the question. You close the session without knowing what the room still wanted to know, and on a selling webinar an unanswered objection often decides the sale."],[8550,"Without reminders, attendance depends on people remembering a session they booked days or weeks ago. Analytics shows the cost as a large **Missed** count: people who registered and never came. EasyWebinar reads a low registered-to-attended rate as a notification problem, not a content one."],[9281,"Without role links, the only way to bring a guest speaker into the room is to give them access to your account. Without a one-click link, every contact you invite from your own list retypes details you already hold. Some of them won't bother, and those registrations are lost."],[6889,"Without simulive, a repeated presentation means presenting live each time, at whatever hour suits the audience. A fully on-demand recording avoids that. But viewers then arrive at different points, so there is no shared conversation to join."],[3384,"Without source tracking you'll know how many people registered, but not which ad, email or post sent them. Budget then follows registration counts, and a channel whose sign-ups never attend can look like the winner. No-shows sit in a list that nobody writes to."],[8645,"Wording the button"],[765,"Words per section"],[2073,"Work through these in order and check the device preview after each one."],[2188,"Work through these in order for each new client. The first two steps take a few minutes; the domain step may need a few hours while DNS catches up."],[4334,"Work through these screens in order on the day, starting about half an hour before the start."],[2503,"Work through these steps in order. Most set-up problems come from skipping the first two."],[3249,"Work through these steps once, then repeat steps 4 to 